 each other''s state under Firefox","A Firefox e2e run on the fix branch passes the previously failing cluster, or every remaining failure is individually explained on the issue","No chromium regression in the same suite"],"context_refs":["Issue #229 comment 6404314471 \u2014 investigation handoff from queue task 1062","backlog-devtoday-code.md \u2014 NEXT note on run 40239827303"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Long-running nightly red on a flagship package; investigation complete, fix prescribed, ownerless until now","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:229', '2026-10-26 10:49:58.535723+00', '2026-10-27 04:33:21.008873+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1110, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'fix(cold-store-reaper): pack duplicate content writes orphan frames — small fix', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/963","title":"fix(cold-store-reaper): pack writes orphan frames and inflates member_count/live_bytes when one call gets duplicate content","number":963,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T11:57:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["upload/fetch/D1 sync behavior","schema changes to the members table","the retention (#939) and budget-enforcement (#938) follow-ups"],"include":["pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py (ColdStore.pack)","pkgs/cold-store-reaper/tests/test_cold_store.py (new regression test)"]},"tests":["python3 -m unittest discover -s pkgs/cold-store-reaper/tests (targeted suite, no network)","new duplicate-content pack regression test"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh api search/issues for ''cold-store-reaper'' and ''cold-store pack duplicate'' on 2026-10-26 returned only #923/#929/#933 (closed) and #938/#939/#940 (different follow-ups); no issue tracks duplicate-content pack","checked_at":"2026-10-26T11:57:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"pack() (pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py:432) appends a frame per input file and inserts members with INSERT OR IGNORE under PK (bundle_id, object_hash); duplicate content in one call leaves orphan frames in the bundle and records member_count/live_bytes counting the duplicates, while the members table holds one row.","evidence":["Verified repro on main a2eef6f7 (local, no network): two identical 180-byte files packed in one call -> bundle 76 bytes (38-byte frame twice), bundles.member_count=2, live_bytes=360, members table exactly 1 row (offset 0, length 38); same result packing the same path twice","pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py:432-503 pack(): one frame per file, INSERT OR IGNORE INTO members, member_count=len(members), live_bytes=sum of all member sizes","pkgs/cold-store-reaper/schema.sql: members PRIMARY KEY (bundle_id, object_hash)","Dedup: gh search ''cold-store-reaper'' issues \u2014 #938/#939/#940 cover budget enforcement, retention, state.json token; none covers duplicate-content pack"],"acceptance":["Packing duplicate content in one call stores each distinct object exactly once (one frame per distinct hash), or pack refuses duplicates with a clear ColdStoreError before writing","bundles.member_count equals the members row count for the bundle and live_bytes equals the sum of member object sizes after such a pack","Regression test in pkgs/cold-store-reaper/tests/test_cold_store.py packs duplicate content and asserts bundle bytes, member_count, live_bytes and members rows agree","Existing cold-store tests pass: python3 -m unittest discover -s pkgs/cold-store-reaper/tests","No behavior change for all-distinct packs"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/963","pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py:432","pkgs/cold-store-reaper/schema.sql"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent accounting corruption and wasted archive space in the cold-store manifest; narrow, repro-backed, single-function fix at normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:963', '2026-10-26 11:59:00.156933+00', '2026-10-26 19:23:39.688325+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1111, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'security(aggregator): move fleet-feed proxy credential off argv and pin laptop host key', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["credential-handling"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/948","title":"security(aggregator): fleet-feed push exposes proxy credential in process argv + host-key verification disabled","number":948,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T12:04:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["rotating the proxy credential itself (not required by this issue)","~/tools/laptop-ssh.sh and other hatch tooling outside developing-today/code"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/scripts/push-fleet-feed.sh","a checked-in known-hosts entry for the laptop host key, if that is the pinning mechanism chosen","a grep-level guard/test for this script"]},"tests":["manual push with /proc cmdline inspection of every spawned process; grep guard","negative test: altered/wrong pinned host key causes the push to fail"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh pr list open search for 948/push-fleet-feed returned no competing PR; gh issue search returned only #948; this fix packet is the follow-up created by triage task 1097","checked_at":"2026-10-26T12:04:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Confirmed by triage task 1097 on origin/main 61705a6684130ecbce1d922b9316471105b81afa: push-fleet-feed.sh:48 builds proxycmd with proxyauth={user}:{pw} and :54 passes it as ProxyCommand to scp/ssh (:60-67), so the shared egress-proxy credential is world-readable in /proc cmdline on every ~5-min push; :50-51 sets StrictHostKeyChecking=no + UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null on a connection authenticated with ~/.ssh/id_ed25519. Note socat itself would also carry proxyauth in its own argv, so merely hiding it from ssh argv is not sufficient - the credential must not be an argument to any process.","evidence":["Triage task 1097 (2026-10-26T12:04Z): git grep proxyauth origin/main hits only pm-stack/aggregator/scripts/push-fleet-feed.sh:48; git grep StrictHostKeyChecking=no hits :50 in the same file","origin/main 61705a66 file lines 48-67 reproduced verbatim by the triage worker (independent of the packet''s a2eef6f evidence)","No ~/.ssh/known_hosts exists on the sandbox (checked 2026-10-26) - no pinned laptop host key exists yet; the fix must capture the laptop (100.99.113.103) host key via the Tailscale route / a trusted channel and check it in or reference it, not just flip StrictHostKeyChecking to yes against an empty file","Credential itself is NOT committed (read from HTTPS_PROXY / ~/tools/secrets.d/mcpx-daemon.env at runtime) - defect is the hand-off mechanism only","Related, OUT OF SCOPE for this code-repo task: ~/tools/laptop-ssh.sh (hatch tooling, not this repo) uses the same socat proxyauth + StrictHostKeyChecking=no pattern at its lines 16-17 - flagged in the triage comment on #948 for separate handling"],"acceptance":["Credential absent from all process cmdlines during a push (ps//proc check covering ssh, scp, and any tunnel helper)","Laptop host key pinned/verified; a mismatched key fails the push","Grep-level guard/test: neither proxyauth= interpolation nor StrictHostKeyChecking=no reappears in push-fleet-feed.sh","Fleet-feed pushes still complete end to end (feed arrives on laptop, remote mv completes)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/948","pm-stack/aggregator/scripts/push-fleet-feed.sh:48","queue triage task 1097"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Confirmed (triage 1097) shared fleet proxy credential exposed via argv plus unverified host key on the same connection; security/credential exposure is priority 10 on the design scale. No committed secret and no active exploitation evidence.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 10, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:948', '2026-10-26 12:05:41.143863+00', '2026-10-26 13:50:50.56304+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1114, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Triage #483: openai.js stale duplicate of codex.js', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/483","title":"fix(quota): openai.js is a stale duplicate of codex.js \u2014 same endpoint and aliases, hardcoded windows, NaN-prone reset conversion, publicly exported but unregistered and untested","number":483,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:10:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["fixing the duplication in this task (that is the follow-up small_fix)","any other quota provider","held or user/owned items"],"include":["read-only verification of providers/openai.js, providers/codex.js, providers/index.js, quota/index.js and consumer references","the verdict comment and routing on #483"]},"tests":["not applicable for triage; the follow-up fix carries the test criteria (codex.test.js, providers/index.test.js, index.load.test.js, bun run check:changed)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"issue number; checked the openchamber queue (empty at Stage 1 start) and the issue''s labels (no queue/* present)","checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:10:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Decide whether #483''s stale-duplicate claim holds on current main and, if so, route the removal as a small fix.","evidence":["Issue #483 documents the duplication with file/line evidence verified on main 46f89f696 by its filer (source/creator)","openai.js (85 lines) and codex.js fetch the same wham/usage endpoint for the same aliases [''openai'',''codex'',''chatgpt'']","providers/index.js reportedly has no openai registry entry while fetchOpenaiQuota is re-exported from two barrels; no openai.test.js exists"],"acceptance":["Claims re-verified against current main or marked stale with evidence","Verdict (confirmed / not confirmed / needs info) posted on #483 with an agent note","If confirmed: a small_fix packet is enqueued in repo-health-openchamber-pilot and the issue labels mirror it"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/483","files/phase-3-rollout-plan-2026-10-26.md"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Normal fleet triage; also serves as the Phase 3 Stage 1 first live packet, exercising the Option B path end to end.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:483', '2026-10-26 13:00:00.402182+00', '2026-10-26 13:54:28.391146+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1115, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(quota): google transformModelData NaN resetTime -> use toTimestamp + tests', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/489","title":"fix(quota): google transformModelData converts an unparseable resetTime to NaN instead of null \u2014 the one quota path bypassing toTimestamp","number":489,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:08:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Other quota providers","Changes to toTimestamp or toUsageWindow semantics"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/google/transforms.js","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/google/transforms.test.js (new)"]},"tests":["New transforms.test.js covering both transforms with valid, unparseable, and missing resetTime","Existing google provider test files (index.test.js) still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Open-issue list for developing-today/openchamber checked 2026-10-26: no open or recent issue mentions google transforms, transformModelData, or a NaN resetTime; #483 covers the separate openai.js stale duplicate","checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:08:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"transformModelData in google/transforms.js converts quotaInfo.resetTime with a raw new Date(...).getTime(), producing NaN for unparseable input, while its sibling transformQuotaBucket in the same file uses the shared toTimestamp helper and returns null. The NaN flows verbatim into the usage window via toUsageWindow, poisoning in-process consumers instead of degrading to ''no reset time known''.","evidence":["Verified on main a763f5d57 by direct node import: transformModelData(''gemini-x'', {quotaInfo:{remainingFraction:0.5, resetTime:''not-a-date''}}, ''gemini'') -> windows.daily.resetAt is NaN; transformQuotaBucket with the same input -> resetAt null","transforms.js:75 is the only unguarded new Date(...).getTime() in the quota tree (grep 2026-10-26); formatters.js calculateResetAfterSeconds guards with Number.isFinite","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/google/ has no transforms.test.js; index.test.js never passes a resetTime"],"acceptance":["transformModelData returns resetAt: null for an unparseable resetTime, matching transformQuotaBucket / toTimestamp semantics","No google provider code path can emit a non-finite resetAt","New transforms.test.js (or equivalent) pins both transforms: valid ISO reset time, unparseable reset time -> null, missing quotaInfo/resetTime, scoped-name prefixing","Existing google provider tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/489","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/google/transforms.js:47","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/google/transforms.js:74-76","packages/web/server/lib/quota/utils/transformers.js (toTimestamp)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Ordinary correctness defect in one provider transform, verified with a reproduction; no security or outage impact, so priority normal (40) per the creator mapping.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:489', '2026-10-26 13:09:33.341383+00', '2026-10-27 16:30:33.099237+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1116, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): nested marks corrupt on save — triage mark-chain emit fix', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/968","title":"id(web): nested marks corrupt on save \u2014 em/strike/code inside strong/em gain &#32; entities and multiplied delimiters, several non-fixpoint","number":968,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:28:37Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["block-level conversion","other comrak extensions","the #944/#953 fixes themselves (regression-check only)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs (create_marked_text, build_mark_chain, inline emit path)"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (targeted)","new nested-mark fixpoint unit tests"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''nested emphasis strong em'' and ''entity spaces markdown'' returned no tracking issue; #944/#953 verified distinct (no nesting required, different symptoms)","checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:28:37Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"prosemirror_to_markdown emit (create_marked_text markdown.rs:1117, build_mark_chain markdown.rs:1167) mishandles adjacent text nodes with overlapping-but-different mark sets: boundary spaces are rendered by comrak as &#32; entities and emphasis delimiters multiply; re-parsing creates more mark boundaries so several inputs degrade further on every save.","evidence":["Verified probe on main aa0d6d10 (standalone crate, verbatim codec): ''**bold _em_ end**'' -> ''**bold&#32;*****em*****&#32;end**'' -> ''**bold&#32;*******em*******&#32;end**'' (non-fixpoint)","''**bold ~~strike~~ end**'' and ''[link *em* text](https://e.com)'' also non-fixpoint; ''*em **strong** end*'', ''**bold `code` end**'', ''*em `code` end*'', ''**_em_ rest**'' corrupt in one save","Parsed ProseMirror is correct in all cases (probe logs: goal hidden_files probe-2026-10-26-0815/out.log, out2.log); single-mark and ***both*** cases round-trip cleanly","Related but distinct: #944 (strong+link order oscillation), #953 (code+link drops link, code early-return markdown.rs:1122)"],"acceptance":["The 8 reproduced nested-mark inputs round-trip open->save byte-identical (modulo documented codec normalizations) and a second round-trip is a fixpoint","No &#32; or other HTML entities for ordinary spaces in emitted markdown for these inputs","New unit tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover nested-mark round-trips including the double round-trip property","Existing codec tests pass; #944/#953 cases do not regress"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/968","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1117","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1167"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent, compounding save corruption of ordinary nested-emphasis writing in user documents; emit-chain fix needs care, so triage at normal priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:968', '2026-10-26 13:29:04.742489+00', '2026-10-26 20:17:01.665822+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1118, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Triage: clean.sh leading-zero tunables read as octal in bash arithmetic (issue #881, from PRs #863/#872)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/863","title":"fix(clean.sh): INT_MAX range backstop for all validated tunables (#862)","number":863,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:36:00Z"},{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/872","title":"fix(clean): NIX_KEEP_DAYS=0 non-negative \u2014 restore scorched-earth GC (#871)","number":872,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:36:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["deletion-tool","silent-behavior-change"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/881","title":"clean.sh: leading-zero tunable values pass validation but bash arithmetic reads them as octal \u2014 010 silently means 8, 008/009 break the age gate at the multiplication sites","number":881,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:36:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["git-discover-repos / git-maintain-repos / spotlight-exclude-artifacts / opencode-db-prune.sh numeric handling (decimal-parsing consumers, verified unaffected)","unrelated clean.sh sweeps"],"include":["clean.sh validation blocks (DOCKER_AGE_DAYS, _clean_positive_vars loop, _clean_nonnegative_vars loop) and their arithmetic use sites"]},"tests":["UNKNOWN_SCRATCH_STALE_DAYS=008/009/010 with --only-unknown-scratch --dry-run in a temp HOME with the scratch root present","NIX_KEEP_DAYS=000 / NIX_KEEP_GENS=010 parse probes","INT_MAX boundary controls from the #863 matrix"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues octal (no hits) and ''leading zero'' (only closed #858/#862/#867/#871 validation-series issues, none on octal interpretation at $(( )) sites); verified live on main 8ae9483b this run","checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:36:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Validation strips leading zeros only to judge range, then hands the raw string to bash arithmetic sites (clean.sh:558, 627/634, 728, 963, 1047/1056/1057, 1123, 1193/1212, 1254/1536, 1396, 1739). Bash $(( )) treats a leading zero as octal: 010=8 (silent wrong cutoff), 008/009=arithmetic error mid-sweep with the run continuing and the age gate inert for that sweep.","evidence":["Main 8ae9483b4e112813304646257d9966299bbf4101, live probe: UNKNOWN_SCRATCH_STALE_DAYS=008 bash clean.sh --only-unknown-scratch --dry-run (temp HOME, scratch root present) -> passes validation, prints ''clean.sh: line 558: 008: value too great for base (error token is \"008\")'', continues past the section","Bash probes of the file''s exact expressions: $((030 * 86400))=2073600 (24d not 30d); $((010 * 60))=480 (8h not 10h); UNKNOWN_SCRATCH_STALE_DAYS=010 runs clean reporting ''>010d old'' while clean.sh:558 computes 8*1440","Validation sites on main: clean.sh ~260-277 (DOCKER_AGE_DAYS), ~300-315 (_clean_positive_vars loop), ~321-340 (_clean_nonnegative_vars loop, incl. NIX_KEEP_DAYS/NIX_KEEP_GENS moved by #872); [ -gt ] tests parse decimal, $(( )) parses octal \u2014 the judged form and the used form disagree","Scope check: --depth/--jobs/--pack-threads consumers (find/xargs/git) and opencode-db-prune''s SQLite interpolation all parse decimal \u2014 clean.sh is the only affected file; single-repo issue correct","Dedupe: gh search issues ''octal'' = no hits; ''leading zero'' = only closed validation-series issues (#858/#862/#867/#871), none covering octal at arithmetic sites"],"acceptance":["Leading-zero tunable forms are either rejected at parse time (existing messages, exit 2) or normalized to the judged decimal value before any use site \u2014 one consistent choice across all three validation sites","Probes pass: UNKNOWN_SCRATCH_STALE_DAYS=008/009 produce no mid-sweep ''value too great for base''; =010 computes a 10-day cutoff; NIX_KEEP_DAYS=000 still selects scorched-earth; NIX_KEEP_GENS=010 means 10 if normalization is chosen","INT_MAX backstop behavior unchanged (2147483647 ok; 2147483648 and >64-bit strings rejected at parse time)","bash -n clean.sh passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/881","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/863","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/872"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"clean.sh deletes files by age; a leading-zero value either silently shrinks the age window (010 -> 8) or disables the age gate entirely for a sweep (008/009), with no parse-time error \u2014 the validation series (#829-#872) left the judged and used forms inconsistent.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:881', '2026-10-26 13:34:38.767453+00', '2026-10-26 13:44:53.760411+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1119, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'fix(clean.sh): normalize leading-zero tunables to their judged decimal value (#881)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/863","title":"fix(clean.sh): INT_MAX range backstop for all validated tunables (#862)","number":863,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:36:00Z"},{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/872","title":"fix(clean): NIX_KEEP_DAYS=0 non-negative \u2014 restore scorched-earth GC (#871)","number":872,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:36:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["deletion-tool","silent-behavior-change"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/881","title":"clean.sh: leading-zero tunable values pass validation but bash arithmetic reads them as octal \u2014 010 silently means 8, 008/009 break the age gate at the multiplication sites","number":881,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["git-discover-repos / git-maintain-repos / spotlight-exclude-artifacts / opencode-db-prune.sh numeric handling (decimal-parsing consumers, verified unaffected)","unrelated clean.sh sweeps","rejecting leading-zero forms (decided against in triage: breaks NIX_KEEP_DAYS=000)"],"include":["clean.sh validation blocks (DOCKER_AGE_DAYS, _clean_positive_vars loop, _clean_nonnegative_vars loop): assign the judged zero-stripped decimal value back to the tunable at validation time"]},"tests":["UNKNOWN_SCRATCH_STALE_DAYS=008/009/010 with --only-unknown-scratch --dry-run in a temp HOME with the scratch root present","NIX_KEEP_DAYS=000 / NIX_KEEP_GENS=010 parse probes","INT_MAX boundary controls from the #863 matrix (2147483647 ok; 2147483648 rejected)","bash -n clean.sh"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh pr list open for dezren39/nix checked at triage: no competing PR for #881/clean.sh octal; this fix packet is the follow-up created by triage task 1118, mirroring the packet-948-fix pattern","checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Validation strips leading zeros only to judge range, then hands the raw string to bash arithmetic sites (clean.sh:558, 627/634, 728, 963, 1047/1056/1057, 1123, 1193/1212, 1254/1536, 1396, 1739). Bash $(( )) treats a leading zero as octal: 010=8 (silent wrong cutoff), 008/009=arithmetic error mid-sweep with the run continuing and the age gate inert for that sweep.","evidence":["Triage task 1118 on fresh origin/main 5e19672c09e65e9f9611db170a1de3087c5f1940 (clean.sh unchanged since 8ae9483b): HOME=<temp> UNKNOWN_SCRATCH_STALE_DAYS=008 ./clean.sh --only-unknown-scratch --dry-run passes validation, prints ''clean.sh: line 558: 008: value too great for base (error token is \"008\")'', and continues","Bash arithmetic probes: $((010 * 1440)) = 11520 (8 days, not 10); $((030 * 86400)) = 2073600 (24 days, not 30)","Validation sites on main: clean.sh 257-277 (DOCKER_AGE_DAYS), 298-316 (_clean_positive_vars loop), 322-341 (_clean_nonnegative_vars loop); each computes a zero-stripped _da/_sv only for judging and never assigns it back","Decision rationale: rejecting leading zeros would break the documented NIX_KEEP_DAYS=000 scorched-earth form restored by PR #872, whose GC branch was changed to arithmetic -eq 0 precisely so 000 selects it; normalization preserves every currently accepted input"],"acceptance":["Leading-zero tunable forms are normalized to the judged decimal value before any use site, consistently across all three validation sites (DOCKER block, _clean_positive_vars loop, _clean_nonnegative_vars loop)","Probes pass: UNKNOWN_SCRATCH_STALE_DAYS=008/009 produce no mid-sweep ''value too great for base''; =010 computes a 10-day cutoff (14400 minutes); NIX_KEEP_DAYS=000 still selects scorched-earth; NIX_KEEP_GENS=010 means 10 generations","INT_MAX backstop behavior unchanged (2147483647 ok; 2147483648 and >64-bit strings rejected at parse time, exit 2 with existing messages)","Plain (non-leading-zero) values behave exactly as before; bash -n clean.sh passes","A comment at the normalization sites explains why the judged form and the used form must agree (the #840/#858/#862 strip technique''s missing half)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/881","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/863","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/872","queue triage task 1118"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"clean.sh deletes files by age; a leading-zero value either silently shrinks the age window (010 -> 8) or disables the age gate entirely for a sweep (008/009). Confirmed reproduction and a decided, bounded fix shape from triage task 1118.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:881', '2026-10-26 13:43:16.914978+00', '2026-10-26 14:38:54.482393+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1120, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'fix(symlinker): make BACKUP undo records unambiguous so --undo restores colon-named files (#883)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["data-loss-adjacent","format-compat"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/883","title":"symlinker: --undo cannot restore backups for filenames containing a colon \u2014 BACKUP records split at the first colon and strand the original file","number":883,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:45:31Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["SYMLINK:/DELETE:/RELINK: record formats (already tab-separated)","--backup-suffix semantics","symlinker features outside the undo record format"],"include":["symlinker.sh BACKUP record writers (:1198/:1204/:1222, :439/:458/:486) and parser (:422-427)","symlinker.sh format doc comment (:122-128)","a new round-trip regression test for colon-named conflicts"]},"tests":["Round-trip probe: colon-named + plain-named conflicts in one --force run, then --undo, byte-compare restored originals","Legacy-format control: hand-written colon-format .undo file for a plain path still restores","bash -n symlinker.sh"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search ''symlinker undo colon OR symlinker BACKUP'' returned no matching issue; open-issue title scan for ''symlinker'' returned none","checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:45:31Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"BACKUP undo records are colon-separated and parsed by first-colon split (symlinker.sh:422-427), so any colon in the original or backup path corrupts the parse; the restore fails as ''backup missing'', the symlink has already been removed, and the original content remains only under the .bak.<timestamp> name.","evidence":["Verified live on main 5e19672: temp in/out dirs, in/a:b.txt (new) vs out/a:b.txt (old) plus plain.txt control; --force --no-input backed up both; --undo restored plain.txt but reported ''Backup gone: b.txt:/.../out/a:b.txt.bak.<ts> (cannot restore /.../out/a)'' and left out/ containing only a:b.txt.bak.<ts>; undo exit code 0","symlinker.sh:425-426: original=\"${rest%%:*}\" backup=\"${rest#*:}\" \u2014 first-colon split","Writers: symlinker.sh:1198, :1204, :1222 (echo \"BACKUP:$lnk:$bak\" / \"BACKUP:$orig:$bak\") and undo-of-undo :439, :458, :486","Sibling record types SYMLINK:/DELETE:/RELINK: are tab-separated (symlinker.sh:1158, :1218, :527)"],"acceptance":["A --force run over a conflict whose filename contains a colon, followed by --undo, restores the original file byte-for-byte at its original path","The BACKUP undo record format is unambiguous (e.g. tab-separated like SYMLINK/DELETE/RELINK) and the format doc comment at symlinker.sh:122-128 is updated","Undo files written by the current colon format still parse for paths without colons (existing ~/.config/symlinker/*.undo files remain usable); undo-of-undo writers emit the same new format","A round-trip regression test (colon name + plain name in one run) is added and passes; bash -n symlinker.sh passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/883"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Undo is the safety net that makes symlinker --force recoverable; for colon-named files it silently strands the user''s original file while exiting 0. Reproduced this run with a plain-name control passing in the same run.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:883', '2026-10-26 13:47:19.972468+00', '2026-10-26 14:28:40.969631+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1121, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Small fix #257: disk telemetry + reclaim step in id e2e nightly (Option A)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["ci-heavy-verification"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/257","title":"CI: nix flake check intermittently dies with ''No space left on device'' in id-test/id-ci","number":257,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:00:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["matrix-splitting the nightly (Option B)","larger runners (Option C, a spend decision)","shared target dir / footprint reduction (Option D)","PR gate workflows"],"include":[".github/workflows/id-e2e-nightly.yml (telemetry + reclaim step)"]},"tests":["one nightly or dispatch run on the fix branch with telemetry in the log","existing PR gates unaffected"],"dedupe":{"basis":"issue number; the code queue was checked 2026-10-26: task 1063 (ci_investigation) was the only task for #257","checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:00:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The nightly full flake check runs build-everything on one runner with no disk telemetry and no reclaim step, so the 2026-10-18 ENOSPC failure mode can recur silently and undiagnosably.","evidence":["Investigation 1063: last confirmed ENOSPC was 2026-10-18; zero hits across all 9 nightly runs since and sampled PR-gate runs","PR path already mitigated by #292 (fast gate + cache) and #869 (per-check matrix runners, sharded integration suite)","The nightly full check is the only remaining single-runner build-everything job (180-min cap) and its logs carry no disk telemetry"],"acceptance":["The id-e2e-nightly workflow logs df -h output before and after the flake check","A reclaim step removes preinstalled toolchains/SDKs the job never uses (the recipe in #257''s body, estimated ~20-30 GB) before the check runs","One nightly (or dispatch) run on the fix branch completes with the telemetry visible in its log and no new failures attributable to the reclaim step","No change to the PR gate workflows"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/257","investigation findings comment on #257 (2026-10-26T02:26Z, task 1063)"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The issue''s own acceptance point and the investigation''s recommended first option; small, bounded, and it makes any ENOSPC recurrence diagnosable at a glance.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:257', '2026-10-26 13:52:36.055505+00', '2026-10-26 22:33:15.850501+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1122, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'fix(symlinker): unique run ids so same-second run->undo cannot destroy the undo file (#886)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["data-loss-adjacent"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/886","title":"symlinker: same-second run\u2192undo silently does nothing and destroys the undo file \u2014 RUN_TIMESTAMP has 1-second resolution and the undo-of-undo file overwrites the source","number":886,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["BACKUP record format (that is #883)","--undo traversal validation (that is #884 / PR #885, coordinate id format with it)"],"include":["symlinker.sh run-id generation (:4) and artifact-name sites (:26, :333, :340, :706, :1140)","a no-sleep run->undo regression test"]},"tests":["Back-to-back run->undo with no sleep: conflict original restored byte-for-byte","Two runs in the same second: both .undo files intact, first still undoable","bash -n symlinker.sh"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search ''symlinker'' returned no timestamp/collision issue; found fresh this run during #884 verification","checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"One-second run ids collide across invocations: the undo run''s undo-of-undo file is the same path as the source undo file and is truncated before the source is read.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main 5e19672 code path: --force run over a conflict followed by --undo in the same second printed ''0 unlinked'', exit 0, left the symlink in place, and the <ts>.undo file afterwards contained only the undo-of-undo header lines (records destroyed)","Control with sleep 2 between run and undo restored the original correctly","symlinker.sh:4 RUN_TIMESTAMP=$(date +%s); artifact sites :26 BACKUP_SUFFIX, :333 UNDO_LOG_FILE, :340 UNDO_OF_UNDO_FILE, :706 LOG_FILE, :1140 UNDO_FILE; undo-of-undo header written at :341-346 before the record-processing loop reads $UNDO_FILE"],"acceptance":["A same-second run->undo sequence unlinks and restores exactly as a later undo does (byte-for-byte restore of the conflict original)","Two normal runs started in the same second each keep their own intact .undo file; the first run remains undoable after the second","The printed ''symlinker.sh --undo <id>'' hint and --undo argument validation (see #884) stay consistent with the chosen run-id format","A regression test performs run->undo back-to-back with no sleep and asserts the restore; bash -n symlinker.sh passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/886","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/884"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Undo silently no-ops and destroys the only recovery record exactly in the scripted back-to-back pattern; reproduced this run with a passing delayed control.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:886', '2026-10-26 13:53:39.436221+00', '2026-10-26 14:28:47.566554+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1123, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Small fix #483: remove stale duplicate quota provider openai.js', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/483","title":"fix(quota): openai.js is a stale duplicate of codex.js \u2014 same endpoint and aliases, hardcoded windows, NaN-prone reset conversion, publicly exported but unregistered and untested","number":483,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing codex.js behavior","any other quota provider","renaming fetchQuota or other public exports beyond fetchOpenaiQuota"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/openai.js","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/index.js (barrel re-export)","packages/web/server/lib/quota/index.js (barrel re-export)"]},"tests":["bun run check:changed","codex.test.js, providers/index.test.js, index.load.test.js"],"dedupe":{"basis":"issue number; triage task 1114 routed here; no existing fix task for #483 in any queue","checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Two implementations of one provider contract; the stale one is publicly exported but unregistered, untested, and missing every fix codex.js received.","evidence":["openai.js hardcodes windows[''5h'']/[''weekly''] and computes reset_at * 1000 directly (NaN for ISO strings); codex.js uses resolveWindowLabel/toTimestamp (6 helper hits) \u2014 verified on current main during triage 1114","providers/index.js has NO openai: registry entry; the module''s only use is line 518 export const fetchOpenaiQuota = openai.fetchQuota; quota/index.js:15 re-exports it","openai.test.js does not exist (404); GitHub code search finds no in-repo consumer of fetchOpenaiQuota outside the two barrels"],"acceptance":["Exactly one implementation of the ChatGPT/wham usage fetch remains: openai.js deleted with fetchOpenaiQuota removed from providers/index.js and quota/index.js barrels, OR openai.js reduced to a re-export of codex.js","bun run check:changed passes (type-check, lint, Knip dead-code at zero findings)","Existing quota tests pass: codex.test.js, providers/index.test.js, index.load.test.js","PR body states the chosen disposition and whether any out-of-repo consumer of fetchOpenaiQuota was found"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/483","triage verdict on #483 by fleet-sweep-rotating (task 1114)"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Confirmed dead duplicate with silent data-quality traps for any future importer; small, bounded, test-covered removal.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:483', '2026-10-26 13:54:11.335966+00', '2026-10-27 15:35:27.484896+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1124, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(quota): VS Code quota port NaN resetAt in google/antigravity paths (#492)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/492","title":"fix(quota): VS Code quota port converts unparseable resetTime to NaN in google and antigravity paths \u2014 the #489 defect in quotaProviders.ts","number":492,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:17:06Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The web-tree google transforms.js instance (that is #489)","Any other provider''s reset handling"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts google models path (:1318-1320) and antigravity fallback path (:1543)","A targeted regression test in the VS Code quota test files"]},"tests":["Unparseable resetTime -> resetAt null for both the google models path and the antigravity fallback path","Valid ISO resetTime -> correct epoch ms","Existing VS Code quota tests (quotaProviders.test.ts, antigravityQuota.test.ts) still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches ''quotaProviders NaN resetAt'' and ''vscode quota resetTime'' returned nothing; #489 acceptance criteria cover only the web google transforms.js","checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:17:06Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Two quota paths in the VS Code port bypass the file''s shared toTimestamp helper and emit NaN instead of null for an unparseable resetTime.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main 8711e6d56: grep -n ''new Date('' packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts shows the only unguarded .getTime() conversions at :1319 and :1543; toTimestamp defined at :418-428 and used by sibling bucket paths at :1289 and :1466","node probe: new Date(''not-a-date'').getTime() === NaN","quotaProviders.ts:1319 google models path and :1543 antigravity fallback path read verbatim this run"],"acceptance":["Both raw new Date(quotaInfo.resetTime).getTime() conversions in packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts (google models path and antigravity fallback path) use the file''s toTimestamp helper, so an unparseable resetTime yields resetAt: null","No code path in the VS Code google/antigravity quota code can emit a non-finite resetAt","A targeted test pins: unparseable resetTime -> null, valid ISO resetTime -> correct epoch ms","Existing VS Code quota tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/492","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/489"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Same verified NaN-poisoning defect as #489 on the second shipping surface; silent data corruption of the reset timestamp rather than a crash, so normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:492', '2026-10-26 14:17:32.209136+00', '2026-10-26 17:37:20.792395+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1126, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'fix(symlinker): undo-of-undo of a --force run cannot relink — RELINK processed before the BACKUP that frees the path (#889)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["data-loss-adjacent"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/889","title":"symlinker: undo-of-undo of a --force run cannot relink \u2014 RELINK records process before the BACKUP that frees the path","number":889,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:36:48Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Single-undo behavior (record formats, exit codes, run ids \u2014 #883/#886/#884 territory)","--force semantics of the undo itself"],"include":["symlinker.sh undo record-processing loop (ordering/deferral of RELINK vs BACKUP)","symlinker.test.sh round-trip regression test"]},"tests":["Full round-trip probe: --force run, undo, undo-of-undo with sleeps; assert symlink recreated, original under .bak.<run-ts>, exit 0","Existing symlinker.test.sh scenarios still pass","bash -n symlinker.sh"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search ''undo-of-undo relink'' and ''symlinker undo undo'' returned only #883/#886/#884; no ordering issue exists","checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:36:48Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Undo record processing is single-pass in file order; undo-of-undo files list RELINK before the BACKUP restore that frees the link path, so the relink always fails for --force runs and the subsequent BACKUP move completes the stranding.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main 69daf91 with sleep-separated invocations and a plain filename: run --force, undo restores ''old'' exit 0, undo-of-undo prints ''Warning: already exists, cannot relink'' + ''Completed with errors.'', out/ left containing only plain.txt.bak.<run-ts>","Identical outcome on the #883/#886 fix branch (PR #887) \u2014 pre-existing behavior, not a regression","During the first undo the SYMLINK case writes RELINK to the undo-of-undo file before the BACKUP case appends the swapped BACKUP record, so the undo-of-undo loop meets RELINK while the restored regular file still occupies the link path"],"acceptance":["run -> undo -> undo-the-undo (no --force on the undos, seconds apart) recreates the symlink pointing at the input file and leaves the original content under its .bak.<run-ts> name, exiting 0","The ordering hazard is fixed generally (BACKUP restores before RELINKs, or deferred relinks) without changing single-undo behavior","A regression test covering the full round-trip is added to symlinker.test.sh and passes; bash -n symlinker.sh passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/889","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/883","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/886"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Undo-of-undo is the documented reversal path for an undo; for every --force run it currently strands the original under .bak.<ts> with no symlink recreated, the exact data-stranding shape #883/#886 fixed for single undos.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:889', '2026-10-26 14:37:09.351374+00', '2026-10-26 16:27:49.005+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1127, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'bump vendored wrangler 4.147.0 -> 4.153.0 so Dependabot advisories become satisfiable (#848)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["supply-chain"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/848","title":"Dependabot wrangler job still red after #842: advisories unsatisfiable inside wrangler''s own pins (miniflare pins undici 7.29.1 < patched 7.30.1; sharp is a filtered subdependency)","number":848,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Dependabot/Renovate configuration changes","Lock overrides/resolutions diverging from the published package (Option 3, not recommended)"],"include":["pkgs/wrangler/default.nix (version, hash, npmDepsHash)","pkgs/wrangler/package-lock.json (regenerated)","pkgs/wrangler/package.json (refreshed stripped copy)"]},"tests":["wrangler derivation builds via PR CI nix build check (or laptop) \u2014 not realised on the sandbox","nix flake check --no-build passes","Post-merge Dependabot run for /pkgs/wrangler inspected for update-job errors"],"dedupe":{"basis":"#848 is the single tracking issue for the wrangler Dependabot residual; its status/blocked was removed 2026-10-26 when the upstream pin moved; no other wrangler-bump task exists","checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Vendored wrangler 4.147.0''s dependency tree contains advisories unsatisfiable inside its own pins (undici via miniflare); fixed upstream in wrangler 4.153.0, so the repo-side fix is the documented version bump.","evidence":["npm registry 2026-10-26 (queried singly): wrangler latest 4.153.0; its miniflare 5.20261023.0-beta; that miniflare''s dependencies.undici = 7.30.1","Repo vendors wrangler 4.147.0 (pkgs/wrangler/default.nix:52) whose tree pins undici 7.29.1 via miniflare \u2014 the unsatisfiable advisory in #848","Bump procedure documented at pkgs/wrangler/default.nix:47-49; vendored package.json strip implemented in postPatch; Renovate ignores the directory (#849) so the bump is manual-only"],"acceptance":["pkgs/wrangler vendors wrangler 4.153.0 (version, tarball hash, regenerated package-lock.json, refreshed stripped package.json, npmDepsHash) and the wrangler derivation builds (CI or laptop verification)","sharp''s version in the 4.153.0 tree is confirmed >= 0.35.5, or the remainder is recorded on #848 under Option 2","A post-merge Dependabot npm_and_yarn run for /pkgs/wrangler completes without update-job errors (or any remainder is the documented deliberate signal)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/848","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/842","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/849"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The last red Dependabot job in the repo becomes green-able: upstream now ships the patched undici inside wrangler''s own pins, and the repo is six wrangler releases behind (4.147.0 vs 4.153.0).","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:848', '2026-10-26 14:39:02.855422+00', '2026-10-26 17:40:13.639886+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1128, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(core): read decimal and compound relative quota resets (#526)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/526","title":"fix(core): relative quota resets with decimal or compound amounts are misread \u2014 \"in 1.5 hours\" ignored, \"in 1 hour 30 minutes\" read as 1 hour","number":526,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:45:34Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Absolute-time parsing in either function","resetMs duration parsing (already handles decimal/compound)","The parseQuotaReset quota-keyword gate"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts RELATIVE_TIME / resetAtFromMessage","packages/core/src/model-route-tuning.ts parseQuotaReset relative branch","Tests in packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts and packages/core/test/model-route-tuning.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-limits.test.ts test/model-route-tuning.test.ts from packages/core","Probe cases: ''in 1.5 hours'' and ''in 1 hour 30 minutes'' return now+5_400_000 from both parsers"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''quota reset decimal OR compound OR 1.5 hours OR relative'' and ''resetAtFromMessage'' returned no matching issue; #523 (closed) covered only the 45s short form","checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:45:34Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Both quota-reset message parsers accept only one integer plus one unit, so decimal amounts match nothing and compound amounts are truncated to the first unit.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main c792e04fe0 via a temporary bun test in packages/core (removed after): resetAtFromMessage(''try again in 1.5 hours'', at)=undefined; retryHintFromMessage(''retry in 1.5 hours'', at)=undefined; parseQuotaReset(''quota exhausted, back in 1.5 hours'', at)=undefined","Compound probe: resetAtFromMessage(''try again in 1 hour 30 minutes'', at)=at+3_600_000 and parseQuotaReset compound likewise, expected at+5_400_000","Control: ModelRouteLimits.resetMs(''1.5h'', at)=5_400_000 \u2014 decimal and compound durations (''6m0s'', ''1h2m3.5s'') are already accepted by resetMs in the same module","Pattern sites: model-route-limits.ts:67 RELATIVE_TIME used at :85-86; model-route-tuning.ts:170 identical inline pattern; consumers step.ts retryHintFromMessage, tuning predict :137 and noteAdjustments :211"],"acceptance":["resetAtFromMessage, retryHintFromMessage and parseQuotaReset return now + 5_400_000 for ''in 1.5 hours'' and for ''in 1 hour 30 minutes''","Existing single-unit forms unchanged (''in 45s'', ''in 45 sec'', ''in 30 minutes'', ''in 3 hours''); non-time messages still return undefined; parseQuotaReset(''try in 5 minutes'') still undefined (quota-keyword gate unchanged)","New targeted tests for decimal and compound forms in packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts and packages/core/test/model-route-tuning.test.ts pass (bun test from packages/core)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/526","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/523"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A decimal-phrased reset gets no hold at all (runner retries into an exhausted quota) and a compound phrasing is systematically short; reproduced this run with controls.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:526', '2026-10-26 14:46:45.562371+00', '2026-10-27 11:29:03.63783+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1129, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'triage: canonical order for daysOfMonth in ModelRouteSchedule.parse (#527)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/527","title":"fix(core): ModelRouteSchedule.parse does not sort daysOfMonth \u2014 canonical shape depends on input order, unlike daysOfWeek","number":527,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:47:24Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["active() matching semantics","daysOfWeek handling (already canonical)"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-schedule.ts daysOfMonth branch in parse (:207-214)","packages/core/test/model-route-schedule.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-schedule.test.ts from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search ''daysOfMonth'' returned only #522 (closed; mixed-list dropping, a different defect); no sort/canonical issue exists","checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:47:24Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"daysOfMonth is the one parsed list in ModelRouteSchedule.parse that is not normalized to a sorted canonical order, so equal windows can parse and describe differently.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main c792e04fe0 via a temporary bun test in packages/core (removed after): parse({daysOfMonth:[15,1,15]}) -> {daysOfMonth:[15,1]}; parse({daysOfWeek:[5,1,5]}) -> {daysOfWeek:[1,5]}","model-route-schedule.ts:203 daysOfWeek sorted after dedupe; :212 daysOfMonth dedupe only; header :13 promises parse normalizes to one canonical shape; describe() :293-295 prints stored order"],"acceptance":["parse({daysOfMonth:[15,1,15]}) and parse({daysOfMonth:[1,15]}) return the identical canonical value","parse({daysOfMonth:[''1'',15,-1]}) still returns {daysOfMonth:[1,15,-1]} (existing test at model-route-schedule.test.ts:14)","active() behaviour unchanged; all existing model-route-schedule tests pass plus a new out-of-order case (bun test from packages/core)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/527","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/522"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Canonicalization inconsistency only \u2014 no functional misrouting today (matching is order-insensitive); low priority, but the -1 sentinel position needs one deliberate call, hence triage rather than small_fix.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:527', '2026-10-26 14:48:14.636233+00', '2026-10-27 19:37:08.406858+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1130, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(core): allow single-digit seconds in ModelRouteSchedule.minutesOf (#528)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/528","title":"fix(core): ModelRouteSchedule.minutesOf requires exactly two second digits while hours/minutes allow one \u2014 \"9:30:5\" rejects the whole window","number":528,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:47:24Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Time range validation (hours 0-23, minutes/seconds 0-59 \u2014 already correct after #517)","normalizeTime output format (already canonical HH:mm)"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-schedule.ts minutesOf regex (:81)","packages/core/test/model-route-schedule.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-schedule.test.ts from packages/core","Probe: minutesOf(''9:30:5'')=570; parse({start:''9:30:5''})={start:''09:30''}; ''9:30:60'' still undefined"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search ''minutesOf'' returned #517 (closed; out-of-range seconds 60-99) and #522 (closed; day lists) \u2014 neither covers the seconds digit-count asymmetry","checked_at":"2026-10-26T14:47:24Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The seconds component of minutesOf requires exactly two digits while hours and minutes allow one or two, so a single-digit second makes parse reject the whole window.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main c792e04fe0 via a temporary bun test in packages/core (removed after): minutesOf(''9:5'')=545, minutesOf(''9:30:15'')=570, minutesOf(''9:30:5'')=undefined, parse({start:''9:30:5''})=undefined","model-route-schedule.ts:81 regex /^(\\d{1,2}):(\\d{1,2})(?::(\\d{2}))?$/ \u2014 seconds group is the only \\d{2}-only component; doc comment :79 lists ''9:5'' as an accepted form and notes seconds round down"],"acceptance":["minutesOf(''9:30:5'') returns 570 and parse({start:''9:30:5''}) returns {start:''09:30''}","Range checks unchanged: ''9:30:60'' and ''9:30:99'' still undefined; all existing model-route-schedule tests pass","Regression test for the single-digit-seconds form added to packages/core/test/model-route-schedule.test.ts (bun test from packages/core)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/528","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/517"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A readable friendly-form time silently drops the entire routing rule; one-regex fix with an existing targeted test file, in the same surface #517 just hardened.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:528', '2026-10-26 14:48:17.407995+00', '2026-10-27 11:30:50.421812+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1131, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'fix(id-web): html_inline passthrough — inline HTML round-trips unescaped (#943)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/943","title":"id(web): inline HTML (<sub>/<sup>/<u>/\u2026) is backslash-escaped on save \u2014 tags become literal text","number":943,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:15:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["HtmlBlock fallback behaviour","image HTML forms (#872/#880/#893)","Editor display polish for paired tags (rendering the subscript/superscript effect in-editor is a follow-on, not this fix)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs (HtmlInline arm + json_to_ast html_inline case + unit tests)","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts (richSchema html_inline node spec)"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (targeted)","new round-trip unit tests for <sub>/<sup>/<u> and one generality case (<kbd> or <span>)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1090 is the only prior task for issue 943 (dedupe repo-health:v1:triage:...:943); gh pr list search for 943/HtmlInline on 2026-10-26 returned no open PR; no fix task for 943 exists in the queue","checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:15:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"markdown_to_prosemirror converts non-img HtmlInline nodes to plain text nodes (markdown.rs:354-362 fallback), and prosemirror_to_markdown''s comrak renderer escapes text-node angle brackets, so opening and saving a markdown file rewrites every inline HTML tag as backslash-escaped literal text.","evidence":["Triage task 1090 verified 2026-10-26 on main 24261355: HtmlInline arm at markdown.rs:354-362 still falls through to text_node_with_marks(html, active_marks) for all non-img tags","git log a2eef6f7..origin/main shows zero commits touching pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs or pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts since the verified probe on a2eef6f7, so the probe results (H<sub>2</sub>O and <u>underlined</u> round-trip to backslash-escaped literal text) carry over to current main verbatim","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts richSchema (prosemirror-schema-basic + lists/tables/image) has no html node and no sub/sup/u marks \u2014 the TS schema must gain the node in the same PR or ProseMirror doc creation rejects it","Mark-based alternative rejected in triage: paired tags are sibling HtmlInline leaves in the comrak AST (not wrappers like Emph/Strong), and create_marked_text (markdown.rs:1117) returns a single wrapper-chain root and drops unknown marks; there is no comrak wrapper node that renders as <sub>/<sup>/<u>","Save-direction precedent: json_to_ast already returns NodeValue::HtmlInline(tag) for sized images at markdown.rs:1027"],"acceptance":["Markdown containing <sub>/<sup>/<u> inline HTML round-trips open->save without backslash-escaping: saved markdown still contains the tags as HTML","Generality: a non-formatting inline tag (e.g. <kbd> or <span class=\"x\">) also round-trips unescaped (full passthrough, no whitelist rejected set)","Existing img / linked-img HTML handling (#872, #880, #893) unchanged; existing web::markdown tests still pass","New unit tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover the <sub>/<sup>/<u> round-trip and the generality case","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts richSchema gains the html_inline atom node in the same PR; the html attr is never rendered via unsanitized innerHTML"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/943","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:354","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1027","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts (richSchema)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent save corruption of common note markup in the id web editor; triage (task 1090) made the representation decision, so this is a scoped implementation at normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:943', '2026-10-26 15:16:20.164055+00', '2026-10-26 20:52:08.751533+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1132, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): marked spans crossing a soft line break corrupt/fragment on save — triage softbreak mark fix', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/981","title":"id(web): marked spans crossing a soft line break corrupt or fragment on save \u2014 single-mark, non-fixpoint","number":981,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:18:56Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["block-level conversion","the #968/#944/#953 fixes themselves (regression-check / coordination only)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs (SoftBreak arm ~:238, create_marked_text :1117, build_mark_chain :1167, inline emit/parse path)"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (targeted)","new softbreak fixpoint unit tests"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Read #968 in full: its trigger is different overlapping mark sets on adjacent nodes and it states single-mark cases round-trip cleanly; no open or closed issue mentions softbreak/soft-break link fragmentation (gh search).","checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:18:56Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"markdown_to_prosemirror''s SoftBreak arm creates a standalone '' '' text node carrying the active marks; prosemirror_to_markdown emits that whitespace-only marked node as its own delimited span, producing ****&#32;****-style corruption for strong/em/strike (non-fixpoint) and fragmented [a](u)[ ](u)[b](u) output for links.","evidence":["Verified probe on main 24261355 (standalone crate, verbatim codec): ''**bold\\nmore**'' -> ''**bold****&#32;****more**'' -> ''**bold**\\*\\* \\***more**'' (non-fixpoint)","''*em\\nmore*'' and ''~~gone\\naway~~'' likewise corrupt and keep changing on the second save; ''[a\\nb](https://e.com \"T\")'' -> ''[a](https://e.com \"T\")[ ](https://e.com \"T\")[b](https://e.com \"T\")''","Parsed ProseMirror is faithful: three text nodes bold/'' ''/more all carrying the single identical mark (probe logs: goal hidden_files probe-2026-10-26-1015/out2.log)","Distinct from #968: that issue requires different overlapping mark sets and states single-mark cases are fine; #944/#953 are mark-order/code-return defects without softbreaks"],"acceptance":["''**bold\\nmore**'', ''*em\\nmore*'', ''~~gone\\naway~~'' round-trip to the normalized single-line form with no &#32; and no multiplied delimiters; second round-trip is a fixpoint","''[a\\nb](url)'' with and without title round-trips as one link","New unit tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover softbreak-crossing marked spans including the double round-trip property","Existing codec tests pass; #944/#953/#968 cases do not regress"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/981","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/968","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:238","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1117"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent, compounding save corruption of ordinary wrapped bold/italic/linked prose in user documents; fix locus spans parse and emit sides, so triage at normal priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:981', '2026-10-26 15:19:16.994925+00', '2026-10-26 20:48:47.722718+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1133, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): HTML blocks rewritten as ```html code blocks on save — triage faithful-preservation design', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/982","title":"id(web): HTML blocks (comments, <details>, <div>) are rewritten as ```html code blocks on save","number":982,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:19:40Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["inline HTML handling (#943)","other block types","editor UI rendering of HTML blocks"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs (HtmlBlock arm :329-352, code_block emit arm :872, PM schema attrs for code_block)"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (targeted)","new HTML-block round-trip unit tests"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search ''html block'' (state all) returned no codec HTML-block tracking issue; #943 covers inline HTML escaping only, verified by reading its title/scope.","checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:19:40Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"NodeValue::HtmlBlock parse arm converts non-img HTML blocks to code_block{params:html}; json_to_ast''s code_block arm always emits a fenced NodeCodeBlock, so HTML comments become visible code fences and <details> blocks are destroyed on any save.","evidence":["Verified probe on main 24261355 (standalone crate, verbatim codec): ''<!-- note: draft -->\\n\\ntext\\n'' -> ''```html\\n<!-- note: draft -->\\n```\\n\\ntext\\n''","''<details>\\n<summary>More</summary>\\n\\nbody\\n</details>\\n'' -> two separate ```html fences with ''body'' stranded as a plain paragraph between them","Code: markdown.rs:341-352 parse fallback (''Convert HTML blocks to code blocks (safe fallback)''); markdown.rs:872 emit arm has no params=html special case (probe logs: goal hidden_files probe-2026-10-26-1015/out.log, out2.log)","Ambiguity: an authored ```html fence parses to the identical PM shape (code_block, params html), so naive raw-HTML emission would corrupt authored fences \u2014 design decision required"],"acceptance":["A design distinguishing converted HTML blocks from authored ```html fences (or otherwise preserving both) is chosen and recorded on the issue","''<!-- comment -->'', ''<details>...</details>'', and a bare ''<div>'' block round-trip byte-identical; second round-trip is a fixpoint","A user-authored ```html fenced block still round-trips as a fenced code block","New unit tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover HTML-block round-trips; existing codec tests pass; sized/linked <img> HTML handling (#893) does not regress"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/982","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/943","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:329","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:872"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Any save vandalizes files containing HTML comments or <details> blocks \u2014 common in notes/READMEs; fix needs a small design decision first, so triage at normal priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:982', '2026-10-26 15:19:59.270919+00', '2026-10-26 20:26:39.51099+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1134, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage: cold-store curl fallback puts R2 secret in argv (issue #983, from PR #976)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/976","title":"fix(cold-store-reaper): curl fallback for S3 downloads urllib cannot deliver","number":976,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:30:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["credential-exposure"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/983","title":"security(cold-store-reaper): PR #976''s curl S3 fallback passes the R2 secret in argv \u2014 the pattern #948/#970 removed the same day","number":983,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["push-fleet-feed.sh (already fixed by #970)","the urllib S3 path (env-only credentials, in-process signing)"],"include":["pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py _curl_fetch / _s3_get_via_curl and its tests"]},"tests":["TestS3CurlFallback suite in pkgs/cold-store-reaper/tests/test_cold_store.py","argv inspection asserting neither credential value appears in any argv element"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list searches for ''curl fallback'' and ''R2 secret argv'' returned no matching issue (only unrelated #681); the argv pattern on current main was read directly from origin/main d715adf9","checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"cold-store-reaper''s S3 curl fallback (PR #976) spawns curl with --user <access>:<secret> in argv; scrubbing error text does not address process-list exposure.","evidence":["origin/main d715adf9 pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py _curl_fetch (~1526-1545): argv includes ''--user'', f\"{access}:{secret}\"; docstring: ''Credentials travel in argv \u2014 the local process list sees them''","PR #976 commit 14617a5958 introduced _curl_fetch / _s3_get_via_curl; S3_CURL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 900 bounds the exposure window","PR #970 (merged ~1h before #976) for issue #948 removed the socat proxyauth argv credential from push-fleet-feed.sh and added push-fleet-feed.guard.sh: ''proxy credential must never be an argv token'' \u2014 that guard covers only that script"],"acceptance":["The R2 access key / secret never appear in any spawned process''s argv on the curl fallback path (test stubs subprocess.run or inspects spawned argv)","Existing TestS3CurlFallback coverage passes, updated for the new credential channel: fallback only after urllib exhaustion, byte-count verified, errors scrubbed","Consider a guard in the spirit of push-fleet-feed.guard.sh covering cold_store.py"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/983","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/976","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/970","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/948"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A live bucket credential is exposed to any local process via argv for the duration of large-object downloads, reintroducing a pattern the repo had just removed and guarded elsewhere the same day.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:983', '2026-10-26 15:33:34.175699+00', '2026-10-26 16:03:27.98989+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1135, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage: D1 manifest schema lacks ''evicted'' CHECK from PR #971 (issue #984)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/971","title":"feat(cold-store-reaper): v4 \u2014 R2 S3 client, backup-supabase, eviction","number":971,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:30:00Z"},{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/965","title":"cold-store-reaper v3: backup retention (prune-backups), get-backup, backup-d1, nightly + drill scripts","number":965,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:30:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["schema-drift","nightly-pipeline"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/984","title":"cold-store-reaper: D1 manifest schema still lacks the v1.2 ''evicted'' CHECK \u2014 first evict --apply will break nightly sync-manifest (follow-up left by PRs #965/#971)","number":984,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["evict --apply itself (no eviction run is requested)","local manifest migrations (already implemented and tested)"],"include":["D1 cold-store-manifest schema CHECK constraints","schema.sql / README caveat text","sync-manifest verification"]},"tests":["sync-manifest against a manifest containing an ''evicted'' object row and a ''trash'' ledger row"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list searches for ''cold-store evicted D1'', ''sync-manifest'', and ''cold-store D1 schema'' returned no matching issue (only unrelated #963 pack-dup and #910); grep of backlog-devtoday-code.md for ''evicted'' returned nothing","checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Local manifest schema v1.2 (''evicted'', PR #971) and v1.1 (''trash'', PR #965) CHECK extensions have no tracked D1-side application; sync-manifest fails once such rows exist.","evidence":["origin/main d715adf9 pkgs/cold-store-reaper/schema.sql:3-5: ''The D1 copy of this schema needs the same one-line CHECK change before evicted rows can sync; sync-manifest fails on the objects statement''","origin/main README.md:256-261 repeats the caveat and notes v1.1 ''trash'' had the same pattern (PR #965)","nightly-backup.sh on main runs prune-backups --apply then sync-manifest under set -euo pipefail (step 4); no evict step yet, so no ''evicted'' rows exist until the first evict --apply"],"acceptance":["D1 cold-store-manifest objects CHECK accepts ''evicted''; transfer_ledger.direction confirmed to accept ''trash''","sync-manifest verified against a manifest containing an ''evicted'' row and a ''trash'' ledger row","schema.sql / README caveat updated to record the applied state, or a repeatable migration step added to the repo"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/984","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/971","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/965"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A documented but untracked prerequisite: the first eviction will break manifest sync in the nightly at the moment the hosted manifest matters most; cheap to close before any evict --apply runs.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:984', '2026-10-26 15:33:37.227139+00', '2026-10-26 16:35:14.321786+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1136, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'triage: route governance wildcard/expired target-set divergence design (#530)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/530","title":"fix(core): route governance judges a wildcard target''s literal pattern \u2014 expanded models escape the check, and expired/disabled targets are still judged (PR #512)","number":530,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:34:18Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Variant filtering of concrete targets (#519)","Route selection/weights/health behaviour in the plugin"],"include":["packages/core/src/session/model-governance.ts routeTargets/assertAllowed target set","packages/core/src/config/plugin/model-routes.ts expansion output (read-only reference or shared helper)","packages/core/test/session/model-governance.test.ts regression tests"]},"tests":["bun test test/session/model-governance.test.ts from packages/core (design stage: existing tests only; implementation stage adds the #530 regression tests)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches ''wildcard route target governance'' and ''routeTargets'' returned only #519 (variant filtering, distinct) and closed #506 (variant remaps)","checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:34:18Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Governance and runtime disagree on the set of models a route target represents: governance judges the literal pattern ref (and expired/disabled targets); the runtime runs the expanded, filtered set.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main c792e04fe0: ConfigModel.ModelID pattern (packages/schema/src/config/model.ts:11) allows * in target model ids; route tuning docs use deepseek/* and openai/gpt-6-* as targets (packages/schema/src/config/model-routes.ts:152)","Plugin: model-routes.ts:262 matchingModels expansion, :261 expired-target skip, :263 disabled-model skip; governance routeTargets builds one literal ref per target and never reads until/enabled"],"acceptance":["Design decision recorded on issue #530: how governance obtains the expanded/filtered target set (plugin output vs catalog expansion in routeTargets)","Follow-up implementation task enqueued (or the fix implemented directly if small) with the issue''s regression tests specified","Existing route-governance tests (#506/#512 variants, plain targets) noted as must-still-pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/530","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/519"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Excluded-model bypass: a governed child can be routed to an excluded model via a wildcard route target because governance judges the literal pattern instead of the expanded models.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:530', '2026-10-26 15:34:24.367381+00', '2026-10-26 16:54:12.336688+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1137, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(quota): shared timestamp helpers leak non-finite values (#494)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/494","title":"fix(quota): shared toTimestamp/normalizeTimestamp leak Infinity and NaN instead of null","number":494,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["VS Code quotaProviders.ts (that is #492)","Web google transforms.js raw conversion (that is #489)","Deciding negative-timestamp policy beyond noting it"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/utils/transformers.js toTimestamp and normalizeTimestamp","A new targeted test file for transformers.js in the same directory"]},"tests":["Non-finite numeric inputs -> null for both helpers","Finite seconds/ms and valid string behaviour unchanged","Existing quota utils/provider tests still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches ''toTimestamp OR normalizeTimestamp OR Infinity timestamp'' returned only #489/#492/#483, none covering the shared web transformers.js helpers","checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Shared quota timestamp helpers return Infinity/NaN for non-finite numeric inputs instead of null, breaking the null contract their string path and toNumber maintain.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main 8711e6d56: node probe importing transformers.js directly gave toTimestamp(Infinity)=Infinity, toTimestamp(-Infinity)=-Infinity, normalizeTimestamp(NaN)=NaN, normalizeTimestamp(Infinity)=Infinity, while toTimestamp(''garbage'')=null","transformers.js:16-26 toTimestamp numeric path, :28-31 normalizeTimestamp, :5-14 toNumber finite guard","Callers: zai.js:194,211 and zhipuai-coding-plan.js:158,173 (nextResetTime), claude/auth.js:52,89 (expiry), ~20 providers use toTimestamp for resetAt"],"acceptance":["toTimestamp returns null for NaN, Infinity, -Infinity numeric inputs","normalizeTimestamp returns null for NaN, Infinity, -Infinity","Finite behaviour unchanged: seconds scaled to ms below 1e12, ms passthrough, valid strings parsed, null/undefined -> null","New unit tests for both helpers cover the non-finite cases","Existing quota tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/494","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/489","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/492"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Shared helpers under ~20 quota providers; silent non-finite resetAt/expiry values rather than a crash, so normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:494', '2026-10-26 15:45:00.032864+00', '2026-10-26 23:51:55.957449+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1138, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'triage(quota): Cursor windowSeconds is time-until-reset, not duration (#495)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/495","title":"fix(quota): Cursor provider reports time-until-reset as windowSeconds, not the window duration","number":495,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:47:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Any change to resetAt/resetAfterSeconds","Other providers'' windowSeconds"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cursor.js buildWindows and buildEnterpriseWindows","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cursor.test.js"]},"tests":["Triage records the confirmed semantics and chosen fix direction on the issue"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search ''cursor windowSeconds OR cursor billing_cycle OR window duration'' returned no tracking issue; cursor.test.js never asserts windowSeconds","checked_at":"2026-10-26T15:47:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Cursor quota windows report time-until-reset in the windowSeconds field that every consumer reads as window duration.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main 8711e6d56: cursor.js:220 and :290 both compute windowSeconds = Math.max(0, Math.floor((resetAt - Date.now())/1000))","grep ''resetAt - Date.now'' across quota providers matches only those two Cursor lines","usageHeadline.ts:57-75 picks the shortest windowSeconds as the headline and treats duration-less rows as last resort; copilot.js passes windowSeconds: null for its monthly window"],"acceptance":["Triage confirms Cursor is the only provider deriving windowSeconds from resetAt - Date.now (cursor.js:220, :290)","A fix direction is recorded on the issue: true cycle duration from billingCycleStart/billingCycleEnd when both known, otherwise null","A follow-up small_fix task is enqueued for the chosen fix, or the issue is updated explaining a different verified conclusion"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/495"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Wrong window semantics distort the usage headline ranking for Cursor users near cycle end; silent misreporting, not a crash, so normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:495', '2026-10-26 15:48:10.840749+00', '2026-10-26 17:40:58.069973+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1139, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Fix: cold-store curl fallback must not put R2 secret in argv (issue #983)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/976","title":"fix(cold-store-reaper): curl fallback for S3 downloads urllib cannot deliver","number":976,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:02:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["credential-exposure"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/983","title":"security(cold-store-reaper): PR #976''s curl S3 fallback passes the R2 secret in argv \u2014 the pattern #948/#970 removed the same day","number":983,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:02:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["push-fleet-feed.sh (already fixed by #970)","the urllib S3 path (env-only credentials, in-process signing)"],"include":["pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py _curl_fetch / _s3_get_via_curl and its tests"]},"tests":["TestS3CurlFallback suite in pkgs/cold-store-reaper/tests/test_cold_store.py","argv inspection asserting neither credential value appears in any argv element"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up to triage task 1134 for the same issue 983; dedupe family ''fix'' is distinct from the completed ''triage'' task for this issue; no existing fix task for 983 was in the queue at triage time","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:02:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"cold-store-reaper''s S3 curl fallback spawns curl with --user <access>:<secret> in argv; the secret is visible in the local process list for up to 900s per fallback download.","evidence":["Triage task 1134 (2026-10-26): fresh origin/main d715adf9 pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py _curl_fetch lines 1526-1545 argv includes ''--user'', f\"{access}:{secret}\"; docstring admits credentials travel in argv; S3_CURL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900 at line 83","Triage verified locally (curl 8.5.0, loopback HTTP server): config supplied on stdin via curl --config - is honoured (credential sent as auth, never in argv or on disk)","TestS3CurlFallback (tests/test_cold_store.py line 1267) stubs at the _curl_fetch seam; no test inspects spawned subprocess.run argv"],"acceptance":["The R2 access key / secret never appear in any spawned process''s argv on the curl fallback path (test stubs subprocess.run and inspects argv)","Credential reaches curl via stdin config (--config - with input=...), with correct escaping of the config value","Existing TestS3CurlFallback coverage passes, updated for the new channel: fallback only after urllib exhaustion, byte-count verified, errors scrubbed, one attempt only","Consider a guard in the spirit of push-fleet-feed.guard.sh covering cold_store.py"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/983","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/976","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/970","queue triage task 1134"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A live bucket credential is exposed to any local process via argv for the duration of large-object downloads, reintroducing a pattern the repo had just removed and guarded elsewhere the same day.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:983', '2026-10-26 16:03:05.733461+00', '2026-10-26 16:11:33.974879+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1140, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'fix(opencode-db): escape --db SQLite URI in prune+vacuum; vacuum fails loudly on unopenable DB (#890)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/890","title":"opencode-db prune/vacuum: --db paths with ?, # or % open through an unescaped SQLite URI \u2014 prune misreports a schema change, vacuum silently succeeds","number":890,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:15:26Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Restore-mode $FROM handling (already escaped via sql_uri_literal)","SQL-literal quoting of --into/--backup paths (separate issue)"],"include":["Every file:${DB} URI construction in opencode-db-prune.sh and opencode-db-vacuum.sh","Vacuum measuring-step error handling"]},"tests":["Scratch DBs in dirs containing ?, #, %: --dry-run both scripts, expect real measurements / clean exit","Normal-path dry-runs unchanged","bash opencode-db-pids.test.sh; bash -n both scripts"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches ''opencode-db-vacuum'', ''URI OR escaping OR quote'', ''vacuum OR prune OR opencode-db in:title'' returned only closed pids/guard issues (#828/#465/#461/#467/#472) and unrelated items; no URI-escaping issue exists","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:15:26Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Unescaped interpolation of $DB into SQLite file: URIs in both scripts; vacuum additionally never checks that its measuring query succeeded.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main 5124cee: valid scratch prune.db in a q?mark directory -> prune dies ''event_sequence has no aggregate_id column -- schema changed'' after sqlite ''unable to open database file''; identical DB on a normal path exits 0 ''Nothing eligible''","Vacuum --dry-run on q?mark/opencode.db: sqlite unable to open, all measurements blank, line 233 ''[: : integer expression expected'', then ''--dry-run: stopping here'' with exit 0","opencode-db-prune.sh:375-377 sql_uri_literal escapes %, ?, #, '' but is used only for $FROM at line 485; all $DB opens are raw file:${DB}?mode=ro; vacuum has no helper (lines 212, 308, 313, 314)"],"acceptance":["Both scripts open --db paths containing ?, #, and % correctly (dry-run, real measurements)","Vacuum exits non-zero with a clear message when sqlite3 cannot open/read the database","Scratch DBs under directories containing ?, #, % pass --dry-run in both scripts; normal-path behavior unchanged","opencode-db-pids.test.sh and bash -n on both scripts pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/890"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"These scripts are the recovery path for a runaway opencode database; a path character silently turning vacuum into a successful no-op (or prune into a false schema alarm) undermines trust in exactly the tool Drew runs when disk is on fire.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:890', '2026-10-26 16:16:21.555987+00', '2026-10-26 17:27:11.093804+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1141, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'fix(opencode-db): escape single quotes in VACUUM INTO / .backup path literals (#891)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/891","title":"opencode-db vacuum/prune: single quote in --into/--backup path breaks VACUUM INTO / .backup SQL literal","number":891,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:16:42Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["--db URI escaping (tracked as #890)","RESTORE_SESSION interpolation (already charset-validated)"],"include":["opencode-db-vacuum.sh VACUUM INTO site","opencode-db-prune.sh .backup site"]},"tests":["Vacuum probe: --into path containing a single quote succeeds, output is a valid SQLite DB at that exact path","Prune probe: --backup path containing a single quote succeeds in an --apply run on a scratch DB","Normal-path runs unchanged; bash -n both scripts"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches ''opencode-db-vacuum'' and ''URI OR escaping OR quote'' returned no SQL-literal quoting issue for these scripts (#721/#709/#731 are flake-tidy name quoting, closed, different code)","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:16:42Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Two SQL-literal interpolation sites do not escape single quotes in user-supplied / DB-derived output paths.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main 5124cee: vacuum --db normal/quote.db --into quo''te/compact.db -y -> ''Error: in prepare, near \"te\": syntax error'' at VACUUM INTO, exit 1, nothing written, after integrity check and WAL checkpoint already ran","opencode-db-prune.sh:870 sqlite3 \"$DB\" \".backup ''$BACKUP''\" is the identical unescaped construction in the --apply path","sql_uri_literal (prune :375-377) already doubles single quotes but is never applied to either site; RESTORE_SESSION is charset-validated at :393 and is not affected"],"acceptance":["--into/--backup paths containing a single quote work end to end in both scripts and produce valid SQLite files at exactly the requested path","Unquoted paths behave exactly as before","bash -n passes on both scripts; opencode-db-pids.test.sh passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/891","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/890"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"--into/--backup exist to point the DB recovery scripts at other volumes; an apostrophe in a volume or folder name kills the run mid-flight with a misleading sqlite syntax error.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:891', '2026-10-26 16:17:01.407718+00', '2026-10-26 17:27:16.102556+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1142, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'fix(opencode-db-vacuum): guard swap against overwriting an existing .old backup (#892)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["data-loss-adjacent"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/892","title":"opencode-db-vacuum: swap silently overwrites an existing ${DB}.old backup \u2014 the only rollback copy","number":892,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:18:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Prune''s backup handling (already guarded)","Backup retention/pruning policy (#659 territory)"],"include":["opencode-db-vacuum.sh preflight/swap ${DB}.old handling"]},"tests":["Sentinel probe: seed ${DB}.old, run vacuum -y on scratch DB, assert sentinel intact or pre-swap refusal","No-.old run unchanged; --no-backup run unchanged","bash -n opencode-db-vacuum.sh; bash opencode-db-pids.test.sh"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches ''opencode-db-vacuum'' and ''old backup overwrite vacuum'' returned only #659 (different: old backups never pruned from disk) and closed guard issues; no .old-overwrite issue exists","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:18:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Swap step mv has no existence check on ${DB}.old, unlike every other overwrite hazard in these two scripts.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-26 on main 5124cee: seeded ''PREVIOUS-BACKUP-SENTINEL'' swap.db.old, ran vacuum -y on a scratch DB; run completed exit 0 reporting ''backup: swap.db.old'', and file(1) afterwards shows swap.db.old is a SQLite database \u2014 the sentinel was silently replaced","Same script refuses to overwrite an existing $COMPACT target; opencode-db-prune.sh:862 refuses to overwrite an existing $BACKUP \u2014 the .old swap is the unguarded outlier"],"acceptance":["A pre-existing ${DB}.old is never silently replaced: sentinel probe survives or the run refuses before swapping","The check runs before any swap mutation (preflight, next to the $COMPACT check)","No pre-existing .old: behavior unchanged, including --no-backup","bash -n opencode-db-vacuum.sh and opencode-db-pids.test.sh pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/892"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"${DB}.old is the sole rollback copy after a vacuum swap; a routine second run destroys it silently, exactly when the user may need it because the first compacted database misbehaved.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:892', '2026-10-26 16:17:41.489762+00', '2026-10-26 17:27:21.836388+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1143, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Small fix: cold-store-reaper D1 caveat text is stale — ''evicted''/''trash'' CHECKs verified already applied to D1 (issue #984 follow-up)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["docs-only"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/984","title":"cold-store-reaper: D1 manifest schema still lacks the v1.2 ''evicted'' CHECK \u2014 first evict --apply will break nightly sync-manifest (follow-up left by PRs #965/#971)","number":984,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any D1 change (already applied and verified)","any schema.sql CHECK definition change (the local definitions are already correct)","evict --apply runs"],"include":["pkgs/cold-store-reaper/schema.sql caveat comments (v1.2 objects and v1.1 transfer_ledger)","pkgs/cold-store-reaper/README.md ''evicted'' caveat paragraph"]},"tests":["pkgs/cold-store-reaper targeted test suite"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up created by triage task 1135 for issue #984; the caveat-text fix is the only remaining acceptance item of #984 after D1 verification","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Triage task 1135 verified 2026-10-26 that the hosted D1 cold-store-manifest schema ALREADY accepts ''evicted'' (objects.state CHECK) and ''trash'' (transfer_ledger.direction CHECK) \u2014 a real sync-manifest run with an ''evicted'' object row and a ''trash'' ledger row succeeded against live D1 and the probe rows were read back, then removed. But pkgs/cold-store-reaper/schema.sql (lines 3-6 and the v1.1 comment above transfer_ledger) and README.md (the ''evicted'' caveat paragraph and the sync section) still say the D1 copy ''needs the same one-line CHECK change'' \u2014 stale text that will send a future operator to re-apply a change that is already live.","evidence":["D1 sqlite_master for objects (queried 2026-10-26 via Cloudflare API, day-to-day token): CHECK (state IN (''hot'',''staging'',''cold'',''rehydrating'',''gone'',''evicted''))","D1 sqlite_master for transfer_ledger: CHECK (direction IN (''upload'',''download'',''trash'')); D1 already holds 2 real ''trash'' ledger rows synced earlier","Probe sync 2026-10-26: temp manifest copy + probe object state=''evicted'' (hash 50e7928a\u2026) + probe ledger row direction=''trash'' kind=''evict'' \u2192 cold-store sync-manifest sent 6 statements / 45 rows, exit 0; probe rows read back from D1, then deleted; D1 restored to 14 ''cold'' objects","origin/main e3467560 pkgs/cold-store-reaper/schema.sql:3-6 still contains the unapplied-caveat wording; README.md evict section repeats it"],"acceptance":["schema.sql and README caveat text updated to record that the D1 CHECK changes (v1.1 ''trash'', v1.2 ''evicted'') were verified applied to the hosted cold-store-manifest D1 on 2026-10-26 (queue task 1135), with the sync-manifest probe evidence","No functional code or CHECK definition changes; docs/comments only","cold-store-reaper targeted tests still pass (python tests in pkgs/cold-store-reaper/tests)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/984"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Stale ''not applied'' warnings for an already-applied hosted schema change mislead the next operator and could cause a needless or wrong D1 rebuild; docs-only, cheap to close.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:984', '2026-10-26 16:34:00.065972+00', '2026-10-26 21:07:05.190632+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1144, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Small fix: preserve footnotes in id web markdown codec — enable footnote extension + footnote node arms (issue #945 follow-up)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/945","title":"id(web): footnotes are backslash-escaped on save \u2014 [^1] syntax mangled, definition orphaned","number":945,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["rendering footnotes in the web UI beyond preserving the markdown","frontend ProseMirror schema changes (if the editor frontend drops unknown node types, name that limitation in the PR per the issue acceptance criteria; the codec round-trip is the deliverable)","other comrak extensions not currently enabled"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs: enable options.extension.footnote in commonmark_options","Parse direction: FootnoteReference -> PM inline node type ''footnote_reference'' with attrs {label}; FootnoteDefinition -> PM block node type ''footnote_definition'' with attrs {label} and the definition''s inline content as children (mirrors the existing image node''s attrs pattern)","Save direction (json_to_ast): arms mapping ''footnote_reference''/''footnote_definition'' back to NodeValue::FootnoteReference/FootnoteDefinition","New round-trip unit tests in markdown.rs"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (CI or laptop)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up created by triage task 1092 for issue #945; gh search for ''footnote'' on 2026-10-25 returned no other issues in developing-today/code","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Footnotes in markdown files are mangled on save in the id web editor: comrak''s footnote extension is never enabled in commonmark_options (pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs), so [^label] references/definitions parse as plain text and comrak''s CommonMark formatter escapes them to literal \\[^label\\] on save. Enabling the extension alone is insufficient: convert_node''s FootnoteDefinition|FootnoteReference arm returns json!(null), dropping them. Triage task 1092 (2026-10-26) confirmed both facts on main e1f0121c and chose the preservation representation below.","evidence":["main e1f0121c pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs commonmark_options (~line 67): enables strikethrough/tasklist/table only; footnote extension off","main e1f0121c markdown.rs ~line 488: NodeValue::FootnoteDefinition(_) | NodeValue::FootnoteReference(_) => json!(null) with comment ''Footnotes not supported - skip''","Save direction prosemirror_to_markdown: json_to_ast -> comrak format_commonmark with the SAME commonmark_options(), so enabling the extension makes the formatter render real Footnote* AST nodes as [^label] natively","Filer probe on main a2eef6f7 (verbatim codec): ''Text with a note.[^1]'' + ''[^1]: The footnote body.'' round-trips to escaped ''Text with a note.\\[^1\\]\\n\\n\\[^1\\]: The footnote body.''"],"acceptance":["A markdown file with a footnote reference + definition round-trips open->save with the footnote intact: emitted as [^label] / [^label]: ... \u2014 not backslash-escaped, not deleted","Re-opening the saved file and saving again yields byte-identical output (stable fixpoint)","New unit tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover the footnote round-trip (reference + definition, multiple footnotes)","No regression to existing codec tests or the strikethrough/tasklist/table extensions (targeted cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown on CI or laptop, not a sandbox build)","Any representation limitation (e.g. frontend schema tolerance for the new node types) is named in the PR body"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/945"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent save corruption of valid markdown: every save of a footnoted file escapes its footnotes into literal text and orphans the definitions.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:945', '2026-10-26 16:44:05.868543+00', '2026-10-26 21:52:26.963783+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1145, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(core): accept zero-padded weekday strings in ModelRouteSchedule.parse (#531)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/531","title":"fix(core): ModelRouteSchedule.parse rejects zero-padded weekday strings","number":531,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:44:20Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["daysOfMonth ordering (#527)","minutesOf seconds digits (#528)"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-schedule.ts dayOfWeek","packages/core/test/model-route-schedule.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-schedule.test.ts from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list/search for parseQuotaReset, zero-padded, daysOfWeek returned only #526/#523/#527/#528; none covers zero-padded weekday strings","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:44:20Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Zero-padded weekday numeric strings (''06'',''00'') are unreadable to dayOfWeek while zero-padded month days parse fine, so parse rejects the whole window.","evidence":["Probe on main c792e04fe0 (temporary bun script in packages/core, removed after): parse({daysOfWeek:[''06'']})=undefined; parse({daysOfWeek:[''6'']})={daysOfWeek:[6]}; parse({daysOfMonth:[''01'']})={daysOfMonth:[1]}","model-route-schedule.ts:63 /^[0-6]$/ single-digit test vs :71 /^-?\\d+$/ for daysOfMonth"],"acceptance":["parse({daysOfWeek:[''06'']}) returns {daysOfWeek:[6]} and [''00''] returns [0]","parse({daysOfWeek:[''07'']}) and [''42''] still return undefined (whole window rejected)","Existing forms unchanged: names, ''6'', trimmed strings, mixed-list rejection","bun test test/model-route-schedule.test.ts from packages/core passes with new zero-padded cases"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/531","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/527","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/528"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Unambiguous friendly spelling silently drops an entire routing window; narrow, reproduced, low-risk fix.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:531', '2026-10-26 16:45:00.96431+00', '2026-10-27 15:31:48.638592+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1146, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(core): unify absolute-time keywords across the two quota-reset parsers (#532)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/532","title":"fix(core): the two quota-reset message parsers disagree on absolute-time keywords","number":532,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:48:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Relative-time forms (#526)","parseQuotaReset quota-keyword gate semantics"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts ABSOLUTE_TIME","packages/core/src/model-route-tuning.ts parseQuotaReset absolute branch","Tests in packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts and model-route-tuning.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-limits.test.ts test/model-route-tuning.test.ts from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues parseQuotaReset returned only #526 (open, relative decimal/compound) and #523 (closed, relative short form); no issue covers absolute-keyword divergence","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:48:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Two parsers for provider reset messages accept disjoint absolute-time keyword sets, so results depend on the import door.","evidence":["Probe on main c792e04fe0 (temporary bun script, removed after): tuning=undefined/limits=date for expires, retry, wait until, try again; tuning=date/limits=undefined for available; both=date for resets control","Keyword sites: model-route-tuning.ts:162-166 vs model-route-limits.ts:65-66; production consumers use limits parser (tuning.ts:137, :211; step.ts:141)"],"acceptance":["Both parsers return the same instant for expires at / retry at / wait until / try again at / available at / resets at messages","parseQuotaReset quota-keyword gate unchanged (non-quota messages still undefined)","Existing tests in model-route-limits.test.ts and model-route-tuning.test.ts pass plus new paired keyword cases","bun test test/model-route-limits.test.ts test/model-route-tuning.test.ts from packages/core passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/532","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/526","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/523"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Same provider message honoured or ignored depending on which exported parser a caller imports; drift pattern already produced #523/#526 in the relative branch.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:532', '2026-10-26 16:46:14.596289+00', '2026-10-27 15:40:43.98404+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1147, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(core): scan past an unparseable first date to a later valid quota reset (#533)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/533","title":"fix(core): an unparseable first date shadows a later valid reset time in both quota-reset parsers","number":533,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:50:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Relative-time forms (#526)","Absolute keyword sets (#532) \u2014 coordinate only"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts resetAtFromMessage","packages/core/src/model-route-tuning.ts parseQuotaReset","Tests in packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts and model-route-tuning.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-limits.test.ts test/model-route-tuning.test.ts from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues parseQuotaReset returned only #526/#523; neither covers first-invalid-absolute shadowing; probe verified this run","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:50:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Single-exec absolute parsing aborts on the first unparseable date instead of scanning for the next valid candidate.","evidence":["Probe on main c792e04fe0 (temporary bun script, removed after): both parsers undefined for invalid-first messages, correct date for control","Sites: model-route-limits.ts:80-84, model-route-tuning.ts:162-169; consumers tuning.ts:137/:211, step.ts:141 via retryHintFromMessage"],"acceptance":["Both parsers return 2026-01-02T00:00:00Z for ''quota reset at 2026-13-01, back at 2026-01-02T00:00:00Z'' and for the ''not-a-date'' probe","Message with only an invalid absolute date still returns undefined from the absolute branch; relative behaviour unchanged","parseQuotaReset quota-keyword gate unchanged","bun test test/model-route-limits.test.ts test/model-route-tuning.test.ts from packages/core passes with new cases"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/533","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/532","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/526"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A stated valid reset is silently dropped, so the runner retries immediately into an exhausted quota instead of holding.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:533', '2026-10-26 16:47:32.196811+00', '2026-10-27 15:30:58.046419+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1148, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'fix(ci): flake-inputs-update supersedes an open update PR in place instead of stacking a duplicate (#946)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/946","title":"ci(flake-inputs-update): no dedupe for an already-open update PR \u2014 consecutive runs stack duplicate PRs for the same pins","number":946,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#913 failure-issue lookup","#917/#918 excerpt fix","The merge/auto-merge/handoff logic after publish (unchanged, only its PR-number source changes)","PR #974 itself \u2014 do not close or edit it as part of the fix; it is the live test fixture for the scenario"],"include":[".github/workflows/flake-inputs-update.yml publish step only"]},"tests":["Workflow syntax check (actionlint/yamllint if available, else python yaml parse)","Dry-run reasoning over three scenarios: no open PR (create as today), open PR with older revs (in-place update, no second PR), open PR with same revs (skip publish)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1095 is the only prior task for issue 946 (dedupe repo-health:v1:triage:...:946); no fix task for 946 exists in the queue; gh pr list on 2026-10-26 shows no open PR fixing the workflow dedupe (#974 is the automation''s own output PR, not a fix)","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"flake-inputs-update''s publish step creates a unique branch and a new PR on every successful changed-pins run without checking for an already-open automation update PR; the handoff path leaves validated PRs open, so consecutive runs stack duplicates and superseded PRs are never closed or updated.","evidence":["Main 69fb652541da16abd5e49940928eb26bdc593dd6, .github/workflows/flake-inputs-update.yml: branch=\"automation/flake-inputs-update-$(date -u +%Y%m%d)-${GITHUB_RUN_ID}\" (~line 218); unconditional pr_url=$(gh pr create ...) at line 238; grep of the whole workflow shows gh pr create/merge/comment/view but NO gh pr list","The handoff path in the same step (lines ~245-264, from PR #914) deliberately leaves a validated PR open for a privileged merge when the workflow token cannot merge \u2014 that open PR is what the next run duplicates","Live instance 2026-10-26: PR #974 OPEN, head automation/flake-inputs-update-20261026-40339534295, title revs openchamber 8711e6d56a4e / opencode c792e04fe054; the next successful changed-pins run would open a second PR for newer revs and nothing would close or update #974","Prior automation PR #912 (20261025 run) merged \u2014 stacking only occurs while a handoff PR waits, which is exactly the protected-main norm for this workflow token"],"acceptance":["A publish run executed while an automation/flake-inputs-update-* PR is open (e.g. handoff PR #974) produces NO second PR: the open PR''s branch, title and body are updated to the new revs in place","Same-revs run: publish is skipped with a clear log line naming the reused PR","Fallback path: if in-place update is impossible, the stale PR is closed with a comment naming the replacement PR before/while the new PR is created \u2014 never two open automation update PRs at once","Merge / auto-merge / handoff behaviour after publish is unchanged and operates on the reused-or-new PR number","Workflow YAML remains valid (actionlint or yamllint clean, or python yaml parse)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/946",".github/workflows/flake-inputs-update.yml publish step (branch ~line 218, gh pr create ~line 238 on main 69fb6525)","Open handoff PR #974 \u2014 the live example of the stacking scenario"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Duplicate automation PRs are a standing consolidation burden and one is live right now (#974 handoff); triage (task 1095) confirmed the bug on current main and decided the in-place supersede design, so this is a scoped workflow-only implementation.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:946', '2026-10-26 16:52:40.088294+00', '2026-10-26 21:13:51.980402+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1149, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(core): route governance expands wildcard targets via shared expansion and drops expired/disabled targets (#530)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/530","title":"fix(core): route governance judges a wildcard target''s literal pattern \u2014 expanded models escape the check, and expired/disabled targets are still judged (PR #512)","number":530,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:50:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Closing #519 (variant filtering of concrete non-route targets) \u2014 note the overlap in the PR, do not claim its closure","Route selection/weights/health/schedule behaviour in the plugin","Changing the existing missing/empty-route fallback in assertAllowed"],"include":["Extract expand/matchingModels/targetSpec from packages/core/src/config/plugin/model-routes.ts into a shared core module consumed by both the plugin and governance (no behaviour change to the plugin)","packages/core/src/session/model-governance.ts: routeTargets target set via shared expansion (wildcard expansion, until expiry drop, disabled drop); effective-variant judging per leaf preserved","assertAllowed catalog plumbing at packages/core/src/session.ts and packages/core/src/session/session.ts call sites (initialized-location catalog only)","packages/core/test/session/model-governance.test.ts regression tests (a)-(e) from the task body"]},"tests":["bun test test/session/model-governance.test.ts from packages/core \u2014 all 22 pre-existing tests plus the new #530 regression tests pass","bun test for the model-routes plugin tests from packages/core \u2014 unchanged pass after the shared-module extraction","bun typecheck from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up enqueued by triage task 1136 per its acceptance criteria; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:530 is distinct from the triage key; gh PR search for 530/routeTargets on 2026-10-26 returned no competing PR","checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:50:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Governance judges the literal wildcard pattern ref and expired/disabled targets; the runtime runs the expanded, filtered set \u2014 an excluded-model bypass plus over-deny for dropped targets.","evidence":["Triage task 1136 design decision on issue #530 (2026-10-26): shared expansion module + catalog dependency for assertAllowed; plugin expand at packages/core/src/config/plugin/model-routes.ts (until skip :261, matchingModels :262, disabled skip :263); governance routeTargets at packages/core/src/session/model-governance.ts builds one literal ref per target and never reads until/enabled","assertAllowed call sites supply only config entries today: packages/core/src/session.ts governanceEntries / assertModelAllowed and packages/core/src/session/session.ts:136,160 \u2014 no provider catalog is available to governance, which is why a catalog dependency must be added rather than governance reading the plugin''s transformed provider output","Baseline on main c792e04fe0: bun test test/session/model-governance.test.ts from packages/core = 22 pass, 0 fail"],"acceptance":["A wildcard target whose expansion includes an excluded model denies the route; a wildcard expanding only to allowed models passes; a wildcard expanding outside the allowed list denies","An expired (until passed) or disabled target does not by itself deny or fail the route","Existing route governance tests (#506/#512 variant tests, plain targets) still pass; plugin expansion behaviour unchanged (single shared implementation)","PR references issue #530 and notes the #519 overlap without closing #519"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/530","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/519"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Excluded-model bypass: a governed child can be routed to an excluded model via a wildcard route target because governance judges the literal pattern instead of the expanded models.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:530', '2026-10-26 16:52:43.588859+00', '2026-10-27 11:10:38.670924+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1150, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'fix(ci): bound flake-inputs-update failure-issue history so the tracking issue never hits GitHub''s body limit (#947)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/947","title":"ci(flake-inputs-update): failure-issue history grows unbounded \u2014 the tracking issue will exceed GitHub''s body limit and stop updating","number":947,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:08:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#913 failure-issue lookup cap (separate issue, its own fix)","#917 excerpt truncation direction (already fixed by PR #918)","The publish/merge/handoff steps of the workflow (the #946 fix, task 1148, owns that region)"],"include":[".github/workflows/flake-inputs-update.yml ''Record the failure on the tracking issue'' step only"]},"tests":["Simulate the body build from synthetic max-size history (30 entries x 5,000-char excerpts) and assert the assembled body stays under 60,000 chars with header fields intact","Workflow syntax check (actionlint/yamllint if available, else python yaml parse)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1096 is the only prior task for issue 947 (dedupe repo-health:v1:triage:...:947); no fix task for 947 exists in the queue; #913 (lookup cap) and #917 (excerpt direction, closed) are distinct defects in the same workflow and are excluded from scope","checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:08:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Each failed flake-inputs-update attempt re-emits the entire prior failure history plus a new ~5,300-char entry with no trimming anywhere, so after roughly a dozen worst-case failures the tracking issue body exceeds GitHub''s 65,536-char limit, gh issue edit is rejected, and the issue silently stops updating.","evidence":["Main 69fb652541da16abd5e49940928eb26bdc593dd6, flake-inputs-update.yml: awk ''/^## Failure history/{found=1; next} found'' extracts the whole prior history into history_file; the body builder cats history_file verbatim followed by the new entry; no size check follows","Excerpt per attempt: grep -v ''copying path'' | tail -n 80 | sed fence-neutralize | tail -c 5000 (line 171) \u2014 ~5,000 chars plus entry header lines (~300) gives ~5,300 chars per worst-case entry","Worst-case arithmetic: header block ~600 chars; (65,536 - 600) / 5,300 \u2248 12.2 \u2014 the ~13th consecutive failed attempt makes gh issue edit reject the body, and every later attempt fails the same way, freezing the tracking issue","Grep of the full workflow for trim/budget/65536/head -c/MAX on main 69fb6525 returns only the line-171 excerpt cap \u2014 no history bound exists","Attempts and First failure are parsed from the old body''s header lines (^Attempts: / ^First failure:), not from the history section, so trimming history cannot corrupt them if the header format is preserved"],"acceptance":["History in the tracking issue body is bounded: at most 10 entries and at most 30,000 chars of history, oldest dropped first, with a visible trimmed-count marker line","Attempts / First failure / Last failure header fields remain accurate after trimming (they parse from the header block, whose format is unchanged)","Simulated body built from 30 synthetic max-size attempts stays under 65,536 chars (target: under the 60,000-char safety threshold after the final drop-oldest pass)","gh issue edit with the simulated body would succeed (size is the only blocker being removed); workflow YAML remains valid (actionlint/yamllint or python yaml parse)","Excerpt behaviour unchanged: 5,000-char tail cap and ~~~ fence neutralization from #917 stay intact"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/947",".github/workflows/flake-inputs-update.yml failure-issue step (~lines 145-210 on main 69fb6525): awk history extract ~line 166, excerpt cap line 171, verbatim re-emit ~lines 196-198","Queue task 1148 (#946) \u2014 same file, publish step; disjoint region, coordinate merge order"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The failure issue is the workflow''s only durable failure signal and it breaks exactly when failure becomes chronic (~13 worst-case attempts); triage (task 1096) confirmed the unbounded growth on current main and decided the bound, so this is a scoped workflow-only implementation.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:947', '2026-10-26 16:55:05.721353+00', '2026-10-26 21:12:03.036132+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1151, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'fix(aggregator): deepen isOrchestrationSection to per-goal fields so a malformed goal cannot crash /today (#949)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/949","title":"fix(aggregator): isOrchestrationSection validates only the top level \u2014 a malformed goal crashes /today instead of falling back","number":949,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Orchestration section schema redesign beyond the fields the consumer dereferences","Consumer-side rewrites of todayFromSection (validator deepening is the decided fix; trivial ?? [] hardening is acceptable but not required)","isFleetFeed validation of other sections"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/feed.ts (isOrchestrationSection per-goal + provenance checks)","pm-stack/aggregator/test/orchestration.test.ts (nested regression cases)"]},"tests":["bun test in pm-stack/aggregator \u2014 existing orchestration.test.ts plus new nested cases","Manual repro from triage: the malformed section used in task 1098 must now fail validation and deriveToday must return the derived view"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1098 is the only prior task for issue 949 (dedupe repo-health:v1:triage:...:949); no fix task for 949 exists in the queue and no open PR touches isOrchestrationSection","checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"isOrchestrationSection validates only the section''s top level, so a goal missing linedUp/stalled/gaps passes validation; todayFromSection then dereferences those fields and throws TypeError, crashing /today instead of using the derived fallback the design intends for malformed sections.","evidence":["Reproduced 2026-10-26 on fresh main 69fb652541da16abd5e49940928eb26bdc593dd6 with bun: malformed section (goal omitting linedUp/stalled/gaps/progressedSinceLastRun, section omitting provenance) \u2014 isOrchestrationSection returned true; todayFromSection threw TypeError: undefined is not an object (evaluating ''g.linedUp.filter'')","feed.ts isOrchestrationSection checks only version/generatedAt/runId, tiers arrays, and dependencies/goals/actions being arrays \u2014 it never inspects individual goals and never checks provenance, although model.ts OrchestrationSection requires provenance: string and GoalMeasurement requires linedUp/progressedSinceLastRun/stalled/gaps","derive.ts todayFromSection dereferences g.linedUp.filter (objectives), g.stalled.filter and g.linedUp.flatMap (momentum), and spreads ...g.gaps \u2014 all throw on undefined; g.progressedSinceLastRun goes through asStringList, which tolerates string/array/missing","Every entry path gates on this one validator: collector scripts/collect-fleet-feed.ts:328 embeds only on pass; live source src/sources/live.ts:587,791 serves only on pass; deriveToday(board, rows, items, section) uses the derived fallback when section is null \u2014 so deepening the validator restores the designed fallback on all paths","Existing tests (test/orchestration.test.ts:47-61) cover only top-level rejections (non-object, version, missing tiers/goals) \u2014 no nested-goal case exists"],"acceptance":["isOrchestrationSection returns false for a goal missing linedUp, stalled, or gaps (one regression test per field, mirroring orchestration.test.ts style)","isOrchestrationSection returns false for a section missing provenance, and true for progressedSinceLastRun in single-string form (the asStringList-normalized shape)","todayFromSection never throws on any section the deepened validator accepts; /today and /api/today.json fall back to the derived view for the malformed sections above","Existing orchestration.test.ts cases still pass (well-formed section accepted, top-level rejections unchanged)","Full aggregator test suite passes (bun test in pm-stack/aggregator)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/949","pm-stack/aggregator/src/feed.ts isOrchestrationSection (~line 63 on main 69fb6525)","pm-stack/aggregator/src/derive.ts todayFromSection: g.linedUp.filter, g.stalled.filter / g.linedUp.flatMap, ...g.gaps; asStringList string-form normalization note","Gate call sites: pm-stack/aggregator/scripts/collect-fleet-feed.ts:328, pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/live.ts:587 and :791"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A single malformed orchestrator output 500s /today and /api/today.json instead of falling back to the derived view \u2014 the fail-soft design is defeated by one shallow validator. Triage (task 1098) reproduced the crash on current main and decided the fix layer, so this is a scoped validator+tests implementation.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:949', '2026-10-26 16:57:50.049647+00', '2026-10-26 21:24:08.212795+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1152, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Verify antigravity-ls baseURL at laptop respawn: serve opencode version vs #232 fallback fix (#951 follow-up)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["cross-repo","needs-laptop-respawn"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/951","title":"antigravity-ls resolves to an empty port in the laptop OpenChamber serve despite ANTIGRAVITY_LS_PROXY_PORT being set (PR #921''s unfixed half, openchamber-side)","number":951,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:12:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing the .opencode/opencode.jsonc template to a literal port","re-fixing the commandcode half (already fixed by #921)"],"include":["laptop OpenChamber serve: opencode version + effective antigravity-ls baseURL capture at respawn","updating the serve''s opencode / openchamber pin if it predates dc72b96651"]},"tests":["manual verification at laptop respawn; record serve opencode version and effective baseURL on issue #951"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up created by triage task 1100; dedupe_key is distinct from the parent triage task (issue:951:respawn-verify) and no other task covers the respawn capture","checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:12:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Triage task 1100 (2026-10-26) identified the root-cause class: a config parser without opencode #232 (dc72b96651, 2026-10-21) treats the whole token ANTIGRAVITY_LS_PROXY_PORT:-18745 as one variable name and substitutes empty, producing http://127.0.0.1:/v1 regardless of the env var. Code side verified correct (.opencode/opencode.jsonc:2109 template; home/common/default.nix:1437 exports the var). Remaining step is live: confirm the laptop serve''s opencode version and effective baseURL at respawn.","evidence":["Issue #951 triage findings comment by queue task 1100 (2026-10-26T17:12Z): code side verified, parser-version root-cause class identified","opencode packages/core/src/config/variable.ts on main supports {env:VAR:-fallback}; landed in dc72b96651 (PR #232, 2026-10-21) with URL-shaped tests in packages/core/test/config/config.test.ts","PR #921 body: antigravity-ls resolved to empty port despite ANTIGRAVITY_LS_PROXY_PORT=18745 in the serving process environ"],"acceptance":["Serve opencode version and effective antigravity-ls baseURL recorded on issue #951 with environ confirmed","If serve predates dc72b96651: serve updated and baseURL re-captured showing 127.0.0.1:18745 (or the env value)","If serve is current and port still empty: openchamber-side investigation filed with the version evidence"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/951","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/921"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The provider stays silently broken until the serve''s parser version is confirmed against the #232 fix; only a laptop respawn can capture it.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:maintenance:developing-today/code:respawn-verify:2026-W44', '2026-10-26 17:08:48.75428+00', '2026-10-26 22:28:00.310329+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1153, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): empty-text links silently deleted on save — triage link representation', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/996","title":"id(web): empty-text links are silently deleted on save \u2014 href lost","number":996,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:12:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["editor schema changes unless the triage shows they are required (report back if so)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs Link arm ~:299 and inline collection / emit path"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (all states) for ''empty link'', ''autolink'', ''task_list'' returned no matching codec issue; #953/#981 are different mechanisms (non-empty text).","checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:12:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Parse-side Link arm (markdown.rs:299) represents links only as marks on child text nodes; an empty-text link has no children, so the mark and href vanish and save emits nothing.","evidence":["Probe main 14dd66b6 verbatim codec: ''[](https://e.com)'' -> PM {paragraph, no content} -> OUT ''''","''before [](https://e.com) after'' -> OUT ''before  after'' (double space, no link)","Linked image with empty alt survives (''[![](img.png)](https://e.com)'' round-trips) \u2014 images are nodes, links are marks only"],"acceptance":["Empty link alone and mid-paragraph round-trip with href/title preserved, or a documented non-silent alternative; result is a fixpoint","Unit tests: empty link alone, mid-paragraph, with title","Existing codec tests pass; #953/#981 link cases do not regress"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/996","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:299"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent, unrecoverable URL loss on an ordinary save; representation choice needed so triage, normal priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:996', '2026-10-26 17:18:34.666807+00', '2026-10-26 22:36:01.544559+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1154, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): ordered task lists lose ordering on save — triage task_list order representation', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/997","title":"id(web): ordered task lists lose their ordering on save \u2014 rewritten as bullet task lists","number":997,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["plain ordered/bullet list behaviour (already correct)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs List arm ~:205-220, task_list json_to_ast arm ~:946, editor schema check in pkgs/id/web"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (all states) for ''ordered task'' / ''task_list'' returned no matching issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Parse discards Ordered/start for task lists; save hardcodes a bullet list for task_list, so ordered checklists silently become unordered on save.","evidence":["Probe main 14dd66b6: ''1. [ ] todo / 2. [x] done'' -> PM task_list with no order -> OUT ''- [ ] todo / - [x] done''","''5. [ ] five / 6. [x] six'' -> bullets; start 5 lost","Controls in same probe: plain ordered list preserves order:3; plain bullet task list round-trips"],"acceptance":["Ordered task lists round-trip ordered, preserving start >1","PM shape is representable in pkgs/id/web editor schema (checked and noted)","Mixed task+plain list (test_task_list_mixed_content) does not regress; unit tests for start 1 and >1"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/997","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:205","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:946"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent loss of sequence/start information in sequenced checklists on an ordinary save; representation choice needed so triage, normal priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:997', '2026-10-26 17:19:52.052352+00', '2026-10-26 23:19:44.684046+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1155, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): bare URLs/emails never become links — triage enabling comrak autolink', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/998","title":"id(web): bare URLs and emails never become links \u2014 comrak autolink extension not enabled in the markdown codec","number":998,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:24:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["editor typing/autocomplete behaviour"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs commonmark_options :67-76 and codec tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (all states) for ''autolink'' returned no issues.","checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:24:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Autolink extension off: bare URLs/emails load as dead text in the editor, invisible to all link-mark features.","evidence":["markdown.rs:70-72 enables strikethrough/tasklist/table only","Probe main 14dd66b6: bare URL and email inputs produce single plain text nodes; angle-autolink control produces a link mark and round-trips"],"acceptance":["Bare URL/email parse to link marks over exactly the URL/email; round-trip fixpoint","URLs in code spans/blocks stay unlinked; trailing-punctuation boundary test","Unit tests added; existing codec tests pass \u2014 or deliberate-off rationale recorded and issue closed"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/998","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:67"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Dead (unclickable) links for documents authored elsewhere; no data loss, so low priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:998', '2026-10-26 17:20:52.115513+00', '2026-10-27 04:56:20.500413+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1156, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'triage: aarch64-darwin node_modules hash stale after PR #488 (#499)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/488","title":"fix(nix): make the node_modules FOD tree deterministic across builders","number":488,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:35:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/499","title":"fix(nix): PR #488 changed the node_modules FOD tree on all systems but only rebaked x86_64-linux \u2014 aarch64-darwin pin now stale","number":499,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The aarch64-linux pin (already tracked in #275)","Any change to the .bin-stripping determinism logic itself"],"include":["nix/hashes.json aarch64-darwin entry","Verification build on an aarch64-darwin builder"]},"tests":["nix build .#openchamber.node_modules on aarch64-darwin reports the hash mismatch (verification) or passes (refutation)","After any pin update, a clean nix build .#openchamber on aarch64-darwin passes the FOD check"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches ''488 darwin'', ''aarch64-darwin stale'' and ''node_modules hash'' returned only #275 (Linux pins only; its 2026-10-26 intake comment confirms the aarch64-linux remainder and never mentions darwin), #422 and #449 (closed, x86_64 class)","checked_at":"2026-10-26T17:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #488 changed the fixed-output derivation''s output tree on all systems but re-measured only x86_64-linux, leaving the previously-working aarch64-darwin hash pin stale.","evidence":["PR #488 diff: nix/hashes.json changes only the x86_64-linux line; aarch64-darwin stays sha256-2TrjBeUL2y50CzQ/QPOB8O91wkGYKptqB3x8KJn6BVU=","git show origin/main:nix/package.nix: install phase strips $out/node_modules/.bun .bin dirs unconditionally (find -mindepth 3 -maxdepth 3 -name .bin -exec rm -rf), no platform guard","git show origin/main:nix/hashes.json still carries the pre-#488 aarch64-darwin value","PR #491 body/diff: competing fix exempted Darwin \u2014 ''its pin was measured on a Mac and reproduces there, and the variance has only been observed on Linux''","Issue #275 evidence: after PR #269 ''the darwin build works'' \u2014 the darwin pin was live, not stale, before #488","Post-#488 opencode-update failures (#490) fail at bun run test, past the nix build \u2014 the rebaked x86_64-linux pin verifies in CI"],"acceptance":["Mismatch verified or refuted with evidence: on an aarch64-darwin builder, building .#openchamber.node_modules on current main either fails with a fixed-output hash mismatch against the pinned aarch64-darwin value, or (if it passes) the issue is closed with the build evidence","If verified, nix/hashes.json aarch64-darwin entry is updated to the hash measured from the post-#488 tree and a clean darwin build passes the FOD check","x86_64-linux entry unchanged; aarch64-linux remainder left with #275"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/499","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/488","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/491","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/275"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A supported platform''s clean build (aarch64-darwin / macOS app flake) is broken by a merged change and no CI exercises that platform, so the breakage is silent; high priority, but verification requires a darwin builder so this is triage first, not a small fix.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'blocked', 20, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:499', '2026-10-26 17:31:51.169159+00', '2026-10-26 17:35:54.575586+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=ex