ys flatMaps dropping unmapped entries; toggleWeekday rebuilds daysOfWeek from windowWeekdays only","git show origin/main:packages/ui/src/lib/routing/routeSchedules.ts confirms the same code on current main","PR #502 test pins it: windowWeekdays({daysOfWeek:[''monday'',''tues'',5,''Mon'',9]}) -> [1,2,5]","developing-today/opencode packages/core/src/model-route-schedule.ts dayOfWeek: trims, lowercases, accepts numeric strings /^[0-6]$/ \u2014 ''Mon'' and ''5'' are valid","Same PR''s readScheduleList design: unreadable entries kept as stored so a save writes them back unchanged and the server names the problem; server validateScheduleWindow refuses bad day entries by name"],"acceptance":["Silent-drop verified or refuted with evidence: on current main, toggleWeekday over a window with daysOfWeek [''Mon'',''fri'',9] either loses the unmapped entries (verified) or preserves/refuses them (refuted, close with evidence)","If verified, a fix makes a toggle unable to silently remove a stored entry: window treated unreadable/read-only, unmapped entries preserved verbatim, or save refused naming the entry","Editor reads OpenCode-valid day forms correctly: case-insensitive names, whitespace, numeric strings","Regression tests cover the mixed-list toggle and the valid-form mapping; existing pinned dropping test updated"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/514","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/502"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent config data loss in a merged editor: a routine Settings toggle can remove days a live schedule applies on, with no error or record; normal priority because it requires a stored non-canonical day form plus a toggle to trigger.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:514', '2026-10-27 01:30:16.541195+00', '2026-10-27 11:02:40.427392+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload,