ontent-Length"],"acceptance":["New streaming Content-Length regression test in bin/design-code-proxy.test.mjs: backend SSE response carries a stale/short Content-Length; client still receives the full rewritten stream including the [DONE] event","Ablation check: removing writeHead''s streaming delete headers[''content-length''] makes the new test FAIL; restoring it makes the whole suite pass","Existing 6 tests still pass (node --test bin/design-code-proxy.test.mjs)","No proxy behaviour change expected \u2014 test/stub only, unless the test exposes a real bug, in which case fix it and say so in the PR"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/688","bin/design-code-proxy.mjs writeHead (~:257-271)","bin/design-code-proxy.test.mjs stub (~:44-75)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A verified untested data-truncation guard: if the streaming Content-Length deletion regresses, SSE clients silently truncate and no test notices (triage 1067 ablation proved it).","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:688', '2026-10-27 02:43:17.817089+00', '2026-10-27 03:12:02.132804+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1229, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): prosemirror_to_markdown panics on misplaced nodes — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1043","title":"id(web): prosemirror_to_markdown panics on misplaced nodes \u2014 json_to_ast never validates block/inline placement","number":1043,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T02:51:30Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1017 table-cell special case (fixed)","comrak upstream changes","editor.ts schema changes unless triage decides coercion needs them"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs json_to_ast placement validation and codec tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (all states) for panic/ill-formed/inline/prosemirror_to_markdown returned no matching issue; #1017 is the table-cell special case of the same class, already fixed \u2014 this is the general placement-validation gap.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T02:51:30Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"json_to_ast places any known node type anywhere; misplaced nodes yield an ill-formed AST that panics (debug) or corrupts output (release).","evidence":["Probe on main cf60812d (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-26-2145/out4.log): t_text_top, t_image_top, t_hardbreak_top, t_para_in_para each panicked at comrak-0.56.0/src/cm.rs:29","Panic message: ''The document to format is ill-formed: InvalidChildType { parent: <Document>, child: <Text(orphan) }''; comrak validation is #[cfg(debug_assertions)] so release builds emit invalid output silently","Controls in out3.log: unknown node type returns Err(UnknownType), heading level 9 clamps to 6, empty doc returns Ok"],"acceptance":["prosemirror_to_markdown never panics and never emits an ill-formed AST for: inline node at doc level (text/image/hard_break), block node insid