 2026-10-27."],"acceptance":["Triage note posted on the issue with decomposition / routing decision","Follow-up implementation packets enqueued for each actionable slice, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1343","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1334 (epic)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries queue/queued as its work order with priority label priority/normal; the safety net enqueues so the work order is never ownerless.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1343', '2026-10-27 07:25:09.112543+00', '2026-10-28 04:09:30.176948+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1329, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1347: footnote docs open empty in web editor — codec node types missing from richSchema (PR #1013)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1013","title":"fix(id-web): preserve footnotes in markdown codec (#945)","number":1013}],"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["data-loss-on-open","editor-only"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1347","title":"id(web): footnote documents open as an empty doc in the web editor \u2014 footnote_reference/footnote_definition missing from richSchema (PR #1013)","number":1347,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T07:28:52Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Rust codec footnote behavior (already fixed by #1013/#1031)","No changes to other node types"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts footnote node specs","editor/codec boundary tests for footnote documents"]},"tests":["Node.fromJSON(richSchema, footnote doc JSON) does not throw","editor open->save round-trip fixpoint for a footnote document"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open+closed issues for footnote/editor/schema, footnote_reference; only #945 and #1031 (both codec-only, closed) match.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T07:28:52Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Markdown codec emits footnote_reference (markdown.rs:545) and footnote_definition (markdown.rs:558) PM node types, but richSchema in pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts defines neither; Node.fromJSON throws and initEditor replaces the whole document with an empty doc on open.","evidence":["PR #1013 merge commit 554dc370b7083c433b5f71b0b7eaa57badcbbdb2","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:545 footnote_reference, :558 footnote_definition (current main)","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts richSchema append block defines html_inline (:216, from PR #1009) but grep for footnote returns nothing (current main)","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts initEditor: Node.fromJSON in try/catch, catch falls back to empty doc"],"acceptance":["richSchema defines footnote_reference and footnote_definition mirroring the html_inline pattern, with inert toDOM rendering","Footnote document opens in web editor with full content, no parse fallback","Open->save round-trip through the editor preserves footnote reference and definition byte-identically","A test covers a footnote doc through Node.fromJSON(richSchema, ...)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1013","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/945"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Opening a footnote document in the web editor silently shows an empty doc; a save could persist the empty doc over the real file. High but not critical: only footnote-bearing files are affected.","timebox_minutes":60}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1347', '2026-10-27 07:31:38.260233+00', '2026-10-27 10:48:17.592161+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1330, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1348: spaced-destination placeholder collision rewrites document text on save (PR #1022)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1022","title":"fix(id-web): preserve spaced link/image destinations in angle form on save (#1019)","number":1022}],"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["rare-literal-collision","codec-only"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1348","title":"id(web): spaced-destination placeholder can collide with document text \u2014 global replace on save rewrites the document''s own words (PR #1022)","number":1348,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T07:28:52Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["No change to the angle-form preservation behavior itself (#1019)","No editor.ts changes"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs substitute_spaced_destinations and its restoration loop","codec tests for placeholder collision"]},"tests":["cargo test for markdown codec spaced-destination suite plus a new collision regression test"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open+closed issues for spaced destination placeholder / placeholder link destination; only #1019 (the %20 bug, closed) matches.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T07:28:52Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Placeholder tokens are derived only from the substitution index with no check against document content, and restoration replaces every occurrence in the rendered output (markdown.rs:1070-1072), so a document containing the literal token gets its own text rewritten on save.","evidence":["PR #1022 merge commit 76672b97df023607d8469d462f21420604fe92d5","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1100-1103 placeholder format idweb-spaced-destination-{}-placeholder (current main)","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1070-1072 output.replace(&placeholder, ...) global restoration (current main)","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1081 substitute_spaced_destinations performs no scan of existing document text"],"acceptance":["Placeholder tokens cannot collide with content already in the document, or restoration is scoped to rendered destination positions","Regression test: document containing the literal token plus a spaced destination round-trips with literal text unchanged","Existing #1019 spaced-destination tests still pass; round-trips remain fixpoints"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1022","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1019"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Deterministic but requires the document to literally contain the fixed placeholder token; corruption is real but the trigger is uncommon. Low priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1348', '2026-10-27 07:31:46.756965+00', '2026-10-27 07:31:46.756965+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1331, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(ui): NoteEditor first-render decorations race the syntax parser (#534)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/534","title":"fix(ui): NoteEditor formatted view is racy on first render \u2014 tail of the note shows raw backticks and list dashes (flaky test, real first-render bug)","number":534,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T07:45:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing what Markdown is stored or how the active (cursor) line behaves","Other CodeMirror editors (CodeMirrorEditor.tsx already forces parsing)"],"include":["packages/ui/src/components/session/project-context/NoteEditor.tsx decoration building / livePreview plugin","packages/ui/src/components/session/project-context/NoteEditor.test.tsx only if a determinism helper is needed"]},"tests":["bun test packages/ui/src/components/session/project-context/NoteEditor.test.tsx (20 consecutive runs)","bun run check:changed"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list -R developing-today/openchamber --state all searches for ''NoteEditor'' and ''backtick formatted'' returned no covering issue (only closed unrelated #330, whose CI hit this flake)","checked_at":"2026-10-27T07:45:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Live-preview decorations are built from a partially parsed syntax tree and never rebuilt when parsing completes, so first render can show raw Markdown markers on the tail of a note.","evidence":["Targeted runs on main efdd08b70: batch 1 = 1 fail/5, batch 2 = 4 fails/8; failure at NoteEditor.test.tsx:57, Received: \"Release\u2022 push the tag- check `changelog`\"","NoteEditor.tsx:82 buildDecorations iterates syntaxTree(state) (tree parsed so far); livePreview plugin rebuilds only on docChanged/viewportChanged/selectionSet/focusChanged","In-repo contrast: CodeMirrorEditor.tsx calls forceParsing at lines 461/518/594; documentSymbols.ts:93 uses ensureSyntaxTree","PR #533 CI tests job failed on this same test while its diff was i18n dictionaries only (recorded in backlog-devtoday-openchamber.md)"],"acceptance":["NoteEditor.test.tsx passes 20 consecutive targeted runs (bun test packages/ui/src/components/session/project-context/NoteEditor.test.tsx)","First render is fully formatted with no user interaction: no backticks, no ''##''/''**'', list items show bullets","Second test still passes: the cursor''s line shows its markers and stored text is untouched Markdown","bun run check:changed passes for the changed files (no new lint/type/anti-slop findings)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/534"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Real first-render product bug in the note editor plus a recurring CI flake that already burned an unrelated PR''s run; normal priority.","timebox_minutes":15}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:534', '2026-10-27 07:47:50.960751+00', '2026-10-27 15:46:46.945139+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1332, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'test(settings): extend settings-search anchor coverage to all pages (#535)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/535","title":"test(settings): settings-search anchor coverage stops at the routing page \u2014 250 of 259 entries unchecked, 7 resolve only dynamically","number":535,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Production behavior changes (unless coverage exposes a genuinely missing anchor \u2014 file separately)","Exempting/allow-listing the 7 dynamic ids without deriving them from source"],"include":["packages/ui/src/lib/settings/search.test.ts anchor coverage","Reading (not necessarily changing) the dynamic anchor sources: ThirdPartyIntegrationsSection.tsx, CatalogExtensionsSection.tsx, SettingsView.tsx, thirdPartyPlugins.ts, catalogExtensions.ts"]},"tests":["bun test packages/ui/src/lib/settings/search.test.ts"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list -R developing-today/openchamber --state all search ''settings search anchors'' returned only closed #325 (routing-only fix) and unrelated #329; no open issue covers the remaining pages","checked_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Settings-search anchor existence is only tested for the routing page; 250 entries, including 7 dynamically-constructed anchors, have no coverage.","evidence":["search.test.ts:196 test extracts only /id: ''([^'']+)'', page: ''routing''/ ids \u2014 9 ids","search.ts entry counts by page: chat 50, general 40, sessions 23, appearance 19, messaging 16, integrations 15, projects 13, agents 11, routing 9, others \u2014 259 total","Literal-scan replication over all ids (this run): exactly 7 missing \u2014 magic-prompts.visible-prompt, magic-prompts.instructions, shortcuts.keyboard-shortcuts, integrations.third-party.opencode-claude, integrations.extensions.excalidraw, integrations.extensions.resource-monitor, extensions.gitIdentity","Backlog triage 2026-10-26 confirmed all 7 resolve today via dynamic/special-cased paths"],"acceptance":["Anchor coverage asserts every entry id in search.ts (all pages), not only page:''routing''","The 7 dynamic ids are covered via anchors derived from their plugin/catalog/ternary/special-case sources; removing one of those constructions makes the test fail","Removing a literal anchor still fails the test (existing routing behavior preserved)","bun test packages/ui/src/lib/settings/search.test.ts passes; any genuinely missing anchor found is filed as its own issue"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/535","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/325"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent-breakage risk across the settings discovery surface; the bug class already occurred once (#325). Normal priority, test-only.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:535', '2026-10-27 07:50:48.863699+00', '2026-10-27 15:49:20.247393+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1333, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Deploy + verify Open Design quota provider on the laptop instance (#536)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":["laptop-deploy","credential-handling"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/536","title":"Deploy + verify: Open Design quota provider live on the laptop instance","number":536,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:13:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Rebuilding the provider or changing its API shape (merged already)","Printing, logging, or committing any credential value","Other providers'' deployment state"],"include":["The laptop openchamber.service install/deploy path","Live verification of /api/quota/opendesign + /api/quota/providers","One Helium-browser credential capture attempt, then block with the exact ask if it fails"]},"tests":["GET /api/quota/providers includes opendesign after deploy","GET /api/quota/opendesign returns provider-shaped JSON (windows or explicit not-configured)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue number is the work identity; #480/#481 were code fixes (closed), this task is the deploy+verify+credential remainder \u2014 distinct identity","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:13:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Merged Open Design quota provider is not deployed to the laptop''s running OpenChamber, and its one-time credential import never landed \u2014 the fleet''s quota picture silently omits the most widely-pooled provider.","evidence":["Live 2026-10-27 ~03:11 CDT: GET localhost:3000/api/quota/providers on the laptop lists 10 providers, no opendesign","Live: GET /api/quota/opendesign returns ok:false, configured:false, error ''Unsupported provider''","PR #520 (the #481 fix) merged 2026-10-27T03:57Z; PR #497 (the #480 fix) merged 2026-10-26 \u2014 the running build predates them"],"acceptance":["Laptop instance /api/quota/providers includes opendesign","/api/quota/opendesign returns a provider-shaped response (windows if configured; explicit not-configured otherwise) \u2014 never ''Unsupported provider''","Deploy time + install path recorded on issue #536","Credential capture either completed (live 5h/7d windows read recorded on the issue) or the task blocked with reason credential-import-needed and the exact ask recorded on the issue"],"context_refs":["Issue #536 body \u2014 verified live reads and the full history (endpoint identification 2026-10-25, PRs #474/#475/#497/#520)","developing-today/code#1189 \u2014 quota coverage parent","~/workspace/open-design-quota-investigation.md \u2014 the 2026-10-25 endpoint investigation"],"max_attempts":5,"priority_reason":"OpenDesign is a member of almost every route pool; its quota blindness corrupts every pool-vs-quota judgment the steward/dispatcher make. Drew asked for this job directly 2026-10-27.","timebox_minutes":120}', 'blocked', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:536', '2026-10-27 08:13:51.662325+00', '2026-10-27 15:56:38.75988+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1334, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(schema): widen Identifier sortable prefix to 14 hex chars and guard counter spill (#561)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/561","title":"fix(schema): Identifier sortable prefix wrapped on 2026-08-14 \u2014 ascending/descending IDs now misorder across the 2^36 ms boundary","number":561,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Re-encoding the prefix in base62 (breaks the hex filename filters in tool-output.ts:40 and shell.ts:97)","Changing the 26-char ID shape, the random-suffix alphabet, or any ID validator","Migrating or rewriting already-minted IDs (accepted as documented in the decision)","Editing the tool-output/shell filename regexes \u2014 new IDs must keep matching them unchanged"],"include":["packages/schema/src/identifier.ts: 14-char hex prefix, 12-char random suffix, counter-spill guard (advance effective timestamp past 0xFFF counter), module comment documenting pre-fix ID treatment","packages/schema/test/identifier.test.ts (new): tests (a)-(e) named in the task body"]},"tests":["bun test from packages/schema \u2014 new identifier.test.ts (a)-(e) plus the existing schema suite pass","bun typecheck from packages/schema"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up enqueued by triage task 1299 per its acceptance criteria; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:561 is distinct from the triage key; issue #561 is the single tracking issue for this fix","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Identifier.create emits only the low 48 bits of the packed timestamp*0x1000+counter as its sortable prefix, wrapping every 2^36 ms and inverting ascending/descending order across the boundary.","evidence":["Triage task 1299 decision on issue #561 (2026-10-27): widen hex prefix 12->14 chars, random suffix 14->12, counter-spill virtual-timestamp guard, pre-fix IDs accepted/documented","identifier.ts:16-30 on main 58d2a8277f: packs timestamp*0x1000+counter (~53 bits) but emits only low 48 bits (6 bytes, shifts 40..0); random part is length-12 = 14 chars","Hex-prefix consumers verified this run: packages/core/src/tool-output.ts:40 filters /^tool_[0-9a-f]{12}/ and packages/core/src/shell.ts:97 matches /^sh_[0-9a-f]{12}.*\\.out$/ \u2014 a base62 prefix would break both; a 14-char hex prefix satisfies both unchanged (this is why base62 re-encoding was rejected)","Capacity check: 62^12 ~= 2^71.4 (rejected option); chosen 14 hex chars = 56 bits holds packed values until timestamp 2^44 ms (~year 2527); 12-char random suffix ~= 71 bits of disambiguation entropy","Probe evidence from #561 on main 58d2a8277f: ascending now 17bf34a93001 < yearAgo a24421e93001 (inverted); no tests exist for identifier.ts (packages/schema/test has no identifier.test.ts)"],"acceptance":["ascending() IDs are strictly lexicographically increasing for increasing timestamps across the 2^36-ms boundary and descending() strictly decreasing, pinned by the new packages/schema/test/identifier.test.ts tests (a)-(c)","More than 4096 IDs minted in one millisecond remain strictly increasing (spill guard, test (d)); ID shape stays 26 chars: 14 hex prefix + 12-char random suffix from the existing alphabet (test (e))","Pre-fix ID treatment is documented in a module comment in identifier.ts: shape/validity unchanged, cross-era misordering accepted as unrecoverable (high bits never stored), guarantee applies among post-fix IDs","The hex-prefix filename consumers (tool-output.ts:40, shell.ts:97) still match new IDs unchanged \u2014 no edits needed there; bun test + bun typecheck pass from packages/schema"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/561"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Session and event IDs are chronological sort keys; everything minted since 2026-08-14 misorders against the prior era. Triage (task 1299) has now made the encoding decision, so the fix is small and fully specified.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:561', '2026-10-27 08:38:21.340329+00', '2026-10-27 11:25:58.79058+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1335, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1351: Design architect: a scheduled per-repo design function with a central potential-projects register', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1351","title":"Design architect: a scheduled per-repo design function with a central potential-projects register","number":1351,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the feature itself in the triage task"],"include":["Triage of issue #1351","Decomposition / routing decision"]},"tests":["Triage only: no test run required; routing decision recorded on the issue"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fleet monitor Duty 1 reconciliation 2026-10-27T08:40Z: issue carries queue/queued (verified by individual gh api view) and a direct live-queue query of repo-health-code-pilot shows no live task naming this issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #1351 was filed with the queue/queued work-order label but no live queue task exists for it; without a packet it sits ownerless.","evidence":["Issue #1351 body (labels kind/feature,status/needs-triage,priority/normal,queue/queued,area/infra,effort/m,meta/enriched): ## Work (Drew, 2026-10-27)\n\nThe fleet has issue creators (find improvements, file them) but no\nfunction that originates *designs* \u2014 coherent multi-step project\nproposals grounded in each repo''s own design material, the way the\ndaily idea engine works for cloud projects but repo-targeted.\n\nBuild `repo-design-architect` (every 6h, one repo per run, rotating):\n\n- Reads the repo''s design memory first (ROADMAP, planning/, docs/,\n  ARCHITECTURE, TODO, open epics) + the central register \u2014 no\n  duplicating an existing thread.\n- Produces at most ONE design per run: a design doc in the goal\n  workspace (`files/designs/`), a **design issue** in the repo\n  (labels: `kind/design` \u2014 coined for this \u2014 plus the standard fleet\n  set, `source/design-architect`), and a row in the central register\n  `files/potential-projects.md` (name, repo, one-line summary,\n  status, design issue + doc links). The register is the central\n  potential-projects list; the design issue is the item of record,\n  carrying the summary and links to issues/PRs/file paths.\n- Files implementation issues ONLY for phases it is sure of (\u22643 per\n  design, concrete scope + acceptance), linked as sub-issues of the\n  design issue and enqueued; open questions stay in the design doc.\n- Designs needing a Drew decision carry `user/review` with the\n  decision in one line at the top.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Job live; first four runs cover all four repos (or record a\n      justified zero-design pass with what was checked).\n- [ ] R"],"acceptance":["Triage note posted on the issue with decomposition / routing decision","Follow-up implementation packets enqueued for each actionable slice, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1351"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries queue/queued as its work order with priority label priority/normal; the safety net enqueues so the work order is never ownerless.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1351', '2026-10-27 08:43:23.164592+00', '2026-10-27 08:43:23.164592+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1336, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1352: Program tending: scheduled care for roadmaps, epics, projects, and stalled PRs', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1352","title":"Program tending: scheduled care for roadmaps, epics, projects, and stalled PRs","number":1352,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the feature itself in the triage task"],"include":["Triage of issue #1352","Decomposition / routing decision"]},"tests":["Triage only: no test run required; routing decision recorded on the issue"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fleet monitor Duty 1 reconciliation 2026-10-27T08:40Z: issue carries queue/queued (verified by individual gh api view) and a direct live-queue query of repo-health-code-pilot shows no live task naming this issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #1352 was filed with the queue/queued work-order label but no live queue task exists for it; without a packet it sits ownerless.","evidence":["Issue #1352 body (labels kind/feature,status/needs-triage,priority/normal,queue/queued,area/infra,effort/m,meta/enriched): ## Work (Drew, 2026-10-27)\n\nThe fleet monitor tends issues and queue state; nobody tends the\nplanning layer. Build `program-tending` (daily, all four repos,\n\u2264~12 actions/run, everything logged):\n\n- **Epics:** open `epic` issues \u2014 child progress, last activity,\n  body-vs-reality. Silent 7+ days \u2192 status comment (last movement,\n  next step, blockers); all children closed \u2192 completion comment\n  proposing closure.\n- **Roadmaps:** ROADMAP.md + planning/roadmaps vs landed work.\n  Drift is fixed by PR (forward-looking rows only \u2014 never Done\n  rows); ambiguous drift gets `meta/roadmap-drift` + a comment\n  instead of a guess.\n- **Projects:** board items whose status contradicts issue/PR\n  reality get corrected where possible; unreadable board state is\n  reported, never fabricated.\n- **Stalled PRs:** open PRs with no activity in 48h+ (and no\n  held/do-not-merge) get one check-in comment naming what they''re\n  waiting on + the next step; fleet-owned PRs that merely need\n  shepherding get a `pr_shepherd` queue packet instead of only a\n  comment. Drew''s own feature PRs: comment at 7 days, never a\n  packet.\n- **Loose ends:** parent/epic notification when children close,\n  duplicate cross-links, and the aging `user/review` list surfaced\n  daily (his queue \u2014 reported, not re-decided).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Job live; first run''s log shows actions (or verified\n      no-actions) in all five sections.\n- [ ] First roadmap-drift PR or `meta/roadmap-drift` application\n      lands within the"],"acceptance":["Triage note posted on the issue with decomposition / routing decision","Follow-up implementation packets enqueued for each actionable slice, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1352"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries queue/queued as its work order with priority label priority/normal; the safety net enqueues so the work order is never ownerless.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1352', '2026-10-27 08:43:31.426647+00', '2026-10-27 08:43:31.426647+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1337, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1356: Pool composition review: 12h audit of pool membership, best-per-pool choice, and right-sizing', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1356","title":"Pool composition review: 12h audit of pool membership, best-per-pool choice, and right-sizing","number":1356,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the feature itself in the triage task"],"include":["Triage of issue #1356","Decomposition / routing decision"]},"tests":["Triage only: no test run required; routing decision recorded on the issue"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fleet monitor Duty 1 reconciliation 2026-10-27T08:40Z: issue carries queue/queued (verified by individual gh api view) and a direct live-queue query of repo-health-code-pilot shows no live task naming this issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #1356 was filed with the queue/queued work-order label but no live queue task exists for it; without a packet it sits ownerless.","evidence":["Issue #1356 body (labels kind/feature,status/needs-triage,priority/normal,queue/queued,area/infra,effort/m,meta/enriched): ## Purpose\n\nDrew (2026-10-27): a regular check on quotas and route pools \u2014 whether the latest models are incorporated, whether the best model per pool is chosen, and whether pool members are right-sized against each other and against the pool''s speed/cost/performance requirements.\n\nThe fleet already has an hourly steward (balances burn across pools as composed) and daily pool-intelligence (AA market data + our measured speeds + add/retire flags). Neither owns *membership*: twice a day, this review audits whether each pool''s composition is still correct and hands the steward changes that are ready to land.\n\n## The three checks (every run, every pool)\n\nPools in scope: scout / workhorse / specialist / summit + *-plan variants in the canonical config (developing-today/code `.opencode/opencode.jsonc`), plus OpenChamber''s routing categories.\n\n1. **Latest-model check** \u2014 newly released models (from pool-intelligence''s AA data + provider catalogs) missing from the pool where they''d belong, named with AA standing vs current members, plan/quota home, and the member displaced or joined.\n2. **Best-per-pool check** \u2014 is each pool''s current lead the right choice given AA values, the pool''s quota window + reset time, AND our historical per-model/per-effort statistics from real sessions (babysitter log, session store, meta-reviewer scorecards)? A lead that wins on AA but loses on our sessions \u2014 or draws on a window about to reset while an equal model sits on a fresh window \u2014 is a misalignmen"],"acceptance":["Triage note posted on the issue with decomposition / routing decision","Follow-up implementation packets enqueued for each actionable slice, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1356"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries queue/queued as its work order with priority label priority/normal; the safety net enqueues so the work order is never ownerless.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1356', '2026-10-27 08:43:37.737464+00', '2026-10-27 08:43:37.737464+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1338, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1358: Babysitter coverage gap: the cron fleet''s own agent sessions have no real-time watcher', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1358","title":"Babysitter coverage gap: the cron fleet''s own agent sessions have no real-time watcher","number":1358,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the feature itself in the triage task"],"include":["Triage of issue #1358","Decomposition / routing decision"]},"tests":["Triage only: no test run required; routing decision recorded on the issue"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fleet monitor Duty 1 reconciliation 2026-10-27T08:40Z: issue carries queue/queued (verified by individual gh api view) and a direct live-queue query of repo-health-code-pilot shows no live task naming this issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #1358 was filed with the queue/queued work-order label but no live queue task exists for it; without a packet it sits ownerless.","evidence":["Issue #1358 body (labels kind/feature,status/needs-triage,priority/normal,queue/queued,area/infra,effort/m,meta/enriched): ## The gap (found in fleet review, 2026-10-27)\n\nThe babysitter (`openchamber-babysitter`, every 20m) watches OpenCode/OpenChamber sessions: verdicts, stall detection, nudges. But the fleet''s *other* working sessions \u2014 the cron agent runs themselves (lane shifts, producers, monitor, steward, dispatcher) \u2014 have no real-time watcher at all.\n\nWhat covers them today: the fleet monitor''s hourly reconciliation, which finds claim evaporation after the fact (labels repaired, handoffs posted), and the lane gate/lock discipline. On 2026-10-26 that meant evaporation on the opencode/openchamber queues was discovered up to an hour late \u2014 task 1149 (#530) burned multiple attempts before its final one died at 7/7 \u2014 and several shift reports never arrived in chat at all (now tracked as the certification problem, #1131). Detection latency, not detection absence, is the gap.\n\n## Scope (assess, then build or formally accept)\n\n- Assess a lightweight run-watch for cron executions: a run sitting in its execute phase far beyond its job family''s p90 duration (baselines exist in run history) gets flagged within ~20 minutes \u2014 e.g. a small periodic check over scheduler run state, or a heartbeat convention lane runs touch at checkpoint time that a watcher can staleness-test.\n- The watcher''s output should be the same shape as the monitor''s repairs (flag + evidence), just faster; intervention stays with the existing owners (monitor repairs, lanes re-claim).\n- Alternatively, if the assessment shows the hour"],"acceptance":["Triage note posted on the issue with decomposition / routing decision","Follow-up implementation packets enqueued for each actionable slice, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1358"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries queue/queued as its work order with priority label priority/normal; the safety net enqueues so the work order is never ownerless.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1358', '2026-10-27 08:43:44.706909+00', '2026-10-27 08:43:44.706909+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1339, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1361: Reviewer scope gap: diff review is static — no runtime verification lane', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1361","title":"Reviewer scope gap: diff review is static \u2014 no runtime verification lane","number":1361,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the feature itself in the triage task"],"include":["Triage of issue #1361","Decomposition / routing decision"]},"tests":["Triage only: no test run required; routing decision recorded on the issue"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fleet monitor Duty 1 reconciliation 2026-10-27T08:40Z: issue carries queue/queued (verified by individual gh api view) and a direct live-queue query of repo-health-code-pilot shows no live task naming this issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #1361 was filed with the queue/queued work-order label but no live queue task exists for it; without a packet it sits ownerless.","evidence":["Issue #1361 body (labels kind/feature,status/needs-triage,priority/normal,queue/queued,area/infra,effort/m,meta/enriched): ## The gap (found in fleet review, 2026-10-27)\n\nThe PR diff reviewers (`pr-diff-review` + `pr-diff-review-b`) are static: they read commits and diffs, verify findings against current main *by reading*, and file issues. They never execute the changed behavior. A regression that only appears at runtime \u2014 a config interaction, a timing/ordering effect, a behavior that typechecks and reads correctly but acts wrong \u2014 is invisible to them and is caught later, by CI if the suite happens to cover it, or by the fleet fixing it after it lands.\n\nThe fleet already pays for this gap in the other direction: several of the queue''s small_fix tasks in October were follow-up fixes for behavior that a diff read as fine.\n\n## Scope (assess per repo, then build the bounded version or record why not)\n\n- Design a bounded runtime-verification step for high-risk findings only: when a reviewer files a finding it labels high-risk (a named risk class in the packet \u2014 e.g. behavior-change-no-test, config/routing touch, data-path change), a verification pass runs the touched package''s targeted tests on the laptop against the PR head (or against main + the diff''s scenario where a PR head isn''t runnable) and attaches the result to the finding''s issue \u2014 turning \"reads wrong\" into \"reproduces\" or \"does not reproduce\" before a solver lane picks it up.\n- Bound it hard: targeted tests only, laptop or CI only (never the sandbox), per-run cap in line with the reviewer batch caps, and no verification step for finding"],"acceptance":["Triage note posted on the issue with decomposition / routing decision","Follow-up implementation packets enqueued for each actionable slice, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1361"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries queue/queued as its work order with priority label priority/normal; the safety net enqueues so the work order is never ownerless.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1361', '2026-10-27 08:43:52.953172+00', '2026-10-27 08:43:52.953172+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1340, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): YAML front matter destroyed on save — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1369","title":"id(web): YAML front matter is destroyed on save \u2014 fences become a rule + setext heading, metadata fused into body text","number":1369,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing how the editor renders normal headings or horizontal rules","front-matter editing UI (preservation only)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs front-matter handling both directions","editor-side representation if a new PM node is chosen (pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts)","codec regression tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (in pkgs/id)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (frontmatter / ''front matter'' / YAML in title) over open+closed returned no codec front-matter issue; nearest are #1306/#1307 (plain .txt fidelity, different path).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The markdown codec parses front-matter fences as a thematic break plus a setext heading, so saving a front-matter doc rewrites its metadata into body structure.","evidence":["Verbatim-codec probe crate on main 0cbb91b1 (comrak 0.56.0), logs probe-2026-10-27-creator-a/out.log + out4.log: frontmatter input parses to [horizontal_rule, heading level 2 with fused YAML text, heading, paragraph] and saves as ''-----\n\n## title: Hello World date: 2026-01-02 tags: \\[a, b\\]\n\n# Heading\n\nBody text.'' \u2014 a fixpoint, so the loss is silent and permanent","Blank-line variant mangles differently (first key becomes a paragraph, a later key the heading) \u2014 no front-matter shape survives","Code: commonmark_options at markdown.rs:81-91 enables strikethrough/tasklist/table/footnotes only; no front-matter handling anywhere in pkgs/id (grep front_matter/frontmatter across src+web returned nothing)"],"acceptance":["Front-matter doc round-trips with the YAML block verbatim (multi-key, blank-line-containing, body starting with heading or plain text)","Front matter is not presented in the editor as an editable heading/paragraph","Control: ''Para one.\n\n---\n\nPara two.'' still round-trips with a horizontal rule","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover the shapes above","TOML (+++) front matter supported the same way or explicitly documented out of scope"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1369","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs commonmark_options (lines 81-91)","pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs ContentMode::Markdown save path (line 1984)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent, permanent metadata destruction on the first save of an extremely common markdown file shape (Obsidian/Hugo/Jekyll/Astro notes and docs).","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1369', '2026-10-27 08:44:02.532573+00', '2026-10-28 04:38:14.433998+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1341, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): mixed task/plain lists unsavable — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1370","title":"id(web): mixed task/plain lists cannot be saved at all \u2014 parse builds mixed lists its own placement validation rejects","number":1370,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["relaxing #1043 placement validation for genuinely misplaced nodes","changing pure task/plain list rendering"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs List parse arm and/or placement rules for list children","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts list schemas if the representation changes","codec regression tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (in pkgs/id)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (''mixed task'', task_list_item) over open+closed returned only distinct list bugs #997/#1032/#1036 (all closed, different mechanisms). No issue tracks mixed same-level task/plain lists.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Parse manufactures mixed-children list docs that the save-side placement validation and the editor schema both forbid, so mixed checklists are unsavable.","evidence":["Verbatim-codec probe on main 0cbb91b1 (comrak 0.56.0), logs probe-2026-10-27-creator-a/out2.log + out3.log: ''- [ ] todo / - plain note / - [x] done'' -> PM task_list with a list_item child -> save Err ''Misplaced node: list_item cannot appear inside task_list''; plain-first order -> bullet_list with task_list_item children -> Err; both ordered variants -> Err","Code: markdown.rs:223-226 is_task_list checks only the first child; placement_allowed markdown.rs:980-981 admits exactly one item kind per list type; validate_placement runs at prosemirror_to_markdown entry (1057-1058)","Controls in the same probe: pure task lists (bullet/ordered/nested/in blockquote) and nested task sublists under plain items round-trip cleanly"],"acceptance":["All four mixed shapes open and save without error; checkbox states and plain items preserved; saved form is a fixpoint","Representation is coherent across codec parse, placement validation, and editor.ts schema; PR notes the choice and its effect on ordered numbering/tightness","Pure task lists and pure plain lists round-trip byte-identically to today","Regression tests in markdown.rs cover mixed bullet and mixed ordered lists in both first-child orders","#1043 misplaced-node tests keep passing (validation not relaxed)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1370","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1043","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs List arm (lines 223-226), placement_allowed (980-981)","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts task_list schema (lines 98-100)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Hard save failure on a common checklist shape: any edit to such a file is stranded when the save errors.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1370', '2026-10-27 08:48:09.072277+00', '2026-10-28 04:40:56.114153+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1342, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): GitHub alert blockquotes lose alert on save — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1376","title":"id(web): GitHub alert blockquotes lose their alert on save \u2014 [!NOTE] marker is backslash-escaped into plain text","number":1376,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["alert editing UI / distinct editor rendering (stretch goal only)","changing plain blockquote behaviour for non-alert content"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs alert handling both directions","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts schema if a new PM node is chosen","codec regression tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (in pkgs/id)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (alert) over open+closed returned no codec alert issue (hits were unrelated aggregator/lab-ops items).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The codec treats the alert marker as literal text, so the renderer escapes it and the alert construct is destroyed on save.","evidence":["Verbatim-codec probe on main 0cbb91b1 (comrak 0.56.0), logs probe-2026-10-27-creator-a/out.log + out3.log + out4.log (raw output): ''> [!NOTE]\n> Remember this.'' saves as ''> \\[!NOTE\\] Remember this.''; [!WARNING] and [!TIP] variants identical; byte count verified 3 single backslashes in the saved line","Code: commonmark_options markdown.rs:81-91 enables strikethrough/tasklist/table/footnotes only; no alerts handling anywhere in the codec"],"acceptance":["All five alert markers (NOTE/TIP/IMPORTANT/WARNING/CAUTION) round-trip unescaped at the start of the first quoted line; saved form is a fixpoint","Alert bodies incl. multi-paragraph alerts preserved","Control: blockquote starting with non-alert bracket text round-trips as a plain blockquote","Representation decision noted in the PR; editor.ts schema updated if a new PM node is introduced","Regression tests in markdown.rs cover NOTE/WARNING round-trips and the non-alert control"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1376","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs commonmark_options (lines 81-91)","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts blockquote schema"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Quiet semantic demotion of the standard GitHub callout syntax in READMEs/docs \u2014 the words survive, so the loss goes unnoticed until the doc is viewed on GitHub.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1376', '2026-10-27 09:04:55.029412+00', '2026-10-27 09:04:55.029412+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1343, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: override with malformed schedule becomes always-on (#570)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/570","title":"fix(core): ModelRouteOverrides.parse drops a malformed schedule and keeps the override \u2014 a time-boxed instruction becomes always-on","number":570,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:50:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["ModelRouteSchedule.parse semantics for valid windows","applies() schedule evaluation"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-overrides.ts parse","packages/core/test/model-route-overrides.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-overrides.test.ts from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''override schedule'' and ''malformed schedule'' returned #535/#536/#522/#517 (different defects) and no covering issue","checked_at":"2026-10-27T08:50:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"A present-but-malformed schedule is silently dropped while the override is kept, widening its time scope to always-on whenever the entry also carries a valid until.","evidence":["Probe on main c007c53436 (probe kept in goal hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-0335/): malformed schedule {start:''25:00''} + valid until -> 1 entry, schedule undefined, applies() true; well-formed future schedule -> entry kept with schedule, applies() false; malformed schedule without until -> 0 entries","model-route-overrides.ts:60-62 conflates absent and malformed schedule; model-route-schedule.ts:12-15 states a typo must make a rule disappear rather than apply at the wrong time"],"acceptance":["parse drops an entry whose schedule field is present but unparseable, with or without a valid until","Entries with no schedule field and entries with a well-formed schedule parse exactly as before","bun test test/model-route-overrides.test.ts from packages/core passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/570"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent widening: a typo in a time-boxed avoid/prefer override makes it always-on for its whole lifetime; normal priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:570', '2026-10-27 09:06:12.625676+00', '2026-10-27 17:07:28.276491+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1344, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: truncators return whole string at width 0-2 (#574)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/574","title":"fix(tui): Locale.truncate/truncateLeft/truncateMiddle return the whole string at width 0-2 \u2014 slice(-0) keeps everything","number":574,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:18:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["truncateWidth/takeWidth (already correct)","callers'' width computations"],"include":["packages/tui/src/util/locale.ts truncate/truncateLeft/truncateMiddle","packages/util/src/path.ts truncateMiddle","packages/util/src/path.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/path.test.ts from packages/util (or its package test layout)","tui locale coverage per repo tui-tests skill if a test home exists"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search for ''truncate'' returned no covering issue (only unrelated CI/telemetry items)","checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:18:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"slice(-0) is slice(0), so when the computed keep-count is 0 the truncators keep the entire string and add an ellipsis, returning text longer than the input at widths 0-2.","evidence":["Probe importing the real Locale module on main c007c53436 (kept in goal hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-0335/): truncateMiddle 0->16 chars, 1->17, 2->18, 3->''a\u2026p'' correct; truncateLeft 0->16, 1->17; truncate 0->''abcdefghijklmno\u2026''","Real util module probe: truncateMiddle(\u2026,1) -> ''\u2026abcdefghijklmnop'', (\u2026,2) -> ''a\u2026abcdefghijklmnop''","dialog-select.tsx:916 calls truncateMiddle(detail, Math.max(1, width())); autocomplete.tsx and dialog-workspaces.tsx pass layout-derived widths"],"acceptance":["truncate/truncateLeft/truncateMiddle never return a string longer than the requested length; 0 -> '''' and 1 -> ''\u2026'' for over-long input","Both copies fixed (tui locale + util path); widths >= 3 unchanged","Regression tests for widths 0/1/2 pass from the package directories"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/574"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Layout overflow at exactly the narrow widths truncation exists for; cosmetic severity, low priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:574', '2026-10-27 09:25:42.917629+00', '2026-10-27 18:44:20.56666+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1345, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): image upload stale insert position — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1379","title":"id(web): image upload completing after the document shrinks is silently lost \u2014 stale insert position throws, success logged as failed","number":1379,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:17:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing the upload endpoint or MAX_IMAGE_SIZE","the ordering policy of #1323 and the oversized-event policy of #1321 (coordinate if worked together)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/image-upload.ts completion-path position fallback and error logging","pkgs/id/web/src/image-upload.test.ts regression tests"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id/web && bunx vitest run src/image-upload.test.ts"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (image upload out of range / stale position / placeholder terms, all states) returned no issue tracking this failure mode; #1321 and #1323 are distinct modes in the same handlers (oversized swallow, completion ordering).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:17:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The image-upload completion path inserts at a stale captured position when its placeholder anchor was deleted, throwing RangeError and losing the image.","evidence":["Vitest probe on main 6f4532ab (image-upload.ts unchanged on current main 0c37bb15; probe removed after run, log probe-2026-10-27-creator-b2/out.log): paste PNG at pos 21 in a 20-char paragraph, replace whole doc with ''x'' (size 24 -> 5), resolve upload OK -> final doc still just ''x'', console: ''[image-upload] Upload failed for a.png: RangeError: Position 21 out of range'' at image-upload.ts:235","Control in same probe with no shrink: image inserts normally","Code: image-upload.ts:228 fallback `found ? found[0].from : insertPos`, :235 unconditional removeTr.insert(pos, imageNode), :239 shared catch logs any throw as ''Upload failed''"],"acceptance":["Regression test: upload resolves after the document shrank past the captured insert position (placeholder deleted) \u2014 image inserted at a valid in-range position per the chosen policy, no RangeError, success not logged as upload failure","Normal path unchanged: placeholder present -> image inserts at the placeholder''s mapped position","A genuinely failed upload still removes only its placeholder and logs an upload failure","Existing web unit tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1379","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1321","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1323","pkgs/id/web/src/image-upload.ts handleImageUpload"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent loss of a successfully uploaded image when the user (or a collaborator) edits during a slow upload, plus a log message that misdirects debugging by claiming the upload failed.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1379', '2026-10-27 09:27:57.416767+00', '2026-10-27 09:27:57.416767+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1346, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): ordered-list delimiter style dropped — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1380","title":"id(web): ordered lists with ) markers are rewritten to . on save \u2014 list delimiter style is dropped by the codec","number":1380,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:29:45Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["bullet marker char preservation (comrak renderer normalizes bullets itself)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs parse + save arms for ordered_list and ordered task_list","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts ordered_list/task_list schema attr","codec regression tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for ''delimiter'' in developing-today/code returned no issues; backlog scan shows #997/#1036 cover order/tight only.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:29:45Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Ordered-list delimiter style (./)) is dropped by the markdown codec in both directions and by the editor schema.","evidence":["Probe on main 17c2be5d (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-creator-a/out5.log case paren-delim-ordered): codec ''1) one\\n2) two'' -> PM ordered_list attrs {order:1, tight:true} -> save ''1. one\\n2. two''","DIRECT comrak control (probe8 in same dir): parse -> format_commonmark preserves ''1) one\\n2) two'' unchanged \u2014 loss is codec-side, not renderer","comrak 0.56 nodes.rs:373: NodeList has ''pub delimiter: ListDelimType''; codec never reads it"],"acceptance":["''1) one\\n2) two\\n'' round-trips byte-identically through markdown -> PM -> markdown and is a fixpoint (codec test)","''1. one'' lists render exactly as before","Ordered task lists keep their delimiter too, or the exclusion is noted in the test","Legacy PM docs without the new attr save exactly as today (period default)","editor.ts ordered_list (and task_list if applicable) schema carries the attr with a period default","Existing web::markdown tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1380","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:254","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1200","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1238"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent irreversible source-style churn on every open->save of a paren-marker document; rendering unaffected, so low priority, but it is the last uncarried NodeList field after #997/#1036.","timebox_minutes":15}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1380', '2026-10-27 09:33:15.634564+00', '2026-10-27 09:33:15.634564+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1347, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: git-discover-repos bad --path exits 0 (issue #940)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["silent-data-loss"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/940","title":"git-discover-repos: a nonexistent --path exits 0 \u2014 callers see a successful empty scan instead of a bad argument","number":940,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:29:38Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["--auto scan set and output format","the other three discovery-vocabulary scripts'' own validation (spotlight''s gap is tracked separately)"],"include":["git-discover-repos seed_path / exit-status handling","a regression probe for bad and mixed --path values"]},"tests":["Probes: --path /nonexistent-xyz; --path <bad> --path <dir with one repo>; --path <valid> unchanged; --auto smoke if cheap"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search for discover/not-a-directory/exit returned #914 (missing --path value), #858/#830/#836 (depth/jobs validation), #875 (--user eval) \u2014 none covers a nonexistent --path value exiting 0","checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:29:38Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"git-discover-repos reports a bad --path on stderr but exits 0, so exit-code-checking callers treat a failed scan as a successful empty one.","evidence":["Main 66df198, git-discover-repos seed_path() (~line 345): bad path prints to stderr and continues; final exit status comes from the emit pipeline","Probe: ./git-discover-repos --path /nonexistent-xyz -> stderr ''not a directory'', exit 0","Probe: --path /nonexistent-xyz --path /tmp/discprobe -> repo listed, exit 0","clean.sh:1331-1332 relies on discovery''s exit code (''|| warn \"discovery failed\"'')","git-maintain-repos:443 exits 1 for a non-directory root \u2014 the house contract discover does not uphold"],"acceptance":["git-discover-repos --path <nonexistent> exits non-zero, naming the path on stderr","Mixed bad+valid --path: valid repos still listed, exit non-zero","--auto and all-valid --path runs unchanged (exit 0, same output); --count/--dry-run for valid input unchanged","Regression probe for the bad and mixed cases is included"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/940"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Discovery is the shared front door for clean/maintain/spotlight; a renamed or unmounted tree silently drops out of every maintenance and cleanup run while logs stay green.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:940', '2026-10-27 09:34:20.511546+00', '2026-10-27 10:36:51.372918+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1349, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): image browser stale view — small fix', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1381","title":"id(web): image browser survives editor teardown \u2014 Insert on the destroyed view throws and the dialog stays stuck over the next document","number":1381,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["redesigning the image browser UI or the /api/images endpoint","changing image upload (see #1321/#1323/#1379 for upload-path work)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/image-browser.ts lifecycle + insert dismissal","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts closeEditor teardown hook (if that route is chosen)","new image-browser regression tests in pkgs/id/web/src"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id/web && bunx vitest run"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (image browser destroyed/overlay/stale and image browser terms, all states) returned no issue tracking this; #718 fixed the same stale-singleton class for search panel and goto-line only.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The image browser dialog has no lifecycle tie to its editor view, so it outlives the view and its Insert path throws on the destroyed view without closing.","evidence":["Vitest probe on main 0c37bb15 (real EditorView + richSchema, mocked /api/images; probe removed after run, log probe-2026-10-27-creator-b2/out2.log): open browser, select the one card (Insert enabled), view.destroy() -> overlay still in DOM; click Insert -> throws ''Cannot read properties of null (reading matchesNode)'', overlay still open afterwards","Code: image-browser.ts:97 overlay appended to document.body; no exported close; main.ts:660 navigateTo calls closeEditor, main.ts:1289 closeEditor destroys the view \u2014 neither touches the overlay; insert handlers :74-75 and :147-148 run insertImage before close() with no try/finally"],"acceptance":["Regression test: open browser, destroy the editor view (simulating closeEditor/navigation) \u2014 overlay no longer in the DOM, or Insert unreachable for a destroyed view","Regression test: Insert and double-click always close the dialog even if the insert dispatch throws","Normal path unchanged: live view, select image, Insert/double-click inserts the image node at the selection and closes","Existing web unit tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1381","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/718","pkgs/id/web/src/image-browser.ts openImageBrowser/insertImage","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts closeEditor"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A modal from a previous document surviving navigation, with its primary action throwing uncaught and failing to dismiss, is a visible UX trap in the editor; fix is small and mirrors the existing #718 pattern.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1381', '2026-10-27 09:48:40.717229+00', '2026-10-28 10:41:29.754537+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1350, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'triage: VS Code port leaks usedPercent above 100 in google/antigravity paths (#545)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/541","title":"fix(quota): clamp usedPercent to [0,100] in google and antigravity transforms (#507)","number":541,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:45:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/545","title":"fix(quota): VS Code port leaks usedPercent above 100 in google and antigravity paths \u2014 the #507 defect in quotaProviders.ts, missed by PR #541","number":545,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:45:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Web server transforms (fixed by PR #541)","Other VS Code provider paths (tracked by #510/#518/#519/#521)"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts google/antigravity usedPercent sites","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts regression coverage"]},"tests":["remainingFraction -0.5 -> usedPercent 100 in google bucket and model-data paths","remainingFraction -0.5 -> usedPercent 100 in antigravity bucket and model-data paths"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches ''usedPercent clamp'', ''VS Code google antigravity percent'', ''VS Code port google'', ''antigravity VS Code'' returned #507 (web only) and VS Code counterparts for other providers (#510 z.ai/zhipu, #518 claude, #519 codex, #521 cursor) but no google/antigravity VS Code counterpart","checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:45:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The VS Code port''s google/antigravity quota paths still compute usedPercent with a lower clamp only, leaking values above 100.","evidence":["PR #541 diff (commit d6ba2ac6): web transforms.js google/antigravity four sites changed to Math.min(100, Math.max(0, 100 - remainingPercent)); PR body Affected surfaces claims VS Code not applicable","git show origin/main:packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts lines 1288, 1317, 1463, 1540 all read ''Math.max(0, 100 - remainingPercent)'' (grep cross-check, main 0a3f98313a2e8ad1ae34df2c07ecab5594622a10)","Same file line 2361 already uses the two-bound clamp Math.min(100, Math.max(0, 100 - remainingPercent))"],"acceptance":["All four quotaProviders.ts sites (1288/1317/1463/1540 on main 0a3f9831, or their current equivalents) clamp usedPercent to [0,100]","Tests pin remainingFraction -0.5 -> usedPercent 100 for google and antigravity VS Code paths","No behavior change for in-range fractions"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/545","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/541","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/507"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Impossible >100% usage displayed to VS Code users on two providers, and the fixing PR''s coverage note actively hides the gap; normal priority because it needs an out-of-range upstream fraction to trigger.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:545', '2026-10-27 10:00:44.542308+00', '2026-10-27 15:27:13.149331+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1352, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1371: Git hygiene reconciliation — push finished work, PR orphaned branches, classify dirty trees', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1371","title":"Git hygiene reconciliation: push finished work, PR orphaned branches, classify dirty trees \u2014 and make it a standing sweep","number":1371,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the full reconciliation itself in the triage task"],"include":["Triage of issue #1371","Decomposition / routing decision, including what the new git-hygiene-sweep job already covers"]},"tests":["Triage only: no test run required; routing decision recorded on the issue"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fleet monitor Duty 1 reconciliation 2026-10-27T09:35Z: issue carries queue/queued (verified by individual gh issue view) and a direct live-queue query of repo-health-code-pilot shows no live task naming this issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #1371 was filed with the queue/queued work-order label but no live queue task exists for it; without a packet it sits ownerless.","evidence":["Issue #1371 body (audit 2026-10-27: 62 commits on no origin branch across 37 trees, 13 dirty trees, 143 GitHub branches ahead of main with no open PR, 289 merged branches): ## Problem (audit 2026-10-27, 188 working trees / 26 repos)\n\nThe fleet''s publish step evaporates the same way its claims used to: work finishes in a worktree and the push/PR step never happens.\n\n- **62 commits on no origin branch, across 37 trees** \u2014 almost all finished queue/sweep work (worst: `wt-1058`, 10 commits). Includes task 1149''s completed #530 branch commit.\n- **13 trees with uncommitted work (139 entries)** \u2014 worst: the home repo (`~`): 98 dirty files **and the fleet''s own Supabase migration commits 0009\u20130012 unpushed**.\n- **143 GitHub branches ahead of main with no open PR** (code 66, opencode 44, openchamber 19, nix 14) \u2014 a mix of Jules debris, bot branches, and real feature work (opencode `session-messaging` +44, `github-tools` +33).\n- **289 fully-merged branches** still on the remotes as cleanup candidates.\n- **Hazard:** task 1157''s cursor-quota work sits dirty in TWO worktrees with divergent heads (`~/git/devtoday-openchamber-wt-1157`, `~/work/oc-wt-1157`).\n- Primary clones are healthy (code/openchamber/nix clean+pushed; opencode 2 behind). One fleet submodule fetch timed out during the audit \u2014 one tree''s status unverified.\n\n## This effort\n\n1. Push every already-com","Issue comment 2026-10-27T08:48Z: standing job git-hygiene-sweep (every 4h) was built by Drew covering duties A/B of this issue \u2014 triage must reconcile what remains vs what that job now owns."],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on the issue: confirmed scope, chosen route, and the follow-up packet/task or closure that results","If the issue is already satisfied by the standing git-hygiene-sweep job or other merged work, cite the evidence and close it; if part remains, enqueue/route that remainder explicitly","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1371"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries priority/high and queue/queued as its work order; the safety net enqueues so the work order is never ownerless.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1371', '2026-10-27 10:08:03.547986+00', '2026-10-27 10:08:03.547986+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1353, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: bound route_usage session targets to the requested window (#576)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/576","title":"fix(core): route_usage session targets and plan-window shares ignore the requested window \u2014 sessionTargetUsage has no since bound","number":576,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:50:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["route_stats (already since-bounded)","#550 no-windowHours omission"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-log.ts sessionTargetUsage","packages/core/src/tool/plugin/route-usage.ts collect","packages/core/src/model-usage.ts sessionReports window shares","regression tests in packages/core/test"]},"tests":["bun test for model-route-log/model-usage/route-usage suites from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search for sessionTargetUsage / route_usage session window returned no covering issue; #550 is the distinct no-windowHours omission","checked_at":"2026-10-27T09:50:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"sessionTargetUsage lacks the since bound every sibling rollup has, so per-target rows and plan-window shares in route_usage count all-time usage while headline session totals count only the requested window.","evidence":["packages/core/src/model-route-log.ts:681-701 sessionTargetUsage has no time predicate; siblings sessionUsage:659/targetUsage:703/dailyUsage:721/offerUsage:737 all take since","packages/core/src/tool/plugin/route-usage.ts:76-84 collect combines sessionUsage(since) with unbounded sessionTargetUsage in one report","packages/core/src/model-usage.ts:190-208 sessionReports window used/percent computed over the all-time rows","Probe on main 9a4174a9c2 (real DB layer): sessionUsage(since=3000) {requests:1,input:100} vs sessionTargetUsage {requests:2,input:1000} for ses_probe with attempts at t=1000 (900 tokens) and t=5000 (100 tokens)"],"acceptance":["A session''s per-target rows in route_usage sum to its headline totals for the requested window","Session plan-window shares count only usage inside the plan window''s lookback","Regression test with attempts on both sides of the boundary passes; existing model-route-log/model-usage/route-usage tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/576"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"route_usage is the usage/quota source of truth for the agent; long-lived sessions get inflated window shares and self-contradictory totals. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:576', '2026-10-27 10:16:39.342707+00', '2026-10-27 18:21:44.496462+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1354, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 1 of design #1384 — supervised stdio transport behind a flag — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1385","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1384 \u2014 supervised stdio transport behind a flag (supervisor owns the child''s pipes)","number":1385,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the supervisor in this triage task","any change to internal/daemon/takeover.go or internal/pool/handoff.go (Phase 2)","HTTP/SSE upstream session resume (design non-goal)"],"include":["issue #1385 and design #1384 with the design doc it links","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/stdio.go, internal/daemon/sessions.go (state-dir precedent), internal/pool transport selection"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./...; defining test from #1385: daemon SIGKILL -> new daemon -> child PID unchanged -> call succeeds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1385 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-27T~10:05Z) with queue/queued and no packet; repo-queue health check at 10:12Z shows the pilot queue live. No prior task can name issue 1385 \u2014 it did not exist before this run.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx daemon upgrades depend on a 726-line takeover handoff that passes stdio children''s pipes between daemon processes (pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon/takeover.go, internal/pool/handoff.go). Design #1384 proposes a per-instance supervisor that owns each child''s pipes for the child''s whole life; Phase 1 (#1385) is the flag-gated experiment proving daemon-restart attach before any takeover code changes.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md:3 \u2014 ''Replace the takeover handoff with a supervisor that owns each stdio child''s pipes for the child''s whole life. The current handoff is a stopgap''","planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md Next: supervisor row at status idea, no issue before #1384/#1385 (filed 2026-10-27)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/stdio.go NewStdio: plain os.Pipe()s chosen so ends can be passed to another process; pending partial-frame buffer and detached state exist only for the handoff","Design issue #1384 (kind/design, user/review for the direction decision) with Phase 1 as its sub-issue #1385; #1385 filed with queue/queued + task/triage by the design architect, no live queue task existed at filing"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1385: scope confirmed against current main, supervisor socket protocol points that triage settled are recorded, and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If triage finds Phase 1 as scoped is not independently landable, say exactly why on the issue and propose the rescoped Phase 1 in the design doc''s terms \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state); the user/review direction decision stays on the design issue #1384, not on #1385"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1385","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1384","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/237"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 is the gate for the whole #1384 design: it proves the attach model with the direct path untouched and default off. Normal priority per the design issue; the direction decision itself sits with Drew on #1384.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1385', '2026-10-27 10:29:17.639997+00', '2026-10-27 16:10:51.812099+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1357, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Fix #1347: footnote node types missing from richSchema — footnote docs open empty in web editor', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["data-loss-on-open","editor-only"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1347","title":"id(web): footnote documents open as an empty doc in the web editor \u2014 footnote_reference/footnote_definition missing from richSchema (PR #1013)","number":1347,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Rust codec footnote behavior (already fixed by #1013/#1031)","Changes to any other node types","Rendering footnotes as live HTML (inert rendering only, per the html_inline precedent)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts footnote node specs","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.test.ts (or sibling test) footnote schema/round-trip coverage"]},"tests":["Node.fromJSON(richSchema, footnote doc JSON) does not throw and preserves label attrs + definition content","editor open->save round-trip fixpoint for a footnote document (codec-level)","existing web unit suite still passes"],"dedupe":{"basis":"One fix packet for issue #1347 from triage task 1329; dedupe key repo-health:v1:fix per design pattern.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Verified on main 95bfedb4 by triage task 1329: the Rust markdown codec emits footnote_reference (pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:545, attrs {label}, inline atom) and footnote_definition (:558, attrs {label}, block content) PM node types, but richSchema in pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts defines neither (grep for ''footnote'' in editor.ts returns nothing). Node.fromJSON throws on the unknown types and initEditor''s catch (editor.ts:~375) falls back to an empty doc, so a footnote document opens empty in the web editor and a save could persist the empty doc over the real file.","evidence":["Triage task 1329 findings on issue #1347 (2026-10-27): bug confirmed on main 95bfedb4d6995684baf7179bbcb31210e3ee63ee","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts:216 html_inline node spec (PR #1009/#943 pattern to mirror); richSchema exported at editor.ts:45 and :283","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:545 footnote_reference JSON {type, attrs:{label}}; :558 footnote_definition JSON {type, attrs:{label}, content: block children}; save path handles both at :1366/:1378","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts initEditor: Node.fromJSON in try/catch, catch creates empty doc via topNodeType.createAndFill()"],"acceptance":["richSchema defines footnote_reference as an inline atom with attrs {label} and inert toDOM rendering, mirroring the html_inline pattern","richSchema defines footnote_definition as a block node with attrs {label} and block content (paragraph+), with inert toDOM rendering","A footnote document opens in the web editor with full content (Node.fromJSON(richSchema, codec JSON for a footnote doc) does not throw)","Open->save round-trip through the editor preserves the footnote reference and definition byte-identically (codec fixpoint)","Web unit tests pass (pkgs/id/web vitest) including a new test covering the footnote doc through Node.fromJSON"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1347","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1013","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/945"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Data-loss-on-open for footnote-bearing documents in the web editor; triaged and verified in task 1329, fix is small and precisely scoped (two node specs mirroring an existing pattern). Same tier as the parent triage (priority/high on the issue).","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1347', '2026-10-27 10:47:06.897543+00', '2026-10-27 10:47:06.897543+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1358, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): heading hard break corrupted on save — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1388","title":"id(web): a heading containing a hard break is corrupted on save \u2014 break becomes a literal backslash and the heading splits into a paragraph","number":1388,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:45:50Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Table-cell break handling (already deliberate #1017 behaviour)","comrak renderer changes (vendored dependency)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs save and/or parse handling of LineBreak inside Heading","codec regression tests near the #1017 table-cell tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search ''hard break'' in developing-today/code returned #1017 (table cells, closed/fixed) and #1043 (placement panics, closed); no heading hard-break issue open or closed. Backlog scan: no heading/break entry.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:45:50Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Heading hard_break children are carried into a comrak Heading AST where a LineBreak cannot survive rendering, corrupting the document on save.","evidence":["Probe on main 95bfedb4 (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-creator-a2/out3.log, cases setext-hardbreak-backslash + setext-hardbreak-spaces): codec parses to PM heading [text ''Title'', hard_break, text ''more here''], saves ''# Title\\\nmore here\n'', re-parses to heading text ''Title\\'' + paragraph ''more here'' (PM_SAME false)","PM-side probe (same dir, out2.log case heading-hardbreak): hand-built heading [text ''a'', hard_break, text ''b''] saves ''## a\\\nb\n'' and re-parses to heading ''a\\'' + paragraph ''b''","DIRECT comrak control (out4.log): parse->format_commonmark renders the same bytes \u2014 the renderer cannot spell a break inside an ATX heading, but the codec''s PM-fidelity contract (cf #1031/#1370) is what''s violated, and #1017 already degrades breaks for single-line table cells in this same file"],"acceptance":["Setext heading ''Title\\'' + ''more here'' + ''====='' (and the two-trailing-spaces variant) round-trips to a single heading containing ''Title more here'' or an equivalent single-line spelling \u2014 no literal backslash, no paragraph split","A hand-built PM heading containing a hard_break saves without corrupting on re-parse; output is a fixpoint","Hard breaks in paragraphs still save as hard breaks (existing behaviour unchanged)","Regression test in web::markdown tests next to the #1017 table-cell tests; existing codec tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1388","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:295","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1141","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1385"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent document corruption on a plain open->save of a valid markdown file: user text gains a literal backslash and a heading splits into heading+paragraph. Reachable from pure markdown input (setext heading) with no exotic editor state.","timebox_minutes":15}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1388', '2026-10-27 10:48:31.923771+00', '2026-10-27 10:48:31.923771+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1361, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Triage #546: fix(quota): VS Code port leaks out-of-range usedPercent in ClinePass path — the #512 defect in quotaProviders.ts', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/546","title":"fix(quota): VS Code port leaks out-of-range usedPercent in ClinePass path \u2014 the #512 defect in quotaProviders.ts","number":546,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:50:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the fix itself in the triage task"],"include":["Triage of issue #546","Decomposition / routing decision"]},"tests":["Triage only: no test run required; routing decision recorded on the issue"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fleet monitor Duty 1 reconciliation 2026-10-27T10:50Z: issue carries queue/queued (verified by individual gh view) and a direct live-queue query shows no live task naming this issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:50:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #546 was filed with the queue/queued work-order label but no live queue task exists for it; without a packet it sits ownerless.","evidence":["Issue #546 body: # fix(quota): VS Code port leaks out-of-range usedPercent in ClinePass path \u2014 the #512 defect in quotaProviders.ts\n\n## Problem\n\nThe web ClinePass provider''s unclamped-`percentUsed` defect (#512) also exists in the VS Code port''s own copy of the provider. #512 scopes only the web provider (`packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cline-pass.js`); the port in `packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts` is a separate implementation and is not covered, following the #509 \u2192 #510 / #515 \u2192 #518 / #516 \u2192 #519 / #517 \u2192 #521 port precedent.\n\n## Evidence (verified this run on main 0a3f98313)\n\n`packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts:3544-3548` (`fetchClinePassQuota`):\n\n```ts\nconst usedPercent = toNumber(asNonEmptyString(limit.percentUsed)\n  ?? (Number.isFinite(limit.percentUsed) ? limit.percentUsed : null));\nif (usedPercent === null) continue;\nwindows[kind.key] = toUsageWindow({ usedPercent, ... });\n```\n\nThe port''s `toUsageWindow` (:496-501) only lower-clamps the derived `remainingPercent` (`Math.max(0, 100 - usedPercent)`), so an out-of-range `usedPercent` reaches the window unchanged.\n\nRuntime probe this run (temporary bun test calling the exported `fetchClinePassQuota` with injected `readAuth`/`fetchImpl`, probe removed after the run):\n\n- `percentUsed: 150` \u2192 window `{usedPercent: 150, remainingPercent: 0}`\n- `percentUsed: ''-20''` \u2192 window `{usedPercent: -20, remainingPercent: 120}`\n- `percentUsed: -20` \u2192 window `{usedPercent: -20, remainingPercent: 120}`\n\nThe port''s own ClinePass tests (`quotaProviders.test.ts`, \"ClinePass quota provider (VS Code parity)\") pin acceptance of finite percentages (`[0, ''0'', ''51'']`) but never an out-of-range one \u2014 the same gap as the web provider. The same file clamps both bounds in its NanoGPT port path (:3181: `Math.max(0, Math.min(100, percentUsed * 100))`).\n\nDedup: searched open + closed issues for \"vscode cline\", \"cline-pass quotaProviders\", and related terms on 2026-10-27 \u2014 no VS Code ClinePass issue exists. #512 is web-only. (The sibling Google/Antigravity port defect is already tracked separately as #545 \u2014 do not fold this into it; different provider and read site.)\n\n## Why it matters\n\nIf the ClinePass API reports over-consumption or a drifting/negative percentage, VS Code users see \"150% used\" / \"120% remaining\" on the quota surface, and threshold coloring and gift-reset math (`100 - usedPercent`) consume the corrupt value \u2014 exactly the failure #512 fixes for web users.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `fetchClinePassQuota` in `packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts` clamps `percentUsed` to [0, 100] for both the numeric and string forms; non-finite/unparseable values stay skipped as today\n- [ ] Regression tests in `packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts` (ClinePass parity block): 150 \u2192 100, -20 / ''-20'' \u2192 0, in-range values (43, ''51'') unchanged\n- [ ] Existing ClinePass VS Code tests still pass\n- [ ] No clamp added inside the shared `toUsageWindow` as the only fix (the wafer overage branch deliberately allows >100 \u2014 same co"],"acceptance":["Triage note posted on the issue with decomposition / routing decision","Follow-up implementation packets enqueued for each actionable slice, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/546"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries queue/queued as its work order with priority label priority/normal; the safety net enqueues so the work order is never ownerless.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:546', '2026-10-27 10:49:33.269475+00', '2026-10-27 16:36:27.236198+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1362, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): image resize west handles inverted — small fix', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1389","title":"id(web): image resize west handles (nw/sw) drag in the wrong direction \u2014 outward shrinks, inward grows","number":1389,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["redesigning the resize UX (e.g. free non-aspect resize, edge handles)","image upload/browser work (#1321/#1323/#1379/#1381)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/image-node-view.ts resize direction by corner","new pkgs/id/web/src/image-node-view.test.ts regression tests"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id/web && bunx vitest run src/image-node-view.test.ts","cd pkgs/id/web && bunx tsc --noEmit"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (''image resize handle'', ''node view resize'', all states) returned no issue tracking this; backlog grep shows no prior resize-direction filing (siblings #1379/#1381/#1321/#1323 are upload/browser lifecycle, distinct).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"ImageNodeView''s resize math ignores which corner handle started the drag, so the two west handles resize in the wrong direction.","evidence":["Vitest probe on main 95bfedb4 (real ImageNodeView + EditorView/richSchema, happy-dom, start width fallback 200px; probe removed after run, log probe-2026-10-27-creator-b3/out.log): se +50px -> 250px (correct control); nw outward -50px -> 150px; nw inward +50px -> 250px; sw outward -50px -> 150px (all inverted)","Code: image-node-view.ts:164 startResize(e, _corner) discards the corner; :185 newWidth = Math.max(50, startWidth + dx) for every handle; editor-compat.css:1301-1320 places nw/sw at left:-5px with nw-resize/sw-resize cursors"],"acceptance":["nw/sw drag outward widens and inward shrinks; ne/se behaviour unchanged; aspect ratio maintained","Min-width (50px) and editor max-width clamps still apply after the sign fix","New image-node-view.test.ts covers all four corners with a real EditorView, including committed width/height attrs on mouse-up","Web unit tests + typecheck pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1389","pkgs/id/web/src/image-node-view.ts startResize/onResizeMove/onResizeEnd","pkgs/id/web/src/editor-compat.css resize handle positions"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Half of the image resize handles do the opposite of the user''s drag and persist the wrong size on mouse-up \u2014 a visible core-editing UX defect with a one-function fix.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1389', '2026-10-27 10:49:38.719658+00', '2026-10-28 10:57:05.665187+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1363, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Fix #541: Roc pin enforcement - build.sh version refusal + CI rebuild of checked-in example modules (F11.18)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/541","title":"id(roc): F11.18 pin the Roc compiler for checked-in example modules and rebuild them in CI","number":541,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:06:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing the pinned Roc version","Rewriting the example Roc sources","Hash-pinning the checked-in .wasm outputs"],"include":["pkgs/id/examples/*/build.sh version refusal","pkgs/id nix check or CI job rebuilding the example modules","pin-drift test mirroring tests/toolchain_pin.rs"]},"tests":["build.sh with a wrong-version roc stub refuses (nonzero exit, clear message)","the new check rebuilds all 7 examples and runs behaviour tests on the outputs","existing nix flake check for pkgs/id still passes"],"dedupe":{"basis":"One fix packet for issue #541 from triage task 1267; dedupe key repo-health:v1:fix per design pattern.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:06:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Triaged in task 1267 on main 95bfedb4: the Roc pin exists (pkgs/id/nix/roc.nix, nightly-2026-10-04-130536d) and CI builds roc-world host.wasm with it (nix-common.nix:36), but (a) every example build.sh still takes ROC from PATH with no version check, and (b) no CI job or flake check rebuilds the 7 checked-in example .wasm modules, so their provenance is unknowable and regressions in them are invisible.","evidence":["Triage findings on issue #541, comment 6440056944 (2026-10-27): per-criterion state table","pkgs/id/nix/roc.nix: tag nightly-2026-10-04-130536d with per-platform sha256 hashes","pkgs/id/examples/territory/build.sh:4 and lounge/build.sh:4: ROC=\"${ROC:-roc}\", no version check in any example build.sh","Checked-in modules: examples/{lounge,roc-chat,roc-counter,roc-grid,roc-screen,territory,tic-tac-toe}/*.wasm; no reference to them in nix-common.nix, default.nix, or .github/workflows/","pkgs/id/tests/toolchain_pin.rs covers only the Rust toolchain pin - the pattern to mirror for Roc"],"acceptance":["Each example build.sh verifies the roc version against the nix/roc.nix tag and refuses to build with any other version","A flake check or CI job rebuilds all 7 example modules with the pinned rocCompiler","The rebuilt modules pass the existing sandbox-suite / fuel-budget behaviour checks (behaviour, not hashes)","A toolchain_pin-style test fails if build.sh or CI drift from the nix/roc.nix tag"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/541","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1235"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Step 13 of the Path to Phase 12 ordered queue (#1235), priority/high + now on the issue; triage in task 1267 confirmed the remaining work is bounded because the pin infrastructure already exists.","timebox_minutes":60}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:541', '2026-10-27 10:55:12.608558+00', '2026-10-27 10:55:12.608558+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1364, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): ImageNodeView src reload on every update — small fix', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1392","title":"id(web): ImageNodeView.update() reassigns img.src on every update for relative sources \u2014 images reload/flicker on unrelated edits","number":1392,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["image resize direction (#1389, same file, separate fix)","image upload/browser lifecycle (#1321/#1323/#1379/#1381)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/image-node-view.ts update() src comparison","regression tests in pkgs/id/web/src/image-node-view.test.ts"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id/web && bunx vitest run src/image-node-view.test.ts","cd pkgs/id/web && bunx tsc --noEmit"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (''image flicker reload src'', ''nodeview update image'', all states) returned nothing; backlog has no prior filing on update() src sync.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"ImageNodeView.update()''s src change-guard compares an absolutized DOM URL against the authored relative attr, so it always fires and reloads the image.","evidence":["Vitest probe on main 95bfedb4 (real ImageNodeView + EditorView/richSchema, happy-dom; probe removed after run, log probe-2026-10-27-creator-b3/out2.log): attrs src /api/files/cat.png; img.src getter http://localhost:3000/api/files/cat.png; getAttribute(''src'') /api/files/cat.png; setter spy counted 1 assignment during update() with an identical node","Code: image-node-view.ts:240 compares this.img.src (absolutized getter) against node.attrs.src (authored relative value); alt/title sync at :241-242 compares attrs directly and is unaffected"],"acceptance":["update() with unchanged attrs performs no img.src assignment","Changing the src attr updates the image exactly once; clearing it clears the image","Regression test covers the unchanged-update no-assignment case and the changed-src case","Web unit tests + typecheck pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1392","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1389","pkgs/id/web/src/image-node-view.ts update()"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Every editor/collab re-render restarts relative-src image loads \u2014 visible flicker and wasted requests in image-heavy docs; one-line-class fix.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1392', '2026-10-27 10:58:13.84662+00', '2026-10-27 10:58:13.84662+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1365, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: make MessagingLog.clip respect its maximum at small limits (#577)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/577","title":"fix(core): MessagingLog.clip exceeds its maximum-characters budget at small limits \u2014 the omission marker is not counted when the tail is dropped","number":577,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing the log operation''s defaults (500 / 4000)","MessagingSearch / MessagingTemplate"],"include":["packages/core/src/messaging/log.ts clip","boundary tests in packages/core/test/messaging-log.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test for messaging-log suite from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list open + search for clip / MessagingLog / maximum characters returned no covering issue; no open issue touches messaging/log.ts clip","checked_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"clip''s marker is not counted when the tail clamps to 0, so clipped log entries exceed the documented per-entry maximum at small chars values.","evidence":["packages/core/src/messaging/log.ts:165-170 clip: head=ceil(chars*0.7), tail=max(0, chars-head-20), marker emitted in full even when tail clamps to 0","packages/schema/src/messaging.ts:392 chars is PositiveInt documented ''Maximum characters per entry''; packages/core/src/tool/plugin/messaging.ts:185 same wording","packages/core/src/messaging.ts:1847 live caller clips every log entry with caller-supplied chars","Probe on main 9a4174a9c2 (real module): clip(1000-char text, 10)=22 chars, 20->29, 30->36, 40->43, 50->50, 100->95","packages/core/test/messaging-log.test.ts:175-181 existing test only asserts length < 140 for chars=100"],"acceptance":["For every positive chars, clip(text, chars).length <= chars whenever text.length > chars (or a documented minimum is enforced at the schema boundary and clip respects every value above it)","Omitted-character count in the marker stays accurate for the head/tail actually kept","New boundary tests (chars 1/10/20/30/50/100) pass; existing messaging-log tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/577"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"chars is the contract callers use to bound log text entering a model context; exceeding it up to 2.2x at tight budgets silently breaks context budgeting. Low priority (defaults are 500/4000, where the formula stays in budget).","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:577', '2026-10-27 11:00:05.382224+00', '2026-10-27 18:25:12.939091+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
