2 parked, openchamber 13/2/4 (+1 blocked), nix 0 queued / 16 done"],"acceptance":["Verification verdict posted on #1130 with monitor repair counts for the measurement window","#1130 closed with evidence if all criteria met; otherwise the unmet criterion is named with a new dated follow-up","Labels on #1130 left truthful"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1130"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Closes out a priority/high process issue whose remaining criteria are purely time-based; prevents #1130 sitting open unaudited after the interim check.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:maintenance:developing-today/code:lane-shift-1130-verify:2026-W44', '2026-10-27 11:02:19.963834+00', '2026-10-27 11:02:19.963834+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1372, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(world): F11.16 replay self-check — implement `id world verify` (double replay + first-divergence report) (#544)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/544","title":"id(world): F11.16 replay self-check (`id world verify`)","number":544,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:02:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Fixing #242 host-event retention itself","Changes to the Record/Replay behaviour or fixture format","Unrelated repos"],"include":["pkgs/id: Verify variant in WorldCommand (cli.rs) + dispatch, built on world_fixture::replay","Tests: example fixture passes, nondeterministic guest fails, comparison unit tests","Docs: #242 host-event caveat in help/fixtures doc; F11.16 status-record row update"]},"tests":["cargo test for pkgs/id world_fixture + cli tests incl. the new verify tests","Existing pkgs/id sandbox/world_fixture tests still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Implementation follow-up enqueued by triage task 1268 on issue #544; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:544 is distinct from the triage task identity (repo-health:v1:triage:...). Checked 2026-10-27 on main 452d69e6: no Verify variant, no double-replay comparison exists.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:02:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Determinism is assumed by replay, fixtures and future replication, but nothing checks it: there is no `id world verify`, so a nondeterministic guest would silently corrupt replay-based workflows.","evidence":["Issue #544 body verified fresh 2026-10-27: state OPEN, labels kind/feature + priority/high + now + effort/m, acceptance = verify replays twice and reports first divergence, nondeterministic guest fails, checked-in examples pass, runs against #239 fixtures, #242 effect documented","Main 452d69e6: cli.rs Record :1858 / Replay :1880, no Verify variant; world_fixture.rs replay() :263, Verdict/Replayed types present (1,142 lines)","Plan exit criterion: .opencode/plans/phase-11-foundations.md F11.16 \u2014 a test with a deliberately nondeterministic guest fails the check","Triage note with the implementation contract: issue #544 comment 6440263132 (queue task 1268)"],"acceptance":["`id world verify` replays a fixture twice, compares the records and reports the first divergence (sequence + both values), exiting nonzero on divergence","A deliberately nondeterministic guest fails verify; the checked-in examples pass; it runs against the #239 fixtures","How host-originated events (#242) affect verification is documented in the command help and/or fixtures doc","Issue #544 acceptance criteria (in its body) met and verified with fresh evidence; PR opened (merged under standing criteria) referencing issue #544"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/544","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1235","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/242",".opencode/plans/phase-11-foundations.md (F11.16)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Step 14 of 14 of the Path-to-Phase-12 ordered queue (#1235) \u2014 the last step; issue carries priority/high + now. Triage task 1268 verified it valid and scoped the implementation.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:544', '2026-10-27 11:02:46.335169+00', '2026-10-27 18:58:41.947929+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1374, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'triage: route_stats speed median vs completed-only doc (#578)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/578","title":"fix(core): route_stats member speed median counts failed and timed-out attempts \u2014 Member.tokensPerSecond documents completed attempts only","number":578,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:10:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["firstTokenMs and inputTokens medians (no completed-only claim)","changing what the attempt writers record"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-review.ts memberOf speed computation","packages/core/test/model-route-review.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test for model-route-review suite from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Open issue list (80) and closed list checked this run: no route-review/route_stats speed issue; #549/#576 cover other route-log/usage surfaces","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:10:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Member.tokensPerSecond median includes failed/timed-out attempts despite documenting completed attempts only.","evidence":["packages/core/src/model-route-review.ts:54-55 field doc promises completed attempts only","packages/core/src/model-route-review.ts:212,222 speeds computed over all attempts, no outcome filter","packages/core/src/session/runner/step.ts:408-411 and packages/core/src/model-route-log.ts:127-130 record tokens_per_second regardless of outcome when tokens and first output exist","Probe on main 9a4174a9c2 (real summarize): success 10 + failure 1000 + timeout 2000 tok/s -> reported tokensPerSecond 1000"],"acceptance":["Member.tokensPerSecond semantics decided and pinned: median over completed attempts only per its doc, or doc/rendering explicitly changed to partial-output inclusion","Regression test with a slow success and fast failed/timed-out attempts carrying tokensPerSecond passes","Existing model-route-review tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/578"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"route_stats speed figures feed routing judgement; crediting aborted attempts'' speeds makes flaky targets look fast. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:578', '2026-10-27 11:05:53.607648+00', '2026-10-27 18:10:54.330431+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1375, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(routes): strict numeric query params at gitlab/github/fs/plan routes (#554)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/554","title":"fix(routes): numeric query params still judged loosely \u2014 GitLab MR number, GitHub page/number, find-in-files and plan-notes limits reinterpret 10junk / 2.9 / 1e3","number":554,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:05:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Git routes'' strict parsers (already correct)","CLI argument parsing (fixed by #433/#446)","Changing defaults or clamping bounds at any site"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/gitlab/routes.js requestNumber (page + pulls/context number)","packages/web/server/lib/github/routes.js issues/list + pulls/list page, pulls/context number","packages/web/server/lib/fs/routes.js find-in-files limit","packages/web/server/lib/routing/plan-routes.js clampLimit","Regression tests for the malformed spellings at each site"]},"tests":["packages/web vitest suites for gitlab routes, github routes, fs routes, routing plan-routes (existing test files for those modules)","bun run check:changed"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all search ''parseInt OR 10junk OR requestNumber OR find-in-files'' returned only the closed strict-parsing family for other sites (#433/#446/#463/#464/#465 CLI and git endpoints, port/weekday parsers); no open or closed issue covers the gitlab/github source-control routes, find-in-files limit, or plan-notes limit","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:05:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Four route sites judge numeric query params with bare parseInt / Number + finiteness, silently reinterpreting 10junk, 2.9 and 1e3, while strict helpers already exist in two of the same files.","evidence":["gitlab/routes.js:139-142 requestNumber bare parseInt vs :144-149 strict requestIssueNumber in the same file; loose uses at :1157 (page), :1172 (pulls/context number), :1204 (page)","github/routes.js:86-91 strict readPositiveIntegerQuery exists; loose Number() page at :2473 (issues/list, effectivePage guard :2507) and :2825 (pulls/list), loose Number() number at :3033 (pulls/context, !number check :3048 catches NaN/0 but not 2.9)","fs/routes.js:1036-1039 bare parseInt limit for GET /api/fs/find-in-files; constants fs/content-search.js:15-16 default 200 / max 500","routing/plan-routes.js:26-29 clampLimit bare parseInt, used at :95 for GET /api/routing/plans/notes","Probe this run (exact helper expressions in node): 10junk -> 10/10/10, 2.9 -> 2/2/2, 1e3 -> 1/1/1 across requestNumber/planClampLimit/fsLimit; abc -> null/50/200 defaults; git routes'' codified standard at git/routes.js:25-29"],"acceptance":["Every site in the issue judges its numeric query parameter by whole text (digits only, positive, safe integer where an identifier), reusing the strict helpers already in the same file where one exists","Malformed values behave as the strict siblings do: page/limit fall back to existing defaults (1 / 200 / 50); number parameters are refused (400 / null path); no silent reinterpretation of 10junk, 2.9, or 1e3","Well-formed values (10, 2, 500) behave exactly as before, including clamping (fs limit max 500, plan-notes limit 1-500)","Regression tests cover: gitlab pulls/context number=10junk and 2.9 refused; gitlab page and github page 2.9 -> default page 1 (not 2.9 upstream); find-in-files and plan-notes limit=10junk/2.9/1e3 -> defaults","No other route''s parameter handling changes; git routes'' strict parsers untouched"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/554","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/463","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/465"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"GitLab pulls/context silently loads a different merge request on a mistyped number \u2014 wrong data presented as authoritative; the repo has fixed this defect class repeatedly and codified the strict standard. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:554', '2026-10-27 11:06:40.177198+00', '2026-10-27 15:51:54.500225+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1376, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'triage: distinct cycle vs depth errors in MessagingTemplate.render (#579)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/579","title":"fix(core): MessagingTemplate.render calls an acyclic deep variable chain a self-reference \u2014 the depth limit and the cycle check share one false error","number":579,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:16:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["classify()/compile() depth handling (silent undefined is a separate surface)","changing MAX_DEPTH without documenting the decision"],"include":["packages/core/src/messaging/template.ts render expand error paths","messaging template tests in packages/core/test"]},"tests":["bun test for messaging template suites from packages/core"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Open issue list (80) checked this run: no MessagingTemplate/render error-message issue; no messaging issues open at all in this area","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:16:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"MessagingTemplate.render conflates a reference cycle with a depth-limit excess in one false error message.","evidence":["packages/core/src/messaging/template.ts render expand: `if (stack.includes(name) || stack.length >= MAX_DEPTH)` returns the single message ''Variable {name} refers to itself''; MAX_DEPTH = 8 in the same file","Probe on main 9a4174a9c2 (real module): acyclic 11-variable chain -> ''Variable {i} refers to itself''; genuine self-reference -> identical wording","Chained template values are a built-in idiom: the private_link constant is ''{separator}{bidirectional}{separator}'' (template.ts constants)"],"acceptance":["Cycle and depth-limit excess produce distinct, accurate error messages","Tests pin: direct and indirect cycles report a cycle; an acyclic over-limit chain reports the depth limit; a chain at exactly the limit still renders","Existing messaging-template tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/579"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The render error is the only diagnostic for a failed template/topic configuration; a false self-reference claim sends debugging in the wrong direction. Low priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:579', '2026-10-27 11:07:03.191294+00', '2026-10-27 17:35:25.134483+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1377, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): adjacent different-type lists end-list comment — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1397","title":"id(web): adjacent lists of different types save an <!-- end list --> comment that reopens as a phantom code block","number":1397,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:08:21Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1032 bullet-marker coalescing (already fixed)","#1370 mixed items within a single list","#1380 ordered-list delimiter style"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs save/parse handling of adjacent different-type lists and codec tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list (open) + gh search ''end list''/''adjacent list'': only #1032 (closed) matches, and it covers bullet-marker adjacency fixed by coalescing (PR #1037); different-type adjacency is the boundary its fix explicitly excludes (markdown.rs:1473-1475). #1370 is mixed items inside one list (distinct); #1380 is ordered-list delimiter style (distinct).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:08:21Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Adjacent different-type lists are corrupted on save (end-list comment) and on reopen (phantom code block).","evidence":["Probe on main 452d69e6 (markdown.rs identical at 95bfedb4 probe copy), hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-creator-a3/out4.log: ''- a\\n1. b\\n'' SAVE -> ''- a\\n\\n<!-- end list -->\\n\\n1. b\\n''; re-parse PM contains code_block{htmlBlock:true, params:html} with text ''<!-- end list -->'' between bullet_list and ordered_list","Same probe: blockquote case ''> - a\\n> 1. b\\n'' second save drops the blank ''> '' line before ''> 1. b'' (MD_FIXPOINT: false)","json_to_ast child loop (markdown.rs:1464-1487) coalesces only bullet_list siblings; HtmlBlock arm (markdown.rs:391-419) converts any HTML block to a code_block with htmlBlock provenance"],"acceptance":["All five probed shapes (bullet->ordered, ordered->bullet, multi-item boundary, task->bullet, blockquote) save with no ''<!-- end list -->'' or other renderer-internal separator in the markdown","Re-parse of the saved text yields exactly the two original lists and no node between them; blockquote shape is a markdown fixpoint across two saves","#1032 behaviour unchanged (adjacent bullet lists still coalesce; its regression tests pass); existing web::markdown tests pass","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover the type-boundary shapes in both directions"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1397","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1032","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1464","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:391"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Save writes renderer-internal markup into user files and the reopened doc model gains a phantom code block between lists; same failure family as #1032 at the boundaries its fix could not merge.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1397', '2026-10-27 11:11:23.68137+00', '2026-10-27 16:22:41.635869+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1378, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): multi-block Tab/Shift-Tab corrupts paragraph, skips code blocks — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1399","title":"id(web): Tab/Shift-Tab with a selection spanning multiple blocks corrupts a paragraph and skips later code blocks","number":1399,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:10:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing single-block indent semantics or the 2-space INDENT unit","list indentation (Tab in lists is a different command path)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/indent.ts indentCommand/dedentCommand multi-block handling","pkgs/id/web/src/indent.test.ts multi-block regression tests"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id/web && bunx vitest run src/indent.test.ts"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (indent / Tab, all states) this run: #714 (closed) covers wrong-line selection WITHIN one code block only; no issue tracks multi-block spanning selections.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:10:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"indent/dedent commands use single-block line math for multi-block selections: later code blocks skipped, spaces inserted into a neighbouring paragraph.","evidence":["Vitest probe on main 452d69e6 (real commands + richSchema; probes preserved in fleet records probe-2026-10-27-0605-b): doc code_block(x\\ny)+paragraph(mid)+code_block(p\\nq), select-all, Tab -> block1 ''  x\\n  y'', paragraph ''mid  '' (spaces appended to prose), block2 unchanged ''p\\nq''","Second probe: code_block(one)+paragraph(keep me)+code_block(two), select-all, Tab -> only first block indented","Controls: single-block selections behave (existing suite); paragraph-only selection returns false (inCode gate indent.ts:42-46 checks only $from parent)","Root cause: indent.ts:63-65 / :100-102 derive blockStart from $from and blockEnd from $to (different nodes when spanning) and scan doc.textBetween as a single block''s text"],"acceptance":["Tab with a multi-block selection indents selected lines of every overlapped code_block and modifies no non-code content","Shift-Tab under the same conditions dedents every overlapped code_block''s selected lines, prose untouched","Existing indent.test.ts suite (incl. #714 cases) passes unmodified","New tests cover code+paragraph and code+paragraph+code selections for both commands, including select-all"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1399","pkgs/id/web/src/indent.ts indentCommand:42-91, dedentCommand:93-160","pkgs/id/web/src/indent.test.ts","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/714"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Select-all + Tab is a standard reindent gesture; today it silently edits prose and leaves code unindented \u2014 data corruption in a basic editor path.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1399', '2026-10-27 11:11:45.985144+00', '2026-10-28 04:57:50.717819+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1379, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'OpenChamber babysitter v1 (#1185): acceptance verification, second-location stub demo, close-out', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1185","title":"OpenChamber babysitter v1: one worker, session rounds, quota + progress report (report-only)","number":1185,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the v1.1 dispatcher/nudges/harvesting work -- that is issue #1187, a separate task","Live-querying the sandbox OpenCode server (:4096) as a data source -- it is off by Drew''s choice","Changes to the developing-today/code repository code","The #1188 session-API inventory and #1189 pool-attribution pilots -- separate queued issues"],"include":["Issue #1185 and the babysitter assets in the keep-the-four-repos-healthy goal workspace (openchamber-babysitter-instruction.md, babysitter-log.md, the openchamber-babysitter cron definition)","One verification babysitter round and the stub-location config/adapter demonstration"]},"tests":["After the stub change, one babysitter round completes and its log section lists the stub location as off/disabled with the round loop otherwise unchanged","gh issue view 1185 fresh after close-out: state and labels match the claimed outcome"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1275 as its follow-up; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1185 is distinct from the triage task identity (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1185). No live task for the acceptance-verification remainder existed at triage time; the babysitter cron is a scheduler job, not a queue task.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #1185''s v1 babysitter exists and runs (cron openchamber-babysitter), but the issue was never closed out: its acceptance criteria are unverified, and the second-location stub demonstration (criterion 4) has not been done -- the babysitter instruction currently states the laptop is the ONLY location.","evidence":["Cron `openchamber-babysitter` exists, enabled, every 20m, owner goal:keep-the-four-repos-healthy; runs succeeding 2026-10-27 (verified via cron list/view/runs in triage task 1275)","hidden_files/babysitter-log.md: rounds 02:37, 02:58, 03:28, 03:37, 04:05, 04:45, 05:00, 05:31, 05:50 CDT on 2026-10-27; round 05:50-06:04 covered 6 bound sessions (2 active + 4 done-unreported) with verdicts verified per PR/issue via gh, plus quota snapshot fetched ~05:59 CDT","hidden_files/openchamber-babysitter-instruction.md (v1, live): laptop-openchamber is the only location; sandbox OpenCode :4096 is NOT a location and never a data source -- no second-location stub exists (grep for stub/second location in babysitter log + instruction: no hits)","Issue #1185 body (fresh gh view 2026-10-27T11:06Z): OPEN, acceptance = one worker on <=30-min cadence; >=3 concurrently bound sessions round with hand-verified verdicts; quota figures carry read age and flag >60-min staleness; second location = config + adapter only demonstrated by stubbing sandbox-opencode","Recent babysitter rounds flag quota gaps explicitly: claude /api/quota read failed (rate limited), meta unsupported by the running server -- flagging exists, formal criterion check still owed"],"acceptance":["A criterion-by-criterion verification checklist is posted on issue #1185 with fresh evidence (cron id/cadence, a named round covering >=3 bound sessions, quota snapshot timestamp/read-age handling)","Second-location stub demonstrated (disabled stub, no live sandbox query, round loop untouched, one round reports it off) OR the conflict is documented on #1185 and that single item escalated with user/escalated naming the decision Drew must make","Issue #1185 is closed with evidence if all criteria are met/waived, with all queue/work/status labels cleaned; if it cannot close, the exact remaining blocker is named on the issue and in the task result"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1185","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1187","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1188","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1189"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries priority/high; triage (task 1275) found the work built and live but never closed out -- this is the remaining acceptance/close-out remainder, smaller than the original build.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1185', '2026-10-27 11:12:18.338523+00', '2026-10-28 04:57:40.663801+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1380, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'OpenChamber dispatch v1.1 (#1187): harvesting/terminal-state close-out + hand-back & nudge acceptance tests', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1187","title":"OpenChamber dispatch v1.1: admission control, hand-backs, stall nudges, harvesting, Workhorse-first routing","number":1187,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the targeted queue binding verb itself if it belongs to #1337/#1272 -- this task consumes it if present and escalates its absence; it does not silently duplicate that work","Dispatching new production work beyond the controlled saturation/stall test sessions","Changes to the developing-today/code repository code","Live-querying the sandbox OpenCode server (:4096) as a data source"],"include":["Issue #1187 and the dispatcher/babysitter assets in the keep-the-four-repos-healthy goal workspace (openchamber-dispatcher-instruction.md, openchamber-babysitter-instruction.md, dispatcher-log.md, babysitter-log.md)","The dispatched openchamber-pilot tasks named in the evidence, driven to terminal/named states through the queue helper","One controlled saturation pass and one controlled stall pass, both fully reverted to normal operation afterwards"]},"tests":["Fresh queue reads after harvesting: each named dispatched task shows its terminal/named status (not queued)","dispatcher-log.md and babysitter-log.md sections for the controlled saturation and stall passes, with the parked task''s fresh status and the nudged session''s next assistant message as evidence","gh issue view 1187 fresh after close-out: state and labels match the claimed outcome"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1276 as its follow-up; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1187 is distinct from the triage task identity (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1187). The dispatched tasks named (1123 etc.) are in repo-health-openchamber-pilot, a different queue; no live repo-health-code-pilot task owns the harvesting/acceptance-test remainder.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"OpenChamber dispatch v1.1 (#1187) dispatches and routes correctly, but nothing harvests: completed sessions'' queue tasks stay queued, so the queue -> session -> PR -> verified terminal state flow (acceptance criterion 1) and the no-evaporation criterion (5) fail today; the hand-back (2) and nudge (3) paths have never been exercised.","evidence":["Cron `openchamber-dispatcher` exists, enabled, every 30m, owner goal:keep-the-four-repos-healthy; dispatcher-log.md runs 2026-10-27 02:47, 03:30, 04:12, 05:31, 06:00 CDT dispatched tasks 1123, 1309, 1310, 1331, 1221, 1222, 1242 to sessions verified engaged by content, Workhorse-first, per-pool quota gate applied","Binding gap (systemic, dispatcher log, repeated every run): dispatched queue tasks remain `queued` -- the claim verb is next-task-only and there is no targeted claim/binding verb; bindings live in issue comments + session titles; targeted binding verb owed on #1337/#1272","Babysitter rounds (babysitter-log.md 04:45, 05:31, 05:50 CDT): sessions for tasks 1123, 1309, 1310, 1221 completed with PRs #539, #542, #543, #551 OPEN while the queue tasks still show queued/attempts 0 -- done-unreported, harvest-ready, unharvested","Hand-backs: none in any dispatcher run -- saturation never occurred (11-12 free slots against cap 12); executor-saturated path untested","Nudges: none in any babysitter round -- no stall has occurred; the one-nudge-then-escalate path (babysitter instruction section 3) is untested","Issue #1187 body (fresh gh view 2026-10-27T11:17Z): OPEN, effort/l, priority/high; acceptance criteria as in this packet''s body; depends on babysitter v1 (live, triage task 1275) and pilots #1188 (API inventory file exists) / #1189 (still open -- meta/claude quota reads still failing in current rounds)"],"acceptance":["Every currently-dispatched task whose session is done (at minimum 1123, 1309, 1310, 1221) reaches a verified terminal or named park/block queue state with PR evidence, or the missing binding mechanism is escalated on #1187 as the named blocker; the harvest step is written into the babysitter/dispatcher instructions","Controlled saturation pass: a chosen candidate is parked executor-saturated with an issue note within one round, and normal admission is restored afterwards (evidence in dispatcher-log.md)","Controlled stall pass: a deliberately stalled bound test session receives exactly one verified nudge; a repeat stall escalates per the max-nudge rule (evidence in babysitter-log.md)","Criterion-by-criterion verdict posted on #1187; issue closed if all criteria met/waived, labels cleaned; the Frontier-week criterion is recorded as a standing interim/weekly-review check"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1187","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1185","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1188","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1189"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries priority/high; triage (task 1276) found dispatch live but dispatched work evaporating at the harvest step -- completed sessions with open PRs and queue tasks still queued is exactly the anti-evaporation failure the fleet rules forbid.","timebox_minutes":60}', 'parked', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1187', '2026-10-27 11:21:57.318286+00', '2026-10-28 10:56:08.482855+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1382, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: mcp-clients Codex inline/array TOML spellings survive (issue #944)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["silent-bypass"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/944","title":"mcp-clients: Codex servers written as [mcp_servers] inline tables or [[mcp_servers.*]] array tables survive enforcement \u2014 reported as removed: none","number":944,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:20Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the JSON and Zed client steps","mcpx itself"],"include":["mcp-clients.py codex() TOML handling","mcp-clients.test.py Codex cases for both spellings"]},"tests":["mcp-clients.test.py (python3) \u2014 existing cases plus new inline-table and array-table seeds","Probes: both spellings in a scratch HOME; re-run idempotency check"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search for mcp-clients/codex returned #906 (one malformed client aborts all) and #905 (Zed context_servers) \u2014 neither covers Codex TOML spellings; mcp-clients.test.py:58,73 seeds only the [mcp_servers.other] table spelling","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:20Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Codex MCP servers in inline-table or array-of-tables TOML spellings are not removed by mcp-clients.py, and the run reports success.","evidence":["Main 71fe33d, mcp-clients.py:74 header regex only matches single-bracket tables; :77 skipping only when name startswith mcp_servers.","Probe: [mcp_servers] + foo = { command = \"evil\", args = [] } -> entry still present after codex(), log says removed: none","Probe: [[mcp_servers.foo]] command=\"evil\" -> block still present after codex(), log says removed: none","Both probes idempotent on re-run: the foreign server is never removed"],"acceptance":["[mcp_servers] parent-table inline entries are removed, leaving mcpx as the only server","[[mcp_servers.<name>]] array-of-tables blocks are removed","removed: report names servers removed in these spellings accurately","Plain [mcp_servers.<name>] behaviour and idempotency unchanged; mcp-clients.test.py gains both spelling cases and passes","Any deliberately unsupported spelling produces a named warning + non-zero exit, not a removed: none success"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/944"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"mcp-clients.py is the every-switch enforcement point for mcpx-only client config (#671); a surviving foreign server silently bypasses the gateway while logs stay green.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:944', '2026-10-27 11:24:19.749454+00', '2026-10-27 14:40:54.889319+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1383, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: install-vscode-patch-agent false success on failed write/load (issue #945)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["false-success"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/945","title":"install-vscode-patch-agent: a failed plist write or launchctl load still prints ''\u2713 Installed and loaded'' and exits 0 \u2014 and ~/Library/LaunchAgents is never created","number":945,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["patch-vscode-insiders.sh patch logic (#909/#931 territory)","the plist''s contents/WatchPaths"],"include":["install-vscode-patch-agent.sh error handling and directory creation","a scratch-HOME/stub-launchctl regression probe"]},"tests":["Scratch HOME + stub launchctl probes: missing LaunchAgents dir, load exits non-zero, happy path (plist written byte-identical, exit 0)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search for install-vscode/patch-agent/plist/launchctl returned no tracking issue; #909/#931 cover patch-vscode-insiders.sh itself, not its installer; #926/#934 are the same false-success family in brew-repair/service-event","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"install-vscode-patch-agent.sh reports ''Installed and loaded'' and exits 0 even when nothing was written or loaded.","evidence":["Main 71fe33d, install-vscode-patch-agent.sh: no set -e; line 19 cat > $PLIST_PATH with no mkdir -p of ~/Library/LaunchAgents; line 47 launchctl load status unchecked; lines 49-56 banner unconditional","Repro: HOME=/tmp/fh3 with stub launchctl (exit 42) -> line 19 ''No such file or directory'', banner printed, rc:0, no plist exists afterwards"],"acceptance":["~/Library/LaunchAgents is created when missing (or the script fails loudly naming it)","Failed plist write exits non-zero naming the write step","Failed launchctl load exits non-zero naming the load step; no success banner","Happy path unchanged: identical plist content, agent loaded, banner, exit 0","Regression probe (scratch HOME + stub launchctl: missing-dir, failing-load, happy path) included"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/945"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The installer is the only way the patch agent gets (re)installed; a false success means workbench patches silently stop re-applying after VSCode Insiders updates.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:945', '2026-10-27 11:26:03.926361+00', '2026-10-27 16:25:43.1507+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1384, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Verify #1188 remainders: live-session fields, paired-client auth flow, nudge call shape', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1188","title":"Pilot: OpenChamber session API inventory for a remote babysitter","number":1188,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing new babysitter features","any credential value in any artifact \u2014 Bitwarden item names only"],"include":["issue #1188 acceptance verification against the inventory doc and babysitter log","pilot #1191 live-run outcomes as evidence"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 verification is by live API calls from the sandbox babysitter host against the laptop stack, as the babysitter rounds already perform"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1277 (dedupe repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1188) is the live task for #1188 at check time; this maintenance-family key is distinct and no live task uses it.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Issue #1188 is partially satisfied: the inventory doc exists and the babysitter system it informed is operating, but three verification items from its own progress note (live-session fields, paired-client auth flow, verified nudge shape) have no recorded closure, and #1191 (their vehicle) is still open.","evidence":["Issue #1188 comment 2026-10-27T04:24Z: first-pass inventory done, doc files/openchamber-api-inventory-2026-10-26.md; remainders named: live-session fields, paired-client auth flow over Tailscale, nudge call shape \u2014 to land with pilot #1191''s live runs","cron.list 2026-10-27: openchamber-babysitter (20m) and openchamber-dispatcher (30m) enabled; hidden_files/babysitter-log.md shows current rounds with per-session verdicts","gh fresh 2026-10-27: #1191 still OPEN (its live runs are the vehicle for the remaining verifications)"],"acceptance":["Each of the three named remainders is marked confirmed-with-evidence or gap-with-workaround on #1188","#1188 closed if all acceptance criteria are met; otherwise the unmet item is named with a new dated follow-up","No credential value appears in any comment, doc, or packet \u2014 Bitwarden item names only"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1188","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1191"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Closes out a priority/high pilot whose remaining items are verification-only and depend on #1191 live runs having happened; prevents it sitting open unaudited.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:maintenance:developing-today/code:oc-api-inventory-1188-verify:2026-W44', '2026-10-27 11:27:01.802733+00', '2026-10-27 11:27:01.802733+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1385, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Pilot (#1189): pool attribution + quota coverage table, one session burn reconstruction, babysitter report spec', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1189","title":"Pilot: per-session pool attribution + quota read coverage for babysitter reports","number":1189,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Fixing the meta quota provider or the claude quota read -- that is openchamber #523 / PR #540 and related work; this pilot documents the gaps and links them","Changes to the developing-today/code repository code","Dispatching or babysitting sessions beyond reading the records of already-finished ones"],"include":["Issue #1189 and the pilot deliverables in the keep-the-four-repos-healthy goal workspace (files/ report, babysitter instruction wording)","Fresh quota reads via the babysitter pattern (laptop /api/quota/*) and the finished-session records in babysitter-log.md / dispatcher-log.md"]},"tests":["The coverage table file exists and names a source/freshness/gap for every pool in provider-quota-registry.md (grep the file for each pool name)","gh issue view 1189 fresh after close-out: state and labels match the claimed outcome"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1278 as the pilot-execution follow-up; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1189 is distinct from the triage task identity (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1189). No live task owns the pilot deliverables; the babysitter/dispatcher crons produce rounds, not this pilot report.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Per-session pool attribution and quota coverage for babysitter reports (#1189): attribution works ad hoc in live rounds, but there is no coverage table, no end-to-end burn reconstruction with error bars, and no report-spec update -- so babysitter reports still promise figures (claude, meta) that no read can currently deliver.","evidence":["Babysitter rounds (babysitter-log.md, 2026-10-27) attribute every enumerated session to a pool/route from the session record (e.g. ses_e82ffc213ffe: cline-pass/deepseek-v4.1-flash via opencode-route deepseek-flash-plan; ses_e82ff46f1ffe: opencode-go/gpt-6-luna) with per-session cost/tokens -- attribution method works in practice","Pool burn deltas observed across single sessions in the 05:50-06:04 CDT round: opencode-go monthly 62.48% -> 62.81% across the #516 session; cline-pass 5h 6% -> 7% across the #534 session -- raw material for the burn reconstruction exists","Quota coverage gaps proven live in every 2026-10-27 round: claude /api/quota/claude ok:false ''Rate limited. Retrying soon.''; meta /api/quota/meta ok:false ''Unsupported provider'' (fix openchamber #523, PR #540 still OPEN at triage); openrouter monthly 100% walled (readable); deepseek shows a PAYG balance only, no window %","No pilot deliverable exists: ls of the goal files/ dir (2026-10-27, triage task 1278) shows no pool-attribution/quota-coverage document; hidden_files/provider-quota-registry.md has provider facts and usage views but not the pilot''s pool x (source, freshness, attribution) table","Issue #1189 body (fresh gh view 2026-10-27T11:25Z): OPEN, effort/s, priority/high; acceptance = coverage table exists, one session burn reconstructed or precise blocker, babysitter report spec updated on the issue"],"acceptance":["Coverage table file exists at files/pool-attribution-quota-coverage-2026-10-27.md covering every registry pool with quota source, observed freshness, attribution method or named gap, and the login each read reflects","One finished session''s pool + burn reconstructed end-to-end in that file with honest error bars, or a precise statement of why it cannot be and the dispatch-time instrumentation that would fix it","Babysitter report-spec comment posted on #1189 promising only pilot-proved figures; babysitter instruction section 4 aligned if it overpromises","Issue #1189 closed with evidence if criteria are met, labels cleaned; any gap that is another issue''s work (e.g. meta quota, openchamber #523 / PR #540) is linked, not duplicated"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1189","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1185","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1187"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries priority/high; it is a named dependency of babysitter v1 (#1185) and dispatch v1.1 (#1187) reporting, and its gaps (claude/meta quota reads) already force per-pool closures in dispatcher runs.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1189', '2026-10-27 11:27:07.201956+00', '2026-10-28 05:05:10.436806+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1386, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: backup-zed installed.txt unsorted find order (issue #946)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/946","title":"backup-zed: installed.txt is written in find/readdir order \u2014 the committed snapshot is unsorted and reshuffles between runs","number":946,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the settings.json/index.json copies in backup-zed.sh","the #854/#860 fixes already in the script"],"include":["backup-zed.sh installed.txt write pipeline ordering","the committed .zed/installed.txt order"]},"tests":["Scratch extensions dir: two runs byte-identical; shuffled creation order still yields sorted output; simulated find failure leaves committed file untouched"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search for backup-zed/installed.txt/sort returned no tracking issue; #854/#860 cover the zsh script_dir bug and the truncation-on-failed-find bug in the same write path, not output ordering","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"backup-zed.sh regenerates .zed/installed.txt in nondeterministic find order.","evidence":["Main 71fe33d, backup-zed.sh:25 find pipeline with no sort","sort -c .zed/installed.txt -> disorder at line 4 (focus-theme) in the committed file itself","Probe: entries created zebra/apple/mango/banana -> find emits banana, mango, apple, zebra"],"acceptance":["installed.txt written in a stable explicit order (e.g. LC_ALL=C sort) regardless of readdir order","Re-running backup-zed with an unchanged extensions dir produces a byte-identical installed.txt","#860 protections preserved: temp file + mv on success only; failed find leaves committed file untouched","Committed .zed/installed.txt regenerated/hand-sorted in the new order"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/946"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A committed snapshot whose value is clean diffs reshuffles on regeneration, making real extension changes unreviewable; the fix is one pipeline stage.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:946', '2026-10-27 11:27:40.152756+00', '2026-10-27 11:51:33.509625+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1387, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): Find panel stale match count — small fix', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1402","title":"id(web): Find panel match count goes stale when the document is edited \u2014 highlights update, the count does not","number":1402,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:27:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing prosemirror-search itself","redesigning the panel UI"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/search-panel.ts doc-change count refresh","pkgs/id/web/src/search-panel.test.ts regression tests"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id/web && bunx vitest run src/search-panel.test.ts"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (''match count search panel'', ''search-panel stale'', ''search panel'', all states) returned no issue tracking a stale find count; #718 (closed) covers the distinct panel-singleton teardown bug in the same file.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T11:27:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Find panel match count is recomputed only on query/replace actions, never on document edits, so it diverges from the (correct) highlight set while the panel is open.","evidence":["Vitest probe on main 37418e56 (real EditorView + createSearchPlugins(), richSchema; probe removed after run): COUNT AFTER SEARCH: 3 matches / DOC NOW: foo / COUNT AFTER EDIT: 3 matches (expected 1 match)","Code: search-panel.ts updateMatchCount is called only at lines 91 (syncQuery), 167, 184, 188 (replace paths); createSearchPlugins returns only search() + keymap \u2014 no view/update hook observes docChanged"],"acceptance":["With the Find panel open and a valid query, editing the document updates the match count label to the true count, including transitions to/from ''No results'' and the singular ''1 match'' form","No re-count on selection-only transactions (refresh gated on docChanged / search-state change)","Regression test in pkgs/id/web/src/search-panel.test.ts: open panel, multi-match query, edit doc, label reflects new count (decrease and increase)","Existing web vitest suite passes; panel open/close, replace and replace-all behaviour unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1402","pkgs/id/web/src/search-panel.ts updateMatchCount (line 64), syncQuery (line 91), createSearchPlugins (line 268)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The count is the user''s only occurrence signal during an edit session; a stale count sends them hunting for matches that no longer exist (or hides new ones).","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1402', '2026-10-27 11:28:31.309099+00', '2026-10-27 11:28:31.309099+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
