d or self-contained fix taken by the worker)","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1368"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Verified user-facing failure mode (infinite reconnect, no error state) on a normal-priority bug; requeued after holder silence past 2x deadline.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1368', '2026-10-27 13:54:37.448082+00', '2026-10-27 13:54:37.448082+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1404, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Small fix #559: schedule validator seconds parity with OpenCode minutesOf', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/559","title":"fix(routing): schedule validator accepts out-of-range seconds (09:30:99) that OpenCode drops, and refuses single-digit seconds (09:30:5) that OpenCode accepts","number":559,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:45:53Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the UI normalizer packages/ui/src/lib/routing/routeSchedules.ts (checked in the issue, not part of the defect)","any opencode-side change (already landed there)"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/routing/model-routes.js windowTimeMinutes + its tests"]},"tests":["openchamber routing/server test suite for model-routes (record exact command in the completion note)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fleet monitor reconciliation 2026-10-27T13:3xZ: live queue dump for repo-health-openchamber-pilot shows no task naming issue 559; the issue was filed at 13:19Z with queue/queued and no packet.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:45:53Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"OpenChamber''s server-side schedule validator accepts out-of-range seconds (silently dropped later by OpenCode, losing the whole schedule) and refuses single-digit seconds OpenCode accepts \u2014 port the opencode minutesOf parity (opencode#517/#528, PRs #518/#573 merged).","evidence":["Issue #559 body: model-routes.js:182-187 source, probe table (09:30:99 accepted vs OpenCode rejected; 09:30:5 refused vs OpenCode accepted), both call surfaces named (validateModelRoute + validateModelRouteSchedules via validateScheduleWindow)"],"acceptance":["validateModelRouteSchedules and validateModelRoute refuse window start/end seconds outside 0-59 with the ''must be a local time'' problem","Single-digit seconds (09:30:5) accepted, matching OpenCode","Regression tests cover both directions; existing routing tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/559","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/517","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/528"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Cross-repo parity remainder with a silent-data-loss direction (schedule dropped whole by OpenCode); normal priority per the issue labels.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:559', '2026-10-27 13:54:47.738482+00', '2026-10-27 15:53:10.110301+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1407, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): marks spanning inline HTML fragment on save — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1412","title":"id(web): marks spanning inline HTML are broken on save \u2014 links fragment around the tags, emphasis leaks &#32; entities","number":1412,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:28Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1407 image-atom mark handling","#880 linked-image linkHref carrying (already works)","#1045 unknown-mark policy for text nodes"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs save-side handling of marks across html_inline atoms (json_to_ast / create_marked_text / append_inline_child) and codec tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list/search (open + closed) for html_inline / ''inline HTML'' / html: no mark-spanning-html_inline issue exists. #943 (closed) introduced the html_inline node for unmarked tags; #1407 covers image atoms only; #968 (closed) is text-run re-nesting. Verified fresh this run on main 37418e56.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:28Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Marks spanning an html_inline atom fragment on save: links split per text run with tags outside the link, emphasis leaks &#32; entities.","evidence":["Probe on main 37418e56 (verbatim markdown.rs copy, comrak 0.56.0), hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-creator-a6/out3.log: ''[a <b>x</b> c](/y)'' parses to text''a ''[link], html_inline''<b>'', text''x''[link], html_inline''</b>'', text'' c''[link] but saves as ''[a ](/y)<b>[x](/y)</b>[ c](/y)''; ''[a <sup>2</sup> c](/y)'' likewise fragments","Same probe: ''*a <b>x</b> c*'' saves as ''*a&#32;*<b>*x*</b>*&#32;c*''; out2.log: ''[a <b>x</b>](/y)'' -> ''[a ](/y)<b>[x](/y)</b>'', stable fixpoint on re-save","Controls in the same probes round-trip clean: ''a <b>x</b> c'' (no marks), ''# a <sub>x</sub>'', ''[<b>x</b>](/y)'', ''**<b>x</b>**''; save html_inline arm markdown.rs:1360-1361 emits NodeValue::HtmlInline with no mark context, unlike the image arm''s #880 link special-case (:1308+)"],"acceptance":["[a <b>x</b> c](/y) and [a <sup>2</sup> c](/y) round-trip with the link intact as a single link span containing the inline HTML (exact markdown or a form re-parsing to the same PM structure)","*a <b>x</b> c* and strong/strikethrough equivalents save as a single mark span containing the tags, with no &#32; or other HTML entities introduced","Already-working cases stay working: unmarked inline HTML (a <b>x</b> c), single-run forms ([<b>x</b>](/y)), and the #943 sub/sup/u cases","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover mark-spanning-html_inline in both directions; existing web::markdown tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1412","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1407","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/943","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1360","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:421"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent rewrite on first open->save for ordinary imported markdown (linked terms with <sup>/<sub>/<b> inside link text); link scope and tag nesting invert, emphasis forms gain literal &#32; entities in user files, and the corrupted result is a stable fixpoint so nothing downstream notices.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1412', '2026-10-27 14:19:42.13309+00', '2026-10-27 16:47:56.144402+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1409, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 1 of design #1414 — persist + resume upstream HTTP sessions — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1415","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1414 \u2014 persist legacy HTTP upstream sessions and resume them after a cold restart","number":1415,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing session persistence in this triage task","any change to takeover behaviour (internal/daemon/takeover.go semantics stay as-is; reuse of pool/handoff.go resume calls only)","expiry fallback / record hygiene on config removal (Phase 2, issue #1416)","legacy SSE upstream sessions and modern-era (2026-07-28) sessions \u2014 no persistable session"],"include":["issue #1415 and design #1414 with the design doc it links","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/http.go and handoff.go, internal/pool/pool.go dial path and handoff.go resume call sites, internal/daemon/sessions.go persistence discipline"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./...; defining test from #1415: session established -> daemon SIGKILL -> restart -> first call succeeds, no second initialize upstream, original Mcp-Session-Id carried)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1415 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-27) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1415 \u2014 it did not exist before this run. Its dedupe key has never been enqueued (unlike #1385, whose key is poisoned by cancelled shadow task 1354 / bug #1298).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx cold restarts re-initialise every legacy HTTP upstream and leak one upstream session per server, because the upstream Mcp-Session-Id and client protocol state live only in memory and in the takeover handoff (pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 3). Design #1414 proposes persisting the resumable state (never resolved headers) in the daemon state dir and restoring through the existing takeover resume calls; Phase 1 (#1415) is the persistence + restore core.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 3 \u2014 ''A cold restart does not resume upstream sessions. The lease table is restored from sessions.json, but the upstream Mcp-Session-Id is kept only in memory and in the takeover handoff''","planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md Next row: ''Resume upstream sessions after a cold restart'' at status idea, no issue before #1414/#1415 (filed 2026-10-27)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/http.go \u2014 HTTPTransport.sessionID/negotiated in memory only; session ID adopted from response header at line ~156; HTTPHandoff.Headers documented as travelling over the takeover unix socket only","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/handoff.go \u2014 Client.SessionState() and mcpclient.Resume(t, s, o) already build a no-handshake resumed client; internal/pool/handoff.go:238,326 are the takeover call sites to reuse","pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon/sessions.go \u2014 SaveSessions/loadSessions precedent: versioned envelope, atomic tmp+rename, defaults.PrivateMode","Design issue #1414 (kind/design, user/review for the direction decision) with Phase 1 as its sub-issue #1415; #1415 filed with queue/queued + task/triage by the design architect, no live queue task existed at filing"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1415: scope confirmed against current main, state-file name and config-fingerprint field set settled or explicitly left open with reasons, and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If triage finds Phase 1 as scoped is not independently landable, say exactly why on the issue and propose the rescoped Phase 1 in the design doc''s terms \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state); the user/review direction decision stays on the design issue #1414, not on #1415"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1415","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1414","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1384"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 is the gate for the whole #1414 design: it proves persisted resume reuses the takeover path with no headers on disk. Normal priority per the design issue; the direction decision itself sits with Drew on #1414.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1415', '2026-10-27 14:22:57.426674+00', '2026-10-27 16:47:29.27535+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1410, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 2 of design #1414 — expiry fallback + record hygiene — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1416","title":"mcpx: Phase 2 of #1414 \u2014 resumed-session expiry fallback (404/401) and record hygiene","number":1416,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the fallback in this triage task","general legacy-client 404 handling beyond the resumed-session first request (roadmap robustness row / nix issues)","graceful-shutdown DELETE semantics, record TTL, dashboard visibility (Phase 3 open questions on #1414)"],"include":["issue #1416, design #1414, Phase 1 issue #1415 and its as-built persistence shape","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/http.go send/close paths, internal/pool reload and config-removal path, TerminateHTTPSession"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./...; defining tests from #1416: forgetful upstream -> resumed call succeeds with exactly one extra initialize; removal -> record gone after reload)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1416 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-27) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1416 \u2014 it did not exist before this run. Its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Persisted resume (#1415) can resurrect a session the upstream has already forgotten or whose credentials rotated while the daemon was down; today the send path has no 404 handling, so that surfaces as a raw caller error, and records for removed servers would linger. Design #1414 Phase 2 adds the drop-and-reinitialise-once fallback for the first request of a resumed session and record hygiene on config removal.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 3 \u2014 cold restart does not resume upstream sessions (the gap #1414/#1415 close; this phase makes resume safe when the session is already gone)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/http.go closeSession (~line 575): a 404 DELETE already counts as ''already forgotten'', not a failure \u2014 the send path has no equivalent 404 handling today","planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md ''Legacy client robustness'' row (proposed): ''Session 404, GET stream, SSE retry, string ids, stream timeout and the version header'' tracked via nix#203, nix#200, nix#201 \u2014 coordination target, not a duplicate","Issue #260 (closed): a removed server''s upstream HTTP session was never DELETEd on the takeover path; TerminateHTTPSession is the existing shape for ending a session nobody owns","Design issue #1414 with Phase 2 as its sub-issue #1416; #1416 filed with queue/queued + task/triage by the design architect, no live queue task existed at filing"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1416: scope confirmed against current main and against the legacy-client-robustness state, overlap with nix#200/nix#201/nix#203 resolved (narrowed if needed), dependency on Phase 1 #1415 recorded, and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If triage finds Phase 2 as scoped is not independently landable after Phase 1, say exactly why on the issue and propose the rescoped Phase 2 in the design doc''s terms \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1416","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1415","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1414","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/260"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 2 makes Phase 1''s resume safe to enable broadly: without the expiry fallback a forgotten upstream session turns a restart into a caller-visible failure. Normal priority; sequenced after Phase 1 (#1415).","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1416', '2026-10-27 14:23:07.893556+00', '2026-10-27 16:48:20.65364+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1411, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'small_fix(quota): guard non-finite timestamps in VS Code quotaProviders.ts helpers (#560)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/560","title":"fix(quota): VS Code port leaks non-finite timestamps \u2014 toTimestamp/normalizeTimestamp in quotaProviders.ts lack the #494 finite guard","number":560,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:23:23Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["calculateResetAfterSeconds and toUsageWindow (correct once helpers are guarded)","Web transformers.js (already fixed by #494)"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts"]},"tests":["Non-finite probe inputs return null after the fix for both helpers","Existing VS Code quota tests pass","bun run check:changed"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches (toTimestamp / non-finite timestamp) returned #494 (web only, closed by PR #501), #492 (the #489 port, different defect), #489/#483; no issue tracks the port''s non-finite timestamp leak","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:23:23Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"VS Code port quota timestamp helpers leak non-finite values (Infinity, -Infinity, NaN) as resetAt instead of null, the #494 defect that was fixed on the web side but never ported.","evidence":["Verified 2026-10-27 on main 3428a415d by verbatim-expression Node probe of both helpers copied from quotaProviders.ts: toTimestamp(Infinity)=Infinity, toTimestamp(-Infinity)=-Infinity, toTimestamp(JSON.parse(''1e999''))=Infinity, normalizeTimestamp(NaN)=NaN, normalizeTimestamp(Infinity)=Infinity","quotaProviders.ts:420-431 toTimestamp number branch has no Number.isFinite check; :2763-2766 normalizeTimestamp has no guard at all; web transformers.js toTimestamp/normalizeTimestamp both guard with Number.isFinite after #494","Downstream: port calculateResetAfterSeconds (:492-496) turns resetAt=Infinity into resetAfterSeconds=Infinity; :1134 expires: toTimestamp(oauthObject.expires) ?? undefined makes an infinite expiry a never-expiring credential"],"acceptance":["Port toTimestamp returns null for Infinity, -Infinity and NaN numeric inputs; finite numbers, strings and seconds->ms scaling unchanged","Port normalizeTimestamp returns null for Infinity, -Infinity and NaN; finite behavior unchanged","Regression tests cover the non-finite inputs for both helpers'' reachable paths","Existing VS Code quota tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/560","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/494"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent misreporting of reset times and a never-expiring credential expiry on a drifting upstream payload; no crash, normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:560', '2026-10-27 14:24:22.01642+00', '2026-10-27 15:29:46.599526+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1412, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'feat(core): QuotaSnapshot derivation with a single staleness contract (design #587, phase 1)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/588","title":"feat(core): QuotaSnapshot derivation with a single staleness contract (design #587, phase 1)","number":588,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Any change to model-route.ts selection behaviour","External quota polling or provider APIs","UI changes"],"include":["packages/core snapshot derivation module + unit tests"]},"tests":["bun test from packages/core (targeted snapshot tests)","bun run check from repo root"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Design issue #587 filed this run after reading #566/#567/#568/#6 in full; no existing issue covers a standalone snapshot derivation \u2014 #568''s telemetry acceptance presupposes it without specifying it.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Three routing features (#566/#567/#568) each presuppose a quota % signal with a staleness rule, but no shared snapshot value exists; quota knowledge in the fork is reporting-only.","evidence":["model-usage.ts windowReport() already derives percent/remaining/resetRule for reporting; selection path never reads it","model-route.ts weightOf(): quota enters selection only as reactive DEMOTED_FACTOR 0.01 demotion after quota errors"],"acceptance":["Snapshot derivation exists in packages/core alongside model-usage.ts, reusing windowReport() rather than duplicating its percent/remaining computation","Unit tests cover: normal window percent+remaining against hand-computed fixture; missing limit -> percent null; missing windowHours -> percent null; stale observation -> stale true; fresh -> stale false; resetAt derivable and non-derivable cases","No behaviour change: no routing/gating/UI code consumes snapshots","bun run check from repo root passes, or pre-existing failures on devtoday/main named in closing note"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/588","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/587","packages/core/src/model-usage.ts windowReport","packages/core/src/model-plan.ts QuotaWindow"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Unblocks #566 gates and #568 controller on a shared contract; pure addition, no behaviour risk, so normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:588', '2026-10-27 14:25:36.081012+00', '2026-10-27 17:45:14.101562+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1413, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'feat(core): per-layer weight attribution in the route decision log (design #587, phase 2)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/589","title":"feat(core): per-layer weight attribution in the route decision log (design #587, phase 2)","number":589,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Selection behaviour changes of any kind","New UI surfaces beyond existing route-review tooling","Gate implementation (#566 owns gates; this issue only adds the log slot)"],"include":["packages/core model-route.ts traced weight computation + decision detail","packages/core model-route-review.ts surfacing","packages/core tests"]},"tests":["bun test from packages/core (targeted route tests, unmodified existing suite)","bun run check from repo root"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Design issue #587 filed this run; #567 and #568 both require this inspection/audit surface in their acceptance criteria but neither files it as standalone work.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Route selections cannot be explained after the fact: the decision log records final effective weights but not which layer (schedule, prefer, tuner adjustment, quota demotion) produced them.","evidence":["model-route.ts nextTarget records ModelRouteLog decision detail with final weights only \u2014 no layer attribution","model-route-review.ts:139 already frames effective weight per candidate as a review concern"],"acceptance":["Decision-log detail includes per-layer weights (base, scheduled, prefer, adjustment, demotion) plus gate-verdict slot for every candidate; additive fields only","Test proves traced weights equal weightOf weights for: scheduled rule in force, prefer override present, adjustment active, demoted target","No behaviour change: existing packages/core route tests pass unmodified","Route-review output shows attribution for a recorded decision","bun run check from repo root passes, or pre-existing failures on devtoday/main named in closing note"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/589","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/587","packages/core/src/model-route.ts weightOf/nextTarget","packages/core/src/model-route-review.ts:139"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Shared audit surface for #567 inspection and #568 controller logging; observability-only, no behaviour risk, so normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:589', '2026-10-27 14:25:41.818371+00', '2026-10-27 18:25:55.155584+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1414, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): image alt-text markup stripped on save — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1417","title":"id(web): inline markup inside image alt text is stripped on save \u2014 emphasis and code spans flattened to plain text","number":1417,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1407 marks wrapping an image (different root cause)","#880/#893 linked and sized image handling","#1045 unknown-mark policy for text nodes"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs parse/save handling of image alt text and codec tests","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts only if the chosen representation requires schema support"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''alt'', ''alt text image'': no alt-markup issue exists. #1407 covers marks AROUND an image (different root cause: Image arm ignoring active_marks); #873 was the retired HTML img-tag emission path; #880/#893 are linked/sized images. Verified fresh this run on main 37418e56.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Image alt-text markup (emphasis, strong, code spans, nested links) is flattened to plain text by the codec''s alt extraction on parse.","evidence":["Probe on main 37418e56 (verbatim markdown.rs copy, comrak 0.56.0), hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-0854-laneA/out.log + out3.log: ''![*alt* text](/x.png)'' -> ''![alt text](/x.png)''; ''![**bold alt**](/x.png)'' -> ''![bold alt](/x.png)''; ''![a `code` b](/x.png)'' -> ''![a code b](/x.png)''; ''![a [link](/y) b](/x.png)'' -> ''![a link b](/x.png)''","Same probe, direct comrak parse->format_commonmark controls with the codec''s options preserve all of these byte-for-byte \u2014 the loss is in the codec, not the renderer","Parse Image arm markdown.rs:354-360 builds attrs.alt via get_text_content (:710), flattening the alt subtree to text literals; save image arm :1308 re-emits the stored plain string"],"acceptance":["![*alt* text](/x.png), ![**bold alt**](/x.png) and ![a `code` b](/x.png) round-trip with alt markup preserved (exact markdown or a form re-parsing to the same alt structure)","Representation is coherent with editor.ts''s plain-string alt attribute; any editor-side limitation is documented in the resolution","Nested-link alt (![a [link](/y) b](/x.png)) is preserved or its flattening is explicitly decided and documented","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover emphasis, strong and code-span alt text in both directions; existing web::markdown tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1417","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1407","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:354","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:710","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1308"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent formatting loss on first open->save for ordinary markdown (alt text with emphasis or code spans is common in imported notes/docs), and the flattened result is a stable fixpoint so nothing downstream notices.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1417', '2026-10-27 14:25:42.575205+00', '2026-10-28 00:37:28.373044+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1415, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Triage #951: #939 flag-shaped guards untested in clean.sh, git-discover-repos, git-maintain-repos, spotlight-exclude-artifacts', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/939","title":"fix(scripts): reject flag-shaped values for value-taking options (#930)","number":939,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:58:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/951","title":"tests: PR #939''s flag-shaped-value guards have no regression tests in clean.sh, git-discover-repos, git-maintain-repos, or spotlight-exclude-artifacts","number":951,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the tests inside this triage task","Behavior changes to the scripts (a non-rejecting guard found by probing is reported on #951 as a bug)"],"include":["Triage of issue #951 against current main","Routing: follow-up packet for the test suites"]},"tests":["n/a \u2014 triage task; the follow-up packet carries the test work"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Filed this run by pr-diff-review after dedupe searches: ''brew-repair''/''flag-shaped'' issue lists show #930 and #941 closed and no open issue covering test coverage for the #939 guards in these four scripts; the brew-list leftover from PR #933 is already tracked separately as #949 (not duplicated).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T13:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Four of the six scripts fixed in PR #939 have no regression test for their new flag-shaped-value guards.","evidence":["PR #939 diff (commit 7c007220): parse-guard changes in clean.sh, git-discover-repos, git-maintain-repos, spotlight-exclude-artifacts, pkgs/opencode-share/opencode-share.sh, symlinker.sh; test changes only in opencode-share.test.sh and symlinker.test.sh","Current main grep over *.test.sh: flag-shaped cases exist only for opencode-share (--source) and symlinker (5 options); git-discover-repos.test.sh (PR #943) tests bad --path exit status for #940, with no flag-shaped case","Manual probes 2026-10-27 on current main: clean.sh --path --dry-run, git-maintain-repos --jobs --dry-run and spotlight-exclude-artifacts --path --dry-run each print ''<script>: <option> requires a value'' \u2014 behavior correct today, unpinned by tests","Source PR #939 is the work subject for the finding; issue #951 is the filed tracking issue"],"acceptance":["Triage note on #951 confirming (or refuting, with evidence) that no flag-shaped regression tests exist for the four named scripts on current main","Follow-up packet enqueued for the test work, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/951","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/939","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/930","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/941"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Coverage gap for a safety guard on destructive/scan tools; the underlying behavior works today, so low priority, but the #930 failure mode (a swallowed --dry-run) is severe if it regresses.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:951', '2026-10-27 14:25:54.665049+00', '2026-10-27 16:52:17.240967+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1416, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'refactor(core): extract one shared governance catalog helper (dedupe PR #569''s two governanceConfig copies)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/591","title":"refactor(core): PR #569 duplicated the governance catalog construction in session.ts and session/session.ts \u2014 extract one shared helper","number":591,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Any behaviour change to ModelGovernance.assertAllowed judging","Changes to ModelRouteExpansion.matchingModels (#530''s shared module)"],"include":["One shared governanceConfig helper in packages/core (e.g. alongside ModelGovernance)","Both call sites (session.ts, session/session.ts) switched to the shared helper"]},"tests":["bun test from packages/core (model-governance and session suites, unmodified)","bun run check from repo root"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Filed this run (lane B pr-diff-review) after reviewing PR #569''s diff and verifying both copies verbatim on current main c3c13e0015. Issue searches 2026-10-27 for governanceConfig/catalog duplication returned nothing; #530 (closed) covered expansion sharing, not this catalog construction.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #569 introduced the governance provider-catalog construction as two duplicated copies (session.ts and session/session.ts) that can drift, undermining the one-shared-implementation principle #530 was filed to establish.","evidence":["PR #569 diff adds the same catalog-building body to packages/core/src/session.ts and packages/core/src/session/session.ts, growing the previously small duplicated governanceEntries helper in each file","Current main c3c13e0015: session.ts:293 governanceConfig used at :326; session/session.ts:117 governanceConfig used at :158 and :186","The snapshot-to-Catalog new Map(Array.from(snapshot.records, ...)) construction appears verbatim in both files"],"acceptance":["The context-to-entries+catalog construction exists exactly once in packages/core/src and both session.ts and session/session.ts call the shared helper","Behaviour unchanged: uninitialized location yields {entries: [], catalog: undefined}; no provider service yields entries with catalog undefined; orElseSucceed fallback semantics preserved","Existing packages/core model-governance and session tests pass unmodified","grep for the snapshot-to-Catalog construction in packages/core/src returns exactly one site"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/591","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/569","packages/core/src/session.ts governanceConfig (line 293)","packages/core/src/session/session.ts governanceConfig (line 117)","packages/core/src/session/model-governance.ts Catalog"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Pure refactor of duplicated logic introduced by a merged PR; low priority and low risk, but drift between the two copies would make route governance judge the same route against different catalogs depending on entry point.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:591', '2026-10-27 14:32:30.049722+00', '2026-10-27 15:52:00.605139+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1417, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'pr-shepherd(core): integrate PRs #552 + #583 (ConfigVariable.substitute) so neither security fix is lost', '{"kind":"pr_shepherd","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":["merge-conflict-resolution"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/590","title":"pr-shepherd(core): PRs #552 and #583 both rewrite ConfigVariable.substitute''s env pass \u2014 land them as one integrated change so neither protection is lost","number":590,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing either fix''s intended semantics (#546 authored-range protection, #547 comment guard)","Fixing #556 (trailing-comment {file:...}) \u2014 related but separate issue"],"include":["packages/core/src/config/variable.ts integrated env/substituteFiles implementation","packages/core/test/config/config.test.ts combined regression tests","Closing the superseded PR with a cross-reference"]},"tests":["bun test test/config/config.test.ts from packages/core (both PRs'' new tests plus the combined case)","bun run check from repo root"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Filed this run (lane B pr-diff-review) after reviewing both diffs in full: identical base blob for variable.ts, incompatible env() return types, same test insertion anchor. Issue searches 2026-10-27 found only the individual bug issues #546/#547 and unrelated #556; no consolidation issue existed.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Open PRs #552 and #583 both rewrite ConfigVariable.substitute''s env pass from the same base with incompatible signatures; landing them independently risks losing one of the two security protections.","evidence":["PR #552 (OPEN, head dab74133): env() returns Substituted {text, authored}; substituteFiles signature changes from (input, text: string) to (input, substituted: Substituted)","PR #583 (OPEN, head 24128526): env() returns string with a // comment-line guard inside the env loop","Both diffs start from variable.ts blob a98bdcd7dbac and insert tests at the same anchor in packages/core/test/config/config.test.ts (after old line 1508)","Current main c3c13e0015 still has the pre-fix env() (variable.ts:26-45), so neither protection has landed"],"acceptance":["One integrated change contains both protections: authored-range tracking for the file pass (#552) and the // comment guard for the env pass (#583)","Both PRs'' new regression tests pass in the same tree, plus a combined case: comment line containing an env token and a {file:...} reference neither substitutes the env value nor reads the file","The superseded PR is closed with a comment linking the integrated PR and issue #590; #546 and #547 both close when the integrated change merges"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/590","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/552","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/583","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/546","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/547","packages/core/src/config/variable.ts ConfigVariable.substitute"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Two security fixes to the same function will conflict on merge; a one-sided resolution silently reintroduces either an arbitrary-file-read (#546) or a comment leak/breakout (#547). Normal priority, medium risk due to merge-resolution hazard.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:pr-set:developing-today/opencode:552-583', '2026-10-27 14:32:45.788175+00', '2026-10-27 17:05:22.067384+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
