fied via agent.tasks query 2026-10-27T14:45Z)"],"acceptance":["Verdict comment on #1409: door evidence re-verified (models.dev catalog + probe record) or refuted with specifics","Routing recorded: either handed to the #1342 controlled-test mechanism with the next action named, or closed/routed with the reason stated","No pool config change is made by this triage task itself"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1409","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1342"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Pool-composition hypothesis with quantified evidence; normal priority \u2014 it changes no behaviour until the #1342 gate passes it.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1409', '2026-10-27 14:35:00.390401+00', '2026-10-28 08:43:17.104519+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1419, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): mark edge-space span loses its mark on reopen — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1418","title":"id(web): a marked span starting or ending with a space loses its mark on reopen when a word character touches it \u2014 saved &#32; form cannot reparse","number":1418,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:47:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1407 marks wrapping an image (different root cause)","#1412 marks spanning html_inline nodes (different root cause)","#1045 unknown-mark policy"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs save-direction mark construction (create_marked_text / insert_marked_chain) and codec tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''&#32;'', ''flanking'', ''edge space emphasis'': #1407 (marks around an image) and #1412 (marks spanning html_inline) leak &#32; by different root causes; #968 (closed, nested-mark fragmentation) and #981 (closed, softbreak-crossing spans) are different shapes. This is a single flat span whose edge space plus a word-character outside neighbour makes the saved form unparseable. Verified fresh this run on main 37418e56.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:47:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Delimiter-mark spans with an edge space emit an &#32; delimited form that fails CommonMark flanking on reparse whenever a word character touches the span on that side; the mark is destroyed on reopen.","evidence":["Probe on main 37418e56 (verbatim markdown.rs copy, comrak 0.56.0, compiled/run on the laptop per the no-sandbox-build rule), hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-0927-laneA-out4.log: PM `a`+em(` b`) -> save `a*&#32;b*` -> reopen plain text `a* b*`, second save `a\\* b\\*` (non-fixpoint); strong -> `a**&#32;b**` same; strikethrough same; `a `+em(`b `)+`c` -> `a *b&#32;*c` -> plain text `a *b *c`; em+strong and heading contexts fail identically","Same probe, controls round-trip PM-identical: span at paragraph start/end, space or punctuation neighbour, span padded on both edges with spaced neighbours (`a *&#32;b&#32;* c`)","Authored-markdown control in the same probe: literal `a*&#32;b*` parses to plain text while `a *&#32;b*` parses to em(` b`) \u2014 the saved form fails CommonMark flanking at the parser level","Save path: create_marked_text markdown.rs:1737 builds wrappers (em/strong/strikethrough :1762-1764) around the run''s full text including edge spaces; insert_marked_chain :1673"],"acceptance":["PM `a` + em(` b`) saves to a form that reopens as the identical PM doc (mark preserved, no literal delimiters in text); same for strong and strikethrough","Trailing-edge mirror: `a ` + em(`b `) + `c` round-trips PM-identical and byte-fixpoint","Combined em+strong edge-space span and the heading context round-trip","Currently-working cases do not regress: span padded on both edges with spaced neighbours, space/punctuation/boundary neighbours, and the #953/#968/#981 mark tests","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover the matrix; existing web::markdown tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1418","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1407","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1412","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1737","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1762"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent destruction of ordinary editor formatting (italicize a space-leading word mid-sentence) plus literal delimiter characters injected into the visible text; non-fixpoint, so later saves compound it with backslash escapes.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1418', '2026-10-27 14:39:56.684033+00', '2026-10-27 16:50:12.650531+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1421, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): edge whitespace stripped on reopen, whitespace-only paragraph deleted — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1420","title":"id(web): edge whitespace in text runs is written on save but stripped on reopen \u2014 a whitespace-only paragraph is deleted outright","number":1420,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1418 marked-span edge spaces inside delimiters (different mechanism)","#1307 Plain/.txt mode byte-faithfulness","#1045 unknown-mark policy"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs save/parse handling of text-run edge whitespace and codec tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''whitespace paragraph'', ''space-only'', ''leading spaces'', ''trailing spaces'', ''empty paragraph'': no edge-whitespace issue exists. #1418 is the marked-span counterpart (edge spaces inside delimiters, different mechanism and fix); #1045 is the unknown-mark policy; #1388 is hard breaks inside headings. Verified fresh this run on main 37418e56.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Unmarked text-run edge whitespace is unrepresentable in markdown, but the codec writes it verbatim on save instead of normalizing or protecting it, so reopen silently loses it \u2014 and deletes a whitespace-only paragraph entirely.","evidence":["Probe on main 37418e56 (verbatim markdown.rs copy, comrak 0.56.0, compiled/run on the laptop per the no-sandbox-build rule), hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-0927-laneA-out2.log: PM paragraph ''  leading spaces'' -> OUT ''  leading spaces\\n'' -> PM2 ''leading spaces'' (non-fixpoint)","hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-0927-laneA-out3.log: PM paragraphs [''   '', ''x''] -> OUT ''   \\n\\nx\\n'' -> PM2 only [''x''] (paragraph deleted); PM ''foo   '' -> PM2 ''foo''; PM ''foo''+hard_break+''  bar'' -> OUT ''foo\\\\\\n  bar\\n'' -> PM2 ''bar''; table header '' A '' / cell '' x '' -> OUT ''|  A  |'' / ''|  x  |'' -> PM2 ''A'' / ''x''","The saved bytes contain the spaces in every case; the loss is on reparse (markdown_to_prosemirror / comrak block parsing), while marked spans protect edge spaces with &#32; entities \u2014 unmarked run edges have no equivalent protection"],"acceptance":["The five probe cases (leading spaces, trailing spaces, after-hard_break spaces, table-cell padding, whitespace-only paragraph) behave per one pinned policy across open->save->open, documented in the resolution","The whitespace-only paragraph no longer silently vanishes on reopen: it round-trips (e.g. as an empty paragraph) or is normalized away at save so the first saved file is already the fixpoint","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover the five cases; existing web::markdown tests pass","Marked-span edge-space handling (#1418) is unaffected"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1420","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1418","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1045","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1057","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1133"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Mostly cosmetic loss (typed indentation, trailing spaces), but the whitespace-only-paragraph case deletes a whole block on reopen, and every case makes the first save a non-fixpoint the user cannot see coming.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1420', '2026-10-27 14:43:05.729438+00', '2026-10-27 16:52:38.579664+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1422, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: parseTime bare-epoch seconds read as milliseconds (#592)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/592","title":"fix(core): MessagingTemplate.parseTime reads epoch-seconds timestamps as milliseconds \u2014 a 10-digit since/until silently becomes January 1970","number":592,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:43:53Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["relative-age and ISO parsing (verified correct)","the quota-reset message parsers (#532/#533)"],"include":["packages/core/src/messaging/template.ts parseTime bare-digit branch","packages/schema/src/messaging.ts since/until annotations if the contract is documented there","regression tests in packages/core/test (messaging / template)"]},"tests":["bun test for messaging suites from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for parseTime / epoch seconds / timestamp since returned no covering issue","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:43:53Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"parseTime''s bare-digit branch assumes milliseconds for every 10+ digit value, so epoch-seconds inputs are silently misread as January 1970 while 9-digit seconds are rejected \u2014 an undocumented, internally inconsistent contract feeding four filter sites.","evidence":["packages/core/src/messaging/template.ts parseTime: /^\\d{10,}$/ branch returns Number(input) unscaled as milliseconds","Probe (laptop, real module, main e82aa33071): ''1767225600'' -> 1767225600 (1970-01-21), ''1767225600000'' -> 2026-01-01, ''999999999'' -> undefined, ISO and ''2h'' forms correct","packages/core/src/messaging.ts:769-774, 823-824, 1752-1753, 1826-1827 since/until + hiddenSince/hiddenUntil filters only error when parseTime returns undefined, so a mis-scaled value passes silently","packages/schema/src/messaging.ts:167 documents since only as ''ISO time or relative age such as 2h or 3d'' \u2014 the bare-epoch form is undocumented"],"acceptance":["No bare-epoch input is silently read as a 1970 instant: parseTime(''1767225600'') and parseTime(''1767225600000'') agree on the 2026-01-01 instant, or the seconds form is rejected so callers raise Invalid time","The bare-epoch contract is documented in the schema annotation and/or the parseTime doc comment","Regression tests cover 9-, 10- and 13-digit inputs alongside ISO and relative forms; existing messaging tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/592"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The since/until filters back message and log search; a seconds-form timestamp quietly disables the time bound (or empties an until query) with no error. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:592', '2026-10-27 14:44:40.305442+00', '2026-10-27 18:54:56.385383+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1425, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): tab/newline destinations corrupted on save (%09 / link destroyed) — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1423","title":"id(web): link/image destinations containing a tab or newline are corrupted on save \u2014 tab becomes %09, newline destroys the link (the #1019 fix only handles spaces)","number":1423,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1019 space destinations (already fixed)","#1348 placeholder collision with document text (keep its safety property, do not redesign)","Text-run edge whitespace (#1420) and marked-span edge spaces (#1418)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs substitute_spaced_destinations trigger condition and codec tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline web::markdown (targeted)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for destination tab/newline/%09 and the backlog: #1019 (closed) fixed spaces only via substitute_spaced_destinations; #1348 covers placeholder collision with document text, a different defect; #1420/#1418 are text-run/mark edge whitespace, unrelated mechanisms. Verified fresh this run on main 37418e56.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The #1019 destination protection is keyed to a literal space only, so tab- and newline-bearing destinations reach comrak''s renderer unprotected and are percent-encoded (tab) or mangled into a link-destroying form (newline).","evidence":["Probe on main 37418e56 (verbatim markdown.rs copy, comrak 0.56.0, compiled/run on the laptop per the no-sandbox-build rule), hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-1027-laneA-out.log: angle-dest-tab IN ''[x](</a\\tb>)'' -> OUT ''[x](/a%09b)'' pm_same=false; angle-dest-newline IN ''[x](</a\\nb>)'' -> OUT ''[x](/a% Ab)'' fixpoint=false pm_same=false, PM2 is plain text (link destroyed); image-angle-dest-newline and ref-def-angle-newline fail the same way","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1091 \u2014 substitute_spaced_destinations skips destinations without a literal space: if !url.contains('' '') { continue; }; the restore step (:1070-:1072) already writes raw destinations in angle form, which parses back byte-identical for tab/newline destinations","Controls in the same probe: %0A and %20 destinations round-trip unchanged; the failure is specific to raw tab/newline characters in the destination"],"acceptance":["[x](</a\\tb>) and the image form round-trip open->save->open with the href byte-identical and the saved form in angle brackets (no %09)","[x](</a\\nb>), the image form, and the reference-definition form ([r]: </a\\nb>) round-trip with the link intact on reopen (no ''% '' mangling, no link loss)","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover tab and newline destinations for links, images, and reference definitions; existing web::markdown tests pass, including the #1019 spaced-destination tests","The widened trigger does not regress #1348''s placeholder-collision concern (placeholder tokens remain collision-safe)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1423","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1019","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1348","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1091","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1081"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent data corruption on save in the same class as #1019: a tab destination is silently rewritten and a newline destination loses the link entirely, triggered by simply opening and saving an authored document.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1423', '2026-10-27 14:53:15.882445+00', '2026-10-27 16:56:26.969951+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1426, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): pipe inside code span splits table cell on open — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1424","title":"id(web): a pipe inside an inline code span in a table cell splits the cell on open \u2014 code mark destroyed, phantom column, trailing fragment dropped","number":1424,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:53:49Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing GFM table semantics for rows with genuinely more cells than the header (spec-conformant drop)","plain-text \\| cell escaping (works today)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs table parse/save handling for code spans containing pipes","round-trip fixpoint regression tests in the same file"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id && cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (table tests)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (table cell pipe / code span table / reference definition / blockquote empty, all states) this run: #1044 is the no-header-row table bug (different), #1004 covers unused link reference definitions, #1002 covers blockquote phantom lines, #954 covers fenced->indented rewrite; no issue tracks a pipe inside a code span splitting a table cell.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T14:53:49Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Table rows are split on unescaped pipes before inline parsing, so a pipe inside a code span breaks the cell: code mark lost, phantom column on save, trailing fragment dropped when the header is narrower.","evidence":["Round-trip probe on main 37418e56 against the codec''s own markdown_to_prosemirror/prosemirror_to_markdown (standalone harness compiled from src/web/markdown.rs, which depends only on comrak + serde_json): input row | `a|b` | c | under a 2-column header parses to THREE plain-text cells \"`a\", \"b`\", \"c\" \u2014 no code mark in the PM doc","Save of that doc emits | \\`a | b\\` | c | \u2014 phantom column, code span destroyed","1-column variant (| A | header, | `a|b` | row): the fragment after the pipe is dropped entirely on save (column count taken from header)","Control: plain-text escaped pipe a\\|b in a cell round-trips correctly today; footnote references and pipes in link titles were not part of this finding"],"acceptance":["Code spans containing pipes survive open->save in table cells: one cell, code mark intact, column count unchanged","The 1-column-header case no longer drops cell content","New round-trip fixpoint tests cover pipe-in-code-span in body cell, header cell, and as a cell''s only content","Existing table tests pass unmodified (test_table, test_table_with_formatting, test_roundtrip_table, test_table_alignment_roundtrip, table-cell does-not-panic tests)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1424","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs commonmark_options:81-91 (table extension :86), NodeValue::Table conversion :438, prosemirror_to_markdown :1057","pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs:147 (codec entry point used by the web editor)"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent data corruption (restructured table, lost code formatting, possible content deletion) in a supported construct combination \u2014 tables documenting shell pipelines, bitwise OR, or type unions commonly contain pipes inside code spans.","timebox_minutes":25}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1424', '2026-10-27 14:58:26.613633+00', '2026-10-28 08:44:32.253395+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1427, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'small_fix(quota): clamp usedPercent to [0,100] in web OpenAI provider (#566)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/566","title":"fix(quota): web OpenAI provider leaks out-of-range usedPercent \u2014 wham used_percent passed through unclamped, unlike the Codex provider on the same endpoint","number":566,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:06:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["codex.js (already clamped)","VS Code quotaProviders.ts (separate issues filed this run for its own gaps)"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/openai.js","a new targeted test for the OpenAI provider windows"]},"tests":["used_percent 150 -> usedPercent 100","used_percent -5 -> usedPercent 0 and remainingPercent 100","In-range used_percent unchanged; missing field stays null","Existing quota tests still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''openai used_percent clamp'', ''usedPercent clamp'', ''clamp Cursor VS Code'', ''clamp VS Code ClinePass'', ''clamp google antigravity VS Code'' on 2026-10-27 returned no issue covering openai.js; #516/#551 covered codex.js only","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:06:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The web OpenAI quota provider leaks out-of-range usedPercent because it passes wham used_percent through unclamped and uncoerced.","evidence":["openai.js:56 usedPercent: primary.used_percent ?? null; :63 usedPercent: secondary.used_percent ?? null \u2014 no toNumber, no clamp (main 3428a415d)","codex.js:94,102,134 clamp the same fields from the same endpoint via clampPercent(toNumber(...))","formatters.js:40-46 toUsageWindow stores usedPercent verbatim and derives remainingPercent as Math.max(0, 100 - usedPercent) only","Laptop probe (~/git/fleet/probe-quota-clamp-20261027/probe.mjs, laptop fork at 3428a415d, real toUsageWindow): 150 -> usedPercent=150 remainingPercent=0; -5 -> usedPercent=-5 remainingPercent=105; 42 -> 42/58","No openai.test.js exists under packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/"],"acceptance":["openai.js coerces used_percent with toNumber and clamps to [0,100] for both primary and secondary windows, matching codex.js; missing/non-numeric stays null","Targeted tests pin 150 -> 100, -5 -> 0 (remainingPercent 100), in-range unchanged, missing stays null","Existing quota tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/566"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent misreporting of OpenAI/Codex usage in the primary Usage surface; same defect class as the seven clamp fixes merged today, normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:566', '2026-10-27 15:06:17.999553+00', '2026-10-27 16:23:44.226318+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1428, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'small_fix(quota): clamp usedPercent to [0,100] in VS Code ClinePass provider (#567)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/567","title":"fix(quota): VS Code ClinePass provider leaks out-of-range usedPercent \u2014 percentUsed never clamped in the port, the web provider clamps since #512","number":567,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:10:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Web cline-pass.js (already clamped)","Other VS Code providers (separate issues filed this run for their own gaps)"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts fetchClinePassQuota","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts ClinePass tests"]},"tests":["percentUsed 150 -> usedPercent 100","percentUsed -5 -> usedPercent 0 and remainingPercent 100","percentUsed ''150'' (string) -> usedPercent 100","Existing VS Code quota tests still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''clamp VS Code ClinePass'' and ''usedPercent clamp'' on 2026-10-27 returned no VS Code ClinePass item; git show --stat 93ceeba0a confirms #550 touched only the web cline-pass.js + test","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:10:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The VS Code ClinePass port leaks out-of-range usedPercent because it kept the web provider''s parse but dropped its clamp.","evidence":["quotaProviders.ts:3557-3558 parse with no clamp; :3561-3565 passes usedPercent verbatim to toUsageWindow (main 3428a415d)","quotaProviders.ts:498-512 toUsageWindow stores usedPercent as given; remainingPercent = Math.max(0, 100 - usedPercent) only","Web parity: cline-pass.js:27 clampPercent, :83-86 identical parse + clampPercent(rawUsedPercent)","quotaProviders.test.ts:630ff ClinePass tests cover 43/17/8 and ''0''/''51'' strings, no out-of-range value"],"acceptance":["fetchClinePassQuota clamps parsed percentUsed to [0,100] via the existing clampPercent helper; unparseable entries still skipped","Tests pin 150 -> 100, -5 -> 0 (remainingPercent 100), string ''150'' clamped, in-range unchanged","Existing VS Code quota tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/567","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/512"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"VS Code is a primary surface; its ClinePass reading disagrees with the web reading of the same account on out-of-range payloads. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:567', '2026-10-27 15:08:08.727271+00', '2026-10-27 15:15:23.028449+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1429, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'small_fix(quota): clamp usedPercent to [0,100] in VS Code Cursor provider (#569)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/569","title":"fix(quota): VS Code Cursor provider leaks out-of-range usedPercent on the individual-plan path \u2014 totalPercentUsed never clamped, the web provider clamps it since #517","number":569,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:14:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Web cursor.js (already clamped)","VS Code Cursor enterprise windows (already clamped)"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts fetchCursorQuota non-enterprise path","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts Cursor tests"]},"tests":["totalPercentUsed 150 -> usedPercent 100","totalPercentUsed -5 -> usedPercent 0 and remainingPercent 100","totalPercentUsed 42 unchanged","Existing VS Code quota tests still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''clamp Cursor VS Code'' and ''usedPercent clamp'' on 2026-10-27 returned no VS Code Cursor item; git show --stat 372388d31 confirms #555 touched only the web cursor.js + test","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:14:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The VS Code Cursor individual-plan path leaks out-of-range usedPercent because totalPercentUsed is never clamped.","evidence":["quotaProviders.ts:2559-2560 toNumber(planUsage.totalPercentUsed) passed verbatim to toUsageWindow (main 3428a415d)","quotaProviders.ts:498-512 toUsageWindow stores usedPercent as given; remainingPercent = Math.max(0, 100 - usedPercent) only","Same-file enterprise paths clamp at :2517,2522; web cursor.js percentFromSpend clamps the explicit value since #517","quotaProviders.test.ts:2045 exercises totalPercentUsed 42 only; the web fix added out-of-range cases to cursor.test.js"],"acceptance":["VS Code Cursor individual-plan path clamps totalPercentUsed to [0,100] via the existing clampPercent helper; missing stays null","Tests pin 150 -> 100, -5 -> 0 (remainingPercent 100), in-range 42 unchanged","Existing VS Code quota tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/569","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/517"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Individual-plan Cursor is the common case on a primary surface; renders >100% or negative usage for accounts the web UI now reports correctly. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:569', '2026-10-27 15:09:17.230613+00', '2026-10-27 15:15:29.518837+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1430, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'small_fix(quota): clamp usedPercent to [0,100] in VS Code Google and Antigravity paths (#570)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/570","title":"fix(quota): VS Code Google and Antigravity paths leak usedPercent above 100 \u2014 remainingFraction derivation clamps only the lower bound, the web transforms clamp both since #507","number":570,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:18:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Web google/antigravity transforms (already clamped)","Other VS Code providers (separate issues filed this run)"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts Google buckets/models and Antigravity groups/models derivations","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts Google/Antigravity tests"]},"tests":["remainingFraction -0.2 -> usedPercent 100 on a Google path and an Antigravity path","remainingFraction 0.4 -> usedPercent 60 unchanged; 1.2 -> usedPercent 0","Existing VS Code quota tests still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''clamp google antigravity VS Code'' and ''usedPercent clamp'' on 2026-10-27 returned no VS Code Google/Antigravity item; git show --stat fc8ecedf2 confirms #541 touched only the web transforms + tests","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:18:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The VS Code Google and Antigravity quota paths leak usedPercent above 100 because their remainingFraction derivation clamps only the lower bound.","evidence":["quotaProviders.ts:1298,1327,1473,1550 identical one-sided derivation Math.max(0, 100 - remainingPercent) (main 3428a415d)","Web parity: google/transforms.js:47,73 and antigravity/transforms.js:24,138 clamp both bounds since #507/#541; VS Code Ollama path :2374 also clamps both bounds","Laptop probe (~/git/fleet/probe-quota-clamp-20261027/probe.mjs) of the exact derivation: remainingFraction -0.2 -> usedPercent 120, 0.4 -> 60, 1.2 -> 0"],"acceptance":["All four derivation sites (:1298, :1327, :1473, :1550) clamp derived usedPercent to [0,100]; missing-fraction null behavior unchanged","Tests pin a Google and an Antigravity path: remainingFraction -0.2 -> 100, 0.4 -> 60, 1.2 -> 0","Existing VS Code quota tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/570","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/507"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Headline Google/Antigravity providers on the VS Code surface render >100% usage for marginally-over-limit buckets while the web UI reports the same account clamped. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:570', '2026-10-27 15:10:47.230557+00', '2026-10-27 15:15:35.298826+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1431, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: attemptParameterRepair floors non-integer strings and accepts Infinity (#595)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/595","title":"fix(core): McpxDiagnose.attemptParameterRepair floors non-integer strings for integer parameters \u2014 \"3.9\" becomes 3 and \"-1.1\" becomes -2 in the suggested repair","number":595,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:11:05Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the boolean, JSON-parse and array-wrap repair paths (verified behaving as documented)","analyzeArgumentMismatch''s mismatch detection (correctly flags these strings; only the repair is wrong)"],"include":["packages/core/src/tool/plugin/mcpx-diagnose.ts string-to-number coercion guard (lines 280-289)","regression tests in packages/core/test/tool-mcpx-features.test.ts or a sibling mcpx-diagnose test file"]},"tests":["bun test for tool-mcpx-features from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for mcpx-diagnose / attemptParameterRepair / parameter repair / integer coercion returned no covering issue","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:11:05Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"attemptParameterRepair''s string-to-number coercion changes values instead of only fixing types: Math.floor turns non-integer strings into different integers (a full unit away for negatives past -1), and non-finite numbers pass the NaN-only guard and serialize to null in the rendered repair.","evidence":["packages/core/src/tool/plugin/mcpx-diagnose.ts:283-285 \u2014 the only guard is trimmed !== \"\" && !Number.isNaN(Number(trimmed)); integer branch applies Math.floor(num) unconditionally","Probe (laptop, verbatim real source, main e82aa33071): integer \"3.9\"->3, \"-1.9\"->-2, \"-1.1\"->-2; number \"Infinity\"->Infinity with JSON rendering {\"ratio\":null}; controls \"42\"->42, \"3.0\"->3, \"1.5\"->1.5 correct","packages/core/src/tool/plugin/mcpx-diagnose.ts:391 diagnoseToolCall attaches repairedParams; :335/:344 formatAutomaticRepair JSON-stringifies them into the ''Automatic Parameter Repair Available'' text the model is told to send; enrichToolFailure stores them in diagnostic metadata","packages/core/test/tool-mcpx-features.test.ts covers only clean coercions (\"5000\"->5000, \"true\"->true); no test pins non-integer or non-finite strings"],"acceptance":["For an integer parameter, a string is only coerced when the parsed number is already an integer (\"42\"->42, \"3.0\"->3 keep working); \"3.9\", \"-1.9\" and \"-1.1\" produce no numeric repair for that property (the type-mismatch hint still stands)","For a number parameter, non-finite results (\"Infinity\", \"-Infinity\") are not repaired; repaired params never contain a value that JSON-serializes to something different (Infinity -> null)","The coercion''s accepted grammar is pinned by tests, including hex/exponent forms (\"0x10\", \"1e3\"), whether they stay accepted or are rejected","New regression tests in packages/core/test/tool-mcpx-features.test.ts (or a sibling mcpx-diagnose test file); existing mcpx tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/595"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The repair fires after a failed tool call and tells the model what to send next; a suggested repair that silently changes the argument''s value (or renders it null) corrupts the retry. Bounded to one guard in one function. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:595', '2026-10-27 15:12:06.431724+00', '2026-10-28 00:40:43.666523+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
