ex.ts \u2014 a refactor can break it with no other signal while nothing runs the suite"],"acceptance":["A workflow runs the cf-container-hello test suite on every PR touching pkgs/cf-container-hello/** and on pushes to main touching it","The workflow''s test step passes on current main (suite verified green at filing: 11 tests OK)","Deliberately breaking one pinned invariant (gate ordering in src/index.ts) makes the new workflow fail, demonstrated on the implementing PR","No production code changes; any suite changes needed for CI are called out separately"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1439","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/955","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1427","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/470"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The tests are the only guard against the #955 unauthenticated SSRF state returning via refactor; unwatched, they provide no protection. Same class as #1427/#470.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1439', '2026-10-27 15:44:57.29294+00', '2026-10-27 17:01:06.390894+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1449, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Fix #1436: mirror code_block params+htmlBlock attrs into editor richSchema', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1024","title":"fix(id-web): preserve HTML blocks on save via code_block provenance attr (#982)","number":1024,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:44:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1436","title":"id(web): PR #1024''s htmlBlock provenance attr is dropped by the editor schema \u2014 HTML blocks still re-fence on editor save (#982 regression path)","number":1436,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to the Rust codec in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs","Implementing inside the triage task 1445 (this packet is the follow-up)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts richSchema code_block attr mirror","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.test.ts round-trip test"]},"tests":["CI: web vitest suite including new fromJSON/toJSON round-trip test for code_block params+htmlBlock","CI: existing editor.test.ts richSchema tests still pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1436 is the work identity; triage task 1445 routes exactly this fix; no other open issue covers the richSchema code_block attr mirror (#1347 is footnote node types, different subject)","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"richSchema code_block declares no attrs, so Node.fromJSON drops the markdown codec''s params and htmlBlock attrs; editor saves re-fence HTML blocks and strip fence languages.","evidence":["Triage task 1445 verified 2026-10-27 against current main via GitHub API: editor.ts richSchema lines 45ff has no code_block override; grep htmlBlock in editor.ts = none; code search htmlBlock repo-wide returns only pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs and a plan doc","markdown.rs:415 parse sets {params: html, htmlBlock: true}; markdown.rs:205-207 authored fences set {params: info}; markdown.rs:1163/1170 save reads params and requires htmlBlock==true to emit HtmlBlock","editor.ts:375 Node.fromJSON(editorSchema, initialDoc); editor.ts:662 state.doc.toJSON(); main.ts:1330 and :1421 post doc to /api/save","editor.test.ts already tests richSchema node presence (line 112ff) \u2014 the natural home for the round-trip test"],"acceptance":["richSchema code_block declares params and htmlBlock attrs following the #880/#881 mirror pattern in pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts, preserving inherited spec fields","editor.test.ts (or adjacent vitest) proves code_block PM JSON with {params: html, htmlBlock: true} and with {params: rust} survives Node.fromJSON(richSchema) -> toJSON() unchanged","No Rust codec changes; authored fences without htmlBlock still save as fences (codec tests unchanged)","PR opened referencing #1436; CI green or infra failures distinguished"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1436","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1024","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/982","queue task 1445 triage"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Live regression path for closed bug #982: any HTML block in a doc opened and saved in the web editor is rewritten as a visible ```html fence; params loss also strips authored fence languages through the editor.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1436', '2026-10-27 15:45:22.337772+00', '2026-10-27 16:30:43.490484+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1450, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): AutoSaveManager concurrent saves + stale completion — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1440","title":"id(web): AutoSaveManager runs concurrent saves and a stale completion marks newer edits saved","number":1440,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:45:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Server-side /api/save handler changes","#1230 e2e harness race","Collab step transport (collab.ts)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts AutoSaveManager serialization + completion guard","Regression tests for AutoSaveManager with a deferred saveFn"]},"tests":["bunx vitest run for the new AutoSaveManager tests (pkgs/id/web, via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for autosave/AutoSaveManager terms: #1230 is the Firefox e2e harness save-count race, #229 its closed parent \u2014 neither covers the production AutoSaveManager concurrency/state logic in main.ts. No other open or closed issue matches.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:45:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"AutoSaveManager''s debounce and retry paths bypass the only in-flight guard, so saves overlap, and stale completions overwrite the state of newer unsaved edits.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe of the verbatim AutoSaveManager extract from main 95cd41f0 with a deferred saveFn (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-autosave/out.log): edit1 -> debounce -> calls=1 state=saving; edit2 during flight -> debounce -> calls=2 maxInFlight=2; resolving save#2 then stale save#1 both land state=saved","Scenario B in the same probe: edit during an in-flight save, then the older save resolves before the new debounce fires -> state ''saved'' while the newer edit is still unsaved and its debounce pending","Code: triggerSave() in main.ts (class :26-200) awaits saveFn() with no re-entry guard; the state===''saving'' guard exists only in saveNow(); onSaveResult() transitions unconditionally"],"acceptance":["At most one saveFn() invocation is ever in flight; an edit during a save schedules exactly one coalesced follow-up save after it settles","A save completion never sets the indicator to ''saved'' when an edit arrived after that save started (dirty generation/epoch or equivalent)","The 429 retry path obeys the same serialization","saveNow() behaviour for idle/unsaved cases is unchanged","Regression tests with a deferred saveFn cover edit-during-flight, stale completion, and 429 retry serialization"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1440","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1230","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:26","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:1296"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Save-integrity: the indicator can claim ''saved'' for unsaved content (data-loss window if the user navigates on it) and overlapping saves interleave the dataset.hash bookkeeping in main.ts saveFile().","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1440', '2026-10-27 15:46:37.75942+00', '2026-10-27 17:08:29.548722+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1452, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(core): check route target until before nested-route expansion (#580)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/569","title":"fix(core): judge route governance targets via shared catalog expansion (#530)","number":569,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00Z"}],"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/580","title":"fix(core): a route target''s until is ignored when the target references another route \u2014 expired nested-route targets stay live in expansion and governance","number":580,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:49:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The documented defaultVariant/variants non-propagation into nested routes (by design, matches plugin)","Changing the until boundary semantics (Date.now() >= until) established by #569 and the plugin"],"include":["packages/core/src/config/plugin/model-routes.ts expand target-loop expiry ordering","packages/core/src/session/model-governance.ts routeTargets expiry ordering","Regression tests for expired and unexpired nested-route targets"]},"tests":["Expired nested-route target contributes no leaves (plugin) and no judged targets (governance)","Unexpired nested-route target still expands and is judged","Concrete-target until behaviour from #569 unchanged"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1398 for #580 completed verification 2026-10-27; dedupe key is the deterministic fix key for issue 580; no open PR owns the fix per gh search at 2026-10-27T15:47Z","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:49:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"A route target''s until is ignored in both runtime expansion and governance when the target references another route, so expired nested-route targets stay live.","evidence":["Triage task 1398 verified on current main 02d758e6e000c11db326f4242078e5a6d68ca204 via gh api contents: packages/core/src/config/plugin/model-routes.ts expand loop \u2014 nested-route branch with continue precedes `if (spec.until !== undefined && Date.now() >= spec.until) continue`","Same check on main 02d758e6: packages/core/src/session/model-governance.ts routeTargets \u2014 `if (selection.providerID === \"opencode-route\") return routeTargets(...)` precedes `if (object?.until !== undefined && Date.now() >= object.until) return []`","Issue #580 OPEN at triage, no held/user-owned/do-not-merge/do-not-auto-edit labels; PR #569 MERGED 2026-10-27T10:51:41Z; no open PR owns this fix (search 2026-10-27T15:47Z)","PR #569 test covers until only on a concrete target {model: ''test/b'', until: 1}; no nested-route until coverage in either suite (from #580 packet evidence)"],"acceptance":["Fix checks target expiry before/regardless of the nested-route branch in both packages/core/src/config/plugin/model-routes.ts and packages/core/src/session/model-governance.ts, keeping runtime and governance in agreement and Date.now() >= until boundary unchanged","Regression tests cover an expired nested-route target (dropped) and an unexpired one (until in the future, still expanded/judged) in the plugin and/or governance suites","Existing model-routes and model-governance suites pass in CI; concrete-target until behaviour from #569 unchanged","PR opened, CI green (or parked on CI per worker rules), and merged under standing criteria; issue #580 closed by the fix"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/580","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/569","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/530"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent defeat of the documented time-limited pool membership mechanism when the expiring membership is wrapped as a nested route: traffic keeps flowing after the deadline and governance judges the targets live; normal priority because it requires that specific configuration shape.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:580', '2026-10-27 15:50:11.816786+00', '2026-10-27 17:37:44.257172+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1453, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'refactor(core): extract one shared governance catalog helper (#591)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/591","title":"refactor(core): PR #569 duplicated the governance catalog construction in session.ts and session/session.ts \u2014 extract one shared helper","number":591,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Any behaviour change to ModelGovernance.assertAllowed judging","Changes to ModelRouteExpansion.matchingModels (#530''s shared module)"],"include":["One shared governanceConfig helper in packages/core/src (issue suggests alongside ModelGovernance in packages/core/src/session/model-governance.ts)","Both call sites switched to the shared helper (session.ts, session/session.ts)"]},"tests":["bun test from packages/core (model-governance and session suites, unmodified)","bun run check from repo root (CI authoritative)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1416 confirmed the duplication verbatim on current main 98f4f4a5b3 and specified this extraction shape; #591 is the single tracking issue","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The provider catalog governance judges route targets against is built by two duplicated ~35-line copies; a change to one copy makes the session-creation path and the switchAgent/setModel paths judge the same route against different catalogs.","evidence":["git show origin/main (98f4f4a5b3) packages/core/src/session.ts:293 governanceConfig(location) and packages/core/src/session/session.ts:117 governanceConfig(session): the snapshot->Catalog new Map(Array.from(snapshot.records, ...)) construction is verbatim in both, same orElseSucceed fallback","Call sites on current main: session.ts:326 (assertModelAllowed), session/session.ts:158 (switchAgent) and :186 (model-selection path)","Only difference between the copies: session/session.ts checks locations === undefined first and derives the ref from session.location; session.ts uses its locations service directly"],"acceptance":["The context-to-entries+catalog construction exists exactly once in packages/core/src and both session.ts and session/session.ts call the shared helper","Behaviour unchanged: uninitialized location yields {entries: [], catalog: undefined}; no provider service yields entries with catalog undefined; locations === undefined (session/session.ts path) yields the empty fallback; orElseSucceed fallback semantics preserved","Existing packages/core model-governance and session tests pass unmodified","grep for the snapshot-to-Catalog construction in packages/core/src returns exactly one site"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/591","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/569"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Behaviour-preserving dedupe of a governance-critical construction; low priority as filed, but drift between the copies would cause inconsistent route denials that are hard to trace.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:591', '2026-10-27 15:50:47.283383+00', '2026-10-27 16:44:20.440161+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1454, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): TS shell-contract u64 cap parity — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1441","title":"id(web): TS shell-contract checker rejects valid u64 values above 2^53-1 that the Rust checker accepts (seed, sequence, offset)","number":1441,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Rust checker changes","Contract JSON changes","Production world client wiring"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/shell-contract.ts u64 bound handling","pkgs/id/web/src/world-contract.test.ts parity regression tests"]},"tests":["bunx vitest run src/world-contract.test.ts (pkgs/id/web, via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for shell-contract u64/parity/MAX_SAFE_INTEGER terms: no issue covers the TS/Rust u64 bound divergence (hits were unrelated closed items #819/#1076).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The TS shell-contract checker invents a 2^53-1 cap for u64 fields that neither the contract nor the Rust checker has, producing false violations for contract-valid frames.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe of verbatim shell-contract.ts + real contract JSON (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-u64/out.log): seed=9007199254740992 -> ok:false ''must be in 0..=9007199254740991''; seed=u64::MAX from wire JSON -> ok:false; view sequence=u64::MAX -> ok:false; controls at/below 2^53-1 -> ok:true","TS source: INTEGER_MAX maps u64 to Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER and checkValue clamps to min(field.max ?? typeMax, typeMax)","Rust source: shell_contract.rs check_value maps FieldType::U64 to u64::MAX; world_session/mod.rs:1162 generates seeds as random::<u64>()"],"acceptance":["checkClientFrame accepts install_begin with seed = 2^53 and with the JSON-parsed form of u64::MAX (parity with the Rust checker)","checkServerFrame accepts view/records frames whose sequence is at or above 2^53","Negatives, non-integers, u16/u32 overflows, and explicit safe-range max violations (total_bytes > 16777216) are still rejected","u64 error messages no longer cite 9007199254740991 as a contract bound","Regression tests in world-contract.test.ts pin the parity cases; Rust checker and contract JSON unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1441","pkgs/id/web/src/shell-contract.ts","pkgs/id/src/shell_contract.rs","pkgs/id/contract/shell-contract.v1.json","pkgs/id/src/world_session/mod.rs:1162"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Conformance-checker parity defect: the TS port fails frames the Rust host accepts and invents a bound the contract does not contain, undermining the F13.1 conformance-proof purpose. No production consumer yet, hence low priority.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1441', '2026-10-27 15:50:54.373896+00', '2026-10-28 08:46:37.375143+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1456, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: ErrorSummary.from returns [] for non-Error thrown values (#600)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/600","title":"fix(core): ErrorSummary.from returns [] for non-Error thrown values \u2014 credential/OAuth failure logs lose the error entirely","number":600,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:50:08Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the 8-entry chain cap and stack omission (unchanged)","caller log sites in credential.ts and mcp/oauth.ts (no change needed once the summary is honest)"],"include":["packages/core/src/util/error-summary.ts primitive fallback in from()","regression tests in packages/core/test/util/error-summary.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test for util/error-summary from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ErrorSummary / error summary returned no covering issue","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:50:08Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"ErrorSummary.from drops non-object thrown values entirely, returning an empty summary for thrown strings/numbers/booleans, so the credential and MCP OAuth failure logs that rely on it record no diagnostic at all for those failures.","evidence":["packages/core/src/util/error-summary.ts:22-24 \u2014 Schema.decodeUnknownOption on a primitive yields None and the loop breaks before recording anything","Probe (laptop, real module, main f1e0c586fe): from(\"boom string\") -> [], from(42) -> []; controls from(new Error(\"real\")) -> [{type:Error,message:real}], from({message:\"plain object\"}) -> [{type:unknown,message:plain object}]","Callers pass Cause.squash(cause), which returns whatever was thrown, including non-Error defects: packages/core/src/credential.ts:152/198/219/240/304 and packages/core/src/mcp/oauth.ts:88/510/529 log errors: ErrorSummary.from(...) as the failure''s only diagnostic","packages/core/test/util/error-summary.test.ts covers only Error instances and their cause chains; no test pins the non-object case"],"acceptance":["ErrorSummary.from on a thrown string returns one entry whose message is that string; numbers/booleans likewise produce an entry with their string form as the message, rather than []","A cause chain that bottoms out in a non-object value keeps the entries above it and appends the primitive''s entry instead of ending the chain silently","Error instances, tagged errors, and plain objects with message/code/errno keep their current summaries (existing tests pass unchanged)","New regression tests in packages/core/test/util/error-summary.test.ts cover: thrown string, thrown number, and an Error whose cause is a string"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/600"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Credential and OAuth setup failures are where third-party SDKs most often throw non-Error values; today those failures log errors: [] and the actual error text exists nowhere else. One function, one decode fallback. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:600', '2026-10-27 15:51:38.009799+00', '2026-10-27 18:56:50.500805+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1459, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'triage: Form when conditions referencing external fields — support or reject accurately (#601)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/601","title":"fix(core): Form validateFields rejects a when referencing an earlier external field \u2014 and reports it as ''must reference an earlier field''","number":601,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:37Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the unconditional external-acknowledgement requirement in validateAnswer (pinned behavior, form.test.ts:288+)","any change to which answers are valid for existing creatable forms"],"include":["packages/core/src/form.ts validateFields/validateWhen treatment of external fields","packages/schema/src/form.ts When documentation if the decision is to exclude external targets","tests in packages/core/test/form.test.ts pinning the chosen behavior"]},"tests":["bun test for form from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for validateFields / external form when returned no covering issue","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:37Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Create-time form validation, the schema When documentation, and the runtime answer evaluator disagree about whether an external field can be referenced by a later field''s when condition, and the validator''s error message misstates the reason for rejection.","evidence":["packages/core/src/form.ts:283 \u2014 if (field.type === ''external'') continue runs before earlier.set, so external fields are invisible to the when-reference check at :286-289","packages/schema/src/form.ts:30-34 \u2014 When doc: ''key must reference a field defined earlier in the form''s field list'', no external exception; ExternalField is a member of the Field union (:102-120)","packages/core/test/form.test.ts:261-267 \u2014 a duplicate key between an external and a string field IS rejected, so the same loop treats external fields as defined for duplicates but undefined for references","Probe (laptop, verbatim form.ts validation section, main f1e0c586fe): external-first + when->auth rejected with the earlier-field message; boolean-first control accepted; validateAnswer({auth:true, code:''x''}) -> undefined, validateAnswer({code:''x''}) -> ''External form field must be acknowledged: auth''","packages/core/src/form.ts:296-310 \u2014 validateWhen has no external branch; an external target would fall into the string-value branch although external answers are booleans"],"acceptance":["A decision is recorded on the issue: external fields either are or are not valid when targets","If valid targets: validateFields accepts a when referencing an earlier external field with a boolean condition value (non-boolean rejected with the boolean message), validateWhen handles the external target explicitly, and tests pin create + reply behavior for a field gated on an external acknowledgement","If not valid targets: the rejection names the real reason (e.g. ''Form field condition cannot reference an external field''), the schema When documentation states the exception, and a test pins the accurate error","Either way, duplicate-key treatment and reference treatment of external fields agree, and all existing form tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/601"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A form author gets a false diagnosis (told their field ordering is wrong when it is not) and the schema doc promises a reference the validator refuses. No runtime breakage today \u2014 the form simply cannot be created \u2014 so low priority, but the contract/validator/runtime inconsistency should be resolved deliberately.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:601', '2026-10-27 15:55:05.682849+00', '2026-10-27 18:33:49.381534+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1460, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(quota): clamp Meta used_percent to [0,100] in web + VS Code providers (#572)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/572","title":"fix(quota): Meta provider (PR #540) leaks out-of-range usedPercent","number":572,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Clamping inside shared toUsageWindow (wafer overage relies on unclamped values)","Any other provider","PR #540 (already merged; this fix lands on main)"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/meta.js buildWindows read sites","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts metaWindowsFrom read sites","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/meta.test.js and packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts Meta regression tests"]},"tests":["packages/web vitest meta.test.js","bun test packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts (Meta block)","bun run check:changed"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1439 confirmed the defect on current main and recommended this fix shape; #572 is the single tracking issue; dedupe key is the deterministic fix key for #572","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The Meta quota provider merged in PR #540 leaks out-of-range usedPercent (and remainingPercent above 100 for negative inputs) in both the web and VS Code implementations because its read sites coerce with toNumber but never clamp to [0,100].","evidence":["meta.js:196/:205 on current main (post-#540 merge 497abe870): usedPercent: toNumber(rolling.used_percent) / toNumber(weekly.used_percent), no clamp helper in file","quotaProviders.ts metaWindowsFrom on current main: usedPercent: toNumber(rolling.used_percent) and toNumber(weekly.used_percent), no clamp","Probe (node, real toNumber semantics from both files): 150 -> 150, -20 -> -20, 42 -> 42, Infinity -> null, NaN -> null; toUsageWindow derives remainingPercent as Math.max(0, 100 - usedPercent), so -20 yields remainingPercent 120","Triage task 1439 (queue, 2026-10-27) confirmed all four sites on current main after PR #540 merged 15:53:59Z"],"acceptance":["Web meta.js: rolling and weekly used_percent clamped to [0,100]; missing/non-finite stays null","VS Code quotaProviders.ts Meta windows: rolling and weekly used_percent clamped to [0,100]; missing/non-finite stays null","Regression tests pin 150 -> 100, -20 -> 0 (remainingPercent 100), in-range unchanged, missing stays null in meta.test.js and the quotaProviders.test.ts Meta block","Existing quota tests still pass and bun run check:changed passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/572","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/540"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Same defect class as the seven sibling clamp fixes merged 2026-10-27; the provider is new (#540) so the leak shipped today. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:572', '2026-10-27 15:55:23.590431+00', '2026-10-27 16:45:20.295487+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1461, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(git): normalize contextLines in the git service diff functions (#578)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/578","title":"fix(git): service-layer diff functions still hand git a fractional -U \u2014 normalize contextLines in the service, not only in the routes","number":578,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:24Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any change to route-level parsing (parseDiffContextLines) or route behavior","any change to valid-value diff output"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js contextLines handling in getNoIndexDiff, readDiff, getRangeDiff, getCommitDiff","service-layer tests for fractional/negative/NaN contextLines"]},"tests":["targeted git service tests (packages/web/server/lib/git/service.test.js) run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for contextLines / ''fractional diff context'' returned only #464 and #465 (both CLOSED, fixed at the route layer by PR #469); the service-layer remainder was recorded as an unfiled REVIEW-FINDING on 2026-10-26 and never filed. No open issue covers it.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:24Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The git service''s four diff functions build the -U argument from an unvalidated number: fractional values become -U2.9 and NaN becomes -UNaN, both rejected by git with exit 129; only the routes above them validate, and getLog in the same file already shows the in-service normalization pattern.","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:3327-3328 \u2014 getNoIndexDiff: Number.isFinite guard only, then `-U${Math.max(0, contextLines)}`; 2.9 -> -U2.9","packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:3402-3403 \u2014 readDiff: same pattern (typeof number && !Number.isNaN)","packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:3589-3590 \u2014 getRangeDiff: same pattern","packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:6713 \u2014 getCommitDiff: no guard at all; NaN -> -UNaN","Probe this run (scratch git repo): git diff -U2.9 -> ''error: --unified expects a numerical value'', exit 129; git diff -U2 exits 0","packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:6365 \u2014 getLog normalizes maxCount in-service (Number.isInteger && > 0 else 50): the precedent contextLines lacks","packages/web/server/lib/git/routes.js:31-34 \u2014 parseDiffContextLines strict ^\\d+$ else 3 (PR #469), so routes are covered and must stay unchanged"],"acceptance":["One shared normalization for contextLines in packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js (integer, >= 0, otherwise the default 3 \u2014 the same rule parseDiffContextLines applies at the routes), used by getNoIndexDiff, readDiff, getRangeDiff, and getCommitDiff","A fractional (2.9), negative, or NaN contextLines passed directly to any of those service functions produces a normal diff with the default context instead of a git error","Valid values (0, 3, 10) behave exactly as today, and route behavior is unchanged","Tests in packages/web/server/lib/git/service.test.js (or the existing git test files, following their patterns) pin the fractional/NaN cases at the service layer"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/578","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/465","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/464","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/469"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"No live caller reaches it today (routes guard), so low priority \u2014 but the service is the layer future callers will trust, its four diff entry points disagree with the routes and with getLog''s in-service normalization in the same file, and the next caller forwarding a computed context reintroduces the #465 exit-129 failure mode.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:578', '2026-10-27 15:57:22.896738+00', '2026-10-27 17:00:26.648098+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1462, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): header subtitle filename innerHTML injection — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1457","title":"id(web): header subtitle injects the raw document filename via innerHTML \u2014 a crafted filename becomes live markup (stored XSS)","number":1457,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T16:14:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Server template changes","The fetchPartial/navigateTo server-HTML swap mechanism itself (audit note only)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts updateHeaderSubtitle DOM construction / escaping","pkgs/id/web regression test for the subtitle rendering"]},"tests":["bunx vitest run (pkgs/id/web subtitle regression test, via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for innerHTML / XSS / subtitle terms: no issue covers the header-subtitle filename sink (only hit in this area is closed #908, the /blob content-type XSS \u2014 different sink, already fixed). Backlog + sweep.log checked: Lane A recent filings are markdown-codec and cold-store items; Lane B recent filings are autosave (#1440), shell-contract u64 (#1441), world presenter (#1431) \u2014 none touch main.ts subtitle rendering.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T16:14:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"updateHeaderSubtitle parses the untrusted document filename as HTML, so a crafted filename injects live markup (event-handler elements) into the id web page.","evidence":["Laptop Bun + happy-dom probe of the verbatim updateHeaderSubtitle (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-subtitle/out.log): markup-img-onerror case produced imgCount=1 with imgOnerror=''alert(1)''; anchor-breakout-svg case produced svgCount=1 with svgOnload=''alert(2)'' and anchorText truncated to ''x''; benign control produced exactly one anchor with text ''notes.md''","Source chain: templates.rs:486 data-filename carries urlencoding::encode(name); main.ts:1197-1201 decodeURIComponent restores the raw name into lastFilename; main.ts:550 subtitle.innerHTML interpolates lastFilename and lastFilePath with no escaping","Contrast in-repo: templates.rs:213/:420 html_escape file names; home.ts renderList/renderTagList use textContent for document/tag names (''tag values are untrusted user metadata'')"],"acceptance":["A filename of ''<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>.md'' renders as literal text inside a single anchor pointing at the file (no img element created)","The anchor href is set as a property/attribute, not string-interpolated into markup, so quotes in a path cannot break out of the attribute","Regression test in pkgs/id/web (vitest/happy-dom) pins both attack cases and the benign control (notes.md -> one anchor, correct text and href)","Fix PR includes an audit note confirming the fetchPartial/navigateTo innerHTML sinks only receive server-template HTML"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1457","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:544-555","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:1196-1202","pkgs/id/src/web/templates.rs:421-422","pkgs/id/src/web/templates.rs:486","pkgs/id/web/src/home.ts"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Verified stored script injection into the id web UI whose payload is a document filename \u2014 peer-deliverable through the p2p store, executes on the victim''s origin where the identity token lives in localStorage. Also mangles honest filenames containing <, >, &.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1457', '2026-10-27 16:04:53.334885+00', '2026-10-27 17:07:21.892338+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1463, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: implement Phase 1 of #1384 — supervised stdio transport behind a flag (issue #1385)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1385","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1384 \u2014 supervised stdio transport behind a flag (supervisor owns the child''s pipes)","number":1385,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T16:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any change to internal/daemon/takeover.go or internal/pool/handoff.go (Phase 2)","HTTP/SSE upstream session resume (design non-goal)","making supervised the default or any state-dir adopt-or-reap scan (Phase 3)","supervisor protocol version negotiation beyond refuse-on-mismatch with an explicit error (no silent direct-spawn fallback when the flag is on)"],"include":["pkgs/mcpx: hidden `mcpx supervise` subcommand (internal/cli) re-execing the same binary","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient: supervised transport implementing the Transport interface; supervisor spawn-on-demand from the transport (connect, else spawn detached re-exec with its own process group, bounded connect retry)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/config: `supervised` bool on Extras (mcpx.supervised)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/pool: Pool.dial() branch to the supervised transport when the flag is on","tests: supervisor pump, attach/detach, single-attach refusal, buffer overflow with frame-boundary trim and dropped-byte reporting, child-exit reporting, defining daemon-SIGKILL reattach test"]},"tests":["pkgs/mcpx: go test ./... (via GitHub Actions CI on the PR)","defining test from #1385: daemon SIGKILL -> new daemon -> child PID unchanged -> call succeeds","with flag off: existing suite unchanged, including internal/e2e/takeover_test.go"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued once by triage task 1354 as the implementation follow-up required by #1385''s acceptance criteria; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1385 keys it to the issue so the fleet monitor cannot double-enqueue it.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T16:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Implement Phase 1 of the mcpx supervisor design (#1384) exactly as scoped in issue #1385 and settled by triage task 1354 (verdict comment on #1385, 2026-10-27): hidden `mcpx supervise` subcommand (re-exec of the same binary) that spawns one stdio child with today''s NewStdio semantics and owns its pipes for the child''s whole life; a supervised mcpclient transport behind a per-server config flag, default off; bounded unattached-output buffer. Everything additive and flag-gated; the direct path and the takeover handoff are untouched.","evidence":["Triage verdict on #1385 (task 1354, 2026-10-27) settles the supervisor socket protocol: state-dir unix socket (defaults.PrivateMode 0600 precedent, internal/daemon/sessions.go), one-line JSON attach handshake each way with protocol version 1 (takeoverVersion precedent, internal/daemon/takeover.go:33), raw byte pump after handshake, single attached daemon (second attach refused in handshake, no preemption), child exit = drain then connection EOF with exit error + stderr tail reported on the reporting handshake, one supervisor per child life (respawn = new supervisor)","Buffer settlement from triage: default 1 MiB tail-keep for unattached child output, trim to the next newline boundary so the reattached stream starts on a frame boundary, cumulative droppedBytes counter reported at every attach; stderr ring stays 64 KiB (internal/mcpclient/stdio.go:147)","Verified on main@95cd41f01e9baad44d780a93cd5fdc5a1b54adb9: internal/daemon/takeover.go is 726 lines, internal/pool/handoff.go 390 lines; NewStdio at internal/mcpclient/stdio.go:82 with Setpgid (L99), plain os.Pipe (L107/111/117), pending partial-frame buffer and detached state; zero occurrences of ''supervise'' in pkgs/mcpx (code search, 2026-10-27)","Transport selection is a single point: Pool.dial() at internal/pool/pool.go:686 branches on cfg.Stdio() to mcpclient.NewStdio; the Transport interface is frame-level Send/Recv/Close/Info at internal/mcpclient/client.go:31","Flag home settled by triage: a `supervised` bool in config.Extras (internal/config/config.go:92, alongside Disabled), surfaced as mcpx.supervised per-server config, default false; framing stays single-homed by generalising StdioTransport''s read path (readLine/pending, stdio.go:242) over the socket connection rather than duplicating it"],"acceptance":["All acceptance criteria of issue #1385, unchanged, including the defining test: daemon + supervised server, make a call, SIGKILL the daemon, start a new daemon \u2014 child PID unchanged and a subsequent call succeeds","With the flag off (default), the full existing mcpx test suite passes unchanged, including internal/e2e/takeover_test.go","go test ./... in pkgs/mcpx passes (run via CI on the PR per fleet policy; defining test may be linux-only consistent with existing takeover test gating)","Supervised transport Close detaches without signalling the child; no changes to internal/daemon/takeover.go or internal/pool/handoff.go","Direction decision on design #1384 remains Drew''s (user/review there); this task only builds the flag-gated, default-off Phase 1 experiment \u2014 do not flip any default and do not start Phase 2"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1385","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1384","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/237"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 is the gate for the whole #1384 design: it proves the attach model with the direct path untouched and default off. Normal priority per the design issue; enqueued by triage task 1354 per #1385''s acceptance criteria.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1385', '2026-10-27 16:09:22.873277+00', '2026-10-28 00:42:37.835516+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1464, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): world records pagination interleave — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1458","title":"id(web): world records view shows a lone stale page when an input event restarts a paginated fetch \u2014 fresh pages are silently discarded","number":1458,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T16:09:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Server-side records protocol changes (the wire format already orders answers; the defect is client state)","World surface rendering (world-surface.ts)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts records fetch sequencing (generation or coalescing)","pkgs/id/web regression test with a mock WebSocket"]},"tests":["bunx vitest run (pkgs/id/web world records regression test, via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for world records pagination / recordsPending / requestRecords terms: zero hits. Backlog + sweep.log checked: no world-records filing exists; nearest is #1440 (AutoSaveManager concurrency, different module, cited as related).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T16:09:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Overlapping paginated records fetches share one unsequenced state triple, so a re-request mid-pagination makes the stale chain close the fresh fetch and renders a lone stale page while discarding the fresh pages.","evidence":["Laptop Bun + happy-dom probe of verbatim world.ts with mock WebSocket (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-worldrecords/out.log): control displayedRecords = {a1:1, a2:2}; interleave displayedRecords = {a2:2} only; wire log shows 3 records requests (A page 1, A continuation after=''x'', B page 1) answered in order","Source: world.ts:212-226 requestRecords resets records/recordsAfter/recordsPending unconditionally; :178-198 records handler merges any page while recordsPending and renders + closes the fetch on any next_after=null page; :170 requestRecords called on every input event"],"acceptance":["In the interleave sequence (input event mid-pagination), the final rendered records are the fresh fetch''s complete set, never a single stale page","Pages/continuations from a superseded fetch cannot merge into, close, or render the live fetch (generation guard or coalescing with dirty-flag refetch)","Regression test (vitest/happy-dom, mock WebSocket, in-order answers) pins the control two-page fetch and the interleave case","Single-page fetches, snapshot-triggered fetch, and the refresh button behave as before"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1458","pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts:119-121","pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts:158","pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts:170","pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts:178-198","pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts:212-226"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The records panel presents authoritative world state; in any active world (input events during a multi-page load \u2014 the common case) it silently shows a truncated stale subset as if complete, with no error or retry.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1458', '2026-10-27 16:10:20.504356+00', '2026-10-28 08:46:35.610768+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1465, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): fix adjacent different-type list save corruption (#1397) — blank-line separation + artifact drop', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1397","title":"id(web): adjacent lists of different types save an <!-- end list --> comment that reopens as a phantom code block","number":1397,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T16:06:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1032 bullet-marker coalescing (already fixed \u2014 do not regress it)","#1370 mixed task/plain items within a single list (bullet task list adjacent to a same-marker bullet list merges on reparse into that problem''s territory \u2014 document, do not fix here)","#1380 ordered-list delimiter style","Any repo other than developing-today/code"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs: json_to_ast child loop (blank-line separation for different-kind adjacent lists), HtmlBlock arm (drop the exact renderer-artifact comment on parse), and codec regression tests"]},"tests":["cargo test web::markdown in CI on the PR (targeted codec tests incl. the new boundary tests and the #1032 fixpoint tests)","Probe-harness check before implementing: an empty-paragraph sibling between two different-kind lists renders as blank-line separation and reparses to exactly the two lists"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1377 as its follow-up; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1397 is distinct from the triage task identity (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1397). No live fix task for #1397 existed at triage time (issue carried only the triage task''s claim).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T16:12:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Adjacent different-kind lists in pkgs/id''s web markdown codec are corrupted on save (<!-- end list --> comment emitted) and on reopen (phantom html code_block between the lists); blockquote shapes are not even save-fixpoints.","evidence":["Fresh repro 2026-10-27 (triage task 1377) on the laptop: standalone probe crate whose lib.rs is md5-identical (cbd6ce760816dc923f0e99a151144e5e) to origin/main pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs at 95cd41f0; all five shapes save ''<!-- end list -->'' (OUT1 lines) and the blockquote shape reports MD_FIXPOINT: false \u2014 output saved at hidden_files/worker-1259/probe1397-fresh.txt","Creator probe (issue filing, main 452d69e6) out4.log PM2 dumps show the phantom code_block{htmlBlock:true, params:html} with text ''<!-- end list -->'' between the two lists on reparse for bullet->ordered, ordered->bullet, and multi-item shapes","markdown.rs on current main: the #1032 coalesce comment (lines ~1464-1475) explicitly scopes itself to bullet_list siblings; ordered_list is NOT merged (restart numbering) and task_list is a distinct PM node type \u2014 different-kind adjacency is unhandled","git log 95bfedb4..origin/main for pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs is empty: the file is unchanged since the creator probe, so the probed behaviour is current-main behaviour"],"acceptance":["All five probed shapes (bullet->ordered, ordered->bullet, multi-item boundary, ordered task->bullet, blockquote bullet->ordered) save with no ''<!-- end list -->'' or other renderer-internal separator in the markdown","Re-parse of the saved text yields exactly the two original lists and no node between them; the blockquote shape is a markdown fixpoint across two saves","A file previously saved WITH the artifact comment reopens without a phantom code_block (parse-side artifact drop), covered by a test","#1032 behaviour unchanged (adjacent bullet lists still coalesce; its regression tests pass); existing web::markdown tests pass in CI","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover the type-boundary shapes in both directions"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1397","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1032","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1370","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:391","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1464"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Save writes renderer-internal markup into user files and reopening corrupts the document model with a phantom code block; same failure family as #1032 at the boundaries its fix could not merge. Issue carries priority/normal.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1397', '2026-10-27 16:21:13.156819+00', '2026-10-27 16:21:13.156819+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
