he atom-loss scope against current main","The pinned representation for an image with alt text, and for an image without alt text, is decided and recorded on the issue","A fix packet is enqueued (or the issue is explicitly parked/blocked with a named reason), including whether footnote_reference atoms are in the same policy or documented out of scope"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1491"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Normal priority: silent data loss on save in the same class #1306 fixed for blocks; the issue''s own priority/normal stands.","timebox_minutes":25}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1491', '2026-10-27 18:25:07.719161+00', '2026-10-27 18:33:56.671006+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1527, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(security): complete the loopback origin alias set (#589)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/544","title":"fix(security): bracket-aware Host parsing so the [::1] origin alias fires (#500)","number":544,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:26:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/589","title":"fix(security): loopback origin aliases are incomplete \u2014 127.0.0.1 and [::1] hosts don''t alias each other (#500 remainder)","number":589,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:26:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any change to the bracket-aware Host parsing from PR #544","any change to publicOrigin settings handling or non-loopback Host handling"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.js getRequestOriginCandidates alias branches","packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.test.js cross-IP alias tests"]},"tests":["targeted security tests (packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.test.js) run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''loopback alias'', ''origin alias'', ''request-security origin'' and ''[::1]'' returned only #500 (the dead [::1] branch defect, fixed by PR #544) \u2014 its tests pin only the localhost-IP directions, not IP-to-IP. No open or closed issue covers the cross-IP alias gap.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:26:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Loopback origin aliases are incomplete: 127.0.0.1 and [::1] Host spellings do not alias each other, so cross-IP loopback origins are rejected (#500 remainder).","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.js on main 0f6a93a52 \u2014 localhost branch adds 127.0.0.1 and [::1] aliases; the 127.0.0.1/[::1] branch adds only the localhost alias","Laptop probe this run (createRequestSecurityRuntime, empty settings store, port 3000): origin 127.0.0.1 + host [::1] -> false; origin [::1] + host 127.0.0.1 -> false; the four localhost-involving directions -> true","packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.test.js \u2014 alias tests cover [::1]-host with [::1]/localhost origins and localhost-host with [::1] origin; no IP-to-IP case"],"acceptance":["Origin http://[::1]:3000 with Host 127.0.0.1:3000 is allowed","Origin http://127.0.0.1:3000 with Host [::1]:3000 is allowed","Cross-IP alias directions also work without a port","https://evil.example.com stays rejected for every loopback Host spelling","request-security.test.js covers both IP-to-IP directions; existing alias and parsing tests keep passing","No change to PR #544 bracket-aware Host parsing or the publicOrigin settings path"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/589","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/500","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/544"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Fail-closed correctness gap in the origin check: legitimate local requests are rejected in two of six loopback directions, the same user-facing failure class #500 set out to remove. No security weakening (non-loopback origins unaffected). Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:589', '2026-10-27 18:26:18.009306+00', '2026-10-27 19:12:44.544567+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1528, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): hard_break placement corrupts headings / drops breaks on save — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1492","title":"id(web): a hard_break inside a heading corrupts on save \u2014 the heading splits, a literal backslash appears and doubles on the next save; hard_breaks at block ends and in a break-only paragraph are silently dropped","number":1492,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:26:48Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Parse-direction softbreak handling (#981, closed \u2014 authored softbreaks joining is comrak-consistent)","Edge whitespace in text runs (#1420, different node/direction)","Mid-paragraph and table-cell hard_break behavior (#1017 \u2014 works, must stay unchanged)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs json_to_ast hard_break placement policy","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs regression tests for the six probed placements"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (via CI)","pkgs/id CI checks on the fix PR"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list across all states with keyword searches ''hard_break heading'' (no matches) and ''hard break'' (only #1406 goto-line counting, CLOSED #1200 PM-extensions feature, CLOSED #981 softbreak-join \u2014 none covers hard_break node placement on save). #1420 covers edge whitespace in TEXT RUNS lost on REOPEN; this is the hard_break NODE corrupted/dropped on SAVE \u2014 different node, direction, and root cause (unconditional LineBreak mapping at markdown.rs:1385). Verified fresh this run on main a1321fd5.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:26:48Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The codec''s save direction emits comrak LineBreak for every PM hard_break regardless of placement (markdown.rs:1385); in single-line blocks (headings) and at block edges that rendering cannot reparse as a break, so saves corrupt headings and silently drop breaks.","evidence":["Probe on main a1321fd5 (verbatim markdown.rs sha256 f0b6b9cdd67dd9bd31624b80ada92e6627fe086f82beab1c2e00217b28dbf7dd on both sides, comrak 0.56.0, compiled and run on the laptop per the no-sandbox-build rule), hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneA-1315/out3.log: heading [a, hard_break, b] -> OUT1 ''# a\\'' + newline + ''b''; reopen PM2 heading text ''a\\'' with b as a separate paragraph; OUT2 ''# a\\\\'' (backslash doubled), OUT3 stable; heading [hard_break, b] mirrors it (''## \\'' -> ''## \\\\'')","Same probe, out2.log + out3.log: heading [a, hard_break] -> ''## a'' (break dropped); paragraph [text, hard_break] -> ''before'' (break dropped); paragraph [hard_break] followed by paragraph x -> saved file is ''x'' only (whole paragraph deleted on save); controls: paragraph [hard_break, text] round-trips exactly (''\\'' + newline + ''after''), mid-paragraph breaks unaffected","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1385 \u2014 save arm ''hard_break'' => NodeValue::LineBreak with no placement check; contrast the MisplacedNode guard (markdown.rs:47-56, #1043) which rejects block/inline misplacement rather than emitting invalid markdown"],"acceptance":["A placement policy for hard_break is picked and pinned in the codec: breaks inside a heading and at block edges are either preserved across open-save-open or normalized at save so the first saved file is already a byte fixpoint and no backslash ever appears as literal heading text","The heading cases never split the heading or demote its trailing text to a paragraph","The break-only paragraph case is explicitly decided (round-trips as an empty paragraph, or dropped at save by the documented policy), not silently deleted as an emergent renderer effect","Regression tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs cover break mid-heading, at heading start, at heading end, at paragraph end, break-only paragraph, and the paragraph-start control; mid-paragraph break behavior (#1017 cell case included) is unchanged","Existing web::markdown tests pass in CI"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1492","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1420","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1017","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:1385","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.test.ts:137"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Every open-save-open cycle on a document with a break in a heading visibly mangles it (split heading, stray doubling backslash, demoted text), and trailing/break-only breaks vanish silently \u2014 silent data corruption in the editor''s core save path, in the standing pkgs/id focus. Fix is small once triage pins the placement policy.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'cancelled', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1492', '2026-10-27 18:27:22.88585+00', '2026-10-27 18:31:58.242637+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1529, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: support external fields as when targets with boolean semantics (#601)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/601","title":"fix(core): Form validateFields rejects a when referencing an earlier external field \u2014 and reports it as ''must reference an earlier field''","number":601,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the unconditional external-acknowledgement requirement in validateAnswer (pinned behavior, form.test.ts:288+)","any change to which answers are valid for existing creatable forms"],"include":["packages/core/src/form.ts validateFields/validateWhen treatment of external fields (register external targets as boolean-typed)","packages/schema/src/form.ts When documentation only if a clarification sentence is needed","tests in packages/core/test/form.test.ts pinning the chosen behavior"]},"tests":["bun test for form from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up fix packet enqueued by triage task 1459 on issue #601; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:601 is the fix identity, distinct from the triage task 1459 which is completing.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"validateFields rejects a when condition referencing an earlier external field with a factually wrong message, contradicting the schema When doc, the duplicate-key treatment of external fields in the same loop, and the runtime''s coherent boolean evaluation of the external acknowledgement.","evidence":["Verified on main e73d850df8 (triage task 1459, 2026-10-27): packages/core/src/form.ts validateFields loop does `if (field.type === \"external\") continue` before `earlier.set(field.key, field)`, so external fields never enter the earlier map and validateWhen has no external branch","packages/core/src/form.ts validateAnswer: an external field''s answer must be exactly true (`value !== true` returns ''External form field must be acknowledged''), so the runtime value a when condition compares against is boolean","packages/core/src/form.ts matches(): `value === when.value` against answer[when.key] evaluates a boolean condition on the external acknowledgement coherently","packages/schema/src/form.ts When doc (lines 25-34): ''key must reference a field defined earlier in the form''s field list'' and ''value must match the referenced field''s type'' \u2014 no external exception stated","packages/core/test/form.test.ts pinned test: duplicate key where the first field is external returns ''Duplicate form field key: a'' \u2014 external fields count as defined for the duplicate check in the same loop"],"acceptance":["A form whose earlier field is external and whose later field has when {key: <external>, op: eq, value: true} passes validateFields / create (no ''must reference an earlier field'' error)","A when referencing an external target with a non-boolean value is rejected with ''Form field condition value must be a boolean'' (same wording as boolean targets)","Runtime behavior pinned by test: answers validate coherently against a form with an external-referencing when (external acknowledgement remains unconditionally required in validateAnswer)","Existing form tests still pass, including the pinned duplicate-key-counts-external test and the unconditional external-acknowledgement tests","The schema When doc remains accurate without an external exception (support direction), or is clarified to state external targets compare against the boolean acknowledgement"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/601"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Low priority (priority/low on #601): an authoring-time rejection with a misleading message for a niche form shape; the pinned support direction is small and contract-consistent.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:601', '2026-10-27 18:33:03.350317+00', '2026-10-27 19:29:22.77188+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1531, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): saveFile decodes dataset.docId — %-filenames save under wrong name or never save — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1494","title":"id(web): saveFile decodes the wrong dataset field \u2014 files with % in their name save under a different name, or can never save at all (URIError wedges AutoSaveManager in ''saving'')","number":1494,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:37:54Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The header-subtitle innerHTML sink (#1457)","AutoSaveManager concurrency/stale-completion semantics (#1440) beyond the throwing-saveFn settle","Server-side save_handler name validation (defense there is optional, not required)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts saveFile filename sourcing","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts AutoSaveManager triggerSave exception settle","pkgs/id/web unit tests for %-names and throwing saveFn"]},"tests":["bunx vitest run on the web unit tests covering saveFile/AutoSaveManager (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for decodeURIComponent / percent filename save / saveFile docId: only #1457 (subtitle innerHTML sink \u2014 different path), #1423 (link destination %09 corruption in the markdown codec \u2014 different module), #908 closed (/blob filename param). Backlog checked: Lane A/B recent filings cover codec, aggregator, highlight, templates pagination, world, autosave concurrency (#1440) \u2014 no saveFile dataset-field filing exists.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:37:54Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"saveFile decodeURIComponent''s dataset.docId, which the server only HTML-escapes (never URL-encodes): %XX names save under the decoded wrong name, and bare-% names throw URIError outside any try/catch, wedging AutoSaveManager in ''saving'' so no save (autosave or manual) can ever succeed.","evidence":["Laptop Bun + happy-dom probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-docid/out.log): exact templates.rs attribute string parsed by a real DOM; verbatim main.ts:1305-1306 -> a%20b.md posts ''a b.md'', %41.md posts ''A.md'', caf%C3%A9.md posts ''caf\u00e9.md'', 100%.md/50%off.md throw URIError; AutoSaveManager replica stays in ''saving'' and saveNow early-returns; dataset.filename control correct for all names","Source: templates.rs:418 doc_id_escaped = html_escape only vs :421 name_urlencoded = urlencoding::encode; routes.rs file_by_name_handler passes &name as doc_id; main.ts grep shows saveFile is the only decodeURIComponent consumer reading dataset.docId \u2014 all others read dataset.filename"],"acceptance":["saveFile posts the actual filename for %-names: a%20b.md saves as a%20b.md (not ''a b.md''), %41.md as %41.md, caf%C3%A9.md as caf%C3%A9.md","Saving 100%.md / 50%off.md succeeds: no URIError, a normal /api/save POST with the raw name, AutoSaveManager returns to saved/idle","A saveFn that throws or rejects cannot leave AutoSaveManager in state ''saving'' \u2014 triggerSave settles into an error/unsaved state and a later saveNow() can retry","Regression tests cover a %XX name, a bare-% name, and a throwing saveFn leaving the manager retryable; plain-name saves (notes.md, ''a b.md'', r\u00e9sum\u00e9.md) unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1494","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1440","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1457","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:1305-1306","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:121-127","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:1195-1196","pkgs/id/src/web/templates.rs:418-421","pkgs/id/src/web/templates.rs:486-487","pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs:1195"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Saving is the editor''s core action: for %-filenames it silently overwrites a different file''s tag (server trusts req.name) or fails permanently with the save UI wedged in ''saving'', losing the user''s edits on reload.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1494', '2026-10-27 18:38:47.241753+00', '2026-10-27 18:38:47.241753+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1532, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: weightLayers reports oldest selection instead of most recent (#628)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/628","title":"fix(core): route_stats weightLayers reports the oldest selection in the window, not the most recent \u2014 memberOf overwrites while iterating newest-first decisions","number":628,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:39:26Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing decisionRows ordering or the route_decision storage","the layers recorded by nextTarget/tracedWeightOf (correct as recorded)","route_stats display formatting"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-review.ts memberOf weightLayers selection (keep first found under the production order) plus the ordering-contract doc comment","regression tests in packages/core/test/model-route-review.test.ts with multiple layer-carrying decisions in newest-first order"]},"tests":["bun test for model-route-review and model-route-log from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for weightLayers / ''weight layers most recent'' / quota snapshot returned only the parent feature #589 (closed, implemented) \u2014 no open or closed issue covers the ordering bug","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:39:26Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"memberOf overwrites weightLayers for every decision while iterating the newest-first production feed, so route_stats reports the oldest selection''s per-layer weights instead of the most recent.","evidence":["packages/core/src/model-route-review.ts:71-73 \u2014 Member.weightLayers doc: ''from the most recent selection it was a candidate in''","packages/core/src/model-route-review.ts:231-235 \u2014 memberOf overwrites weightLayers on every decision that carries layers for the target","packages/core/src/model-route-log.ts:630-643 \u2014 decisionRows documented ''newest first'', orderBy desc(RouteDecisionTable.time); the only production caller (route-stats.ts:75) feeds it straight to summarize","packages/core/src/model-route-review.ts:33-41 \u2014 Decision carries no timestamp, so summarize cannot reorder; the ordering contract is implicit and unpinned","Probe (laptop, real module, main e73d850df8): newest-first decisions with base 99/50/1 -> weightLayers.base = 1 (oldest); oldest-first -> 99","packages/core/test/model-route-review.test.ts:179-195 \u2014 the #589 test uses a single decision, so overwrite ordering is untested"],"acceptance":["With decisions supplied in the production (newest-first, decisionRows) order, weightLayers is the attribution from the first (most recent) decision that carries layers for the target; a later-in-list decision never overwrites it","A decision without layers for the target does not clear or replace an attribution already found (pre-#589 rows keep the fall-through behaviour)","The ordering contract summarize relies on is stated where it is consumed (doc comment on summarize/memberOf or on Decision)","New regression test: at least two decisions carrying different layers for the same target, supplied newest-first, asserting the newest one''s layers are reported; the existing single-decision test passes unchanged","All existing model-route-review and model-route-log tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/628","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/589"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"route_stats prints these layers as the explanation of a member''s current weighting; whenever weights changed mid-window (schedule, learned adjustment, demotion) the tool silently explains the stale oldest weights \u2014 the exact case #589 attribution was built to diagnose. Bounded one-function fix plus a regression test. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:628', '2026-10-27 18:40:40.591334+00', '2026-10-27 19:34:44.721198+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1533, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: QuotaSnapshot daily rule rolls out-of-range times over (#629)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/629","title":"fix(core): QuotaSnapshot daily reset rule rolls out-of-range times over \u2014 ''daily 25:99 UTC'' yields a fabricated reset instead of null","number":629,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:41:55Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["validating resetRule at plan upsert time (a separate design question)","the explicit resetAt parsing itself, beyond the decide-and-pin question in the issue body","staleness/percent derivation in the same module"],"include":["range validation of the daily rule components in packages/core/src/quota-snapshot.ts resetAtOf","regression tests in packages/core/test/quota-snapshot.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test for quota-snapshot from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for ''QuotaSnapshot resetRule daily'' and ''quota snapshot'' returned only the parent feature #588 (closed, implemented) \u2014 no issue covers out-of-range daily components","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:41:55Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"QuotaSnapshot.resetAtOf never range-checks the daily reset rule''s hour/minute, so out-of-range components roll over via setUTCHours into a fabricated reset instant instead of the documented null.","evidence":["packages/core/src/quota-snapshot.ts:63-66 \u2014 daily rule regex admits hours 24-99 and minutes 60-99; captures go straight into setUTCHours, which rolls overflow over","packages/core/src/quota-snapshot.ts:53-56 \u2014 module contract: anything without a single derivable instant ''yields null rather than a guess''","packages/core/src/model-plan.ts:36 \u2014 QuotaWindow.resetRule is a free-form Schema.String; no upstream validation exists","Probe (laptop, real module, main e73d850df8, now=2026-10-27T12:00Z): ''daily 25:99 UTC'' -> 2026-10-28T02:39:00Z; ''daily 12:60 UTC'' -> 2026-10-27T13:00:00Z; controls ''daily 23:59 UTC'' -> 2026-10-27T23:59Z and ''daily 00:00 UTC'' -> 2026-10-28T00:00Z correct","packages/core/test/quota-snapshot.test.ts:94-122 \u2014 existing tests cover only a well-formed daily rule; no out-of-range case"],"acceptance":["A daily rule whose hour is > 23 or whose minute is > 59 yields resetAt: null (no rollover): e.g. ''daily 25:99 UTC'', ''daily 12:60 UTC'', ''daily 24:30 UTC'' at any now","Well-formed daily rules are unchanged, including next-occurrence behaviour when today''s time has passed, and single-digit hours (''daily 9:05 UTC'')","The explicit-resetAt and rolling/free-text paths are unchanged; the past-explicit-resetAt question in the issue body is decided and pinned by a test either way","New regression tests in packages/core/test/quota-snapshot.test.ts pin the out-of-range cases; all existing quota-snapshot tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/629","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/588"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Snapshots are the single quota signal for the #587 consumers (#566/#567/#568, not yet reading them), so the impact is latent but the fix is one range check: a mistyped or model-written rule currently produces a plausible wrong reset time instead of failing visibly as null. Low priority, xs effort.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:629', '2026-10-27 18:42:20.678785+00', '2026-10-27 20:25:15.011833+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1534, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): blockquote splits in two on save after a no-info code block — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1496","title":"id(web): saving a blockquote splits it in two when a no-info code block is followed by more quoted content \u2014 everything after the block leaves the quote","number":1496,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The lone-block fence->indent rewrite itself (#954) and quote-leading blank lines (#1002), except where the chosen fix overlaps","Parse direction (markdown_to_prosemirror) \u2014 verified correct"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs save direction (prosemirror_to_markdown, json_to_ast code_block/blockquote construction) and its round-trip tests","Coordination call with #954: shared fix vs standalone workaround"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for blockquote/code/comrak terms before filing: #954 covers the fence->indented rewrite for lone blocks and asserts fixpoint stability (contradicted by the trailing-content cases); #1002 covers leading blank lines when a quote starts with a non-paragraph block and its not-first control holds only at quote end. Neither covers following content being ejected / the quote splitting. Backlog checked.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"prosemirror_to_markdown (via comrak format_commonmark) renders a no-info code block inside a blockquote as an indented block and drops the quote prefix for every following sibling, so the saved file parses back as two blockquotes.","evidence":["Laptop verbatim-codec probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneA-codec/all-out.log, cases in probe-main5.rs): mid-fence-nolang-then-para/list/heading/two-paras and two-fences-in-quote all reopen with a DIFFERENT PM structure (two blockquotes); mid-fence-lang-then-para byte-identical and stable; mid-table/mid-hr controls stable","Raw comrak 0.56 parse -> format_commonmark of the same input reproduces the ejection exactly (probe-main4.rs run), isolating the mechanism to the renderer the save direction relies on; markdown_to_prosemirror output verified correct (blockquote[paragraph, code_block, paragraph])"],"acceptance":["Round-trip tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs: blockquote with a no-info fenced code block followed by (a) a paragraph, (b) a list, (c) a heading, (d) a second code block \u2014 each reopens to the same ProseMirror structure as the opened document (one blockquote, all blocks inside)","The ```rust mid-quote control and the table/thematic-break mid-quote controls still round-trip as today","If the fix lands via #954, the trailing-content cases are in its test set and #1496 closes by reference; a standalone save-direction workaround is equally acceptable","Existing web::markdown tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1496","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/954","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1002","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs (prosemirror_to_markdown / json_to_ast / format_commonmark save path)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent structural corruption on a no-edit open/save: quote attribution breaks and the saved document no longer matches what the user wrote; worse than the formatting drift in #954/#1002 (both priority/low) because the document model itself changes.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1496', '2026-10-27 18:45:42.475329+00', '2026-10-27 18:45:42.475329+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1535, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(routes): parse bindingRevision strictly in GitHub and GitLab read routes (#592)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/592","title":"fix(routes): bindingRevision query param is judged loosely \u2014 1e3, 0x10, 2.0 and empty all reinterpret to a valid revision in GitHub and GitLab read routes (#554 remainder)","number":592,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:53:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the across-repositories references path (JSON body contexts)","any change to binding-service validateAuthority semantics","any other route''s numeric parsing"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/github/routes.js validateReadContext bindingRevision parsing","packages/web/server/lib/gitlab/routes.js validateReadContext bindingRevision parsing","regression tests for both providers'' read-context validation"]},"tests":["targeted route/binding tests run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''bindingRevision'', ''binding revision'', ''read context'' and ''validateReadContext'' returned no issue covering this parameter; #554 (closed) enumerated page/number/limit sites only and its fix PR #558 did not touch the bindingRevision conversions.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"bindingRevision query param is judged loosely in both source-control read routes: 1e3, 0x10, 2.0, padded/signed spellings and empty all reinterpret to a valid revision (#554 remainder).","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/github/routes.js:436 and packages/web/server/lib/gitlab/routes.js:377 \u2014 bindingRevision: Number(req.query?.bindingRevision)","packages/web/server/lib/source-control/binding-service.js:434-441 \u2014 validateAuthority judges the converted number (Number.isInteger + >= 0, then exact equality with current.revision)","Laptop probe this run (~/git/fleet/probe-bindingrev/probe.mjs): ''2.0'', '' 2 '', ''+2'' -> 2 pass gate; ''1e3'' -> 1000; ''0x10'' -> 16; '''' -> 0; ''2.9''/''10junk''/missing fail the gate"],"acceptance":["?bindingRevision=1e3 is refused even when the current revision is 1000","?bindingRevision=0x10 is refused even when the current revision is 16","?bindingRevision=2.0, '' 2 '' and +2 are refused even when the current revision is 2","?bindingRevision= (empty) is refused even when the current revision is 0","?bindingRevision=0 and plain decimal revisions validate exactly as before in both providers","Regression tests cover both the GitHub and GitLab validateReadContext paths; the across-repositories JSON-body path is unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/592","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/554"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"bindingRevision is the staleness/authority token for source-control reads; reinterpreted spellings weaken its exact-match contract, and the empty-string-to-0 case validates where a missing parameter is refused. Same defect class as #554. Normal priority: the legitimate UI client always sends plain decimals.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:592', '2026-10-27 18:54:48.238248+00', '2026-10-27 20:24:07.308184+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1536, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(security): add [::1] to the dev-mode loopback helpers (#594)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/591","title":"fix(security): complete the loopback origin alias set (#589)","number":591,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/594","title":"fix(security): dev-mode loopback helpers omit [::1] \u2014 isLocalDevClientOrigin and the frame-ancestors dev sources cover localhost/127.0.0.1 only (#589 sibling)","number":594,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["getRequestOriginCandidates alias logic (#589 / PR #591)","the packaged-client origin set","allowsLocalDevOrigins gating","any relaxation of the port requirement in isLocalDevClientOrigin"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.js isLocalDevClientOrigin + buildFrameAncestorsPolicy dev sources","packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.test.js regression tests"]},"tests":["targeted security tests (packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.test.js) run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''dev origins'', ''frame-ancestors'', ''isLocalDevClientOrigin'', ''ALLOW_DEV_ORIGINS'' and ''[::1] dev'' returned no covering issue; #589 covers only getRequestOriginCandidates and its body/acceptance do not mention the dev helpers (noted as left-for-later in the 2026-10-27 13:10 creator backlog entry).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Dev-mode loopback helpers omit [::1]: isLocalDevClientOrigin and the frame-ancestors dev sources cover localhost/127.0.0.1 only (#589 sibling).","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.js:24 \u2014 isLocalDevClientOrigin regex lists localhost|127.0.0.1 only","packages/web/server/lib/security/request-security.js:37 \u2014 dev frame-ancestors sources push 127.0.0.1 and localhost only","Laptop probe this run (~/git/fleet/probe-devloopback/probe.mjs): http://[::1]:5173 -> false, https://[::1]:5173 -> false, localhost/127.0.0.1 -> true, evil.example.com -> false; frame-ancestors dev sources contain no [::1]","packages/web/server/lib/ui-auth/ui-passkeys.js:67 \u2014 isLocalRpId counts ::1 as local, as does the main alias path in the same security file"],"acceptance":["isLocalDevClientOrigin accepts http://[::1]:<port> and https://[::1]:<port>","isLocalDevClientOrigin still rejects non-loopback origins and port-less loopback origins","buildFrameAncestorsPolicy({ allowLocalDevOrigins: true }) includes an [::1] dev source; with dev origins off the policy is byte-identical to today","request-security.test.js pins the [::1] acceptance, a non-loopback rejection, and the [::1] frame-ancestors source","No change to getRequestOriginCandidates (#589/PR #591), packaged client origins, or allowsLocalDevOrigins gating"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/594","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/589","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/591"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Dev-only, opt-in surface (OPENCHAMBER_ELECTRON_DEV / OPENCHAMBER_ALLOW_DEV_ORIGINS): no released-server impact, so low priority; filed because the loopback lists in one security file should agree and IPv6-first localhost resolution makes the gap reachable in normal dev setups.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:594', '2026-10-27 18:57:23.279944+00', '2026-10-27 20:00:42.151598+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe