ame #556, branch queue/1236-556-file-comment; body states both substitution passes use the new shared commented() helper","git show origin/main packages/core/src/config/variable.ts: commented() defined lines 33-37ff, used at env pass ~line 76 and file pass ~line 119 on main e730a678","PR #605 labelled queue/queued by pr-diff-review at filing time, as it is itself the work subject"],"acceptance":["PR #605 is closed (not merged) with a comment citing merged PR #620 and the shared commented() helper on main","The closing comment records the check that #605''s commit 83fc14cd carries nothing #620 lacks, including its trailing-comment test cases","#556 remains closed; no code change is made"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/646","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/605","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/620","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/556"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A stale duplicate PR left open invites an accidental merge that would conflict with and narrow the merged fix; low priority, trivial disposition.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:pr-set:developing-today/opencode:605-620', '2026-10-27 19:35:14.228482+00', '2026-10-27 20:07:53.64069+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1547, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'test(scripts): pin #921 missing-value branch (trailing/empty) in clean/discover/maintain/spotlight suites (#970)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/970","title":"tests: PR #921''s missing-value guards (trailing/empty option value) are unpinned in clean/discover/maintain/spotlight \u2014 #964 pinned only the flag-shaped branch","number":970,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:57:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Any change to the scripts under test or their argument parsers","Changes to other test suites"],"include":["clean.test.sh: trailing + empty-value run per covered option (--path, --depth, --docker-age), exit 2 + option named + no side effects","git-discover-repos.test.sh: same for its covered options","git-maintain-repos.test.sh: same for its covered options (--path, --depth, --jobs, --pack-threads, --reflog-expire)","spotlight-exclude-artifacts.test.sh: same for its covered options"]},"tests":["All four suites pass on an unaffected tree (laptop or CI), including existing flag-shaped and valid-value controls","Ablation: temporarily break the -n check in one script copy \u2014 the new runs fail; restore","nix build .#checks.<system>.clean-tests .#checks.<system>.git-discover-repos-tests .#checks.<system>.git-maintain-repos-tests .#checks.<system>.spotlight-exclude-artifacts-tests (laptop or CI)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1544 after confirming #970; dedupe_key is the issue''s fix key, distinct from the triage key repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:970","checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:57:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The missing/empty-value branch of the #921 guards in four scripts is pinned by no test; a refactor dropping the -n check would pass all four suites while restoring #914''s empty-path full-scan worst case.","evidence":["Triage task 1544 on main a9976ee: guard sites clean.sh:3, git-discover-repos:4, git-maintain-repos:5, spotlight-exclude-artifacts:2 = 14 total","clean.test.sh:52, git-discover-repos.test.sh:93, git-maintain-repos.test.sh:54, spotlight-exclude-artifacts.test.sh:54 \u2014 each suite''s only per-option invocation is run \"$opt\" --dry-run","Behavioral probes (triage): trailing option and empty-string value both exit 2 with ''<script>: <option> requires a value'' on all four scripts","Siblings pin both branches: brew-repair.test.sh scenario F (trailing), opencode-db-args.test.sh:51,56 (empty value)"],"acceptance":["Each of the four suites gains, for every value-taking option it already covers, a trailing-option run and an empty-string-value run, each asserting exit 2, the option named on stderr, and no side effects","Existing flag-shaped and valid-value controls keep passing; suites still run under their existing flake checks"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/970","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/921","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/951","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/964"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Low: guards exist and work today \u2014 only the regression pin for one branch is missing. Bounded test-only change.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:970', '2026-10-27 19:40:56.91041+00', '2026-10-28 00:35:55.401992+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1548, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: JSON stores share one temp path — concurrent writes ENOENT / diverge — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1509","title":"aggregator: concurrent writes to the JSON stores share one temp path \u2014 most fail with ENOENT (returned as ''400 invalid''), and persisted records don''t match the calls that succeeded","number":1509,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:40:31Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The card-state derivation (card-state.ts) \u2014 #1474''s territory","File format changes or a move to a real database","GitHub/Project writes (the aggregator never writes those)"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/comments.ts persist(): unique temp name and/or serialized writes","pm-stack/aggregator/src/actions.ts persist(): same fix","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/live.ts registry write: same fix (stop silently swallowing the collision)","server.ts: persistence failures return 5xx, not 400 invalid","Regression test: >=10 concurrent adds, fulfilled == reloaded"]},"tests":["bun test in pm-stack/aggregator (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)","Concurrent-add probe rerun: all batches fulfill, reloaded counts match"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''aggregator persist concurrent tmp rename'', ''comments store race'', ''aggregator comments actions store'': no filing covers the store persistence race \u2014 nearest are #1474 (card-state rejected-restore derivation, different defect, same app) and the closed dashboard feature issues #1152/#1154/#1450. Backlog checked: today''s lane A/B filings cover codec, world session metrics, petnames, saveFile \u2014 none touches aggregator store persistence.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:40:31Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"CommentsStore, ActionsStore and the live session-registry writer persist via a shared pid-only temp path with no serialization: concurrent writes collide on rename (ENOENT, surfaced as 400), and persisted contents diverge in both directions from the calls that succeeded.","evidence":["Probe on laptop with verbatim tree (Bun 1.4.2): COMMENTS n=20 fulfilled=1 rejected=19 ENOENT rename, reloaded=1; COMMENTS n=20 fulfilled=2 rejected=18, reloaded=19; ACTIONS n=20 fulfilled=2 rejected=18, reloaded=1; ACTIONS n=20 fulfilled=3 rejected=17, reloaded=19 \u2014 log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneA-1435/out.log","Source read on main 931f1771: comments.ts:121, actions.ts:441, sources/live.ts:594 all build the temp path as `${file}.tmp-${process.pid}` with no write serialization; server.ts handlers map any add() throw to 400 invalid comment/action"],"acceptance":["Concurrent add/markTriaged/markGithubResult/markResult calls on one store all fulfill, and a fresh reload returns exactly the records the fulfilled calls wrote \u2014 no ENOENT, no extras, no losses","Temp files are unique per write (or persists are serialized per store) at all three sites: comments.ts, actions.ts, sources/live.ts","A persistence I/O failure is no longer reported to HTTP clients as 400 invalid comment/action (5xx or explicit persistence-error body)","A regression test fires >=10 concurrent adds at a store and asserts fulfilled count == reloaded count","Sequential behaviour unchanged: same file format, same atomic rename publish, same actions clientToken dedupe"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1509","pm-stack/aggregator/src/comments.ts:121","pm-stack/aggregator/src/actions.ts:441","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/live.ts:594","pm-stack/aggregator/src/server.ts:324-332"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The dashboard''s write path loses/erroneously reports writes under ordinary concurrency (two tabs, orchestrator triage/result posts racing a human comment): valid input gets spurious 400s, rejected writes can silently persist (duplicate on retry), and registry/result transitions are silently dropped. Data-integrity defect in the fleet''s triage surface; bounded blast radius (single-host loopback/tailnet service), hence priority/normal.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1509', '2026-10-27 19:41:37.565987+00', '2026-10-28 09:35:21.305093+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1549, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Repo-universe issue tracker: watch every repo we own or depend on, pull its issues into one tracked system', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1511","title":"Repo-universe issue tracker: watch every repo we own or depend on, pull its issues into one tracked system","number":1511,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:41:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["building the full system inside this triage task","changing fleet job scopes before the design is reviewed"],"include":["design for the repo-universe inventory, scheduled issue checker, pull-in surface, and track/resolve workflow","filing the linked implementation issues"]},"tests":["Design posted on #1511 and checked against the issue acceptance criteria","Implementation issues filed and linked from #1511"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Title/keyword search across developing-today/code open+closed issues 2026-10-27 found no existing issue tracking a cross-repo issue-intake system; nearest is #899 (orchestrator triage for the four fleet repos only).","checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:41:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"No system watches GitHub issues outside the four fleet repos; issues in Drew-owned side repos and upstream dependencies go unseen and untracked.","evidence":["2026-10-27 all-repos census: ~146 clones across laptop+sandbox, dozens of nested upstream repos in /home/user/repo-archive","Fleet jobs (creators, monitor, queue) are all scoped to the four home repos only","Filed at Drew''s direction 2026-10-27"],"acceptance":["A design is posted on issue #1511 covering inventory source, checker cadence/mechanism, pull-in surface choice (mirrored issues vs index) with reasoning, and the track/resolve workflow","Implementation issues are filed and linked from #1511 for each buildable piece","The universe list artifact covers every Drew-owned GitHub repo plus census-named upstreams, each classified"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1511","https://github.com/dezren39/hatch-personal/issues/1"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Problems in owned side repos and depended-on upstreams are currently invisible until they bite; the census made the blind spot concrete.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1511', '2026-10-27 19:42:05.15152+00', '2026-10-28 11:01:30.455003+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1552, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: MessagingTemplate.parseTime accepts calendar-invalid dates (#647)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/647","title":"fix(core): MessagingTemplate.parseTime accepts calendar-invalid dates \u2014 Date.parse rolls Feb 30 to Mar 2 instead of Invalid time","number":647,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:41:56Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the quota-reset parsers in model-route-limits.ts / model-route-tuning.ts (already fixed under #609)","the bare-epoch and relative branches of parseTime (fixed under #592 / working)","changing the callers'' Invalid time contract in messaging.ts"],"include":["calendar validation of ISO-shaped inputs in packages/core/src/messaging/template.ts parseTime","regression tests in packages/core/test/messaging-template.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test for messaging-template from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for ''parseTime'' returned only #592 (closed, epoch-seconds scaling in the same function \u2014 a different defect); search for calendar-invalid/Feb 30 returned only the #609 family, whose sites are model-route-limits.ts and model-route-tuning.ts, not parseTime","checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:41:56Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"MessagingTemplate.parseTime trusts a bare Date.parse, so calendar-invalid ISO dates roll over into the next month instead of being rejected as Invalid time by its callers.","evidence":["packages/core/src/messaging/template.ts:504-517 \u2014 parseTime falls back to bare Date.parse and returns it unless NaN; Date.parse rolls overflow days into the next month","Probe (laptop, real module, main b2b2caf2e9, now=2026-10-27T00:00Z): ''2026-02-30'' -> 2026-03-02; ''2026-02-29'' -> 2026-03-01; ''2026-04-31'' -> 2026-05-01; ''2025-02-29T00:00:00Z'' -> 2025-03-01; ''2026-13-01'' -> undefined; controls ''2024-02-29'', ''2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'', ''2h'' correct","packages/core/src/messaging.ts:769-774 (+ :823-824, :1752-1753, :1826-1827) \u2014 callers raise Invalid time only when parseTime returns undefined; a rolled date silently becomes the time_created bound","packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts:48-70 \u2014 parseAbsoluteTime already implements and documents the exact round-trip check for this rollover class (#609)","packages/core/test/messaging-template.test.ts:61-83 \u2014 existing parseTime tests cover epochs, one valid ISO timestamp and a relative form; no calendar-invalid case"],"acceptance":["parseTime returns undefined for calendar-invalid ISO dates: 2026-02-30, 2026-02-29, 2026-04-31, 2025-02-29T00:00:00Z \u2014 so messaging callers raise Invalid time","Valid forms unchanged: leap-valid 2024-02-29, date-only and full ISO timestamps including zone offsets, relative forms (90s/15m/2h/3d/1w), and the 10-digit seconds / 13-digit ms bare epochs from #592","Non-ISO Date.parse forms (e.g. ''Jan 5 2026'') are decided and pinned by a test either way","New regression tests in packages/core/test/messaging-template.test.ts pin the invalid-date cases and valid controls; all existing messaging-template tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/647","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/609","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/592"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"User-facing messaging since/until bounds silently query the wrong day on a common typo class (Feb 29/30, Apr 31), with no error surfaced; the established fix pattern already exists in-repo from #609, so the change is small and low-risk. Normal priority, s effort.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:647', '2026-10-27 19:42:42.597484+00', '2026-10-28 00:30:38.455838+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1554, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'test(vscode-patch): fixture suite for patch-vscode-insiders contracts + path seam (#969)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/969","title":"patch-vscode-insiders: PRs #925/#938 exit-code and write-back contracts have no test \u2014 no suite drives the real script","number":969,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:00:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing the script''s default paths, output text, or patch behavior","Changes to install-vscode-patch-agent or its suite beyond what the new check wiring requires"],"include":["patch-vscode-insiders.sh: minimal override seam (env or arg) for the app/workbench paths, defaulting exactly to the current hardcoded values","patch-vscode-insiders.test.sh: fixture suite covering the acceptance cases against the real script","flake.nix: patch-vscode-insiders-tests check mirroring the existing script-test checks"]},"tests":["Suite passes on the laptop against the real script; second-run mtime/bytes assertion included","Ablations: unconditional write-back makes the mtime case fail; missing-JS exiting 0 makes that case fail","nix build .#checks.<system>.patch-vscode-insiders-tests on laptop or CI (note: laptop nix sandbox has a pre-existing /usr/bin/env gap for some script checks \u2014 compare against main baseline if it bites)","Default-path run with no override behaves byte-identically in output to main''s script on the same fixture (paths retargeted only via the seam)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1543 after confirming #969; fix dedupe_key distinct from triage key repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:969","checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:00:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"patch-vscode-insiders.sh''s write-only-when-changed and missing-target/missing-JS exit-1 contracts (#925/#938) have no committed test; the script''s hardcoded /Applications paths prevent driving the real script against a fixture without a seam.","evidence":["Triage task 1543 on main a9976ee: grep over *.test.sh finds patch-vscode-insiders only in install-vscode-patch-agent.test.sh:38, which writes a stub (printf ''# stub patch script'')","flake.nix:733 wires install-vscode-patch-agent-tests only; no check runs the real patch script","patch-vscode-insiders.sh:7 and :98 hardcode /Applications paths; :84 and :121 write only if content != original; missing-JS branch prints ERROR + Patch 5 target-not-found and sets status=1; exit $status","gh pr view: #925 and #938 each changed only patch-vscode-insiders.sh"],"acceptance":["patch-vscode-insiders.test.sh drives the real script against a fixture app tree via an override seam defaulting to the current /Applications paths","Cases: all patches apply exit 0; second run changes neither bytes nor mtimes exit 0; unrelated CSS/JS exits 1 naming Patch 1, Patch 2, Patch 5; missing JS exits 1 naming Patch 5; missing CSS exits 1","Suite wired as a flake check mirroring existing script-test checks","Default behavior with no override set is unchanged (same hardcoded paths, same output text)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/969","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/925","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/938","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/909","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/931"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Issue carries priority/normal: the script''s exit code is the launchd agent''s only failure signal, and both behavior contracts are currently unpinned.","timebox_minutes":60}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:969', '2026-10-27 19:48:16.129431+00', '2026-10-27 20:16:31.328386+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1559, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'F11.8 slice 2: committed benchmark baselines + re-baseline doc — issue #539', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["bench-baselines"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1512","title":"F11.8 slice 2: committed benchmark baselines + re-baseline doc \u2014 issue #539","number":1512,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["CI regression reporting (slice 3, separate task)","New benchmarks beyond the four from slice 1","F11.7 live metrics (issue #553)"],"include":["Run the four slice-1 benchmarks on a documented reference machine and commit the baseline results in the location/format the harness supports","A re-baseline doc: how baselines were produced, on what hardware, and the exact commands to regenerate them"]},"tests":["benchmarks run via the just recipe from slice 1 and produce the committed baseline outputs"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Slice 2 of the #539 triage decomposition, enqueued once by slice-1 task 1308 at completion; no slice-2 packet existed before.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"F11.8 slice 1 (PR #1387, queue task 1308) added the pkgs/id benchmark harness and four benchmarks (guest replay of N events, journal append+fsync, checkpoint compaction, session fan-out to K clients) with just/nix runners, but no committed baselines exist yet, so benchmark numbers are not comparable across runs or machines.","evidence":["Issue #539 acceptance criteria + triage decomposition (queue task 1262): slice 2 = committed baselines with re-baseline doc","Slice 1 implemented in PR #1387 (branch queue/1308-539-bench-harness @ ace10d6e): pkgs/id/benches + just recipe + nix app","Enqueued by queue task 1308 completion (2026-10-27) per the slice-1 packet''s completion instructions"],"acceptance":["Committed baselines exist for all four slice-1 benchmarks","Re-baseline doc names the hardware, harness version/settings, and regeneration commands","Baselines reproduce approximately (same order of magnitude) when re-run via the just recipe on the same machine","Slice 3 (non-blocking CI regression reporting >20%) enqueued as a follow-up queue task against issue #539 before this task completes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1512","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/539","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1387"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Slice 2 of 3 for F11.8: committed baselines are what slice 3''s CI regression reporting compares against.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1512', '2026-10-27 19:51:26.952711+00', '2026-10-28 04:21:15.527049+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1560, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'F11.8 slice 3: non-blocking CI benchmark regression reporting (>20%) — issue #539', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["depends-on-slice-2","ci"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1513","title":"F11.8 slice 3: non-blocking CI benchmark regression reporting (>20%) \u2014 issue #539","number":1513,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Blocking CI gates on benchmark regressions","The baselines themselves (slice 2)","New benchmarks beyond the four from slice 1"],"include":["CI wiring that runs the four benchmarks on PRs (or a scheduled workflow) and compares against the committed slice-2 baselines","A non-blocking report (PR comment, job summary, or artifact) naming any benchmark regressing >20%; the check must not fail the build on regression alone"]},"tests":["id workflow PR gate (fast lane) still green","Report artifact/comment verified on a test PR or workflow_dispatch run"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Slice 3 of the #539 triage decomposition, enqueued once by slice-1 task 1308 at completion; no slice-3 packet existed before.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"F11.8 slices 1-2 provide the pkgs/id benchmark harness and committed baselines, but nothing reports regressions: a change that makes guest replay, journal append, checkpoint compaction, or session fan-out >20% slower would land unnoticed.","evidence":["Issue #539 acceptance criteria + triage decomposition (queue task 1262): slice 3 = non-blocking CI regression reporting at >20%","Slice 1 implemented in PR #1387 (queue task 1308); slice 2 (committed baselines) enqueued as a separate task and is this slice''s dependency","Enqueued by queue task 1308 completion (2026-10-27) per the slice-1 packet''s completion instructions"],"acceptance":["Gate verified at claim time: slice-2 committed baselines are merged; otherwise park naming the dependency","A run with an artificially slowed benchmark produces a report naming it and its regression percentage","A normal run produces a report with no regressions and all required PR checks stay green (non-blocking)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1513","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/539","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1387"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Slice 3 of 3 for F11.8: closes the loop so the Phase 12 numeric exits stay measured after baselines land.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1513', '2026-10-27 19:51:31.347191+00', '2026-10-28 07:36:49.831458+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1561, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Docs: translated mirrors missing sections on projects, scheduled-tasks, walkthrough (#601)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/601","title":"Docs: translated mirrors are missing whole sections on projects, scheduled-tasks, and walkthrough pages","number":601,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["locales that already carry the section (nl/tr for scheduled-tasks, de/nl/tr for walkthrough)","pages covered by #332 (auto-model-routing) and #339 (install, notes-todos-plans, desktop-browser)","any code or non-docs file"],"include":["packages/docs/content/docs/{de,es,fr,ja,ko,nl,pl,pt-br,tr,uk,zh-cn}/projects.mdx \u2014 add the folders section","packages/docs/content/docs/{de,es,fr,ja,ko,pl,pt-br,uk,zh-cn}/scheduled-tasks.mdx \u2014 add the Loops section","packages/docs/content/docs/{es,fr,ja,ko,pl,pt-br,uk,zh-cn}/walkthrough.mdx \u2014 add the first section"]},"tests":["docs:validate / heading-count sweep over the three pages after the change (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches for ''projects.mdx'', ''scheduled-tasks'', ''walkthrough'' and ''translated mirrors'' returned only #332 (auto-model-routing) and #339 (install/notes-todos-plans/desktop-browser); neither covers these three pages. Heading sweep re-run this run over all docs pages.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Translated mirrors missing whole sections on projects, scheduled-tasks, and walkthrough pages.","evidence":["packages/docs/content/docs/projects.mdx:30 \u2014 ''Group sessions in folders'' (English 6 sections, 60 lines); de/projects.mdx has 5 sections, 48 lines, jumping :24 -> :30 (Project environment)","packages/docs/content/docs/scheduled-tasks.mdx:26 \u2014 ''Loops: scheduled tasks as markdown files'' spans :26-:67 (English 78 lines); de/scheduled-tasks.mdx is 35 lines with 4 sections; nl/scheduled-tasks.mdx:26 carries the section","packages/docs/content/docs/walkthrough.mdx:14 \u2014 ''How a stop is marked'' is the first English section; es/walkthrough.mdx has 7 sections, 71 lines vs 85 English, starting at ''What it can review''"],"acceptance":["projects.mdx: all 11 mirrors gain ''Group sessions in folders'' in the English position; every mirror reaches 6 ## sections","scheduled-tasks.mdx: de,es,fr,ja,ko,pl,pt-br,uk,zh-cn gain the Loops section after ''Create a task''; every mirror reaches 5 ## sections; nl/tr untouched","walkthrough.mdx: es,fr,ja,ko,pl,pt-br,uk,zh-cn gain ''How a stop is marked'' as the first section; every mirror reaches 8 ## sections; de/nl/tr untouched","Translations follow each mirror''s existing terminology on the same page; no other sections or pages change","A heading-count sweep over the three pages shows no deficit in any locale after the change"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/601","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/332","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/339"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Docs-only gap, no code or runtime impact, so low priority; the scheduled-tasks Loops section is over half that page and the projects section is missing in every locale, so it should not stay invisible.","timebox_minutes":120}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:601', '2026-10-27 19:55:45.000455+00', '2026-10-28 02:18:31.155976+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1562, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'refactor(github-routes): remove always-true canonical flag / dead legacy branches (#602)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/602","title":"refactor(github-routes): eight read handlers carry an always-true canonical flag \u2014 the retired legacy branches (incl. loose Number number parsing) are dead code","number":602,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:05:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["githubAuthRoutePaths dual registration (genuinely live on both paths)","the canonical mutation executor","any route registration change","GitLab routes"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/github/routes.js \u2014 the eight handlers: pr/status, repo/upstream, repo/branches, issues/list, issues/get, issues/comments, pulls/list, pulls/context"]},"tests":["GitHub route suites (routes.test.js, routes.auth.test.js, routes.aliases.test.js, routes.mutations.test.js) on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh searches for ''retired legacy GitHub'', ''dead code github routes'', ''canonical dead branch'' and ''non-canonical'' returned no covering issue; #554/#558 fixed live parsing only, #592 covers bindingRevision.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:05:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Always-true canonical flag and dead legacy branches in eight GitHub read handlers.","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/github/routes.js:26 \u2014 canonicalGitHubRoutePath returns only /api/source-control/github<suffix>; handler registrations at :1688/:1974/:2067/:2469/:2651/:2743/:2821/:3028 are canonical-only","packages/web/server/lib/github/routes.js:308-313 \u2014 legacy /api/github twins of exactly these routes answer 410 via retireLegacyResourceRoute (suffix lists :27-31)","packages/web/server/lib/github/routes.js:2656 and :2748 \u2014 canonical ? readPositiveIntegerQuery(...) : Number(requestedNumber) \u2014 the loose side is unreachable","routes.auth.test.js expects 410 for the legacy paths (:195/:261/:411/:436/:731/:733/:939/:1157/:1159/:1161); routes.mutations.test.js:1034 likewise"],"acceptance":["The canonical flag and unreachable non-canonical branches are removed from the eight handlers; canonical behaviour is the only behaviour","No route registration changes: canonical paths behave exactly as before and legacy /api/github paths still answer 410 SOURCE_CONTROL_CONTEXT_REQUIRED","The loose Number(requestedNumber) expressions in issues/get and issues/comments are gone; number is read only via readPositiveIntegerQuery","GitHub route suites (routes.test.js, routes.auth.test.js, routes.aliases.test.js, routes.mutations.test.js) pass with no test deleted","Scope is the eight handlers only; githubAuthRoutePaths dual registration and the mutation executor are untouched"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/602","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/554"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Dead-code / audit-clarity issue with no live behaviour defect, so low priority; filed because the dead branches preserve the retired unbound behaviour in source and forced re-derivation during the #554/#592 audits.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:602', '2026-10-27 20:00:33.259978+00', '2026-10-27 20:03:37.860609+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1563, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(world-manifest): plan/diff seed + ceiling misreports — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1519","title":"id(world-manifest): plan/diff misreport seed and ceiling \u2014 a seed-only change reports ''no drift'' and is never applied, while a ceiling reorder reports drift that grants (set-compared) ignore","number":1519,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The #818 CLI-wiring fabricated-state problem","Omitted-field semantics settled by #817","Any change to the manifest TOML format"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/world_manifest.rs plan(): seed-only reconciliation ruling + implementation","pkgs/id/src/world_manifest.rs plan(): set-based ceiling comparison","world_manifest module tests for both behaviours"]},"tests":["cargo test world_manifest module (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''module_hash empty'', ''manifest seed drift'', ''ceiling order'', ''world diff no drift seed'': only #818 (OPEN, CLI wiring fabricates seed=0/empty-schedules current state \u2014 distinct layer, this defect reproduces in pure plan() against a correct hand-built state), #817 (CLOSED, omitted-field semantics), #807/#556/#534 (feature epics). Backlog checked: no world_manifest filing exists; Lane A''s same-phase areas (aggregator persist #1509, joined-metrics #1506) deliberately avoided.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"plan()/diff() report ''no drift'' for a seed-only change (never applied) and report drift for a ceiling reorder that is semantically empty, while the grants comparison in the same function is set-based.","evidence":["Laptop probe crate compiling the real world_manifest.rs + world_caps.rs (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-manifest/out.log + main.rs): CASE2 seed-only 99 vs 7 -> steps=[] diff=''no drift''; CASE3 ceiling order-only -> [SetCeiling]; CASE3b grants order-only -> []; CASE5 schedule-add control -> [ScheduleAt]","Source contrast in one function: plan() compares grants via BTreeSet (world_manifest.rs:231-240) but ceiling via ordered slice (:242-249); seed enters plan only inside the InstallModule branch (:207-218) despite WorldState.seed being part of the compared projection (:63-64)"],"acceptance":["A seed-only difference produces an explicit reconciliation outcome (reinstall step, or surfaced as unreconcilable-without-reinstall drift) pinned by a test; ''no drift'' for a differing seed is not an accepted outcome","Ceiling comparison is set-based like grants: reordering the same ceiling names yields an empty plan; a genuinely different ceiling still yields SetCeiling","Tests cover seed-only diff, ceiling reorder (no step), ceiling set change (step); grants behaviour unchanged","cargo test for the world_manifest module passes; apply_is_idempotent and the #817 regression tests still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1519","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/818","pkgs/id/src/world_manifest.rs:63-64","pkgs/id/src/world_manifest.rs:207-218","pkgs/id/src/world_manifest.rs:231-249"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"diff is the admin''s drift oracle for the declarative world manifest: a false ''no drift'' silently strands a seed change (the seed drives the program''s deterministic initializer), and order-noise drift trains admins to ignore diff output.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1519', '2026-10-27 20:03:04.022569+00', '2026-10-28 11:06:27.505342+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1564, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'refactor(github-routes): remove always-true canonical flag / dead legacy branches (#602)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/602","title":"refactor(github-routes): eight read handlers carry an always-true canonical flag \u2014 the retired legacy branches (incl. loose Number number parsing) are dead code","number":602,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:10:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["githubAuthRoutePaths dual registration (:22, registrations :1326+) \u2014 genuinely live on both paths","The mutation executor / runCanonicalMutation path","Any route registration change or behaviour change"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/github/routes.js: the eight read handlers'' canonical flag and non-canonical branches only"]},"tests":["GitHub route suites on laptop or CI, not the sandbox: routes.test.js, routes.auth.test.js, routes.aliases.test.js, routes.mutations.test.js","check:changed on laptop / CI pr checks"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1562 re-verified the issue verbatim on current main 1ebb8577 (routes.js identical to the issue''s verified base 67d7e88ed); #602 is the single tracking issue and this is its fix packet","checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:10:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Eight GitHub read handlers carry an always-true canonical flag, so their unreachable non-canonical branches (unvalidated read context, loose Number parsing, empty-result fallbacks) persist as misleading, resurrectable dead code.","evidence":["routes.js:1694/1977/2072/2474/2655/2747/2826/3035 \u2014 const canonical = req.path.startsWith(''/api/source-control/'') in all eight handlers; 164 total ''canonical'' occurrences in the file","routes.js:26 canonicalGitHubRoutePath returns only /api/source-control/github<suffix>; the eight handlers register only through it (:1688, :1974, :2067, :2469, :2651, :2743, :2821, :3028)","routes.js:27-30 retiredLegacyGitHubGetRoutes lists exactly the eight suffixes; :312-313 registers them under /api/github to retireLegacyResourceRoute answering 410 SOURCE_CONTROL_CONTEXT_REQUIRED (:310)","routes.js:2656 and :2748 \u2014 canonical ? readPositiveIntegerQuery(req, ''number'') : requestedNumber ? Number(requestedNumber) : null (loose branch unreachable)","routes.js:1698/1981/2079/2478/2665/2757/2830/3047 \u2014 if (canonical && !trustedContext) guards in all eight handlers; fallbacks at :2012 (defaultBranch = canonical ? null : ''main''), :2551-2558 (reposToQuery[0] fallback, if (!canonical) issues branch)","routes.auth.test.js:195/261/411/436/731 pin legacy /api/github paths at 410; routes.mutations.test.js:1034 likewise"],"acceptance":["In the eight handlers, the canonical flag and its unreachable non-canonical branches are removed; canonical behaviour is the only behaviour","No route registration changes: canonical paths behave exactly as before and every legacy /api/github path still answers 410 SOURCE_CONTROL_CONTEXT_REQUIRED","The loose Number(requestedNumber) expressions in issues/get and issues/comments are gone; number is read only via readPositiveIntegerQuery","GitHub route test suites (routes.test.js, routes.auth.test.js, routes.aliases.test.js, routes.mutations.test.js) pass with no test deleted","Scope is routes.js''s eight handlers only: githubAuthRoutePaths dual registration and the mutation executor are untouched"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/602","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/554","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/592"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Behaviour-preserving dead-code removal in a security-adjacent file; low priority as filed, but the dead unvalidated branches are a resurrection and audit-confusion risk.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:602', '2026-10-27 20:03:25.807682+00', '2026-10-28 00:37:57.035716+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1565, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'atlas backups: canonical local atlas.db has no routine backup; nightly Turso atlas dump times out — triage (HIGH, Drew order 2026-10-27)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["data-loss-exposure","privacy-local-only-content","depends-on-flake-backup-service"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1515","title":"atlas backups: canonical local atlas.db has no routine backup (gitignored, ad-hoc copies only); nightly Turso atlas dump times out","number":1515,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:05:00Z"},"queue":"repo-health-code-pilot","scope":{"exclude":["implementing the snapshot routine or the export fix in this triage task","publishing or copying the local-only chunks to Turso (Drew''s standing decision \u2014 off-machine snapshots go to the private Drive/R2 backup stores only)","interrupting or restarting the running Qwen3 embedding pass on the laptop","the sandbox/laptop general backup setup itself (owned by the flake/init work under #1516)"],"include":["issue #1515 and umbrella audit #1516","cold-store-nightly-backup job definition + the Turso export path it runs (code repo pkgs/cold-store-reaper scripts)","~/hatch-personal/workspace/turso-atlas/data/ (canonical DB, snapshots, gitignore rules) \u2014 read-only inspection","coordination refs: #1514 (sibling gap, in hand), dezren39/nix#976 (flake backup service)"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-ups must run (nightly job dry-run/export of the atlas DB end-to-end with timing; sqlite3 integrity_check on a restored snapshot; freshness-check output)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"agent.tasks queried 2026-10-27T20:1xZ for dedupe_key like ''%1515%'' \u2014 zero rows; issue #1515 was filed by the backup audit today with no queue labels and no packet; its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:05:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Two compounding backup failures for the atlas corpus: (1) the canonical local atlas.db is gitignored, so the every-minute hatch-personal autocommit never covers it; its only copies are ad-hoc and same-disk, and the local-only content (6,941 chunks / 2,226 sessions, never published to Turso by Drew''s decision) exists nowhere else. (2) The nightly cold-store Turso atlas export fails on a 300 s download timeout at ~525 MB, so even the published half has no successful off-machine filing evidenced.","evidence":["Issue #1515 (backup audit 2026-10-27, verified firsthand): canonical DB ~/hatch-personal/workspace/turso-atlas/data/atlas.db, 1.49 GB, modified 2026-10-27 02:07; gitignored via hatch-personal .gitignore lines 33 and 48 (workspace/turso-atlas/data/*.db.gz, workspace/turso-atlas/data/**/*.db)","Only copies: sandbox atlas-2026-10-25.db.gz / atlas-2026-10-26.db.gz (same disk) and laptop ~/atlas/atlas-2026-10-26.db \u2014 no routine, no off-machine copy of the canonical DB","cold-store-nightly-backup 2026-10-27 03:12 CDT run: D1 OK, Supabase filed OK, 3 of 4 Turso DBs filed to Drive; atlas FAILED \u2014 curl: (28) Operation timed out after 300001 milliseconds with 524901755 bytes received; turso export: ERROR: atlas: dump download failed","Laptop ~/atlas/v3/ embedding DBs (incl. the Qwen3 pass, ~113h of compute) also unbacked; rebuildable from corpus.db only at full recompute cost, and corpus.db itself lives only on the laptop","Drew''s order 2026-10-27 15:00 CDT (main chat): gap #1 (#1514) handled immediately by hand; gap #2 (#1515) queued for immediate high-priority pickup; laptop+sandbox regular backups directed into the NixOS flake (init sets up sandbox backups, the flake sets up laptop backups) \u2014 umbrella audit issue #1516, nix-side tracker dezren39/nix#976"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1515: both halves confirmed or corrected against current state (latest cold-store-nightly run result for the atlas export; canonical DB size/mtime + gitignore state re-verified; v3/corpus exposure stated)","Implementation follow-up packet(s) enqueued from this triage: (a) routine daily compressed snapshot of the canonical atlas.db to Drive + R2 with retention and a visible freshness check, folded into the NixOS flake backup service work (#1516 / dezren39/nix#976) \u2014 no snowflake timer if the flake service is where it lands; (b) Turso atlas export fix (streaming/chunked download or enlarged window) in the cold-store nightly path so 4 of 4 Turso DBs file","Follow-up acceptance includes one evidenced restore spot-check of a filed atlas snapshot (the audit''s standing rule: an unrestored backup is a hypothesis)","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state; priority/high stays while Drew''s raise stands)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1515","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1516","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1514","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/976"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Curator raise per Drew''s direct order 2026-10-27 15:00 CDT (''queue 2 for immediate high priority pickup''). Maps to the 20 tier: a broken priority automation (nightly backup export) with exact reproduction (300 s timeout at 524,901,755 bytes), guarding content that exists in exactly one place and cannot be re-derived.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1515', '2026-10-27 20:05:19.33663+00', '2026-10-28 00:43:56.560874+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1566, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(directory): directory.jsonl torn-tail bricks Directory::open — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1521","title":"id(directory): a torn final line in directory.jsonl bricks the directory \u2014 Directory::replay refuses the crash-torn tail that ArtifactLog (loaded in the same open) drops and truncates","number":1521,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:10:26Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Petnames store (#1499 \u2014 separate filing, separate fix)","Any change to the journal entry format or apply rules","Silently dropping newline-terminated corrupt lines (must stay fatal)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/directory.rs replay(): torn-tail drop+truncate mirroring FileJournal::open semantics","directory module tests for torn tail, corrupt complete final line, torn-after-valid"]},"tests":["cargo test directory module (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''torn'', ''crash-torn'', ''directory journal'', ''GroupLog'': only #1499 (OPEN, Petnames::open only, pkgs/id/src/petname.rs; names FileJournal/Outbox as good examples, does not cover directory). Backlog checked: no directory-journal torn-tail filing exists.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:10:26Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Directory::replay has no torn-tail handling: an unterminated truncated final line (crash mid-append) fails every Directory::open forever, unlike FileJournal/ArtifactLog/Outbox in the same codebase.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/directory.rs:516-517 replay: serde_json::from_str(line).with_context(...)? \u2014 no missing-final-newline check, no truncation","pkgs/id/src/directory.rs:527-543 append: single write_all of line+b''\\n'' then sync_data \u2014 crash mid-write leaves an unterminated partial JSON fragment","pkgs/id/src/directory.rs:471-473 Directory::open = Self::replay(path)? then ArtifactLog::open \u2014 the journal bricks the open while the artifact log loaded seconds later survives the same crash (artifact.rs:575-600)","House semantics precedent: world_store.rs:85-130 FileJournal::open torn-tail drop+truncate with corruption still fatal; envelope_outbox.rs:143-165 and directory_log.rs:196-235 same pattern"],"acceptance":["Directory::replay/open loads all complete entries from a journal with an unterminated truncated final fragment, drops the fragment, and truncates the file to the last complete line","A newline-terminated unparseable line (any position, including last) still fails with the existing malformed-line error","A complete entry refused by apply still fails replay (existing test directory.rs:2601 passes)","New tests: torn final fragment loads+truncates; complete-but-corrupt final line errors; torn fragment after valid entries keeps earlier entries"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1521","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1499","pkgs/id/src/directory.rs:505-525","pkgs/id/src/directory.rs:527-543","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:85-130","pkgs/id/src/artifact.rs:575-600"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The directory journal holds accounts/friendships/group membership; its own append path can produce the torn tail its load path refuses, so one crash makes the directory permanently unopenable without manual file surgery.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1521', '2026-10-27 20:11:21.228197+00', '2026-10-28 01:47:46.746561+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1567, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(groups): groups.jsonl torn-tail bricks GroupLog::open — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1522","title":"id(groups): a torn final line in groups.jsonl bricks every group command \u2014 GroupLog::open refuses the crash-torn tail that FileJournal and Outbox drop and truncate","number":1522,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:12:02Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Petnames store (#1499) and directory journal (#1521) \u2014 separate filings, separate fixes","Any change to the event format, the fold, or append behaviour","Silently dropping newline-terminated corrupt lines (must stay fatal)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/groups/log.rs open(): torn-tail drop+truncate mirroring FileJournal::open / Outbox::open semantics","groups log module tests for torn tail and torn-after-valid"]},"tests":["cargo test groups::log module (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''torn'', ''crash-torn'', ''GroupLog'', ''groups.jsonl'': only #1499 (OPEN, Petnames::open only) and #1521 (filed this run, directory journal only). No GroupLog torn-tail filing exists.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:12:02Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"GroupLog::open has no torn-tail handling: an unterminated truncated final line (crash mid-append) fails every group command forever, unlike FileJournal/Outbox in the same codebase.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/groups/log.rs:56-64 open: .map(from_str.with_context)? .collect::<Result>()? \u2014 no missing-final-newline check, no truncation","pkgs/id/src/groups/log.rs:137-150 append: single write_all of line+''\\n'' then sync_data \u2014 crash mid-write leaves an unterminated partial JSON fragment","pkgs/id/src/commands/group.rs:200,361,395: every group command starts with GroupLog::open(...)? \u2014 one torn tail blocks all group operations","House semantics precedent: world_store.rs:85-130 FileJournal::open and envelope_outbox.rs:143-165 Outbox::open torn-tail drop+truncate with corruption still fatal; existing groups/log.rs:386-392 test covers only the newline-terminated corrupt case"],"acceptance":["GroupLog::open loads all complete events from a log with an unterminated truncated final fragment, drops the fragment, and truncates the file to the last complete line","A newline-terminated unparseable line (any position, including last) still fails; existing test_a_line_that_is_not_an_event_is_an_error passes unchanged","New tests: torn final fragment loads+truncates; torn fragment after valid events keeps earlier events and projection() folds","No change to event format, fold, or append behaviour"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1522","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1499","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1521","pkgs/id/src/groups/log.rs:48-71","pkgs/id/src/groups/log.rs:137-150","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:85-130","pkgs/id/src/envelope_outbox.rs:143-165"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"groups.jsonl is the whole local group history and every group command opens it first; its own append path can produce the torn tail its load path refuses, so one crash makes group operations permanently fail without manual file surgery.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1522', '2026-10-27 20:12:48.625341+00', '2026-10-28 11:05:59.367717+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1569, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(world): fork refuses crash-torn journal read_journal_entries — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1523","title":"id(world): fork refuses a crash-torn journal that the world''s own open repairs \u2014 read_journal_entries has no torn-tail case, so a torn world opens fine but can never be forked","number":1523,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:10Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Petnames (#1499), directory journal (#1521), group log (#1522) \u2014 separate filings","Changing FileJournal::open''s established torn-tail semantics","Silently dropping newline-terminated corrupt lines (must stay fatal)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs read_journal_entries / fork path: exclude unterminated final fragment with a visible warning","world_store tests for fork with torn tail and fork with corrupt complete final line"]},"tests":["cargo test world_store module (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''torn'', ''read_journal_entries'', ''fork torn'', ''fork corrupt journal'': only #1499 (petnames) plus #1521/#1522 filed this run (directory journal, group log). No fork/world-journal torn-tail filing exists.","checked_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:10Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"read_journal_entries has no torn-tail case, so fork_world refuses crash-torn source journals that FileJournal::open on the same file repairs and opens.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:459-462 read_journal_entries: from_slice(line).with_context(''is corrupt'')? for every non-empty \\n-split chunk \u2014 final unterminated fragment included","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:85-130 FileJournal::open: unterminated last line = torn append, dropped + truncated to good_len with tracing::warn; complete corrupt lines bail","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:479 fork_world: read_journal_entries(&src_dir.join(''journal.jsonl''))? as its first step on a cold journal","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:190: the helper''s other caller (append version-bump) is shielded by open''s truncation \u2014 fork is the unshielded caller"],"acceptance":["fork_world succeeds on a source journal with an unterminated truncated final fragment; the fork replays to the parent''s last complete entry and the exclusion is visible (warning log or fork note)","A newline-terminated unparseable line (any position, including last) still fails with the corrupt-journal error","New tests: fork with torn final fragment succeeds; fork with complete-but-corrupt final line fails","FileJournal::append version-bump behaviour (#227) unchanged for opened journals"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1523","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1499","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1521","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1522","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:452-466","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:85-130","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:479"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Fork (F12.2) is the template/backup path; the post-crash recovery case is exactly when a journal may carry a torn tail and exactly when an admin wants a fork \u2014 and the ''is corrupt'' message misdiagnoses a recoverable torn append as corruption.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'claimed', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1523', '2026-10-27 20:14:56.980835+00', '2026-10-28 11:11:35.908514+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1570, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: pm-dashboard-backup advances journal cursor on failed offsite run (issue #981)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["backup-cursor"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/981","title":"pm-dashboard-backup: a failed offsite run still advances the journal cursor (.last-run-epoch) \u2014 those journals never reach R2/Drive","number":981,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:13:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["modules/laptop-backups.nix unit/timer definitions","The archive format, manifest, or retention windows","Issue #982 (old-date self-prune) \u2014 separate fix, may land independently"],"include":["modules/pm-dashboard-backup.sh marker-write placement (advance only on full success)","A stubbed regression test for the script (scratch HOME; stub bws, rclone, journalctl)"]},"tests":["Stubbed harness: scratch HOME, stub bws (fake credential names), stub journalctl, stub rclone with selectable R2/Drive failure; assert exit codes and marker contents per scenario"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for pm-dashboard-backup / last-run-epoch / marker returned only #976 (the feature request this script implements); no issue covers the marker semantics","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:13:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"pm-dashboard-backup.sh advances .last-run-epoch after the local leg only, so a run that fails on R2/Drive permanently skips its journal window in all later offsite archives.","evidence":["modules/pm-dashboard-backup.sh:128 documents window start = min(last successful run, 24h ago); :191 writes the marker before legs 2+3 at :223/:228","Repro on main d5e11fd (stub bws/journalctl/rclone, scratch HOME): marker preset to 1000000000, R2 copyto exits 42 -> script exits 1 with ''FAILED R2 upload failed'', marker afterwards = 1793146175 (~now)","Control: same harness with healthy rclone completes local + R2 + Drive legs, exit 0"],"acceptance":[".last-run-epoch is advanced only after local + R2 + Drive legs all succeed; a non-zero exit leaves the marker at its previous value","The next run after an offsite failure re-includes the failed run''s journal window","Happy path unchanged: marker advances once, all copies sha256-verified","Regression test covers R2 failure, Drive failure, and full success with stubbed tools"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/981","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/976"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A single transient offsite failure silently creates a permanent gap in the offsite journal record this backup exists to keep; the local copy is pruned after 30 days, making the gap total.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:981', '2026-10-28 00:29:59.664082+00', '2026-10-28 02:00:40.144065+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1571, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Docs: add the missing sections to the install, notes-todos-plans, and desktop-browser mirrors (#339)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/339","title":"Docs: translated mirrors are missing whole sections on install (Nix), notes-todos-plans, and desktop-browser pages","number":339,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Pages covered by #601 (projects, scheduled-tasks, walkthrough) \u2014 separate queue task","Re-translating or editing any existing mirror content","English page changes"],"include":["packages/docs/content/docs/{de,es,fr,ja,ko,nl,pl,pt-br,tr,uk,zh-cn}/install.mdx \u2014 add Nix section (11 files)","packages/docs/content/docs/{de,es,fr,ja,ko,nl,pl,pt-br,tr,uk,zh-cn}/notes-todos-plans.mdx \u2014 add Deleting and undo + Agents (10 files)","packages/docs/content/docs/uk/notes-todos-plans.mdx \u2014 add Agents only","packages/docs/content/docs/{de,es,fr,ja,ko,pl,pt-br,zh-cn}/desktop-browser.mdx \u2014 add Size and appearance (8 files)"]},"tests":["bun run docs:validate (696+ pages)","Programmatic heading-count comparison of every mirror against English for the three pages","CI substantive checks on the PR (build/tests/type-check/lint/gate)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #339 is the canonical filing for these three pages; #332 (auto-model-routing, fixed by PR #599) and #601 (projects/scheduled-tasks/walkthrough, queue-claimed separately) cover different pages. No open PR touches these mirrors.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Readers of the translated docs never learn that the Nix install path, notes/todos deleting-and-undo and agents features, or the desktop browser size/appearance options exist, because the mirrors never received those English sections.","evidence":["Heading scan on main 28c5b0c10 (2026-10-28 triage, issue #339 verdict note): install EN 5 vs all mirrors 4; notes EN 6 vs 10 mirrors 4 and uk 5; desktop-browser EN 6 vs 8 mirrors 5 and nl/tr/uk 6","Same scan confirms auto-model-routing mirrors now match English at 8 sections in all 11 locales after PR #599, so the pattern and validation from #332 apply directly"],"acceptance":["Every mirror of install.mdx has the same ## section count as English (5), including a translated Nix section in the English position","Every mirror of notes-todos-plans.mdx has 6 ## sections; uk gains only the Agents section, the other 10 gain Deleting and undo + Agents","Every mirror of desktop-browser.mdx has 6 ## sections; the 8 deficient mirrors gain Size and appearance between ''Let the agent drive'' and ''Developer tools''; nl/tr/uk untouched","Pre-existing mirror content is preserved verbatim (programmatic content-preservation check, as in PR #599)","docs:validate passes and PR CI substantive checks are green before merge"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/339","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/599","packages/docs/content/docs/install.mdx","packages/docs/content/docs/notes-todos-plans.mdx","packages/docs/content/docs/desktop-browser.mdx"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Docs completeness: the missing Nix section hides a whole install path from non-English readers, but no code or data is affected, so low priority.","timebox_minutes":180}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:339', '2026-10-28 00:32:56.228606+00', '2026-10-28 01:39:55.772834+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1572, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: pm-dashboard-backup backfill for an old date pruned by its own retention sweep before upload (issue #982)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["backup-prune"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/982","title":"pm-dashboard-backup: a backfill/re-run for a date older than 30 days is pruned by its own retention sweep before upload \u2014 the just-created, verified archive is deleted and the run fails","number":982,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:31:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["modules/laptop-backups.nix unit/timer definitions","Remote prune semantics for other days'' directories","Issue #981 (journal cursor) \u2014 separate fix, may land independently"],"include":["modules/pm-dashboard-backup.sh prune ordering / same-run exclusion (or up-front date validation)","A stubbed regression test for the script (scratch HOME; stub bws, rclone, journalctl)"]},"tests":["Stubbed harness: scratch HOME, stub bws (fake credential names), stub journalctl, stub rclone backed by a fake remote dir; assert old-date and current-date run outcomes and that the archive exists after the run"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for pm-dashboard-backup / prune returned only #976 (the feature request this script implements); sibling #981 covers the journal-cursor bug in the same script, a different mechanism","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:31:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"pm-dashboard-backup.sh''s own 30-day prune runs between archive creation and offsite upload, so a backfill for an older date deletes its archive mid-run and fails.","evidence":["modules/pm-dashboard-backup.sh:20 DATE from $1; :193 ''local OK'' logged; :195-201 prune rm -rf''s every $ROOT/20??-??-?? dir older than the :196 cutoff, including the just-created one; uploads only start at :223","Repro on main d5e11fd (stub bws/journalctl/rclone, scratch HOME): ''pm-dashboard-backup.sh 2020-01-01'' -> manifest covers 13 files, ''local OK ... (1473 bytes, sha256 ed6a7c...)'', ''pruned local 2020-01-01'', rclone source missing, ''FAILED R2 upload failed'', exit 1; afterwards no copy exists locally or in the fake remote","Control: same harness for the current date completes local + R2 + Drive legs, exit 0"],"acceptance":["A run for a date older than the 30-day cutoff never deletes the archive it created in that same run","If the contract is up-front rejection, the error names the date and retention window and exits non-zero before building an archive","Daily current-date run unchanged: archive built, uploaded to R2 + Drive, sha256-verified, genuinely old day dirs still pruned locally and remotely","Regression test covers an old-date run and a current-date run with stubbed tools"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/982","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/981","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/976"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The out-of-cadence re-run is exactly the recovery path for a missed or damaged day; for any date past the retention window it destroys the verified archive it just built and reports a misleading remote-leg failure.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:982', '2026-10-28 00:34:11.374042+00', '2026-10-28 02:05:24.282542+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1573, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: getFilenameTruncated returns nearly the whole filename at maxLength 0 (#653)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/653","title":"fix(util): getFilenameTruncated returns nearly the whole filename at maxLength 0 \u2014 slice(0, -1) keeps everything","number":653,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:34:34Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["truncateMiddle (already guarded under #574)","getDirectory single-segment behavior (pinned intentional by path.test.ts: getDirectory(''file'') === ''/'')","the session-ui caller (no change needed; it passes a fixed 14)"],"include":["maxLength <= 0 guard in packages/util/src/path.ts getFilenameTruncated","width 0/1/2 regression tests in packages/util/src/path.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test for path.test.ts from packages/util (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list search for ''getFilenameTruncated OR truncate'' returned #574 (closed) as the only truncate-family hit: it covered Locale.truncate/truncateLeft/truncateMiddle and the util truncateMiddle copy, not getFilenameTruncated, whose fallback branch retains the same slice trap. No open issue names getFilenameTruncated.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:34:34Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"getFilenameTruncated''s fallback branch slices with maxLength - 1, so at maxLength 0 or negative it returns nearly the whole filename instead of an empty/at-most-maxLength result.","evidence":["packages/util/src/path.ts:21-29 \u2014 getFilenameTruncated fallback: available <= 0 returns filename.slice(0, maxLength - 1) + ''\u2026''; at maxLength 0 that is slice(0, -1), keeping all but the last character","packages/util/src/path.ts:31-40 \u2014 sibling truncateMiddle in the same file guards maxLength <= 0 with an explanatory slice(-0) comment (the #574 fix); getFilenameTruncated never got the equivalent guard","Probe (laptop, real module, main d29aa1df71): getFilenameTruncated(''/repo/long-component-name.tsx'', 0) -> 23 chars; -1 -> 22; -5 -> 18; (''/repo/README'', 0) -> ''READM\u2026''; (''/repo/a.txt'', 0) -> ''a.tx\u2026''; controls at widths 1/2/3/5/14/16/20 exact; truncateMiddle(''abcdefghijklmnop'', 0) -> ''''","packages/util/src/path.test.ts \u2014 getFilenameTruncated pinned only at maxLength 16; truncateMiddle pinned at widths 0-2; no getFilenameTruncated small-width test","packages/session-ui/src/message/comment-card.tsx:66 \u2014 sole live caller passes a fixed 14, so this is a latent contract break for any width-deriving caller, not a live visual bug"],"acceptance":["getFilenameTruncated(path, 0) returns '''' and negative maxLength never returns a string longer than the maxLength = 0 result","For every maxLength >= 0 the returned string''s length is at most maxLength, with an extension present, absent, or longer than maxLength","New tests in packages/util/src/path.test.ts cover widths 0, 1 and 2 for getFilenameTruncated, mirroring the existing truncateMiddle width tests","Existing behavior at normal widths is unchanged (the pinned 16-character case and the rest of path.test.ts stay green)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/653","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/574"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Latent contract break in a shared util: the sole caller passes a fixed width today, but the function promises at-most-maxLength output and its sibling in the same file was already fixed for the identical trap (#574). One-guard fix plus tests, xs effort, low priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:653', '2026-10-28 00:35:47.54879+00', '2026-10-28 01:31:48.979197+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1574, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 1 of #1531 — exec identity core: a script''s identity folds in its resolved directory (internal/config) — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1532","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1531 \u2014 exec identity core: a script''s identity folds in its resolved directory (internal/config)","number":1532,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the identity change in this triage task","any daemon/pool/watch wiring change \u2014 the design requires none; Phase 2 of #1531 covers daemon-level tests and TODO/roadmap closure","interpreter-as-command servers and sibling-loading native binaries (open questions on #1531)"],"include":["issue #1532 and design #1531 with the design doc it links","pkgs/mcpx/internal/config/execid.go and execid_test.go, pkgs/mcpx/internal/defaults (ExecHashMax), pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 4 and planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md identity row (read-only references)"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./internal/config/... via CI; defining tests from #1532: cross-directory identical script differs, same-directory identical script keeps, cross-directory identical non-script keeps, script vs non-script with same bytes differ, framing non-alias, large-file stat identity unchanged)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1532 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-27) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1532 \u2014 it did not exist before this run, so its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"A stdio server''s ExecIdentity is the bytes of its executable, which is wrong for a program that finds its own files relative to its real location: a node script beside its node_modules, re-pointed at a byte-identical copy in another directory, keeps its child under reload and the exec watch and keeps running with the old directory''s dependencies (pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 4; caveat in internal/config/execid.go). Design #1531 records the decision: a hashed script''s identity is content + resolved directory; binaries stay content-only; large files stay stat/inode. Phase 1 (#1532) is that core change in internal/config only.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/config/execid.go:16-43 header caveat: identity is the bytes of the file; a node script beside its node_modules re-pointed at an identical copy in another directory keeps its child with the old location''s dependencies; only mcpx restart moves it; above limits.execHashMax the identity is the inode so such a copy is restarted instead","pkgs/mcpx/internal/config/execid.go:114-130 ExecStamp.Identity() is the single identity implementation (sha256 of content when Size <= defaults.ExecHashMax, else stat hash of inode/size/mtime/mode); callers: Resolved.ExecState (execid.go:56), pool construction (internal/pool/pool.go:199), exec watch re-check (internal/pool/execwatch.go:84)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/config/execid.go:94-99 ExecStamp.Path is already the filepath.EvalSymlinks-resolved real path, so the directory to fold in is in hand","pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 4 asks for this decision (include the program''s directory for scripts, or always restart a re-pointed link); planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md Next row ''Decide what a stdio server''s identity is'' at status proposed, linked only to the TODO; no prior code-repo issue covers ExecIdentity (searched 2026-10-27)","Existing identical-copy tests are all same-directory (internal/config/execid_test.go:63, internal/daemon/reload_identity_test.go:162, internal/daemon/exec_watch_test.go TestExecWatchFollowsARepointedLinkByWhatItRuns), so the directory rule changes behaviour only in the untested cross-directory case; one exact-hash assertion (execid_test.go:25, a #!/bin/sh script pinned to its bare content hash) is knowingly changed by the design"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1532: scope confirmed against current main, hash framing settled or explicitly left open with reasons, and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If triage finds Phase 1 as scoped is not independently landable, say exactly why on the issue and propose the rescoped Phase 1 in the design doc''s terms \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1532","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1531"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 is the gate for the whole #1531 design: Phase 2''s daemon-level proof is dependency-gated on this core. Normal priority per the design issue.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1532', '2026-10-28 00:37:27.956649+00', '2026-10-28 02:16:24.583277+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1575, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 2 of #1531 — daemon proof: cross-directory re-point restarts on reload and the exec watch; TODO/roadmap closure — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1533","title":"mcpx: Phase 2 of #1531 \u2014 daemon proof: cross-directory re-point restarts on reload and the exec watch; TODO/roadmap closure","number":1533,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the tests or closure in this triage task","any change to internal/config identity semantics \u2014 that is Phase 1 (#1532); defects found there are filed against #1532, not patched here","interpreter-as-command servers and sibling-loading native binaries (open questions on #1531)"],"include":["issue #1533, design #1531, Phase 1 issue #1532 and its merge state","pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon/reload_identity_test.go and exec_watch_test.go, pkgs/mcpx/internal/pool/execwatch.go (read-only), pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md, planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./internal/daemon/... ./internal/pool/... via CI; defining tests from #1533: cross-directory re-point restarts on reload and on the live watch with exactly one server.restart event, same-directory re-point keeps, neighbour pool untouched)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1533 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-27) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1533 \u2014 it did not exist before this run, so its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Design #1531 changes what a stdio script''s exec identity is (content + resolved directory), but the decision is only real once both paths that consume identity \u2014 config reload (a changed ProcessID yields a new pool) and the periodic exec watch (a changed identity replaces a live pool''s children) \u2014 are proven to restart on a cross-directory re-point and keep on a same-directory one. Today the daemon tests pin only the same-directory keep case and carry the old caveat in their comments, and pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 4 plus the roadmap row remain open. Phase 2 (#1533) is the proof tests plus that closure.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon/reload_identity_test.go:162 TestReloadFollowsAForRePointedCommandByWhatItRuns pins the current choice with the caveat in its comment (lines 148-161): an identical copy in another directory is kept, child keeps the old location''s dependencies; its wrapper copies (first/second/other) are all in one directory","pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon/exec_watch_test.go TestExecWatchFollowsARepointedLinkByWhatItRuns covers the same same-directory keep case on the live watch path, with a setExecWatch/recordLifecycle harness (20ms tick) that counts server.restart events","pkgs/mcpx/internal/pool/execwatch.go:103-112: a changed identity on the watch path emits server.restart (reason ''executable changed'', with path/oldIdentity/newIdentity) and replaces only that pool''s children \u2014 the machinery Phase 2''s tests exercise; no wiring change is expected","pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 4 and planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md row ''Decide what a stdio server''s identity is'' (status proposed) are the originating records Phase 2 closes once the proof tests land","Design #1531 dependency note: Phase 2 requires Phase 1 (#1532) merged \u2014 without the core change its cross-directory tests cannot pass"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1533: scope confirmed against current main, the Phase 1 gate state stated explicitly (landed / not landed), and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is parked/labelled as gated with the gate named)","If triage finds Phase 2 as scoped is not independently landable once Phase 1 has merged, say exactly why on the issue and propose the rescoped Phase 2 in the design doc''s terms \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state, including the gate)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1533","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1531","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1532"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 2 completes #1531: it proves the identity decision on both consuming paths (reload and the live exec watch) and closes the TODO/roadmap records the design originated from. Gated on Phase 1. Normal priority per the design issue.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1533', '2026-10-28 00:37:37.574581+00', '2026-10-28 04:43:35.395747+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1576, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'projector(github): decodePem base64-of-PEM unwrap — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1529","title":"projector(github): GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY ''base64 of PEM'' form fails \u2014 decodePem never unwraps it, appJwt throws Invalid keyData","number":1529,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:02:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Renaming env vars or changing the documented contract","Any change to JWT claims, installation-token flow, or the read-only REST surface"],"include":["pm-stack/projector/src/github.ts decodePem: base64-of-PEM unwrap","pm-stack/projector/test/github.test.ts: PEM-text and base64-of-PEM fixtures (pkcs1 + pkcs8)"]},"tests":["bun test pm-stack/projector/test/github.test.ts (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''decodePem'', ''base64 PEM'', ''GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY'' in developing-today/code returned no existing issue. Backlog checked: no projector/github.ts filing exists.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:02:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"decodePem never unwraps base64-of-PEM, so the documented GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY form fails key import with Invalid keyData; tests cover only base64-of-DER.","evidence":["Laptop reproduction reported by new-issue-creator-code-b run 2026-10-27 15:20 CDT: base64-of-PEM input -> appJwt FAIL ''Invalid keyData''; plain PEM and base64-of-DER succeed","Source trace: decodePem (github.ts:16-23) strips ----- markers (absent in base64-of-PEM) and returns the base64 unchanged; appJwt (:66-67) performs exactly one Buffer.from(b64, ''base64''), which for base64-of-PEM yields ASCII PEM text, not DER","test/github.test.ts:5-9 testKeyB64 exports format ''der'' only \u2014 the documented PEM forms have no coverage"],"acceptance":["appJwt succeeds with raw PEM text, base64 of DER, and base64 of PEM for the same key, in both PKCS#1 and PKCS#8 variants","decodePem unwraps base64-of-PEM (decoded text starting with ''-----BEGIN'' is treated as PEM and its body extracted); raw-PEM and base64-of-DER behavior unchanged","test/github.test.ts gains PEM-text and base64-of-PEM fixtures next to the existing DER controls; projector test suite passes in CI","Env var names and the documented contract in the github.ts header are unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1529","pm-stack/projector/src/github.ts:6","pm-stack/projector/src/github.ts:16-23","pm-stack/projector/src/github.ts:66-67","pm-stack/projector/test/github.test.ts:5-20"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The projector''s GitHub App auth is its self-healing path beyond webhooks; an operator following the documented encoding gets a projector that cannot authenticate at all, with an error pointing at the key data rather than the encoding.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1529', '2026-10-28 00:38:27.089718+00', '2026-10-28 11:12:09.038093+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1577, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Triage: search.sh: the #957 failed-''brew list'' fix (PR #959) has no committed regression test (#983)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/983","title":"search.sh: the #957 failed-''brew list'' fix (PR #959) has no committed regression test","number":983,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing search.sh behaviour","brew-repair.sh and its suite (covered by #949/#954)"],"include":["search.test.sh (new) + flake.nix check wiring"]},"tests":["The new suite itself, run via the flake check in CI"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for ''search.sh brew list test'' and ''search test brew'' returned no covering issue; #957 (closed) is the original bug, not test coverage. Checked 2026-10-27.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"search.sh''s #957 loud-failure behaviour rests only on a one-off manual verification from PR #959; nothing in CI would catch a refactor restoring the silent false report.","evidence":["PR #959 diff: exactly one file, search.sh +25/-3, commit 0c1ba8f5 \u2014 no test, no flake.nix change","Repo tree on main (gh api git/trees, 2026-10-27): search.sh present, no search test path; flake.nix grep for search.sh/search.test empty","PR #954 (sibling #949 fix) added brew-repair.test.sh scenarios K-L in the same PR"],"acceptance":["A committed search.test.sh drives the real search.sh with stub brew + scratch /Applications: failing brew list -> exit 1, step named, no findings; missing brew -> same; working brew -> only non-cask apps reported; empty list -> all apps reported, exit 0","Suite asserts brew list runs exactly once per invocation","Suite wired into flake.nix checks like sibling script suites and passes in CI","search.sh behaviour unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/983","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/959","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/957","search.sh:20-31"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A standalone utility''s output is a findings list a user acts on; the regression would be silent but the blast radius is one script, so normal priority.","timebox_minutes":60}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:983', '2026-10-28 00:40:48.814732+00', '2026-10-28 01:04:56.086285+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1578, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Triage: branch-cleanup: actions/checkout is the repo''s only unpinned action — and PR #962 would bump the mutable tag instead of pinning the SHA (#984)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/984","title":"branch-cleanup: actions/checkout is the repo''s only unpinned action \u2014 and PR #962 would bump the mutable tag instead of pinning the SHA","number":984,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Other workflows'' pins (already SHA-pinned)","Branch-cleanup logic, schedule, or safeguards"],"include":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml checkout line (directly or via PR #962''s branch)"]},"tests":["Dry-run workflow_dispatch of branch-cleanup after the pin","grep audit: all uses: lines in .github/workflows/ are full-SHA pinned"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for ''checkout pin SHA'' and ''actions/checkout v7 pin'' returned nothing; no issue covers action pinning in this repo. Checked 2026-10-27.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"branch-cleanup.yml executes a mutable-tagged third-party action in a contents:write workflow; a re-pointed v4/v7 tag would run with a branch-deleting token.","evidence":["Main branch-cleanup.yml:33: uses actions/checkout@v4; permissions contents:write at :17-19","opencode.yml:35 + mcpx-nixbuild.yml:56: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1 (SHA-pinned)","PR #962 diff: @v4 -> @v7 (mutable tag), mergeable clean per API 2026-10-27","gh variable list 2026-10-27: BRANCH_CLEANUP_LIVE=true (set 2026-10-27T18:31Z); PR #966 made the schedule daily"],"acceptance":["branch-cleanup.yml uses actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1, matching the other workflows","No workflow in .github/workflows/ references an action by mutable tag","Branch-cleanup still runs green on a dry-run dispatch after the change"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/984","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/961","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/962",".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml:33"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Supply-chain exposure in the one workflow with standing branch-delete power, running live daily; every other workflow already follows the pinning convention, so the fix is small and standard.","timebox_minutes":60}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:984', '2026-10-28 00:40:52.886247+00', '2026-10-28 00:56:56.398896+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1579, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'atlas backups: make snapshot routine prove success (verdict+3 destinations+restore check) AND fix Turso atlas export timeout (#1515)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["data-loss-exposure","privacy-local-only-content"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1515","title":"atlas backups: canonical local atlas.db has no routine backup (gitignored, ad-hoc copies only); nightly Turso atlas dump times out","number":1515,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Publishing local-only chunks to Turso","A new separate timer/job (fold into atlas-local-backup-daily)","Interrupting the laptop Qwen3 embedding pass"],"include":["atlas-backup.py verdict/logging correctness + a clean end-to-end run","Verification of laptop + R2 (supabase-backups/atlas/<date>/) + Drive (local-atlas) destinations","One restore spot-check with sqlite3 integrity_check on a filed snapshot","backup-log.md freshness record","Cold-store nightly Turso export path for atlas (streaming/chunked/resume or enlarged window)"]},"tests":["atlas-backup.py run prints ATLAS-BACKUP <date> OK and appends the same verdict to backup-log.md","sqlite3 integrity_check on restored snapshot returns ok; row counts recorded","Destination listings for laptop/R2/Drive captured in the PR/issue note","Nightly or manual-equivalent cold-store export run: atlas dump completes, 4 of 4 filed"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1565 per issue #1515 acceptance; snapshot-half follow-up, distinct dedupe suffix from the turso-export follow-up; no prior fix packet for #1515 existed","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The atlas snapshot routine was built 2026-10-27 but has never recorded a successful verdict: backup-log.md shows only a FAILED-early entry 