re (:1036) \u2014 prints Match/Mismatch/NotCompared from replayed.verdict and bails on Mismatch","PR #1468 pkgs/id/src/world_fixture.rs replay_collecting computes verdict(header, records) per replay and stores it in Replayed.verdict inside Verification \u2014 discarded by the CLI"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1539 confirming or refuting the discarded-header-verdict finding against current main","Follow-up routed: verify prints the header verdict alongside the agreement line, the agree-but-mismatch case is explicit with a documented exit-code choice, and a test covers that case","Labels left truthful on #1539 (queue/* mirrors task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1539","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1468","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/544"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Operator-facing correctness/UX gap in a new self-check command: a fixture that no longer reproduces the recorded world looks fully verified. No data risk. Low priority (packet 70).","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1539', '2026-10-28 00:45:39.177871+00', '2026-10-28 00:45:39.177871+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1585, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Wire the port-opencode-theme integration suite into an automated run with an explicit skip (#139)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/139","title":"test(themes): port-opencode-theme integration suite is run by nothing \u2014 not collected by the test runner, dedicated script referenced nowhere, sibling-checkout precondition undocumented","number":139,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Modifying ../opencode (separate repository, read-only per repo AGENTS.md)","Changing porter behaviour in scripts/port-opencode-theme.ts beyond documentation of the precondition","Collecting other .integration.* files that may appear later without their own skip gate"],"include":["scripts/run-isolated-tests.mjs \u2014 collect .integration.ts (or an equivalent explicit inclusion)","scripts/port-opencode-theme.integration.ts \u2014 guarded sibling imports / explicit skip + env-var sibling override + header documentation","Documentation of the sibling-layout precondition where a porter contributor will find it"]},"tests":["Root test run (bun run test) without a sibling checkout: suite visibly skips, overall run green","With a sibling opencode checkout present: suite passes 7/7 through the automated path","bun run check:changed on the PR","CI substantive checks on the PR (build/tests/type-check/lint/gate)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #139 is the canonical filing; prior sweep triages (2026-10-27 12:24 and 18:21Z comments) recorded disposition only and no fix task exists in the openchamber queue (queue health at pickup: queued 0, claimed 2 = #601/#339, blocked 2). No open PR touches the collector or the suite (open PRs are only Drew''s #503/#216 and dependabot #401).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The only integration suite for the OpenCode theme porter is collected by no test run and referenced by no CI job, and its hard-coded sibling-checkout precondition is undocumented, so porter regressions (contrast, syntax/diff colour mapping, round-trip) pass every check.","evidence":["Main 029f69675: scripts/run-isolated-tests.mjs:24 TEST_FILE = /\\.(test|spec)\\.(js|cjs|mjs|jsx|ts|tsx)$/ \u2014 .integration.ts not matched","grep of .github/ and package.json: themes:port:opencode:test appears only at its package.json:89 definition","port-opencode-theme.integration.ts contains 7 test( cases and statically imports ../../opencode/packages/ui/src/theme/resolve and .../v2/resolve, so a missing sibling fails module resolution before any test runs","Verified this run: no sibling ''opencode'' directory exists beside the sandbox clone, matching the issue''s opaque-failure reproduction"],"acceptance":["The integration suite runs in at least one automated check (CI or the root test run) whenever its sibling-checkout precondition is present","When the precondition is absent, the outcome is an explicit, visible skip/notice \u2014 not silence and not an opaque module-not-found failure","The sibling-layout requirement (directory named opencode beside this repo, or its env-var override) is documented where a contributor running the porter will find it","With the sibling present, the suite still passes 7/7","Root test run stays green in an environment without the sibling checkout"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/139","scripts/run-isolated-tests.mjs","scripts/port-opencode-theme.integration.ts","scripts/port-opencode-theme.ts","package.json"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A whole porter suite silently not running means theme regressions ship green; no user-facing breakage today, so normal priority.","timebox_minutes":120}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:139', '2026-10-28 00:45:54.45647+00', '2026-10-28 03:01:36.707816+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1587, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: SnapshotStore unreadable records (pair finiteness + ts routing) — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1540","title":"aggregator: SnapshotStore accepts records it can never read back \u2014 non-finite estimate pairs and non-ISO timestamps pass validation, append reports success, and dedupe never sees them","number":1540,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:47:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The #1509 concurrent-write race in comments/actions/live stores","Any change to the on-disk JSONL format or the dedupe key for valid records","Upstream estimate arithmetic in the extractors"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/snapshots.ts isSnapshotRecord pair branch: finiteness + low <= high","pm-stack/aggregator/src/snapshots.ts ts validation vs snapshotFileFor/readAll routing consistency","aggregator tests for both rejected classes plus the finite-pair control"]},"tests":["bun test for the aggregator snapshot tests (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''snapshot store aggregator'', ''isSnapshotRecord'', ''SnapshotStore'': only epics/designs (#1258, #902, #1184, #1047) and unrelated closed items \u2014 no filing covers the snapshot validator/store contract. Backlog checked: Lane A covered aggregator persist races (#1509), card-state (#1474), needs-order (#1485) \u2014 different modules/mechanisms; snapshots.ts was not covered by either lane this phase.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:47:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"isSnapshotRecord accepts records (non-finite/inverted estimate pairs, non-ISO timestamps) that SnapshotStore writes to lines/files readAll can never return, so append reports success, history silently lacks them, and dedupe re-appends them forever.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe with the verbatim snapshots.ts (sha256 49b14289; hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-snapshots/probe.ts + out.log): scalar NaN refused, pair {low:NaN,high:10} and {low:Infinity,high:10} and inverted {low:50,high:10} accepted; NaN-pair append #1 = 1, stored line carries low:null, readAll = 0, append #2 = 1 (dedupe broken); ts ''October 20, 2026'' accepted, snapshotFileFor = usage-October.jsonl, append = 1, readAll = 0; finite-pair ISO control append 1 / re-append 0 / readAll 1"],"acceptance":["isSnapshotRecord rejects estimate pairs with a non-finite low or high, mirroring the scalar branch, and rejects low > high","isSnapshotRecord rejects a ts that snapshotFileFor cannot route to a file matching the readAll usage-(YYYY-MM).jsonl pattern","Regression tests: appending a NaN/Infinity-pair record and a non-ISO-ts record each append 0 and write nothing; the finite-pair ISO control still appends once and dedupes on re-append","No change to the on-disk format or the dedupe key for valid records"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1540","pm-stack/aggregator/src/snapshots.ts:17","pm-stack/aggregator/src/snapshots.ts:20-22","pm-stack/aggregator/src/snapshots.ts:26-42","pm-stack/aggregator/src/snapshots.ts:99","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/live.ts:757-759"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The snapshot store is the append-only usage history whose contract is that writer re-runs are safe because dedupe makes appends idempotent; records in either class silently break that contract \u2014 counted as stored, never shown, and re-appended on every writer run.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1540', '2026-10-28 00:48:21.245536+00', '2026-10-28 00:48:21.245536+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1588, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: QuotaSnapshot explicit resetAt rolls calendar-invalid dates over (#655)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/655","title":"fix(core): QuotaSnapshot explicit resetAt rolls calendar-invalid dates over \u2014 ''2026-02-30'' becomes a Mar 2 reset","number":655,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:50:14Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the daily resetRule branch (already fixed under #629)","the past-explicit-resetAt contract (returned as recorded; pinned by an existing test)","quota percent/remaining derivation (untouched)"],"include":["calendar validation of the explicit resetAt branch in packages/core/src/quota-snapshot.ts resetAtOf, reusing ModelRouteLimits.parseAbsoluteTime or equivalent","regression tests in packages/core/test/quota-snapshot.test.ts for Feb 30 / non-leap Feb 29 / Apr 31 explicit resetAt values"]},"tests":["bun test for quota-snapshot.test.ts from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list search for ''calendar-invalid'' returned #647/#609/#502/#471 (all closed, other parsers); search for ''QuotaSnapshot'' returned #587/#588/#629 \u2014 #629 covered only the daily-rule branch of resetAtOf, not the explicit resetAt branch. No open or closed issue names the explicit-resetAt calendar rollover.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:50:14Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"QuotaSnapshot.resetAtOf returns Date.parse''s rolled-over date for calendar-invalid explicit resetAt values instead of null.","evidence":["packages/core/src/quota-snapshot.ts:60-65 \u2014 explicit resetAt branch: parsed = Date.parse(window.resetAt); if finite, return parsed \u2014 no calendar round-trip","packages/core/src/quota-snapshot.ts:53-56 \u2014 module contract: an explicit resetAt ''is returned as recorded''; a rolled date is not the recorded one","packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts:48-70 \u2014 parseAbsoluteTime, the shared calendar check added under #609, documented as shared by every quota-reset parser in this surface; resetAtOf does not use it","Probe (laptop, real module, main 4a50304a73): resetAt 2026-02-30 -> 2026-03-02; 2026-02-29 -> 2026-03-01; 2026-04-31T12:00 -> 2026-05-01; 2025-02-29 -> 2025-03-01; 2026-10-27T25:00 -> null; controls 2026-10-27T17:00 and 2024-02-29 correct; ''not-a-date'' -> null","packages/core/test/quota-snapshot.test.ts:94-145 \u2014 tests pin explicit valid/past resetAt and #629 daily out-of-range cases, never a calendar-invalid explicit resetAt"],"acceptance":["A calendar-invalid explicit resetAt (2026-02-30, 2026-02-29 non-leap, 2026-04-31) yields resetAt null from QuotaSnapshot.derive, never a rolled-over date (or, if triage chooses fall-through to a valid daily rule on the same window, that choice is stated and pinned by a test)","The fix reuses ModelRouteLimits.parseAbsoluteTime or an equivalent component round-trip rather than adding a third copy of the calendar check","Valid explicit values are unchanged, including a past resetAt returned as recorded (existing test stays green) and leap-day 2024-02-29","New regression tests in packages/core/test/quota-snapshot.test.ts cover Feb 30, non-leap Feb 29, and Apr 31 as explicit resetAt values","Daily-rule behaviour from #629 is unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/655","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/629","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/609"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Shared quota signal (design #587) reports a fabricated reset instant for a free-form string field with no upstream validation; the shared fix helper already exists in-repo. Small scoped fix plus tests, normal priority.","timebox_minutes":60}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:655', '2026-10-28 00:52:11.077611+00', '2026-10-28 01:12:51.619377+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1590, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: quota-current future-dated freshness — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1541","title":"aggregator: a future-dated gatherer read is ''fresh'' forever until its date passes \u2014 quota-current freshness has no upper bound, so one skewed measuredAt pins a pool''s windows for weeks","number":1541,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:53:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The freshness bound (20 min) or semantics for past-dated reads","The gatherer writer itself (scripts/gather-quota.ts) \u2014 the reader must be robust to a skewed stamp","The #1540 snapshot-store validator (different module)"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-current.ts entryState: future-side bound with a pinned skew tolerance","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-current.ts overlay precedence sort: future entries cannot outrank fresh ones","test/quota-current.test.ts future-dated regression cases"]},"tests":["bun test test/quota-current.test.ts (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''quota-current future'' and ''measuredAt fresh stale gatherer'': only #899/#898/#910 (closed orchestrator/aggregator features) and #1175 (OPEN feature: quota-plane status view \u2014 a display feature, not this freshness defect). Backlog checked: no quota-current filing exists from either lane; Lane A''s aggregator filings (#1509, #1474, #1485) are different modules.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:53:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"entryState bounds only past age, so a future-dated gatherer entry is fresh-ok indefinitely, replaces pool windows and choices, and outranks genuinely fresh entries.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe driving the real overlayQuotaCurrent (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-snapshots/probe2-quota-future.ts + out2.log): at fixed now, 5m/19m-ago entries replace the pool window (42 vs 68) with freshness ok, 21m-ago is stale and keeps 68, while +1h and +30d future entries replace the window and report freshness ok and gatherer provider state ok"],"acceptance":["An entry whose measuredAt is more than the pinned clock-skew tolerance in the future is not classified fresh-ok: it surfaces as stale (or error) and does not replace the pool''s windows","The fresh-ok precedence sort cannot let a future-dated entry outrank a genuinely fresh entry for the same service","Regression tests in test/quota-current.test.ts cover measuredAt at +1h and a far-future date alongside the existing past-offset controls","No change to the freshness bound or semantics for past-dated reads"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1541","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-current.ts:41-52","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-current.ts:56-61","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-current.ts:139-141","pm-stack/aggregator/test/quota-current.test.ts"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The quota plane''s freshness rule is the dashboard''s data-honesty contract and feeds the routing choices; one clock-skewed gatherer write currently presents itself as the freshest truth for as long as the skew lasts (a month in the verified case).","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1541', '2026-10-28 00:53:54.572794+00', '2026-10-28 00:53:54.572794+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1591, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'small-fix: Form date-time format accepts calendar-invalid dates (#656)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/656","title":"fix(core): Form date-time format accepts calendar-invalid dates \u2014 ''2026-02-30T10:00:00Z'' passes validation","number":656,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:53:31Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["whether date-time should require ISO 8601 shape at all (non-ISO forms like ''Jan 5 2026'' are currently accepted; that contract question is noted in the issue for triage, not changed by this fix)","the date format (already round-trips correctly)","other form formats (email/uri/pattern)"],"include":["calendar round-trip of the ISO date part in packages/core/src/form.ts isDateTime","date/date-time format regression tests in packages/core/test/form.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test for form.test.ts from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search for ''isDateTime'' and ''date-time Feb'' returned nothing; gh issue list search ''form date-time'' returned only the calendar-invalid family for other parsers (#647/#609/#502/#471, all closed) and #601 (form when/external, unrelated). No issue covers Form format validation for date-time.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:53:31Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Form isDateTime accepts calendar-invalid dates because it only checks for NaN, and Date parsing rolls day overflow into the next month.","evidence":["packages/core/src/form.ts:374-376 \u2014 isDateTime is only !Number.isNaN(new Date(value).getTime()); Date parsing rolls day overflow into the next month instead of NaN","packages/core/src/form.ts:368-372 \u2014 sibling isDate round-trips via toISOString().slice(0,10) === value, so format ''date'' rejects 2026-02-30 in the same file","packages/core/src/form.ts:333-334 \u2014 validateField routes format ''date'' to isDate and ''date-time'' to isDateTime","Probe (laptop, real validateAnswer, main 4a50304a73): date-time ''2026-02-30T10:00:00Z'' -> accepted, ''2026-02-29T10:00:00Z'' -> accepted, ''2026-04-31T10:00:00Z'' -> accepted; ''2026-01-01T25:00:00Z'' and ''T10:60'' -> rejected; ''2024-02-29T10:00:00Z'' and ''2026-01-15T10:30:00Z'' -> accepted; format ''date'' controls: ''2026-02-30'' rejected, ''2024-02-29'' accepted","packages/core/test/form.test.ts \u2014 format tests cover URI only; no date or date-time format cases exist"],"acceptance":["validateAnswer rejects calendar-invalid date-time values (2026-02-30T..., non-leap 2026-02-29T..., 2026-04-31T...) with ''Expected date-time for form field: <key>''","Valid values keep passing, including leap-day 2024-02-29T... and ISO date-times with offsets; time-overflow rejections stay rejected","The check round-trips date components only when the value carries an ISO YYYY-MM-DD date part, so non-ISO acceptance is not silently changed","New tests in packages/core/test/form.test.ts cover date-time calendar-invalid and leap-valid cases and pin existing date format behaviour"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/656","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/609","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/647"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A declared date-time form field is a validation promise downstream code trusts; accepting Feb 30 silently shifts the instant by days on re-parse. The round-trip technique already exists in the same file. Small scoped fix plus tests, normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:656', '2026-10-28 00:55:25.746655+00', '2026-10-28 02:02:12.240579+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1592, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: pin actions/checkout to the repo-standard SHA in branch-cleanup.yml (issue #984)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/984","title":"branch-cleanup: actions/checkout is the repo''s only unpinned action \u2014 and PR #962 would bump the mutable tag instead of pinning the SHA","number":984,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:57:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Other workflows'' pins (already SHA-pinned)","Branch-cleanup logic, schedule, or safeguards","Merging or pushing to Renovate PR #962 / branch renovate/actions-checkout-7.x"],"include":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml checkout line, on our own queue/* branch + PR","Post-merge dry-run workflow_dispatch of branch-cleanup"]},"tests":["grep audit: all uses: lines in .github/workflows/ are full-SHA pinned after the change","Dry-run workflow_dispatch of branch-cleanup after the pin (dry_run=true) completes green"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1578 after confirming #984; dedupe_key is the issue''s fix key, distinct from the triage key repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:984","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:57:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"branch-cleanup.yml executes a mutable-tagged third-party action in a contents:write workflow that runs live daily; a re-pointed v4 (or v7) tag would run with a branch-deleting token.","evidence":["Main 593bff2 .github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml:33: uses: actions/checkout@v4; permissions contents:write (lines 17-19); schedule daily + workflow_dispatch","Full uses: audit 2026-10-28 (triage task 1578): mcpx-nixbuild.yml:56 actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1, :58 DeterminateSystems/nix-installer-action@3138316df39ed29be04236d7ffc686fa525866aa # v23; opencode.yml:35 same checkout SHA pin, :40 anomalyco/opencode/github@77fc88c8ade8e5a620ebbe1197f3a572d29ae91a # github-v1.2.19 \u2014 branch-cleanup is the only mutable tag","gh variable list 2026-10-28: BRANCH_CLEANUP_LIVE=true (set 2026-10-27T18:31Z) \u2014 the workflow deletes branches live every day","PR #962 (app/renovate, branch renovate/actions-checkout-7.x) is OPEN/CLEAN and would change @v4 -> @v7, still a mutable tag; per fleet rule, upstream/bot-owned nix PRs are never merged by workers"],"acceptance":["branch-cleanup.yml uses actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1, matching the other workflows","No workflow in .github/workflows/ references an action by mutable tag (grep audit of uses: lines)","Branch-cleanup runs green on a dry-run workflow_dispatch after the change","Renovate PR #962 is NOT merged or pushed to; the fix lands on our own queue/* branch + PR"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/984","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/962",".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml:33",".github/workflows/opencode.yml:35",".github/workflows/mcpx-nixbuild.yml:56"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"High: supply-chain exposure in the one workflow with standing branch-delete power, running live daily; the fix is a one-line pin to the SHA the repo already uses twice.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:984', '2026-10-28 00:55:33.680453+00', '2026-10-28 01:01:43.606169+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1593, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'small_fix(quota): drop remains_time fallback from MiniMax windowSeconds (#606)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/606","title":"fix(quota): MiniMax providers report time-until-reset as windowSeconds \u2014 remains_time fallback fabricates the window duration when timestamps are absent","number":606,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:57:47Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Hardcoding 18000/604800 durations","VS Code port (already correct: null fallback)","Cursor windowSeconds (#495, fixed)","usedPercent derivation in minimax-shared (coercePercent clamps both bounds)"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/minimax-shared.js","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/minimax-shared.test.js"]},"tests":["minimax-shared.test.js passes with updated expectations","bun run check:changed"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh searches ''minimax windowSeconds'' and ''remains_time'' returned only #484 (resolved test-coverage) and unrelated providers; #495 is Cursor, different provider/file","checked_at":"2026-10-28T00:57:47Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"MiniMax web quota providers report time-until-reset as windowSeconds when start/end timestamps are absent.","evidence":["Verified on main 029f69675 by reading minimax-shared.js:78-89,127-128 and minimax-shared.test.js:209-216 (test expects windowSeconds 9664 from remains_time 9664502 at 50% remaining)","VS Code port fetchMiniMaxQuota (quotaProviders.ts) derives windowSeconds only from start/end, null otherwise","Consumers: usageHeadline.ts picks shortest windowSeconds; UsageGiftResetButton.tsx:22-25 classifies resets by exact duration (18000/604800)"],"acceptance":["windowSeconds is null for interval and weekly windows when the payload has remains_time but no usable start/end pair","Start/end derivation unchanged: floor((resetAt-startAt)/1000)","minimax-shared.test.js updated (fallback test and remains-only model-pick assertions expect null); all other minimax tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/606"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent misreporting of a headline quota figure that drifts every poll; no crash, normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:606', '2026-10-28 00:57:55.281496+00', '2026-10-28 01:55:36.624524+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1595, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(world): crash-torn records.namespace bricks world — triage #1544', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1544","title":"id(world): a crash-torn or empty records.namespace bricks the world forever \u2014 RecordsStore::open makes a torn cache file fatal, and writes it non-atomically","number":1544,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:01:02Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing FileJournal/ArtifactLog/Outbox torn-tail semantics (separate filings #1499/#1521/#1522/#1523)","Recovering the old records doc itself when its namespace is lost (it is a cache; a fresh doc is the accepted recovery, as in the doc-gone case)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/world_records.rs open(): warn-and-recreate on unparseable namespace file","pkgs/id/src/world_records.rs: atomic namespace write (temp + rename)","world_records tests for empty/garbage/valid-live/valid-gone namespace files"]},"tests":["cargo test world_records module (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''records.namespace'', ''RecordsStore'', ''namespace file corrupt'', ''records doc torn'': only unrelated #439 (world-dir gitignore). No records.namespace / RecordsStore filing exists.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:01:02Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"RecordsStore::open makes an unparseable records.namespace fatal and writes that file non-atomically, so a crash-torn cache file permanently bricks a world''s startup.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/world_records.rs:71-78 open(): text.trim().parse::<NamespaceId>() failure propagated with ? (''parse records namespace in ...'') \u2014 no recovery case for empty/garbage content","pkgs/id/src/world_records.rs:79-84 the doc-gone case already warns (''records doc ... is gone; creating a new one'') and recreates \u2014 a torn file gets strictly worse treatment than a deleted doc","pkgs/id/src/world_records.rs:86-92 namespace written with a single non-atomic tokio::fs::write (truncate-then-write, no temp/rename/fsync)","pkgs/id/src/world_records.rs:3-9 module doc: the records doc is a cache of authoritative state, never a second source of truth \u2014 discarding a torn namespace loses nothing authoritative","pkgs/id/src/commands/serve.rs:575-577 sole production caller passes <world_dir>/records.namespace and propagates with await?, so the world fails to start on every restart","Laptop probe (real RecordsStore::open + Docs::memory, test probe_corrupt_namespace_file_bricks_open): empty file -> Err ''Invalid string length''; torn ''abc123partial'' -> Err ''Odd number of digits''; log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-creator-a-records-ns.log"],"acceptance":["RecordsStore::open with an empty or unparseable records.namespace succeeds: visible warning naming the file and the recovery, new records doc created, namespace file rewritten","Namespace file written atomically (temp file in same directory + rename), so a crash mid-write cannot leave a torn file at the real path","Well-formed namespace + existing doc still reopens that doc (happy path unchanged); well-formed namespace + gone doc keeps warn-and-recreate","New tests: open with (a) empty namespace file, (b) garbage/partial namespace file, (c) valid namespace + live doc round-trip, (d) valid namespace + gone doc","id serve world startup no longer fails solely because of a torn records.namespace"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1544","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1523","pkgs/id/src/world_records.rs:71-92","pkgs/id/src/commands/serve.rs:575-577","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1587"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Worst-case timing: the torn write only happens when the process dies unexpectedly \u2014 exactly when an operator restarts id serve expecting worlds back. One world then never starts, the parse error hides the safe remedy (delete a cache file), and nothing self-heals.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1544', '2026-10-28 01:02:19.418518+00', '2026-10-28 01:02:19.418518+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1597, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'small_fix(quota): stop Wafer provider fabricating usedPercent 0 when percent is absent (#608)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/608","title":"fix(quota): Wafer provider fabricates usedPercent 0 when the payload omits current_period_used_percent \u2014 counts in the same payload say otherwise","number":608,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:03:46Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The deliberate >100 overage allowance for a present percent","windowSeconds derivation in wafer.js (true start/end difference, correct)","VS Code port (no wafer provider there verified this run \u2014 do not assume)"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/wafer.js","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/wafer.test.js"]},"tests":["wafer.test.js passes with new regression tests","bun run check:changed"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh searches ''wafer usedPercent''/''wafer'' returned only #484 (closed test-coverage) and other providers'' clamp issues","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:03:46Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Wafer quota provider reports usedPercent 0 when current_period_used_percent is absent instead of deriving it or reporting null.","evidence":["Laptop probe on main 029f69675 (wafer.test.js harness, fetch stubbed): payload {remaining_included_requests:40, included_request_limit:100} -> ok:true, usedPercent 0, remainingPercent 100, valueLabel ''40 / 100 left''","wafer.js:67 usedPercentRaw = toNumber(current_period_used_percent) (null when absent); :82-84 ?? 0 in both branches; :71 no-data guard requires all four fields null","Copilot provider derives usedPercent from remaining/entitlement, null when unknown; toUsageWindow maps null usedPercent to remainingPercent null"],"acceptance":["Percent absent + remaining 40/limit 100 -> usedPercent 60","Percent absent + only overage_request_count present -> usedPercent null (not 0)","Present-percent behaviour unchanged, incl. overage >100 and negative clamping; existing wafer tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/608"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent fabrication of the headline quota figure (0% used while 60% consumed) if the upstream payload drops the percent field; no crash, normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:608', '2026-10-28 01:03:51.199136+00', '2026-10-28 02:19:38.011998+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1599, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: add search.test.sh regression suite + flake check for search.sh (#957 behaviour) (issue #983)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/983","title":"search.sh: the #957 failed-''brew list'' fix (PR #959) has no committed regression test","number":983,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:04:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing search.sh behaviour","brew-repair.sh and its suite (covered by #949/#954)"],"include":["search.test.sh (new) driving the real search.sh with a stub brew","flake.nix check wiring on the neighbouring script-suite pattern","At most a minimal, documented, behaviour-preserving testability seam for the hardcoded /Applications path, if the fixer cannot create a scratch /Applications in the check environment"]},"tests":["The new suite itself, run directly and via the new flake check (laptop or CI)","Ablation: restore the old process-substitution behaviour in a scratch copy of search.sh \u2014 the suite fails"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1577 after confirming #983; dedupe_key is the issue''s fix key, distinct from the triage key repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:983","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:04:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"search.sh''s #957 loud-failure behaviour rests only on one-off manual verification from PR #959; nothing automated would catch a refactor restoring the silent false report.","evidence":["Main 6e720e8 git tree (recursive): search.sh present; no search.test.sh or search test path (only unrelated archive/ docs match ''search'')","Main 6e720e8 flake.nix: grep for ''search'' returns nothing \u2014 no check references search.sh","PR #959 (merged 2026-10-27T15:44:36Z) files = [search.sh] only \u2014 no test, no flake change; its verification was manual stub-brew runs","Current search.sh: BREW_LIST captured once with status checked; failure echoes ''search: error: brew list --cask failed'' + brew stderr and exits 1; per non-matching app it also calls ''brew search <name>''","search.sh hardcodes /Applications (first leg) and uses ~/Applications (second leg, HOME-relative)"],"acceptance":["A committed search.test.sh drives the real search.sh with stub brew: failing brew list -> exit 1, step named on stderr, no findings reported; missing brew -> same; working brew -> only non-cask apps reported; empty list -> all apps reported, exit 0","Suite asserts ''brew list'' runs exactly once per invocation (stub log)","Suite is wired as a flake check on the neighbouring script-suite pattern and passes via that check (laptop or CI)","search.sh behaviour unchanged (any testability seam is minimal, documented on the PR, and behaviour-preserving)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/983","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/957","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/959","pkgs/brew-repair/brew-repair.test.sh"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The #957 silent-false-report bug class already recurred across sibling scripts (#949 in brew-repair); without a committed suite, a refactor of search.sh can restore it silently. Bounded test-only change.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:983', '2026-10-28 01:04:31.776194+00', '2026-10-28 01:33:52.850201+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1600, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(world): min_tick_ms never enforced, time.tick:1 drives ~1000 journaled updates/sec — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1546","title":"id(world): min_tick_ms (1000) is never enforced \u2014 a program can subscribe to time.tick:1 and drive ~1,000 journaled program updates per second","number":1546,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:04:24Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing MAX_TICK_INTERVALS (4) or tick delivery-while-present semantics","Schedule (schedule.at) timing \u2014 separate mechanism"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/world_caps.rs Subscription::parse and/or world actor arm/fire path","pkgs/id/src/world/mod.rs + core.rs WorldLimits validation","world_caps / world actor tests for the boundary"]},"tests":["cargo test world_caps (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search open+closed for ''time.tick'', ''tick interval'', ''min_tick'': no tick-floor filing (only unrelated quota epic #1149).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:04:24Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"min_tick_ms is dead config: tick subscriptions below 1000ms are accepted and delivered/journaled at the raw interval.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/world/mod.rs:78,96 min_tick_ms field + default 1000; repo-wide grep finds no other reference (verified on sandbox and laptop clone)","pkgs/id/src/world_caps.rs:165-172 Subscription::parse: ms>0 => Tick(ms), only 0/non-numeric become Unknown","pkgs/id/src/world/actor.rs:468-478 arm() uses Duration::from_millis(raw ms); 481-500 fire_ticks re-arms raw; 341-376 deliver() runs update + persists JournalEntry::System per tick","pkgs/id/src/world/core.rs:59-75 WorldCore::new validates every other WorldLimits field nonzero, not min_tick_ms","pkgs/id/docs/2026-10-07T00-20-00Z_architecture_roc_worlds/2026-10-07T00-20-00Z_architecture_roc_worlds.md:729 documents time.tick:<ms> as >= 1000 ms"],"acceptance":["Sub-floor tick interval cannot drive sub-floor delivery: refused (like time.tick:0) or clamped to min_tick_ms \u2014 one documented behaviour","min_tick_ms validated in WorldCore::new or removed in favour of a named enforced constant; no dead config remains","Tests pin 999 (no sub-second delivery) and 1000 (works); 0/non-numeric Unknown behaviour unchanged","Doc and code agree on the floor"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1546","pkgs/id/src/world/mod.rs:78","pkgs/id/src/world_caps.rs:165-172","pkgs/id/src/world/actor.rs:468-478"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A granted program can busy-loop the host and grow the journal ~1000 entries/sec per interval; the bound exists in field, default and doc but is enforced nowhere.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1546', '2026-10-28 01:04:58.572828+00', '2026-10-28 01:04:58.572828+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1601, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'projector: read-API limit unvalidated — ?limit=-1 dumps whole table, ?limit=2.7 500s — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1547","title":"projector: read-API limit is never validated \u2014 ?limit=-1 returns the whole table and ?limit=2.7 500s the request","number":1547,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:08:07Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Auth changes for read endpoints","Pagination cursors / offset support"],"include":["pm-stack/projector/src/server.ts limit parsing for /items and /comments","pm-stack/projector/src/store.ts listItems/getComments/getCommentsForSubject if the clamp lands there","pm-stack/projector/test/ limit cases"]},"tests":["bun test in pm-stack/projector (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search open+closed for ''projector limit'': no filing; openchamber #604 is the same loose-Number family in a different repo/codebase.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:08:07Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Read-API limit query parameter is never validated or clamped; negative = unbounded, fractional = driver error/500, NaN reaches the driver.","evidence":["pm-stack/projector/src/server.ts:119 limit: Number(searchParams.get(''limit'') ?? 200) \u2014 no integer/sign/range check","pm-stack/projector/src/server.ts:128 same pattern, default 500, for /comments","pm-stack/projector/src/store.ts:188-191,267,283 limit = opts.limit ?? default passes -1/NaN/2.7 into LIMIT ?","SQLite verified this run: LIMIT ? bound -1/-5 returned all 10 rows; bound 2.7 raised datatype mismatch; bound 0 returned 0","pm-stack/projector/src/server.ts:110-141 /items and /comments handlers have no try/catch (unlike /health and webhook)"],"acceptance":["limit parsed as positive integer at one layer and clamped to a named per-endpoint maximum; absent keeps defaults 200/500","?limit=-1, 0, 2.7, abc, 999999999 never yield unbounded results or a 500 (default/clamp or 400 naming limit)","Tests pin negative, fractional, non-numeric, over-max, and exact ?limit=3","No change for well-formed callers (aggregator live reads use refs=, not limit)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1547","pm-stack/projector/src/server.ts:119","pm-stack/projector/src/store.ts:188"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Unauthenticated read endpoints can be forced into full-table responses with one parameter, and a fractional value is a one-request 500; the bound the parameter exists to provide is illusory.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1547', '2026-10-28 01:08:37.60664+00', '2026-10-28 01:08:37.60664+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1602, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): upload filename collision — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1549","title":"id(web): image upload stores by filename with no collision handling \u2014 a second paste named ''image.png'' silently un-names the first","number":1549,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Document save semantics (a save still updates its own name''s tag)","The /blob/{hash} URL shape","reconcile_upload_filename type reconciliation (#908, closed)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs upload_handler: collision handling for the stored upload name (pinned by triage: uniquify or archive-first)","The nameless-upload fallback name''s uniqueness within one second","upload_router_tests regression: two same-name uploads, different bytes"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib web::routes upload_router_tests (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''upload image.png tag'', ''pasted image filename'', and the open-issue list scan: no upload-naming/collision filing exists. Adjacent but distinct: #1379 (upload insert position after doc shrink, client side), #908 closed (filename/type reconciliation), #1494 (saveFile dataset decode). Backlog checked: neither lane has filed upload naming.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Upload keys images by a non-unique filename and bare-overwrites the name tag, so same-name uploads (every clipboard paste is ''image.png''; nameless fallback repeats within a second) un-name earlier images.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe with the real image-upload.ts (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneA-uploadname/probe.ts + out.log): P1 fixed-clock generatePasteFilename identical across calls; 200 tight-loop calls -> 1 distinct name; P2 two different Files named ''image.png'' both arrive via FormData (uploadImageFile''s exact call shape) with filename ''image.png''","Code read on main a120b9a9: routes.rs:1553 bare tags().set overwrite; metadata tags keyed by filename at :1562/:1575/:1588; images_list_handler :1613+ and get_file_name :1015+ are tag-keyed, so a re-pointed tag un-names the first image; fileops.rs:15-16 archive-on-replace is the contrasting house pattern"],"acceptance":["Two uploads that arrive under the same filename both remain listed by images_list_handler and resolvable by name afterwards, under one pinned behaviour (uniquified later name or archive-first)","The nameless-upload fallback name cannot repeat for two uploads in the same second","Regression coverage in upload_router_tests: two same-name uploads with different bytes \u2014 both images still listed/resolvable, first upload''s name record not silently merged","No change to document save semantics and no change to the /blob/{hash} URL shape"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1549","pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs:1491-1499","pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs:1553","pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs:1613","pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs:15-16","pkgs/id/web/src/image-upload.ts:57-76"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Pasting screenshots is a core editor flow; the second paste silently removes the first image from the image browser and name lookup with no error anywhere \u2014 a silent data-visibility loss on a routine action.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1549', '2026-10-28 01:17:08.440055+00', '2026-10-28 01:17:08.440055+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1603, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: pm-dashboard-backup DATE argument is never validated (issue #989)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["backup"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/989","title":"pm-dashboard-backup: the DATE argument is never validated \u2014 ''not-a-date'' backs up successfully and can never be pruned, ''../../x'' creates directories outside the backup root","number":989,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["modules/laptop-backups.nix unit/timer definitions","Issue #981 journal cursor and #982 prune ordering \u2014 separate fixes","Retention windows themselves (30 days stays)"],"include":["modules/pm-dashboard-backup.sh DATE validation near the top of the script","A stubbed regression test for the script (scratch HOME; stub bws, rclone, journalctl)"]},"tests":["Stubbed harness: scratch HOME, stub bws (fake credential names), stub journalctl, stub rclone backed by a fake remote dir; assert malformed dates are rejected with nothing created/uploaded and a valid date completes all legs"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --search pm-dashboard-backup returned only #981, #982, #976; none covers malformed-DATE validation (searched 2026-10-28)","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"pm-dashboard-backup.sh never validates its DATE argument, so malformed dates succeed as unprunable backups and path components escape the backup root.","evidence":["modules/pm-dashboard-backup.sh:20 DATE=\"${1:-$(date +%F)}\" unvalidated; :24 OUTDIR=$ROOT/$DATE; local prune glob :197 \"$ROOT\"/20??-??-??; remote prune regex :215 ^20[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$","Stubbed harness on main 6e720e8: ''not-a-date'' -> ''local OK'', R2 + Drive uploads, ''OK dashboard not-a-date backed up'', exit 0; resulting dirs match neither prune pattern","''../../escaped'' -> created $HOME/escaped (outside $ROOT) via mkdir -p $OUTDIR, then tar/verify errors outside the backup tree","''2026-02-30'' -> archive built and ''local OK'' logged for a nonexistent calendar date"],"acceptance":["A DATE that is not a real YYYY-MM-DD calendar date (wrong shape, non-date text, 2026-02-30, or containing / or ..) is rejected up front: error names the value, exit non-zero, no directory created, nothing uploaded","No-argument timer path and a valid explicit date behave exactly as today: archive built, sha256-verified, uploaded to R2 + Drive","Stubbed regression test covers at least one malformed date and one valid explicit date"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/989","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/981","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/982"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The manual backfill path is the recovery path for this backup; a typo''d date silently produces an unprunable misnamed backup set on all three destinations or writes directories outside the backup root, while reporting success.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:989', '2026-10-28 01:22:20.371407+00', '2026-10-28 04:09:46.470431+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1604, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: mcp-clients Codex step corrupts config.toml on header-shaped lines inside multi-line strings (issue #990)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["config-rewrite"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/990","title":"mcp-clients: Codex step treats a header-shaped line inside a multi-line string as a real table \u2014 config.toml is corrupted (invalid TOML) and a phantom server is reported removed","number":990,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Zed and JSON client steps (already string/comment-aware)","Real mcp_servers spelling handling from #944/#956 \u2014 behavior for real tables must not change"],"include":["mcp-clients.py codex() string-state tracking for multi-line basic and literal strings","mcp-clients.test.py regression cases"]},"tests":["python3 mcp-clients.test.py \u2014 full suite passes including the new multi-line string cases; tomllib parses every rewritten fixture"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search ''mcp-clients string'' and ''mcp-clients multi-line'' returned #929 (Zed, closed), #905, #956 \u2014 none covers Codex TOML multi-line strings (searched 2026-10-28)","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcp-clients.py''s Codex parser has no multi-line string state, so header-shaped lines inside string values corrupt config.toml.","evidence":["mcp-clients.py:255 codex(); header regexes applied to every line; value_depth/kept_depth at :270-285 track brackets only, and kept_depth is armed only in the at_root branch","Repro on main 6e720e8, scratch HOME: input valid TOML with [profiles.demo] instructions string containing ''[mcp_servers.evil]'' -> output ''removed: evil'', exit 0, resulting config.toml fails tomllib with ''Unterminated string'', [profiles.demo2] swallowed into the string","Runs on every home-manager switch via homeUser.nix mcpClients activation, per the module docstring"],"acceptance":["The multiline-string fixture round-trips byte-for-byte inside the string, [profiles.demo2] survives, no phantom removal is reported, and the output parses with tomllib with [mcp_servers.mcpx] appended","A real [mcp_servers.<name>] table alongside a multi-line string elsewhere is still removed and reported; header-shaped lines inside '''''' literal strings are ignored too","mcp-clients.test.py gains regression cases for multi-line basic and literal strings containing header-shaped lines; the full existing suite still passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/990","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/929","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/956"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Runs on every switch against the live Codex config; a profile whose prompt/instructions contain example TOML silently corrupts config.toml into invalid TOML while reporting success and a phantom removal.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:990', '2026-10-28 01:29:52.339004+00', '2026-10-28 07:29:00.973045+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1605, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(discovery): announcement timestamp ordering/freshness — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1552","title":"id(discovery): peer announcements carry a timestamp nothing checks \u2014 a replayed or out-of-order announcement overwrites newer peer state and can keep a departed peer ''live'' forever","number":1552,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Signing or otherwise authenticating announcements (larger design question)","The gossip transport / distributed-topic-tracker itself","The stale-probe cleanup loop''s RPC behaviour (it works as designed once a peer can actually go stale)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/discovery.rs PeerDiscovery::update: timestamp ordering (not-newer does not overwrite) and freshness bound for ancient stamps","pkgs/id/src/discovery.rs tests: out-of-order, ancient-timestamp, and in-order control cases"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib discovery (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues (open + recently closed) for ''discovery announcement'', ''PeerDiscovery'', ''peer stale replay announcement'', and issue list search ''gossip peer'': no filing covers announcement ordering/freshness \u2014 nearest hits are unrelated (#542 cost visibility, #732 world-keyboard, #898 orchestrator). Backlog checked: neither lane has filed in discovery.rs; Lane A''s current areas (image upload #1549, codec, world metrics) and Lane B''s own earlier areas (aggregator snapshots/quota, torn-tail family, world manifest) deliberately avoided.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PeerDiscovery::update ignores timestamp_secs: an older announcement overwrites newer state and any announcement, however ancient, manufactures freshness on arrival.","evidence":["Laptop probe compiling the verbatim pkgs/id/src/discovery.rs (sha256 52b897d2cfa2c620f54ac7945e1bad66435472e73327c43cd87ef2bc56ee3d99 identical both sides; hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-discovery/main.rs + out.log): ts=2000 state (new-name/42) overwritten by replayed ts=1000 (old-name/7); in-order control correct; timestamp_secs=1 announcement accepted as live peer (peers()=1, stale_peers()=0)"],"acceptance":["An announcement whose timestamp_secs is not newer than the stored announcement''s for that node does not overwrite the stored announcement (equal timestamps: a documented deterministic rule)","An announcement stamped older than the pinned bound relative to local wall-clock time does not make a peer live or refresh its freshness; a genuinely new announcement still can","Regression tests in discovery.rs: out-of-order delivery keeps the newer announcement; an ancient-timestamp announcement is not fresh in peers(); in-order controls still pass","No new trust assumptions in serve.rs \u2014 the guarantee lives in PeerDiscovery or a checked entry point it exposes","Signing announcements is out of scope"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1552","pkgs/id/src/discovery.rs:356-364","pkgs/id/src/discovery.rs:430-437","pkgs/id/src/commands/serve.rs:1278","pkgs/id/src/commands/serve.rs:1312-1352"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The peer table is the operator''s discovery view (id peers / REPL / web /peers) and blob_count its only content signal; today it can be rolled back by ordinary gossip reordering and pinned to a phantom peer indefinitely by replaying one captured unsigned announcement, while the stale-peer cleanup is structurally unable to see that case.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1552', '2026-10-28 01:31:45.492634+00', '2026-10-28 01:31:45.492634+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1607, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage #1558: PR #1242 sops secrets stranded on feat/openclaw-summarize — not on main, wrapper repoint never filed', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1242","title":"OpenClaw secrets via sops-nix (bws mirror)","number":1242,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1558","title":"fix(openclaw): PR #1242''s sops-nix secrets landed on a stranded feature branch \u2014 not on main, and the promised /run/secrets/openclaw wrapper repoint was never filed","number":1558,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the landing or the wrapper repoint inside this triage task","Rotating or re-mirroring any secret values"],"include":["Triage of issue #1558 against current main","Routing: follow-up packet for landing the 3-file change + wrapper repoint + activation verification"]},"tests":["n/a \u2014 triage task; the follow-up packet carries the verification work"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Filed this run by pr-diff-review after dedupe searches: issue searches for ''openclaw sops'', ''openclaw-summarize'', and ''1242'' return only #1243 (unrelated ACP adapter), #1030 (summarize plugin), and #1371 (general git hygiene, which does not name this branch or PR); no open or closed issue covers the stranded #1242 change or its follow-up.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #1242 merged into a feature branch that never landed on main, so its sops-nix OpenClaw secrets change and its promised wrapper repoint follow-up are both undone while the PR reads as merged.","evidence":["PR #1242 API: base=feat/openclaw-summarize, head=feat/openclaw-sops, merged=true, merge_commit 53ebc06e, own commit 259363f5 feat(nixos): decrypt OpenClaw tokens via sops-nix from the bws mirror","git merge-base --is-ancestor 53ebc06e origin/main fails (NOT-IN-MAIN); git cat-file -e origin/main:nixos/hosts/amd-openclaw-secrets.nix fails (MISSING)","git diff origin/main...origin/feat/openclaw-summarize --stat: amd-openclaw-secrets.nix +22, nixos/hosts/default.nix +1, secrets/sops/common/bws.yaml re-sync \u2014 exactly #1242''s change; branch tip is the #1242 merge, no PR from it to main","Current main home/openclaw/default.nix:21 comment and environment block (~line 80) still use ~/.secrets/openclaw/gateway-token; git log on home/openclaw since the #1242 merge is empty"],"acceptance":["Triage note on #1558 confirming (or refuting, with evidence) that #1242''s change is absent from main and the wrapper repoint is undone","Follow-up packet enqueued for landing feat/openclaw-summarize''s 3-file change on main plus the home/openclaw /run/secrets/openclaw repoint, or a documented no-action rationale on the issue","Issue labels updated to match the routing decision"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1558","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1242","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1490","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1371"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Merged-looking but unlanded secrets migration: the sops declarations are dead config on an unmerged branch, the gateway still depends on manually created ~/.secrets files, and the branch could be cleaned up as ''merged'' losing the change.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1558', '2026-10-28 01:36:19.73331+00', '2026-10-28 02:37:50.150895+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1608, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'fix(client): PR #596 regeneration drops ProviderInfo — update consumers or keep alias so typecheck passes', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/659","title":"fix(client): PR #596''s regenerated client drops ProviderInfo \u2014 client solid data and plugin TUI context no longer compile (CI typecheck TS2724)","number":659,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The #560 server/protocol behaviour itself (tracked on #560 and PR #596)","OpenAPI document regeneration (#660)","provider.get availability semantics (#661)"],"include":["PR #596 branch (sweep/560-provider-models)","packages/client generated types + src/solid/data.ts","packages/plugin/src/tui/context.ts"]},"tests":["bun run check from repo root (CI typecheck job on the PR)","packages/client check:generated"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''ProviderInfo'' and ''provider models api/provider'' on 2026-10-27 lane-B run returned no existing issue for the dropped type; nearest is open #560 (the parent feature) and closed #450 (a different stale-client incident).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #596''s client regeneration removes the ProviderInfo export while two in-repo consumers still import it, breaking client/plugin typecheck on the PR itself and renaming a published client type without a compatibility alias.","evidence":["PR #596 diff (head 4c0f8c5a): packages/client/src/promise/generated/types.ts deletes export type ProviderInfo, adds ProviderInfoWithModels; ProviderList/GetOutput switch to the new name","Current main 41c8a35f: packages/client/src/solid/data.ts:24 imports ProviderInfo (used :104 provider?: ProviderInfo[]); packages/plugin/src/tui/context.ts:17 imports ProviderInfo from @opencode/client (used :136)","PR #596 CI typecheck job 122285053434: src/solid/data.ts(24,3): error TS2724: ''\"../promise\"'' has no exported member named ''ProviderInfo''","Current main generated/types.ts:2167 still exports ProviderInfo \u2014 regression is PR-introduced"],"acceptance":["PR #596 (or successor) keeps a ProviderInfo alias or updates both consumers (client solid/data.ts, plugin tui/context.ts) to the with-models type","Typecheck passes for @opencode/client and @opencode/plugin on the PR (no TS2724)","Generated client produced by bun run generate from packages/client per repo AGENTS.md, not hand-edited"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/659","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/596","packages/client/src/solid/data.ts:24","packages/plugin/src/tui/context.ts:17"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Blocks #560''s fix from landing: the PR is red on its own typecheck for a proven PR-caused reason. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:659', '2026-10-28 01:36:49.668294+00', '2026-10-28 03:06:28.31643+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1609, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 1 of #1554 — one durable task store across MCP and /v1 (internal/tasks wiring) — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1555","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1554 \u2014 one durable task store across MCP and /v1 (internal/tasks wiring)","number":1555,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the store wiring in this triage task","client-side task execution (Phase 2 of #1554, #1556) and register truth-up / nix#209 closure (Phase 3, #1557)","operational limits, cooperative cancel, audit logging (open questions on #1554)"],"include":["issue #1555 and design #1554 with the design doc it links","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpserver (tasks.go, server.go), internal/daemon/ops.go taskStore, internal/cli/serve.go App.MCPServer, internal/tasks, internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go (read-only references)"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./... via CI; defining tests from #1555: cross-surface visibility, MCP cross-connection invisibility preserved, restart durability with working-task reaping, standalone behaviour unchanged)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1555 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-27) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1555 \u2014 it did not exist before this run, so its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx has one task-store type but two live instances: the MCP server''s private in-memory store and the daemon /v1 surface''s SQLite-backed store. Tasks are invisible across surfaces and MCP tasks die with the process, contradicting the internal/tasks package''s own stated design. Design #1554 Phase 1 (#1555) wires the daemon''s single durable store into mcpserver.Server.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpserver/tasks.go tasks(): the MCP server lazily creates tasks.New() (in-memory); field taskStore at internal/mcpserver/server.go:273-274; no injection seam exists","pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon/ops.go:436-453 taskStore(): the daemon creates a separate store \u2014 tasks.Open(<state>/tasks.db) with tasks.New() fallback \u2014 used by /v1 handlers and internal/daemon/routes_proto.go, routes_exec.go, input_required.go; a task started over MCP is invisible to /v1 and vice versa (dezren39/nix#209 TASK-27)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go:112 gap ext-tasks-durable-before-response (issue #209): ''the task store is an in-memory map; a task does not survive the daemon'' (TASK-20)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/tasks/tasks.go header states the design intent (''Two stores would be two sets of expiry bugs... a task started over one surface would be invisible from the other''); the type is shared, the instance is not. Store is mutex-guarded; Open() reloads persisted rows and reaps a non-terminal row to Failed (''daemon restarted before task completion'', tasks.go:243-249)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/serve.go:474 App.MCPServer() already wires daemon-shared pieces into mcpserver.New (Notify, Passthrough, Timing); standalone constructions at internal/cli/adapter.go:195 and openapi.go:90 keep private stores under the design"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1555: scope confirmed against current main, seam shape and the winning PollInterval setting settled or explicitly left open with reasons, and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If triage finds Phase 1 as scoped is not independently landable, say exactly why on the issue and propose the rescoped Phase 1 in the design doc''s terms \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1555","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1554","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/209"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 closes the oldest structural item in nix#209 (TASK-27/TASK-20) and makes MCP tasks durable; Phase 3 of the design is gated on it. Normal priority per the design issue.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1555', '2026-10-28 01:37:06.641503+00', '2026-10-28 02:41:23.716262+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1611, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'triage(server): align or document PR #596 provider.get''s unfiltered model embedding vs list''s available set', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/661","title":"fix(server): PR #596 provider.get embeds models from the unfiltered state record while provider.list embeds only snapshot.available \u2014 disabled/stale-connection providers leak their catalog through get","number":661,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Client ProviderInfo consumer break (#659)","OpenAPI regeneration (#660)","Any change to snapshot()''s availability filter itself"],"include":["PR #596 branch (sweep/560-provider-models)","packages/server/src/handlers/provider.ts","packages/core/src/provider.ts definition()","packages/server/test/provider.test.ts"]},"tests":["packages/server provider tests (existing nonblocking + models tests, plus new pinning test)","bun run check from repo root"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Filed this run (lane B pr-diff-review) after reading PR #596''s handler/core diff against current main 41c8a35f snapshot() filter; issue search ''definition snapshot available provider'' on 2026-10-27 returned nothing; #560 covers the zero-models problem, not the get/list set mismatch.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #596 serves model inventories for providers the list endpoint (and the snapshot availability/source-connection filter) deliberately withholds, because provider.get reads the raw state record while provider.list reads snapshot.available.","evidence":["PR #596 handler (head 4c0f8c5a): list = snapshot().available.map(withModels); get = providers.definition(id) -> withModels(definition), no availability check","PR #596 core: definition() = Effect.sync(() => state.get().get(id)) \u2014 any recorded definition","Current main 41c8a35f Provider.snapshot filter: activation disabled excluded; sourceConnection mismatch with current connection excluded (''Never combine the previous account''s discovered endpoints/models with a new connection'')","PR #596''s new server test covers only an enabled, available custom provider"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict recorded on #661: get aligned to the list/available set, or unfiltered get declared deliberate","If aligned: disabled or source-connection-stale provider returns ProviderNotFoundError from provider.get, pinned by a server test; nonblocking read contract preserved or its change justified","If kept: protocol endpoint description documents the unfiltered get and a test pins get returning models for a provider absent from list"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/661","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/596","packages/core/src/provider.ts Provider.snapshot / Provider.definition","packages/server/src/handlers/provider.ts"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Low priority: a list/get consistency and stale-catalog exposure question introduced by an unmerged PR; cheapest to resolve before #560 lands rather than after consumers depend on the get behaviour.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:661', '2026-10-28 01:37:51.219657+00', '2026-10-28 02:57:17.177704+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1612, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 3 of #1554 — compare-register truth-up and dezren39/nix#209 closure — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["depends-on-1555","depends-on-1556"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1557","title":"mcpx: Phase 3 of #1554 \u2014 compare-register truth-up and dezren39/nix#209 closure","number":1557,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["doing the truth-up in this triage task","any implementation work (Phases 1-2 own it)","the open questions on #1554 (limits, cooperative cancel, audit, ID entropy, input relay) \u2014 they stay questions on the design issue"],"include":["issue #1557 and design #1554 with the design doc it links","pkgs/mcpx/docs/compare/register/tasks.md and capabilities.md, internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go, planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md (read-only references for triage)"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification the follow-up must do (each rewritten register row spot-checkable against its cited code symbol on current main; gate evidence = merge state of #1555/#1556)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1557 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-27) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1557 \u2014 it did not exist before this run, so its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The mcpx conformance register (docs/compare/register) still describes the pre-fix tasks state, and the origin issue dezren39/nix#209 remains open, even though most of its server-side charge has landed and Phases 1-2 of design #1554 finish the rest. Design #1554 Phase 3 (#1557) rewrites the register to as-built, repoints still-open conformance gaps, updates the roadmap row, and closes the origin issue with evidence.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/docs/compare/register/tasks.md (read 2026-10-27) still marks landed behaviour with the pre-fix verdicts \u2014 TASK-05/06/07/08/11/12/13/15/18/22/24 rows say the 2026 shapes are missing, while internal/mcpserver/tasks.go implements them (modernTask, created, detailedNow, handleModernTask, withRelatedTask, missingTasks)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go:105-112: eight Gap entries cite issue #209 (tasks-get-implies-list, tasks-failed-status-message, tasks-document-unbound, tasks-rate-limit, tasks-resource-limits, tasks-audit, ext-tasks-cancel-cooperative, ext-tasks-durable-before-response) \u2014 the last is retired by Phase 1; the rest stay open questions on #1554 and need repointing when nix#209 closes","planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md Next row ''Tasks, which are advertised and not implemented'' (status proposed) links only dezren39/nix#209; the design #1554 audit (2026-10-27) verified the server-side rows landed and scoped the remainder into Phases 1-2","Cross-repo set rule (fleet): dezren39/nix#209 is the origin issue for this set; closure happens from the mcpx-canonical repo with evidence, no duplicate filed \u2014 the same handling design #1481 recorded for nix#254"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1557: dependency gate explicitly checked (Phase 1 #1555 and Phase 2 #1556 merged or not, with PR evidence), and either the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued or the issue is parked naming the missing phase","If the gate is met and triage finds the truth-up scope changed (e.g. register format moved), say exactly what changed on the issue \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1557","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1554","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1555","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1556","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/209"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 3 is the design''s closure step: a stale conformance register is how the next real gap gets ignored, and nix#209 stays open until the register tells the truth. Sequenced strictly after Phases 1-2. Normal priority per the design issue.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'parked', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1557', '2026-10-28 01:37:51.992156+00', '2026-10-28 10:11:20.664883+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1613, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 2 of #1554 — client task execution for taskSupport "required" tools (internal/mcpclient) — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1556","title":"mcpx: Phase 2 of #1554 \u2014 client task execution for taskSupport \"required\" tools (internal/mcpclient)","number":1556,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing client task execution in this triage task","relaying an upstream task''s inputRequests to the downstream client (open question on #1554 \u2014 this phase returns a named error instead)","Phase 1 store wiring (#1555) and register truth-up / nix#209 closure (Phase 3, #1557)"],"include":["issue #1556 and design #1554 with the design doc it links","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient (client.go CallTool, Tool.Execution, Era handling, modern.go), internal/pool/pool.go call site, internal/mcpserver/tasks.go as the interop reference (read-only)"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./... via CI; defining tests from #1556 against fake legacy and modern upstreams: required tool completes via task, optional stays plain, cancel propagates, fault surfaces, input_required named error, malformed response errors without hanging)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1556 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-27) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1556 \u2014 it did not exist before this run, so its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx''s MCP client never task-augments a call and never declares the tasks extension upstream, so a pooled tool declared taskSupport ''required'' cannot be called the way its server demands; mcpx''s own server-side task machinery then surfaces the failure inside its tasks. Design #1554 Phase 2 (#1556) teaches mcpclient per-era task execution for required tools only.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/client.go:171-174: Tool.Execution carries taskSupport raw (''Kept raw and forwarded'') \u2014 nothing in mcpclient reads it; grep finds no tasks/ method strings in internal/mcpclient","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/client.go:1164 CallTool is a plain tools/call on every path; the pool''s call site is internal/pool/pool.go:1051 \u2014 an upstream tool with taskSupport ''required'' cannot be executed as its server demands (dezren39/nix#209 TOOL-21 client half)","The client never declares the tasks extension to an upstream (CAP-26 client direction, nix#209); Client.Era already distinguishes legacy from modern upstreams (see ReadResource''s era-dependent error handling, client.go ~1196)","Server side of the same design is landed and is the interop reference: internal/mcpserver/tasks.go maybeTask/created/handleModernTask implement both eras'' shapes (flat Task + resultType ''task'', ttlMs/pollIntervalMs, DetailedTask, tasks/update, -32021)"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1556: scope confirmed against current main, the CallTool seam settled or explicitly left open with reasons, and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If triage finds Phase 2 as scoped is not independently landable, say exactly why on the issue and propose the rescoped Phase 2 in the design doc''s terms \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1556","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1554","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/209"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 2 makes every tool an upstream declares callable through the gateway \u2014 a correctness gap in the pool''s core promise \u2014 and Phase 3 of the design is gated on it. Independent of Phase 1. Normal priority per the design issue.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1556', '2026-10-28 01:38:03.70331+00', '2026-10-28 02:40:54.359911+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1614, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: implement schemaval core — JSON Schema 2020-12 validator + dialect policy (#1482 fix)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1482","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1481 \u2014 schemaval core: a real JSON Schema 2020-12 validator + dialect policy (no call-path changes)","number":1482,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Any change to ListTools, CallTool, Client.answer, codegen, or the daemon; enforcement of any kind","Any change to internal/mcpspec","Format assertion (formats stay annotations in v1)","Phases 2\u20133 of design #1481 (list-time compilation, call-time enforcement)"],"include":["New package pkgs/mcpx/internal/schemaval wrapping github.com/santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6 (only import site; go.mod gains exactly this one direct dependency)","Dialect policy (2020-12 default; 2019-09/draft-07/draft-06/draft-04 declared; else typed UnsupportedDialect), offline-only $ref resolution (typed UnresolvedRef), 1 MiB schema-size bound, path-carrying flattened validation errors, formats as annotations","Defining tests per the acceptance list, including the counting-test-server zero-HTTP test and the 2^53+1 integer fidelity test","Dialect document in pkgs/mcpx/docs/ + mechanism note in pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_messages.go"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/mcpx && go test ./... (via CI on the PR per fleet policy)","new internal/schemaval tests: dialect corpus, draft-07, UnsupportedDialect, UnresolvedRef, zero-HTTP remote-ref, 2^53+1 fidelity, path-qualified errors, oversize-schema rejection"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Implementation follow-up enqueued by triage task 1513 on issue #1482; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1482 is distinct from the triage task identity (1513). No schemaval package or santhosh-tekuri dependency exists on current main (verified 2026-10-28).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx has no real JSON Schema validator for tool/elicitation schemas: internal/mcpspec is a test-only protocol-frame validator kept out of the binary by TestNotImportedByBinary. Phase 1 builds the validator core (santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6 behind internal/schemaval) with the dialect policy, offline-only $ref resolution, a 1 MiB compile bound, and path-carrying errors \u2014 with no call-path changes, so later phases can adopt it incrementally.","evidence":["Triage task 1513 verified on current origin/main (2026-10-28): pkgs/mcpx has NO internal/schemaval package and pkgs/mcpx/go.mod has no santhosh-tekuri entry (direct requires: charmbracelet bubbles/bubbletea/lipgloss, tetratelabs/wazero, yaml.v3, modernc.org/sqlite)","internal/mcpspec exists as the test-only protocol-frame validator with TestNotImportedByBinary at pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpspec/mcpspec_test.go:235","Schema-size evidence for the settled 1 MiB bound: mcpspec vendored protocol schemas on main measure 87,877 B (2024-11-05), 89,428 B (2025-03-26), 108,234 B (2025-06-18), 174,323 B (2025-11-25), 181,474 B (2026-07-28) \u2014 the largest schema documents in the repo; tool input schemas are typically a few KB","internal/conformance/coverage_messages.go exists (register() for Messages/errors/_meta/JSON Schema rows) \u2014 the note about the validator mechanism lands there","Validator decision already recorded on design issue #1481 per dezren39/nix#254 acceptance: adopt santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6 behind internal/schemaval; mcpspec stays test-only"],"acceptance":["Defining tests pass: (a) 2020-12 keyword corpus incl. prefixItems, unevaluatedProperties, boolean schemas, $defs internal refs; (b) declared draft-07 schema compiles and validates per draft-07; (c) unsupported $schema dialect returns the typed UnsupportedDialect error, distinct from a generic compile error; (d) unresolvable $ref is a compile error; (e) a schema with a remote $ref is a compile error with ZERO HTTP requests observed by a counting test server; (f) integer 9007199254740993 (2^53+1) validates as integer and fails a maximum: 9007199254740992 check correctly; (g) a nested required/type violation returns the path-qualified one-line error form","A schema larger than 1 MiB (1048576 bytes) fails compilation with a typed/bounded error (settled bound, triage task 1513)","pkgs/mcpx/go.mod gains exactly one new direct dependency (github.com/santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6); internal/schemaval is its only import site","internal/mcpspec is untouched and TestNotImportedByBinary still passes","Dialect document exists in pkgs/mcpx/docs/ stating supported dialects (2020-12 default; 2019-09, draft-07, draft-06, draft-04 declared), the no-network rule, the 1 MiB bound, and formats-as-annotations; internal/conformance/coverage_messages.go notes the validator mechanism exists","Full suite passes: cd pkgs/mcpx && go test ./... (via CI on the PR per fleet policy)","Issue #1482 acceptance criteria (as filed) are met and the issue closes via the implementation PR"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1482","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1481","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpspec/mcpspec_test.go:235 (TestNotImportedByBinary)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_messages.go"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 of the approved #1481 design; Phases 2\u20133 (list-time compilation, call-time enforcement) are blocked on this core existing. Issue priority/normal.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1482', '2026-10-28 01:38:42.491231+00', '2026-10-28 04:52:12.631479+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1616, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 2 of #1481 — implement CallTool argument validation (-32602) + structuredContent output warning — issue #1483', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["depends-on-1482"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1483","title":"mcpx: Phase 2 of #1481 \u2014 validate tool arguments at CallTool (enforce, -32602) + structuredContent against outputSchema (warn-only)","number":1483,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:45:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Elicitation answer validation (Phase 3, issue #1484)","Enforcing outputSchema (warn-only this phase)","Format assertion; per-server validation-mode config; codegen changes","Starting before Phase 1 (#1482) is merged \u2014 park naming the dependency if claimed early"],"include":["ListTools: compile InputSchema/OutputSchema via internal/schemaval beside checkToolHeaders; uncompilable schema = tool excluded + Warning; validators cached per tool keyed by schema hash","CallTool: validate arguments before send; failure = -32602 Invalid Params naming tool + path-qualified reason; upstream receives zero calls","mcpserver invoke path: -32602 validation errors pass through as protocol errors, never isError results","CallTool result path: structuredContent validated against outputSchema warn-only (Warning + lifecycle event, result delivered unchanged)","Defining tests from issue #1483 + argument-validation benchmark within the triage-set budget (<=100us/op median, <=1ms worst, representative nested schema); record measured numbers on #1483","Conformance matrix + gap registry rows named in #1483 updated"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/mcpx && go test ./... via CI on the PR (fleet CI-first policy)","Defining test: invalid args -> -32602 with upstream call count 0","Defining test: unsupported-dialect tool absent from ListTools and gateway tools/list, Warning emitted","Defining test: non-conforming structuredContent delivered unchanged with Warning recorded","Benchmark: argument validation on representative nested schema within triage budget, measured numbers recorded on #1483"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1515 per issue #1483 acceptance (triage verdict + implementation follow-up packet enqueued, flagged depends-on-1482); no prior fix packet for issue 1483 existed \u2014 the only prior task naming 1483 is triage task 1515 itself with a distinct triage dedupe key","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:45:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx never validates tool-call arguments against the tool''s inputSchema and never checks structuredContent against outputSchema: invalid arguments are shipped upstream and non-conforming results are relayed silently.","evidence":["Triage task 1515 (2026-10-28T01:40Z) verified on main: GET contents pkgs/mcpx/internal/schemaval -> 404 (Phase 1 #1482 not merged; its triage task 1513 was in progress)","mcpclient/client.go: Tool struct carries InputSchema/OutputSchema as json.RawMessage; CallTool marshals {name, arguments} and sends with no schema validation","mcpclient/modern.go:495 checkToolHeaders precedent: invalid per-tool definition = excluded at list time + Warning; pool/pool.go:1018 wires OnWarning to lifecycle events","mcpserver/server.go ~1006: generic invoke errors become isError tool results; only UpstreamError relays as protocol error \u2014 -32602 needs an explicit pass-through","Issue #1483 acceptance criteria + design #1481 Phase 2 section (design doc files/designs/code-mcpx-json-schema-validation.md in the keep-the-four-repos-healthy goal workspace)"],"acceptance":["Phase 1 (#1482) merged to main before implementation starts (gate checked at claim time; otherwise park)","All defining tests in issue #1483 pass in CI","The -32602 error reaches gateway callers as a protocol error, not an isError result (gateway-surface test)","Benchmark measured numbers recorded on #1483 and within the triage-set budget or the overrun is explained on the issue"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1483","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1482","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1481","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/254"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 2 is the user-visible core of #1481: it closes the MUST conformance rows and generates the output-warning data the design''s enforcement-flip question needs. Sequenced strictly after Phase 1 (#1482).","timebox_minutes":45}', 'parked', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1483', '2026-10-28 01:40:35.222965+00', '2026-10-28 11:01:09.749542+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1617, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: registry merge wipes sparse-omitted fields — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1560","title":"aggregator: registry merge wipes a session''s model/title/directory when a later sparse record omits them \u2014 the durable store forgets what it knew","number":1560,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:38:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The concurrent-write temp-path race in the JSON stores (#1509 \u2014 separate issue, even where the registry persist shares the pattern)","SessionFeedEntry mapping in sources/opencode.ts (sparse entries are legitimate input)","Registry record identity/keying (source, id)"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/registry.ts mergeRecords: absent (undefined) incoming fields must not overwrite stored values; label degradation rule","Triage ruling on parentId: whether incoming null may clear a stored parent","Regression test in the aggregator suite for sparse-over-full merge"]},"tests":["bun test test/slice3.test.ts (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''mergeRecords'', ''session registry'', ''registry merge model'': no existing filing. Open-issue list scan: adjacent #1509 is the concurrent JSON-store temp-path race (different mechanism/module behaviour \u2014 persist write race, not merge semantics); the registry persist in live.ts shares that tmp-path pattern but #1560 is about which fields survive a merge, not write atomicity.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:38:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mergeRecords'' spread overwrites stored SessionRecord fields with undefined/null from sparse incoming records, violating its own ''when present'' contract, and the loss is persisted to the durable registry store.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe with the real registry.ts (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneA-registrymerge/probe.ts + out.log): stored full record (model-a/title/directory/parent ses_parent/tokens 500) + sparse newer incoming -> merged model/title/directory undefined, parentId null, label ''ses_1''; persisted JSON has no model key; special-cased fields (tokens 500 kept, lastSeenAt advanced to 12:00Z, startedAt kept) behaved as documented; control incoming with model-b replaced correctly (tokens 700)","Code read on main a120b9a9: registry.ts:126-127 bare spreads with special cases only at :128-131; doc contract ''when present'' at :113; recordFromSessionEntry always-key shape :31-52 with label fallback :40; opencode.ts mapOne sparse fields :171-178; live.ts mergeIntoRegistry persist :614-631 and incoming construction :965"],"acceptance":["Merging an incoming record whose model/title/directory are undefined preserves the stored values; incoming parentId null does not erase a stored non-null parent unless triage explicitly decides and documents that semantic","A title-less incoming record does not degrade a stored label that came from a title","Present incoming values still win; tokensTotal max, lastSeenAt newest, startedAt earliest, and taskRefs union keep working","Regression test: sparse recordFromSessionEntry record merged over a full stored record asserts stored fields survive; existing slice3 merge test still passes","Per-field treatment matches the registry.ts doc comment''s ''when present'' contract (comment updated if a field is deliberately exempted)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1560","pm-stack/aggregator/src/registry.ts:110-133","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/opencode.ts:171-178","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/live.ts:614-631","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/live.ts:965","pm-stack/aggregator/test/slice3.test.ts"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The registry is the durable identity store behind /sessions (#906 \u00a73) whose purpose is remembering sessions after they leave the feed; every live read merges into it, so one sparse re-read permanently erases a session''s model/title/directory/parent and its human-readable label \u2014 silent durable data loss on a routine path.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1560', '2026-10-28 01:41:04.802322+00', '2026-10-28 01:41:04.802322+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1618, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'triage: prefer override factor/weight of 0 silently becomes the x3 default (#662)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/662","title":"fix(core): a prefer override''s factor/weight of 0 is silently dropped \u2014 the target gets the default \u00d73 lift instead","number":662,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:58Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the absent-field PREFERRED_FACTOR default itself (pinned behaviour for genuinely unstated preferences)","scheduled config weight rules (schema-validated PositiveFinite, unaffected)","learned adjustments'' factor handling in ModelRoute.addAdjustment (a different, programmatic surface)"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-overrides.ts parse treatment of present-but-invalid factor/weight","tests in packages/core/test/model-route-overrides.test.ts pinning the chosen contract"]},"tests":["bun test for model-route-overrides.test.ts from packages/core (run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list search for ''factor prefer override weight zero'' returned no issues; gh search for ''PREFERRED_FACTOR'' returned none; open-issue list reviewed this run (661/660/659 are PR #596 findings, unrelated). #536/#570 covered malformed lists/schedules in the same parser, not factor/weight.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:58Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"ModelRouteOverrides.parse drops a present-but-invalid prefer factor/weight to absent, and absent means the default x3 PREFERRED_FACTOR lift in tracedWeightOf.","evidence":["packages/core/src/model-route-overrides.ts:79-84 \u2014 factor/weight guards require > 0 and finite, else the field is dropped to undefined while the entry is kept","packages/core/src/model-route.ts:727,795-796 \u2014 PREFERRED_FACTOR = 3; tracedWeightOf applies item.weight if set, else weight *= item.factor ?? PREFERRED_FACTOR","packages/schema/src/config/model-routes.ts:11,156-163,191-197 \u2014 the same factor/weight fields on scheduled weight rules are PositiveFinite (isGreaterThan(0)): zero is invalid there, not ''absent''","packages/core/src/model-route-overrides.ts:46-48,62-66 \u2014 the same parser drops whole entries for malformed scope lists (#536) and present-but-unreadable schedules (#570) instead of widening them","Probe (laptop, real modules, main 41c8a35f60): parse factor 0 -> field absent; factor -1 -> absent; weight 0 -> absent; factor 0.5 / weight 0.25 preserved; end-to-end weightFactor(factor:0) = 3, weightFactor(weight:0) = 3, weightFactor(factor:0.5) = 0.5","packages/core/test/model-route-overrides.test.ts:113-116,231-256 \u2014 tests pin the absent-field x3 default and valid factors/weights, never a present-but-invalid value"],"acceptance":["A prefer override whose factor or weight is present but not positive-finite (0, negative, Infinity via 1e999) does NOT fall back to PREFERRED_FACTOR; triage picks drop-the-entry or honour-0 and the choice is stated in a comment at the guard site and pinned by tests","An override with factor and weight genuinely absent keeps today''s behaviour: prefer lifts by PREFERRED_FACTOR (existing test at model-route-overrides.test.ts:113-116 stays green)","Valid values are unchanged (factor 0.5, weight 0.25 parse and apply as today)","New regression tests in packages/core/test/model-route-overrides.test.ts cover factor: 0 and weight: 0 at parse level plus one end-to-end weightFactor assertion"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/662","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/536","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/570"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A user''s explicit routing instruction in a hand-editable shared file is silently inverted to the maximum default preference; the contract decision is small and the precedents (#536/#570, PositiveFinite schema) are in-repo. Normal priority, triage first because drop-vs-honour is a contract choice.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:662', '2026-10-28 01:43:03.010603+00', '2026-10-28 04:09:17.901447+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1619, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: validate elicitation form answers against requestedSchema in client.answer (fix #1484, gated on #1482)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["depends-on-1482"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1484","title":"mcpx: Phase 3 of #1481 \u2014 validate elicitation form answers against requestedSchema in client.answer","number":1484,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:48:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing internal/schemaval itself (Phase 1, #1482)","tool argument/output validation (Phase 2, #1483)","decline/cancel and URL-mode behaviour changes; re-ask/retry UX","everything else under #255 (elicitation storage protection, redaction, CLI review UI); sampling validation (#256)"],"include":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/modern.go Client.answer validation after applyDefaults, using internal/schemaval from #1482","tests in pkgs/mcpx for the three defining cases (wrong-typed answer -32602, defaulted field validates, input-required inheritance) plus the uncompilable-schema warn-and-relay case"]},"tests":["pkgs/mcpx: go test ./... (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)","defining tests: wrong-typed answer rejected with -32602 and not relayed; defaulted field validates; input-required round inherits the check; uncompilable requestedSchema relays with warning"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Implementation follow-up enqueued by triage task 1518 on issue #1484 per that packet''s instructions; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1484 is distinct from the triage task 1518 identity; no fix task for #1484 existed at enqueue time.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:48:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"An elicitation answer is relayed upstream checked only for non-emptiness, not against the requestedSchema the server supplied; Phase 3 adds schemaval validation in Client.answer after applyDefaults, gated on Phase 1 (#1482) providing internal/schemaval.","evidence":["Triage task 1518 verified on current main db6f7d00 (2026-10-28): modern.go:246 Client.answer \u2014 elicitation/create handler output passes through applyDefaults (:297) and is returned unvalidated; applyDefaults (:398) parses requestedSchema (:405) for defaults only; no schemaval reference anywhere in modern.go","pkgs/mcpx/internal on main db6f7d00 has NO schemaval package (directory listing verified) and issue #1482 (Phase 1) is OPEN \u2014 the dependency gate is unmet at enqueue time","resolveInput (modern.go, input-required flow) routes answers through answer(), so the check inherits with no extra wiring"],"acceptance":["Wrong-typed elicitation answer is rejected: the requesting server receives -32602, the answer is not relayed, and a Warning is logged","A defaulted field (filled by applyDefaults) validates \u2014 defaults are applied before validation","An uncompilable requestedSchema relays the answer unvalidated with a warning, never a hard failure","Decline/cancel answers and URL-mode elicitation are byte-for-byte unchanged","The input-required (resolveInput) round inherits the same validation via answer()","Defining tests pass: wrong-typed answer rejected with -32602; defaulted field validates; input-required round inherits the check"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1484","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1481","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1482","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/modern.go:246"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 3 completes design #1481 and satisfies dezren39/nix#254''s elicitation acceptance item with the same validator as tool schemas; small and independent of Phase 2 once Phase 1 (#1482) lands.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1484', '2026-10-28 01:44:15.698457+00', '2026-10-28 05:48:50.287157+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1621, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'docs(protocol): regenerate the three OpenAPI documents for PR #596''s provider shape change', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/660","title":"docs(protocol): PR #596 changes the /api/provider HttpApi shape but regenerates none of the checked-in OpenAPI documents","number":660,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Client regeneration and the ProviderInfo consumer break (#659)","provider.get availability semantics (#661)"],"include":["PR #596 branch (sweep/560-provider-models)","packages/protocol/openapi.json","services/www/openapi.json + services/www/public/openapi.json"]},"tests":["bun run check:generated in packages/protocol","bun run check:generated in services/www"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Filed this run (lane B pr-diff-review) from PR #596''s file list (no openapi.json) cross-checked against the generation scripts; issue searches for ProviderInfo/api/provider models on 2026-10-27 returned no existing stale-openapi issue for this PR; PR #597 is the precedent that regenerated all three documents.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #596 changes the protocol API shape without regenerating the checked-in OpenAPI documents, so the published contract keeps showing /api/provider returning plain Provider.Info with no models.","evidence":["PR #596 file list (head 4c0f8c5a): protocol/src/groups/provider.ts changed; no packages/protocol/openapi.json, services/www/openapi.json, or services/www/public/openapi.json","packages/protocol/script/generate-openapi.ts builds the document from OpenApi.fromApi(ClientApi); --check fails when the checked-in file differs","services/www/script/generate-openapi.ts:3-4 copies packages/protocol/openapi.json to the two www targets","PR #597 (same review batch) regenerated all three documents for a smaller schema-annotation change"],"acceptance":["packages/protocol/openapi.json regenerated via bun run generate in packages/protocol and contains Provider.InfoWithModels with models on both provider endpoint responses","services/www/openapi.json and services/www/public/openapi.json regenerated from the protocol document","bun run check:generated passes in packages/protocol and services/www"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/660","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/pull/596","packages/protocol/script/generate-openapi.ts","services/www/script/generate-openapi.ts"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Low priority on its own, but it leaves the published API contract describing exactly the pre-#560 shape the PR exists to fix, and trips the generated-docs gate. Quick regeneration fix.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/opencode:issue:660', '2026-10-28 01:44:34.634539+00', '2026-10-28 03:01:09.986463+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1622, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(directory): drop + truncate torn final line in Directory::replay, mirroring FileJournal::open (#1521 fix)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1521","title":"id(directory): a torn final line in directory.jsonl bricks the directory \u2014 Directory::replay refuses the crash-torn tail that ArtifactLog (loaded in the same open) drops and truncates","number":1521,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["#1499 Petnames::open torn tail (separate issue/task)","world_store.rs / artifact.rs / envelope_outbox.rs / directory_log.rs behavior (already correct \u2014 reference only)","Changing the append path''s write+sync protocol"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/directory.rs Directory::replay/open torn-tail handling (drop unterminated final line, warn, truncate) and tests"]},"tests":["cargo test --offline directory (targeted, on laptop or CI per fleet rules)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up fix packet enqueued by triage task 1566 on issue #1521; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1521 is distinct from the triage identity. #1499 (open) is the same defect class in Petnames::open only (pkgs/id/src/petname.rs) and does not cover the directory journal.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"A crash-torn final line in directory.jsonl bricks the directory permanently: Directory::replay refuses the unterminated partial entry instead of dropping and truncating it like the sibling JSONL stores.","evidence":["Triage task 1566 verified on main a120b9a9: Directory::replay (directory.rs ~505-525) uses text.lines() with ? on parse failure, no torn-tail case; Directory::append (~527-543) single write_all + sync_data; Directory::open (~471) is replay first, so one torn append bricks every open","FileJournal::open (world_store.rs:85-130): unterminated last line dropped + file truncated to good_len + tracing::warn; terminated unparseable line bails as corruption \u2014 the house semantics to mirror","ArtifactLog::open (artifact.rs:575-600) truncates everything after the last newline in the load path \u2014 precedent for truncating inside replay/open","Existing test replay_rebuilds_the_directory_and_refuses_a_broken_journal (directory.rs:2601) covers an apply-refused complete entry only; no torn-tail test exists (grep ''torn'' in directory.rs: no hits)"],"acceptance":["Directory::replay/open on a journal whose final line is an unterminated truncated fragment loads all complete entries, drops the fragment, and truncates the file to the last complete line, with a warning log (mirrors FileJournal::open / ArtifactLog::open)","A parseable but unterminated final entry is dropped too (never acknowledged \u2014 same rule as FileJournal::open)","A newline-terminated line that does not parse, anywhere including the last line, still fails with ''directory journal line N is malformed''","A complete entry that apply refuses still fails replay (existing test at directory.rs:2601 keeps passing)","New tests cover: torn final fragment (loads + truncated), terminated-corrupt final line (errors), torn fragment after valid entries (earlier entries intact)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1521","pkgs/id/src/directory.rs (replay/append/open)","pkgs/id/src/world_store.rs:85","pkgs/id/src/artifact.rs:575"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Durable-record bricking: the directory journal''s own append path can produce exactly the torn tail its load path refuses, turning a recoverable crash into a permanently unopenable directory (accounts/friendships/groups). Semantics are already established by three sibling stores; fix is one load path plus tests.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1521', '2026-10-28 01:46:47.645906+00', '2026-10-28 07:14:43.614925+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1624, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'triage: session-activity v1 fields under design #612 phase 1 (#524)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/524","title":"Session-activity API: expose per-session status, last-activity, model + provider for external babysitters","number":524,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the endpoint changes inside the triage timebox","changing the { type } field or any UI snapshot endpoint (/api/sessions/snapshot, /api/sessions/status)","the managed-server registry (#525) or contract docs/fixture (#614)"],"include":["triage of #524 against current main","promotion: enqueue the phase-1 implementation packet (or ready-label) referencing design #612"]},"tests":["n/a for triage; implementation tests are specified in the promoted packet (shape-pinning tests for /api/session-activity)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Design #612 (filed 2026-10-27 by repo-design-architect) links this issue as a phased sub-issue; gh issue list search for session-activity / managed-servers / observability returns only #524, #525, #612, #614 \u2014 no other open issue covers this work","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"GET /api/session-activity returns only { [sessionId]: { type: phase } }: getSessionActivitySnapshot (session-runtime.js:366) drops the updatedAt the phase map already records (:176), and there is no status, model/provider, or tool-in-flight field \u2014 the fleet babysitter''s stall detector is blocked on last-activity.","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/notifications/routes.js:287 \u2014 app.get(''/api/session-activity'') returns getSessionActivitySnapshot() only","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/session-runtime.js:366-372 \u2014 snapshot projects only data.phase; :176 records { phase, updatedAt: Date.now() } and the snapshot drops updatedAt","packages/web/server/lib/notifications/runtime.js:266-269 \u2014 assistantStepMeta already remembers per-message agent + modelID server-side (precedent for model/provider fields)","Design #612 + design doc files/designs/openchamber-external-observability-contract.md (fleet goal workspace) \u2014 the five contract rules this phase implements"],"acceptance":["Triage records on #524: the current snapshot shape verified against main, and which tracked in-process source supplies each phase-1 field (phase updatedAt, session-state status, assistantStepMeta-style model memory, tool state)","Either an implementation (fix) packet for #524 is enqueued referencing design #612, or #524 is labelled ready with the verified scope in an agent note","No field is specified that the server does not already track in-process (per #612 phase 1 bounds); anything needing new tracking is noted on #612 as a question, not added to #524''s scope"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/524","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/612"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Priority normal per #524: the fleet babysitter''s stall detector (developing-today/code#1192) is blocked on the last-activity field; the fix is bounded and additive, data already tracked in-process.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:524', '2026-10-28 01:47:20.008262+00', '2026-10-28 02:28:13.629487+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1625, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'triage: managed-server registry read under design #612 phase 2 (#525)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/525","title":"Managed-server registry: stable discovery of per-project OpenCode servers for external tooling","number":525,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the endpoint inside the triage timebox","any control surface (start/stop/drain) \u2014 the read stays read-only","changing the registry on-disk format or the reaper safety model","recording new fields at spawn time (open question on #612)"],"include":["triage of #525 against current main","promotion: enqueue the phase-2 implementation packet (or ready-label) referencing design #612"]},"tests":["n/a for triage; implementation tests are specified in the promoted packet (key-set/secret-absence test, ground-truth probe)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Design #612 (filed 2026-10-27 by repo-design-architect) links this issue as a phased sub-issue; gh issue list search for session-activity / managed-servers / observability returns only #524, #525, #612, #614 \u2014 no other open issue covers this work","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"There is no API read of OpenChamber''s managed OpenCode servers: the authoritative records exist (lifecycle state.json, the per-process registry dir) but external tools must scrape ps or read files that were never an interface \u2014 and state.json contains the managed password and agent-tool token, so direct file reads are a credential-exposure path.","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/opencode/managed-opencode-state.js \u2014 state.json holds pid/port/binary/fingerprint AND the managed password + agent-tool token (''the file is 0600 and never logged'')","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/managed-process-registry.js:179 \u2014 registerManagedProcess records pid, ownerPid, port, binary, runtime, startedAt, one file per process; no API reads it","Issue #525 \u2014 seven dynamic ports observed in one evening (4747, 13420, 34437, 34707, 37249, 37621, 40967); acceptance: one call returns the live list matching ss/process ground truth, stopped servers disappear within one poll cycle","Design #612 + design doc files/designs/openchamber-external-observability-contract.md \u2014 contract rules 3\u20135 govern this phase"],"acceptance":["Triage records on #525: absence of an existing registry read verified on main, and the authoritative source for each registry field (lifecycle state, managed-process registry entries, session runtime count)","Either an implementation (fix) packet for #525 is enqueued referencing design #612, or #525 is labelled ready with the verified scope in an agent note","The allowlist/secret-absence requirement is carried verbatim into the promoted scope"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/525","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/612"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Priority low per #525 itself: ergonomics for every future external tool, not a blocker. The design contract is what makes it safe to build (secret allowlist), so triage now prevents an ad-hoc unsafe read later.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:525', '2026-10-28 01:47:23.592729+00', '2026-10-28 01:53:33.34096+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1626, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'triage: observability contract docs + conformance fixture, design #612 phase 3 (#614)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/614","title":"docs(web): external observability contract documentation + paired-client conformance fixture (design #612, phase 3)","number":614,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["writing the documentation or fixture inside the triage timebox","documenting proposed (not landed) shapes as fact","any production behaviour change (phase 3 is docs + fixture/tests only)"],"include":["triage of #614 including the landed-shape dependency check on #524/#525"]},"tests":["n/a for triage"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Design #612 (filed 2026-10-27 by repo-design-architect) links this issue as a phased sub-issue; gh issue list search for session-activity / managed-servers / observability returns only #524, #525, #612, #614 \u2014 no other open issue covers this work","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Phases 1\u20132 of design #612 (#524, #525) fix two external API shapes, but nothing yet documents the shared contract for consumers or lets a paired client verify a server honours it \u2014 the absence that left #524''s probe reporting the live shape ''couldn''t be confirmed''.","evidence":["Issue #614 body \u2014 scope and acceptance filed with the design (document both reads + the five rules + observed-not-configured caveat; fixture asserts key sets, version, watcherReady semantics, secret absence, stopped-server behaviour)","Design #612 \u2014 phases 1\u20132 (#524, #525) are this phase''s inputs; their landed shapes are the document''s subject","Issue #524 body \u2014 the original probe could not confirm the live /api/session-activity shape; that documentation gap is this phase''s reason to exist"],"acceptance":["Triage records on #614 whether #524 and #525 have landed; if not, the dependency is recorded and #614 is not promoted to implementation yet","If landed: divergences between landed payloads and design #612 are listed on #614 (and #612 updated or flagged), doc location and fixture placement are named","Promotion (implementation packet or ready label) happens only with the landed-shape dependency satisfied"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/614","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/612"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Priority low: documentation/fixture phase; value is preventing the next external consumer from re-deriving the contract from source. Sequenced after #524/#525 by design.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:614', '2026-10-28 01:47:27.010256+00', '2026-10-28 08:44:07.960725+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1628, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'merge the biome/treefmt formatting fix PR #1562 for #1561', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1561","title":"id(web): biome-check + treefmt-check red on main \u2014 world-surface.test.ts array formatting (from PR #1542)","number":1561,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:12:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Any logic change to world-surface.ts or its tests","Re-litigating the #1542 merge (already on main; fix-forward only)"],"include":["Merging PR #1562 after fresh verification that biome-check and treefmt-check pass","Closing issue #1561 via the merge"]},"tests":["PR #1562 CI: biome-check pass, treefmt-check pass, test-web-unit pass"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Single fix-forward PR #1562 already exists for issue #1561 (filed 2026-10-28 by the Lane B worker that merged #1542); this task only routes its merge. No other task references #1561.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:12:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #1542 merged a biome formatting error into pkgs/id/web/src/world-surface.test.ts on main; PR #1562 carries the formatter-prescribed fix and only needs a verified-green merge.","evidence":["gh pr checks 1542 verified twice on 2026-10-28: biome-check FAIL (job 122566291227, formatter diff on sequenceGlyphs array in world-surface.test.ts) and treefmt-check FAIL on run 40611675179; merge commit 5a0173c2 is on main","Laptop fix verification: biome check --write produced exactly the one-line array collapse (4db4ab9e); biome check clean after; bunx vitest run src/world-surface.test.ts 6 passed"],"acceptance":["PR #1562 merged with biome-check and treefmt-check green (verified with fresh gh pr checks calls, twice if the first listing looks inconsistent \u2014 this fleet has seen fabricated check listings)","Issue #1561 closed by the merge","No other files changed beyond pkgs/id/web/src/world-surface.test.ts formatting"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1561","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1562","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1542"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Main is red on biome-check/treefmt-check until this merges; every subsequent id PR inherits the noise. Issue priority/normal.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1561', '2026-10-28 01:51:57.15368+00', '2026-10-28 03:40:18.917417+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1629, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix: managed-server registry read GET /api/managed-servers under design #612 phase 2 (#525)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/525","title":"Managed-server registry: stable discovery of per-project OpenCode servers for external tooling","number":525,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:50:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any control surface (start/stop/drain) \u2014 the read stays read-only","changing the registry on-disk format or the reaper safety model","recording new fields at spawn time (open question on #612, incl. VS Code parity writer)","phase 1 (#524) and phase 3 of design #612"],"include":["new GET /api/managed-servers route in the web server, served from lifecycle/registry state via existing validated readers","allowlist projection of registry/lifecycle/session-runtime fields per design #612 phase 2, with a test pinning the exact key set and secret-field absence","ground-truth probe/test: live list matches ss/process ground truth, stopped servers disappear within one poll cycle"]},"tests":["key-set/secret-absence test: response keys are exactly the allowlist; no password, token, fingerprint, or args anywhere in the payload","ground-truth probe: endpoint list matches ss/process ground truth at probe time; a stopped server disappears within one poll cycle","targeted web-server test suite for the new route (own-server complete entry, cross-instance sparse entry with explicit nulls and status unknown)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Promoted by triage task 1625 from issue #525, phase 2 of design #612; no open PR on developing-today/openchamber implements /api/managed-servers (open-PR scan 2026-10-28) and no existing registry read exists on main f77bcc1","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:50:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"There is no API read of OpenChamber''s managed OpenCode servers: the authoritative records exist (lifecycle state.json, the per-process registry dir) but external tools must scrape ps or read files that were never an interface \u2014 and state.json contains the managed password and agent-tool token, so direct file reads are a credential-exposure path.","evidence":["Triage task 1625, 2026-10-28: main f77bcc12efb5097056f4fd32eedde1aecf39747f \u2014 packages/web/server/lib/notifications/routes.js exposes /api/session-activity, /api/sessions/snapshot, /api/sessions/status etc. and no /api/managed-servers; code search for managed-servers in developing-today/openchamber returns 0","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/managed-process-registry.js:179-189 \u2014 registerManagedProcess records {pid, ownerPid, port, binary, runtime, startedAt}, one file per process in the registry dir; readAllEntries (same file, internal) is the validated reader used by the reaper; no API reads it","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/managed-opencode-state.js:29-47,76-77 \u2014 readManagedOpenCodeState validates pid/port/binary/fingerprint/password; the file holds the managed password and agent-tool token (''the file is 0600 and never logged''); readDrainingOpenCodeRecords in the same file is the validated draining-records reader","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/lifecycle.js \u2014 own-server version comes from the OpenCode health payload (classifyOpenCodeVersion / health read, not opencode --version); draining status from the draining registry built on readDrainingOpenCodeRecords; current/default directory tracked by the lifecycle (noteCurrentDirectory)","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/session-runtime.js:366 \u2014 getSessionActivitySnapshot projects the session runtime''s tracked maps; live session count for the own-server entry is derived from that runtime state, not a process scan","Design #612 rules 3-5 + agent note on #525 (2026-10-28T01:43Z): GET /api/managed-servers {version, serverTime, servers[]}; own-server entry complete (directory, port, version, status incl. draining, startedAt, live session count), cross-instance entries carry what the registry record has with null for the rest and status \"unknown\" when liveness is unverifiable"],"acceptance":["GET /api/managed-servers returns {version: 1, serverTime, servers[]} matching registry/process ground truth at probe time; stopped servers leave the list within one poll cycle (no zombies)","Own-server entry is complete (directory, port, version, status incl. draining, startedAt, live session count); cross-instance entries are sparse with explicit nulls and status \"unknown\" when liveness is unverifiable \u2014 unknown fields are null, never fabricated 0/now/dropped","Allowlist projection \u2014 no password/token/fingerprint/args: projection is an explicit allowlist \u2014 state.json holds the managed password and agent-tool token and neither they nor fingerprint/args may be reachable through this read (a test pins the key set)","Read is served from lifecycle/registry state via existing validated readers (readManagedOpenCodeState, readDrainingOpenCodeRecords, the managed-process registry reader), never a process scan; read stays read-only (no start/stop/drain control surface)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/525","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/612"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Priority low per #525 itself: ergonomics for every future external tool, not a blocker. The design contract is what makes it safe to build (secret allowlist), so building under #612 prevents an ad-hoc unsafe read later.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:525', '2026-10-28 01:52:02.588343+00', '2026-10-28 04:58:15.425756+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1630, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'docs: add the missing Custom / Other providers subsection to 9 providers.mdx mirrors (#615)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/615","title":"Docs: providers page mirrors are missing the whole \"Custom / Other providers\" subsection in 9 locales (#601 remainder at heading level 3)","number":615,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["nl and tr providers mirrors (already complete)","any other docs page or section","the pages tracked by #339/#601"],"include":["packages/docs/content/docs/{de,es,fr,ja,ko,pl,pt-br,uk,zh-cn}/providers.mdx \u2014 add the translated subsection + step-2 clause"]},"tests":["docs:validate on laptop or CI, not the sandbox","heading-count sweep at every heading level over all docs pages"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh searches for ''providers.mdx'', ''Custom Other providers'' and ''translated mirrors'' returned only #601 (projects/scheduled-tasks/walkthrough, counted ## headings only) and #339 (install/notes-todos-plans/desktop-browser, closed); neither lists providers.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"providers.mdx mirrors missing the ''Custom / Other providers'' subsection in 9 locales.","evidence":["packages/docs/content/docs/providers.mdx:18-29 \u2014 English ''### Custom / Other providers'' subsection (63 lines total)","packages/docs/content/docs/de/providers.mdx \u2014 50 lines, headings :10 -> :22 with no ###; same shape in es/fr/ja/ko/pl/pt-br/uk/zh-cn","packages/docs/content/docs/nl/providers.mdx:18 and tr/providers.mdx:18 carry the subsection \u2014 translated for some locales, never carried to the rest","Every-heading-level sweep this run over all docs pages: providers.mdx is the only remaining deficit outside #339/#601 pages"],"acceptance":["All 9 listed mirrors gain a translation of ''Custom / Other providers'' in the English position; every mirror''s heading set matches English at every level (1 #, 5 ##, 1 ###); nl/tr untouched","Step 2 of ''Connect a provider'' in those 9 mirrors restores the Other/Custom alternative","Translations follow each mirror''s existing terminology on the same page; no other sections or pages change","Heading sweep at every level over all docs pages shows no deficit outside #339/#601 pages; docs:validate passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/615","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/601","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/339"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A whole provider class (custom/OpenAI-compatible endpoints) is undocumented in 9 locales; normal priority, docs-only risk.","timebox_minutes":60}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:615', '2026-10-28 01:55:30.122454+00', '2026-10-28 02:30:32.763175+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1631, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(quota): VS Code Wafer port no longer fabricates usedPercent 0 (#616)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/616","title":"fix(quota): VS Code Wafer port fabricates usedPercent 0 when the payload omits current_period_used_percent \u2014 the #608 defect in quotaProviders.ts","number":616,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:57:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the web provider wafer.js (#608 owns it)","the deliberate overage behaviour for a present percent above 100","any other VS Code quota provider"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts fetchWaferQuota usedPercent derivation","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts first Wafer regression tests"]},"tests":["targeted VS Code quota tests (packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts) run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh searches for ''wafer vscode'' and ''wafer'' returned #608 (web-only scope and acceptance), #484 (web test coverage, closed) and other providers'' clamp issues; no issue tracks the port''s missing-percent fabrication.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:57:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"VS Code Wafer port fabricates usedPercent 0 when current_period_used_percent is absent (the #608 defect in the port).","evidence":["packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts:3280 \u2014 usedPercentRaw = toNumber(payload?.current_period_used_percent), null when absent","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts:3296-3298 \u2014 both branches apply ?? 0, identical to web wafer.js:82-84 (#608)","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.ts:3285 \u2014 no-data guard passes when counts are present and percent is null","packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts \u2014 grep for wafer/Wafer returns nothing: no port Wafer coverage"],"acceptance":["Percent absent with remaining 40 / limit 100 -> usedPercent 60 in the VS Code Wafer window","Percent absent with only overage_request_count present -> usedPercent null, not 0","Percent present cases unchanged, including overage >100 and negative clamp","Existing VS Code quota tests pass; new Wafer tests live in packages/vscode/src/quotaProviders.test.ts"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/616","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/608"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Same harm as #608 on the VS Code surface: an invented 0% used while most of the allowance is gone; normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:616', '2026-10-28 01:57:09.694817+00', '2026-10-28 02:32:20.088962+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1632, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: generatedAt parse/future freshness gates — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1564","title":"aggregator: a garbage or future-dated generatedAt is ''live'' forever \u2014 the orchestration diagnosis and fleet-feed gate never check that the timestamp parses","number":1564,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:57:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["quota-current measuredAt freshness (#1541 \u2014 separate issue, separate fix)","Snapshot record ts validation (#1540)","Changing the 90m orchestration stale threshold or the 15m feed stale threshold themselves"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/feed.ts: orchestrationSectionProblem/diagnoseOrchestrationSection/isFleetFeed generatedAt parse + future-tolerance rules","pm-stack/aggregator/src/health.ts feedAgeMs derivation if it needs the same guard","Regression tests in pm-stack/aggregator/test/orchestration.test.ts (and health.test.ts if touched)"]},"tests":["bun test pm-stack/aggregator/test/orchestration.test.ts pm-stack/aggregator/test/health.test.ts (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list search (open + all) for ''generatedAt stale future orchestration diagnosis feed freshness'' and ''future-dated'': only hit is #1541 (quota-current measuredAt freshness, different module/gate/fix surface). Backlog checked: neither lane has filed in feed.ts diagnosis; Lane A current areas (registry merge #1560, upload naming #1549) and Lane B''s own earlier areas (discovery #1552, quota-current #1541, snapshots #1540) deliberately avoided.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T01:57:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"generatedAt is validated as a string, never as a date: unparseable stamps produce NaN ages that compare as live, and future stamps clamp to age 0, so the freshness gates in feed.ts/health.ts can never fire for them.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe driving the real pm-stack/aggregator/src/feed.ts (sha256 13d18193d2fb0d1a3d562116e23cdb86f1115d377b0e9f7930154064831603f8 identical both sides; hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-feeddate/probe.ts + out.log): -10m control live, -2h control stale; ''not-a-date'' -> live/ageMs NaN/''NaNd old''; +30d -> live/ageMs 0/''fresh''; isFleetFeed(garbage)=true, isFleetFeed(+30d)=true"],"acceptance":["A section whose generatedAt does not parse diagnoses as invalid (failing check named generatedAt), not live; orchestrationSectionProblem remains the single source of truth for the gate","A section/feed stamped implausibly in the future (beyond a small pinned clock-skew tolerance) is not reported live/fresh; the tolerance is pinned in a test","isFleetFeed rejects a feed whose generatedAt does not parse; loadFeed returns null for it","feedAgeText/ageMsText can never render ''NaNd old'' for an input that reaches them","Regression tests in pm-stack/aggregator/test/orchestration.test.ts (plus health tests if buildHealth changes): garbage date, future date, existing fresh/stale controls; existing orchestration/health suites pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1564","pm-stack/aggregator/src/feed.ts:120-135","pm-stack/aggregator/src/feed.ts:165-176","pm-stack/aggregator/src/feed.ts:193-204","pm-stack/aggregator/src/feed.ts:225-227","pm-stack/aggregator/src/health.ts:229"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The orchestration diagnosis is the dashboard''s honesty backbone (#1139/#1140): it decides the stale banners on Today/Needs-you, the ''live (fleet feed)'' provenance claims, and /health''s degraded flag. One malformed or skewed publisher timestamp defeats all of them at once and presents stale tiers/goals/measurements as live readings indefinitely, with no banner and no health signal.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1564', '2026-10-28 01:58:19.108908+00', '2026-10-28 01:58:19.108908+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1634, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: fold a script''s resolved directory into its exec identity (fix #1532)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1532","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1531 \u2014 exec identity core: a script''s identity folds in its resolved directory (internal/config)","number":1532,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:22:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["daemon/pool/watch wiring changes (none required by the design; Phase 2 of #1531 covers daemon-level tests and TODO/roadmap closure)","interpreter-as-command servers and sibling-loading native binaries (open questions on #1531)","the stat/large-file branch, the missing: form, and non-stdio servers"],"include":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/config/execid.go: #! detection while streaming the hashed branch, framed directory fold-in for scripts, header caveat update","pkgs/mcpx/internal/config/execid_test.go: update the one pinned bare-hash expectation to the framed script hash; add the defining tests (cross-directory script differs, same-directory script keeps, cross-directory non-script keeps, script vs non-script same bytes differ, framing non-alias, large-file stat identity unchanged)"]},"tests":["pkgs/mcpx: go test ./internal/config/... (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)","defining tests above, incl. the framing non-alias construction and the updated TestExecIdentityFollowsTheExecutableNotTheCommandName expectation"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Implementation follow-up enqueued by triage task 1574 on issue #1532 per that packet''s instructions; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1532 is distinct from the triage task 1574 identity; no fix task for #1532 existed at enqueue time.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:22:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"ExecStamp.Identity() is bytes-only for hashed files, so a script re-pointed at a byte-identical copy in another directory keeps its old child (and the old directory''s sibling dependencies); Phase 1 folds the resolved directory into script identities under a non-aliasing framing.","evidence":["Triage task 1574 verified on current main db6f7d00 (2026-10-28): execid.go ExecStamp.Identity() hashes content (sha256:<16hex>) when regular && Size <= defaults.ExecHashMax, else stat hash; header caveat (lines ~23-27) states the bytes-only rule and the re-pointed node script caveat this phase removes for scripts","ExecStamp.Path is already the filepath.EvalSymlinks-resolved real path (ExecStamp()), so filepath.Dir(s.Path) is the resolved directory with no new resolution work","execid_test.go TestExecIdentityFollowsTheExecutableNotTheCommandName pins a #!/bin/sh script''s identity to its bare content sha256 \u2014 confirmed present on main; the design (Phase 1 section) names this as the one existing expectation Phase 1 owns updating","Design doc code-mcpx-stdio-exec-identity.md lines 120-136 + 225-230: fold the resolved directory under a distinct framing (marker + separators) so no (content, directory) pair aliases another; exact framing left to Phase 1 \u2014 settled by triage 1574 as content || 0x00 || ''mcpx:exec-dir'' || 0x00 || dir (NUL can never appear in a filesystem path, so the trailing component is unambiguous)"],"acceptance":["Cross-directory identical script (same bytes, symlink re-pointed to a copy in another directory) yields a DIFFERENT identity; same-directory identical script keeps its identity","Cross-directory identical NON-script file keeps its identity (content-only, byte-identical hash input to today)","A script and a non-script file with the same bytes have different identities","Framing non-alias: no two distinct (content, directory) pairs produce the same hash input \u2014 the marker segment is NUL-led and a filesystem path cannot contain NUL, so the trailing directory component is uniquely recoverable (test constructs near-miss pairs, e.g. content/marker boundary shifts)","Large-file (over ExecHashMax) stat identity is byte-for-byte unchanged; missing and non-stdio forms unchanged","Identity string keeps the sha256:<16 hex> form for the hashed branch; the only caller-visible change is script identities moving to the framed hash","TestExecIdentityFollowsTheExecutableNotTheCommandName updated to the framed expectation (the one existing assertion the design knowingly changes); all other existing execid/identity tests pass unmodified"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1532","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1531","pkgs/mcpx/internal/config/execid.go"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 of design #1531: gives script-based stdio servers a correct identity (re-pointed identical scripts restart into the right dependencies) with a single-implementation, low-risk change in internal/config; Phase 2 (daemon proof + TODO/roadmap closure) is gated on it.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1532', '2026-10-28 02:15:50.471443+00', '2026-10-28 04:00:11.362931+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1635, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): unreferenced footnote definitions deleted on save — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1565","title":"id(web): unreferenced footnote definitions are silently deleted on save \u2014 a definitions-only document saves as an empty file","number":1565,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:25:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing referenced-footnote round-trip behaviour (#945/#1031)","editor richSchema wiring (#1347)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs parse direction (definition preservation) and/or codec module docs","codec regression tests for orphan/mixed/definitions-only footnote definitions"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (in pkgs/id)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches this run (''footnote'' in title; ''unreferenced footnote'', ''orphan footnote'') over open+closed returned only #945/#1031 (closed, referenced-footnote handling), #1347 (editor richSchema wiring, different layer) and #1004 (link reference definitions, different construct/syntax). No issue tracks unreferenced footnote definitions.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:25:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"comrak never emits unreferenced footnote definitions as AST nodes, so the codec''s parse direction drops them and any save deletes them permanently.","evidence":["Verbatim-codec probe on main db6f7d00 (comrak 0.56), built/run on the laptop, logs hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-creator-a2/probe_out3.log: orphan-footnote-def-with-text -> PM single paragraph, save ''Hello world.\\n''; only-footnote-def -> PM empty-doc placeholder, save ''''","two-defs-one-referenced in the same probe: PM carries only the referenced definition [^a]; [^b]: unused is dropped in the same save","Layer isolation in the same probe: raw comrak parse_document (footnotes extension on) of ''[^a]: just a definition\\n'' yields zero AST children; of ''Hello.\\n\\n[^a]: orphan\\n'' yields only the Paragraph \u2014 comrak never emits the unreferenced FootnoteDefinition node"],"acceptance":["An unreferenced footnote definition survives a load/save round trip (verbatim or equivalent form), or the limitation is documented in the codec module docs and the issue closes citing it","Referenced footnote definitions (single/multi-paragraph, block children) round-trip exactly as today (#945/#1031 unchanged)","A definitions-only document does not save as an empty file under the chosen fix (or is covered by the documented limitation)","Regression tests in markdown.rs cover orphan, mixed referenced+unreferenced, and definitions-only cases","Existing web::markdown tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1565","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1004","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/945","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1031","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs commonmark_options (lines 81-91), FootnoteDefinition arm (559-575)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent data loss on a plain open/save in the codec''s flagship footnote support; a definitions-only note is wiped to an empty file.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1565', '2026-10-28 02:25:48.414488+00', '2026-10-28 02:25:48.414488+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1636, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'meta-exporter: window_duration_secs unvalidated — missing/junk duration exports a window-NaNs window as success — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1566","title":"meta-exporter: window_duration_secs is never validated \u2014 a missing/junk duration exports a ''window-NaNs'' window as a successful reading","number":1566,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Aggregator quota-gather-map changes","New window-name mappings in the aggregator"],"include":["pm-stack/meta-exporter/meta-quota-export.mjs parseSubscriptionQuota validation","pm-stack/meta-exporter/meta-quota-export.test.mjs drift cases"]},"tests":["node --test pm-stack/meta-exporter/ (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search open+closed for ''meta-exporter duration'', ''meta-quota-export'', ''window_duration_secs'': no filing; #1301 is the parent feature, not this defect.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"parseSubscriptionQuota does not validate window_duration_secs; a drifted/missing duration yields a success document with a garbage-named window instead of failing closed as unparseable.","evidence":["pm-stack/meta-exporter/meta-quota-export.mjs:67-68 contract: ''Throws on any shape drift \u2014 fail-closed, never partial zeros''","pm-stack/meta-exporter/meta-quota-export.mjs:76-90 the validated field set omits window_duration_secs; :79 reads it, :91 names the window from it unchecked","Verified this run (node, real module, main db6f7d00): missing -> [window-NaNs, weekly]; ''abc'' -> window-NaNs; -5 -> window--5s; 0 -> window-0s \u2014 all successful parses","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-gather-map.ts FILE_EXPORT_WINDOW_SECONDS knows only 5h/weekly; :144-155 pushes any named window through with windowSeconds ?? null"],"acceptance":["window_duration_secs must be finite and > 0; missing/non-numeric/zero/negative throws ExportError unparseable (exit 6) naming the field","18000 -> 5h, 3600 -> 1h, other positive -> window-<n>s naming unchanged","meta-quota-export.test.mjs gains missing/''abc''/0/negative duration cases in the shape-drift test","Success/failure document shapes and exit codes unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1566","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1301","pm-stack/meta-exporter/meta-quota-export.mjs:79","pm-stack/meta-exporter/meta-quota-export.test.mjs"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The exporter''s whole design is fail-closed so a drifted console payload can never masquerade as a reading; this one unvalidated field defeats it and injects a garbage window into quota-current while the service reports ok.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1566', '2026-10-28 02:27:11.985167+00', '2026-10-28 02:27:11.985167+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1637, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'feat(web): session-activity v1 fields — lastActivityAt, status, model/provider, toolInFlight (#524)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/524","title":"Session-activity API: expose per-session status, last-activity, model + provider for external babysitters","number":524,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing the per-session { type } field (frozen by design #612; UI and VS Code bridge consume it)","any change to /api/sessions/snapshot or /api/sessions/status","the managed-server registry (#525) and the contract docs/fixture (#614)","adding new tool tracking for toolInFlight (question recorded on #612; phase 1 ships null)","redesigning the contract \u2014 open questions live in #612"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/opencode/session-runtime.js \u2014 getSessionActivitySnapshot v1 projection (lastActivityAt, status, model/provider slots, toolInFlight, envelope version/serverTime/watcherReady as designed)","packages/web/server/lib/notifications/runtime.js \u2014 extend the assistant-step memory to retain providerID alongside modelID and expose the per-session remembered model/provider to the snapshot","packages/web/server/lib/notifications/routes.js \u2014 route-shape documentation comment at /api/session-activity","tests pinning the response key set and the null-when-unknown semantics"]},"tests":["new/updated snapshot tests pinning the v1 key set, lastActivityAt from the phase updatedAt, status passthrough, model/provider remembered incl. providerID, and null-when-unknown semantics","existing session-runtime / notifications test suites pass via CI check:changed on the PR (never run on the sandbox)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1624 as the promotion step for #524 phase 1 of design #612; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:524 is distinct from the triage task''s identity (repo-health:v1:triage:...:524). #525 (registry) and #614 (docs/fixture) are separate phases with their own packets.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"/api/session-activity exposes only the session phase as { type }; the fleet babysitter''s stall detector (developing-today/code#1192) is blocked on the missing last-activity timestamp, and status, model/provider, and tool-in-flight are absent. Design #612 phase 1 specifies the additive v1 field set; triage task 1624 verified every field''s in-process source on main ddfbc4922.","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/notifications/routes.js:287 \u2014 GET /api/session-activity returns getSessionActivitySnapshot() and nothing else (verified on main ddfbc4922)","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/session-runtime.js:366 \u2014 snapshot projects only { type: data.phase }; the phase map entry already records updatedAt at session-runtime.js:176 (setSessionActivityPhase stores { phase, updatedAt: Date.now() }) and the snapshot drops it","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/session-runtime.js:229/:285 \u2014 sessionStates map stores { status, lastUpdateAt, metadata } (busy/retry/idle), readable via getSessionState","packages/web/server/lib/notifications/runtime.js:258-269 \u2014 assistantStepMeta + lastAssistantStepBySession remember { agent, modelID } from the latest assistant message info; providerID is present on that same info (packages/web/server/lib/event-stream/translate-v2.js:244, session.step.started) but not retained today","No per-session in-process tool tracking exists in session-runtime or the notifications runtime (grep verified, triage task 1624) \u2014 toolInFlight phase-1 value is explicit null per design #612 rule 2"],"acceptance":["With a session active, /api/session-activity entries carry type (unchanged), lastActivityAt (the phase map updatedAt), status (session-state status), model/provider as { modelID, providerID } | null from the latest assistant message info, and toolInFlight as boolean | null (null in phase 1 \u2014 no tracked source exists)","Top-level version: 1 and serverTime are present, plus watcherReady with honest semantics (never a fabricated true; semantics pinned by a test)","Unknown fields are explicit nulls, never 0, ''now'', or silently dropped (design #612 rule 2); an empty watcher state is distinguishable from unknown via watcherReady","A test pins the exact response key set (top-level and per-session) so later additions stay additive-only","The response shape is documented at the route (comment on routes.js /api/session-activity) where API consumers will find it","Existing session-activity and notifications tests still pass; check:changed green on the PR (CI, per repo AGENTS.md)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/524","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/612","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1192"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The babysitter stall detector (code#1192) is blocked on lastActivityAt specifically; the field already exists in-process, so this is a small additive projection under a settled design (#612).","timebox_minutes":120}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:524', '2026-10-28 02:27:57.008938+00', '2026-10-28 02:59:26.522846+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1638, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(waiting): no total cap on the waiting pool — per-author cap is Sybil-defeated — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1567","title":"id(waiting): the waiting pool has no total cap \u2014 the per-author cap is Sybil-defeated, so one peer can make a node hold (and persist) unbounded waiting events","number":1567,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:34:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Sync protocol changes","Changes to release order or expiry semantics"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/waiting.rs WaitingLimits + hold enforcement + module doc","pkgs/id/src/event_store/ waiting restore behaviour if over-cap rows need handling","waiting pool / event-store tests for the total cap"]},"tests":["cargo test for waiting + event_store modules on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search open+closed for ''waiting pool'' and ''waiting events cap total'': no filing covers a total cap or Sybil authors.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:34:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"WaitingPool bounds held events only per author and by age; with free self-certifying author identities the total held (in memory and in on-disk waiting rows) is unbounded.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/waiting.rs:5-7 doc claim: ''Two caps bound what a peer can make a node hold'' \u2014 per-author + age only","pkgs/id/src/waiting.rs:44-61 WaitingLimits has exactly two fields: per_author, max_age_ms; defaults 256 and 7 days (:33-38)","pkgs/id/src/waiting.rs:296-322 hold() checks only waiting_count(author) >= per_author; insert/park/restore funnel through hold","pkgs/id/src/chain.rs:321+ decode verifies the header signature against the embedded author key \u2014 author identities are self-certifying and free to mint","pkgs/id/src/event_store/waiting_rows.rs:1-12 held events are mirrored to redb waiting rows on disk and restored on open"],"acceptance":["WaitingLimits gains a total cap across all authors (named default constant), enforced in hold so insert/park/restore all respect it","Refusal distinguishes total-full from author-full, or documents why one WaitRefusal variant serves both","Restore-on-open with rows over a lowered total does not brick the store; excess handling defined and tested","waiting.rs module doc updated so the stated bound is the real bound","Test: (total+1)-th held event spread across distinct authors is refused while every per-author count is below its cap; existing per-author/age tests keep passing"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1567","pkgs/id/src/waiting.rs:5","pkgs/id/src/event_store/waiting_rows.rs:1"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"An ingest-side resource bound that an attacker fully controls is not a bound: one peer can grow a node''s memory and on-disk waiting table without limit for up to 7 days per event, while the docs assert the opposite.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1567', '2026-10-28 02:29:09.522704+00', '2026-10-28 02:29:09.522704+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1639, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Small fix #1485: unify needs-order sorts on the since axis in render.ts', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1485","title":"aggregator: Needs-you ''Newest first'' sorts tier cards by lastSeenAt while ''Oldest first'' sorts by since \u2014 the two orders are not reverses, and a 30-day-old card can lead ''Newest first''","number":1485,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:32:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The preference store / effectiveNeedsOrder (tier-items.ts) \u2014 it returns the saved order correctly","Session-card ordering semantics (already consistent)","Card-state suppression derivation (#1474, different function)"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/render.ts needs-order sort axes + deadline tiebreak","pm-stack/aggregator/test/dashboard-overhaul.test.ts divergent-axis regression tests for newest and oldest"]},"tests":["bun test test/dashboard-overhaul.test.ts (via CI)","full aggregator bun test suite (via CI)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1512 is the only prior queue task for #1485 besides the triage packet itself; no fix task existed at triage completion (checked 2026-10-28T02:32:00Z); no open PR touches the render needs-order sorts","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:32:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"render.ts applies the #1456 card-order preference with mismatched axes: newest uses lastSeenAt, oldest uses since, so for tier-item cards the two orders are not reverses and ''Newest first'' ranks by last-seen rather than by how new the card is.","evidence":["Triage 1512 fresh read of main db6f7d002bc6ede3f6ca61aa706920b7b4a36930: render.ts tier cards set sinceMs=Date.parse(item.since), seenMs=Date.parse(item.lastSeenAt); newest sorts b.seenMs-a.seenMs, oldest sorts a.sinceMs-b.sinceMs, deadline tiebreaks on seenMs \u2014 mismatch verbatim","Creator probe (packet 1512 evidence, main 49e67083, Bun on laptop): NEWCARD(since 1h ago, lastSeenAt 2h ago) vs OLDCARD(since 30d ago, lastSeenAt 5m ago) -> newest [OLDCARD, NEWCARD], oldest [OLDCARD, NEWCARD] (identical, not reverses); agreeing control reverses correctly","Test gap confirmed fresh by triage 1512: dashboard-overhaul.test.ts has only a newest render test with a shared since (~:326); no oldest render test, no divergent-axis test"],"acceptance":["newest and oldest sort tier-item cards on the single sinceMs axis, so the two orders are exact reverses for the same card set","Session cards keep behaving as today (their since/lastSeenAt are the same instant)","The deadline tiebreak uses sinceMs (not seenMs), with the axis and tiebreak direction noted in a code comment at the sort site","Regression tests in pm-stack/aggregator/test/dashboard-overhaul.test.ts cover tier cards whose since and lastSeenAt orderings disagree, for both newest and oldest, plus the agreeing control","Full aggregator test suite passes in CI"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1485","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1456","pm-stack/aggregator/src/render.ts needs-order sorts (~:2302-2305 on db6f7d00)","pm-stack/aggregator/test/dashboard-overhaul.test.ts:326"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The Needs-you list is the user''s triage surface and the card order is a standing preference he set in #1456; ''Newest first'' burying genuinely new arrivals under long-waiting re-seen cards is the opposite of the control''s promise, and newest/oldest returning the same list makes the preference look broken. Fix is small (one axis + tests) with the axis decision already made in triage 1512.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1485', '2026-10-28 02:33:42.110047+00', '2026-10-28 03:41:32.616447+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1640, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Fix #1558: land PR #1242''s stranded sops-nix OpenClaw secrets on main + /run/secrets/openclaw wrapper repoint', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1242","title":"OpenClaw secrets via sops-nix (bws mirror)","number":1242,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:40:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["secrets-adjacent: changes which files the gateway reads tokens from; no secret values are handled"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1558","title":"fix(openclaw): PR #1242''s sops-nix secrets landed on a stranded feature branch \u2014 not on main, and the promised /run/secrets/openclaw wrapper repoint was never filed","number":1558,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Rotating or re-mirroring any secret values","Unrelated changes from the old feat/openclaw-summarize worktree"],"include":["Landing feat/openclaw-summarize''s 3-file #1242 change on main","home/openclaw /run/secrets/openclaw wrapper repoint","Activation verification on the OpenClaw host"]},"tests":["CI on the landing PR green","Post-merge activation check: /run/secrets/openclaw/gateway-token exists on the host and gateway service is active"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by queue worker lane D as the routing outcome of triage task 1607 for issue #1558; no open PR from feat/openclaw-summarize to main exists and no other task covers landing this change.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #1242 merged into feat/openclaw-summarize instead of main, so its sops-nix OpenClaw secrets change never landed and the promised home/openclaw wrapper repoint from ~/.secrets/openclaw/* to /run/secrets/openclaw/* was never done. Triage task 1607 re-verified all of this against fresh origin/main db6f7d002bc6ede3f6ca61aa706920b7b4a36930 on 2026-10-28.","evidence":["git merge-base --is-ancestor 53ebc06e613fde4ddaf0f916b7715ebc3038d887 origin/main FAILS (verified 2026-10-28, origin/main=db6f7d002bc6ede3f6ca61aa706920b7b4a36930)","git cat-file -e origin/main:nixos/hosts/amd-openclaw-secrets.nix FAILS (missing on main)","git diff origin/main...origin/feat/openclaw-summarize --stat = exactly 3 files: nixos/hosts/amd-openclaw-secrets.nix +22, nixos/hosts/default.nix +1, secrets/sops/common/bws.yaml re-sync (129 insertions, 103 deletions)","Branch tip of origin/feat/openclaw-summarize IS the #1242 merge commit 53ebc06e; gh pr list --head feat/openclaw-summarize (all states) returns no PR to main","origin/main:home/openclaw/default.nix line 21 and environment block (~line 80) still use ~/.secrets/openclaw/gateway-token; git grep ''run/secrets/openclaw'' origin/main returns nothing"],"acceptance":["Land the 3-file change from feat/openclaw-summarize on main via a branch + PR (PR from the branch or equivalent cherry-pick), CI green, merged per standing criteria","Repoint home/openclaw wrapper environment paths from ~/.secrets/openclaw/* to /run/secrets/openclaw/* for the gateway token (and Slack bot/app tokens if the gateway config consumes them), only after the sops secrets materialize on activation","Verify on the target host that /run/secrets/openclaw/* materialize on activation and the gateway starts with the repointed paths; close #1558 with the evidence"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1558","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1242"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Merged-looking but unlanded secrets migration: dead sops config on a stranded branch that could be cleaned up as ''merged'', losing the change; gateway still depends on manually created ~/.secrets files.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1558', '2026-10-28 02:36:59.52493+00', '2026-10-28 02:36:59.52493+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1641, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Fix #1556: mcpx client task execution for taskSupport ''required'' tools (internal/mcpclient, Phase 2 of #1554)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1556","title":"mcpx: Phase 2 of #1554 \u2014 client task execution for taskSupport \"required\" tools (internal/mcpclient)","number":1556,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing in the triage task","Relaying an upstream task''s inputRequests downstream (open question on #1554)","Phase 1 store wiring (#1555) and Phase 3 register truth-up / nix#209 closure (#1557)","Any internal/mcpserver change"],"include":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient (CallTool path, era handling, modern initialize capabilities)","Defining tests in internal/mcpclient against fake legacy + modern upstreams"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/mcpx && go test ./... via CI on the PR","New defining tests per acceptance (fake legacy + modern upstreams)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by queue worker lane D as the routing outcome of triage task 1613 for issue #1556; the issue''s own packet was the triage packet (dedupe repo-health:v1:triage:...:1556), no fix packet for 1556 exists.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx''s MCP client never task-augments a call and never declares the tasks extension upstream, so a pooled tool declared taskSupport ''required'' cannot be called the way its server demands. Triage task 1613 verified on main db6f7d00: Tool.Execution is carried raw (client.go:171-174) and read nowhere in mcpclient/pool; CallTool (client.go:1164) is a plain tools/call; no tasks/get, tasks/result, tasks/cancel or io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks references exist in internal/mcpclient or internal/pool.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/client.go:171-174 \u2014 Tool.Execution carries taskSupport raw ''Kept raw and forwarded''; git grep taskSupport over internal/mcpclient+internal/pool returns ONLY this comment","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/client.go:1164 CallTool(ctx, name, args) \u2014 plain tools/call with header-mismatch retry; receives no Tool definition and the Client struct caches no tool list (ListTools at client.go:1051 is a fresh call each time)","Only two non-test CallTool callers: internal/pool/pool.go:1051 (lease.Client().CallTool(cctx, tool, args)) and client.go:1257 (in-client wrapper) \u2014 CallTool IS the narrowest shared seam","Client.Era already distinguishes EraLegacy/EraModern (client.go:212-220); modern.go exists for the modern era path","Server-side interop reference exists: internal/mcpserver/tasks.go:148-182 already parses Execution taskSupport the same way","Issue #1556 states Phase 2 does NOT depend on Phase 1 (#1555) \u2014 no gate"],"acceptance":["SEAM (settled by triage 1613): implement inside CallTool''s path in internal/mcpclient \u2014 both callers share it, so the pool call site keeps its signature; CallTool must resolve the named tool''s taskSupport itself (add a per-Client cached tool-execution lookup, e.g. lazy ListTools snapshot; if the implementer instead changes a caller signature, justify it on #1556 per the issue''s acceptance)","Legacy era, taskSupport ''required'': send params.task, poll tasks/get at the task''s poll interval until terminal, return the tasks/result payload (related-task meta included)","Modern era: initialize declares extensions[\"io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks\"]; on a flat Task result poll tasks/get and return the DetailedTask''s inlined terminal result/error (no tasks/result in the extension)","TTL is the outer bound; context cancel/deadline sends tasks/cancel best-effort and returns the context error; a failed task surfaces its fault in the client''s existing error shapes","input_required returns a distinct NAMED error type stating the upstream task asked a question this phase does not relay (name it in the PR and on #1556)","Malformed task responses (missing {task}, wrong shape, unknown status) are call errors \u2014 never a hang, never an unbounded poll","taskSupport absent/''optional''/''forbidden'' tools follow today''s plain-call path byte-for-byte; no internal/mcpserver changes","Defining tests against fake legacy and modern upstreams (existing fake-server rig) cover: required completes via task (exact get/result sequence legacy; extension declared + inlined result modern), optional stays plain, cancel propagates, fault surfaces, input_required named error, malformed errors without hanging","Verification via CI per fleet policy: cd pkgs/mcpx && go test ./... green on the PR"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1556","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1554"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 2 of approved design #1554: pooled ''required'' taskSupport tools are uncallable through mcpx today; blocks Phase 3 (#1557) and the nix#209 client-half closure.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1556', '2026-10-28 02:40:00.472433+00', '2026-10-28 02:40:00.472433+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1642, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 1 of #1554 — inject the daemon''s one durable task store into mcpserver.Server — issue #1555', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1555","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1554 \u2014 one durable task store across MCP and /v1 (internal/tasks wiring)","number":1555,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Phase 2 client-side task execution (#1556)","Phase 3 register truth-up / nix#209 closure (#1557)","operational limits, cooperative cancel, audit logging (open questions on #1554)","changes to internal/tasks semantics or to either surface''s protocol/wire shape","injecting a store into standalone embeddings (adapter.go, openapi.go) or the CmdServe stdio shim, per the triage disposition in the body"],"include":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpserver (server.go exported store field; tasks.go tasks() uses the injected store when present)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon (ops.go: exported accessor returning the existing taskStore() instance)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli (root.go / serve.go: wire the daemon''s single store into the daemon-served MCP server at App.MCPServer())","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go (retire gap ext-tasks-durable-before-response)","defining tests from #1555: cross-surface visibility, MCP cross-connection invisibility preserved, restart durability with working-task reaping, standalone behaviour unchanged"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/mcpx && go test ./... (via CI per fleet policy)","new defining tests: cross-surface visibility, cross-connection invisibility, restart durability/reaping, standalone unchanged"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1609 for #1555 routed here per its packet instructions; dedupe key is the fix key for issue 1555, distinct from the triage key repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1555; no fix task for #1555 existed at triage completion.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx has one task-store type but two live instances: the MCP server''s private in-memory store and the daemon /v1 surface''s SQLite-backed store. Tasks are invisible across surfaces and MCP tasks die with the process, contradicting the internal/tasks package''s own stated design.","evidence":["Verified on main db6f7d00 (triage 1609): internal/mcpserver/tasks.go:32-39 tasks() lazily creates tasks.New() and sets PollInterval from Timing.resolved().TaskPoll; unexported taskStore field at internal/mcpserver/server.go:273-274; no injection seam exists","internal/daemon/ops.go:436-453 taskStore() creates the daemon''s own store via sync.Once: tasks.Open(<state>/tasks.db) with tasks.New() fallback, PollInterval from protoTasks.pollInterval at :450","internal/cli/serve.go App.MCPServer() (~:473) sets exported fields post-construction (srv.Notify :475, srv.Passthrough :477, srv.Timing incl. TaskPoll already read from protoTasks.pollInterval) \u2014 the wiring style the new seam follows","internal/cli/root.go:331-351: daemon.NewServer(...) and srv.MCP = &lazyMCP{app: a} are built in the same process, so the daemon-served MCP server can receive the daemon''s store","Standalone constructions verified: internal/cli/adapter.go:195 mcpserver.New(nil, ...) and internal/cli/openapi.go:90 mcpserver.New(nil, \"mcpx\", version) \u2014 no store, behaviour must stay unchanged","internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go:112 Gap ext-tasks-durable-before-response: ''the task store is an in-memory map; a task does not survive the daemon''; internal/tasks/tasks.go:245 reaps a working task on reload to Failed with ''daemon restarted before task completion'' and its header states the one-store design intent"],"acceptance":["mcpserver.Server accepts an injected *tasks.Store via an exported field set in App.MCPServer(); exactly one store instance exists per daemon; injected store is used by Server.tasks() with no lazy creation","Cross-surface test: a task started through the MCP surface is visible via the daemon store (Get/List/result) under the same id, and a daemon-side task is reachable through the same shared instance","Visibility preserved: MCP connection B cannot get/list/cancel connection A''s owned task; /v1-started tasks (no MCP owner) are not listed by any MCP connection (legacy list requires an owner match)","Restart durability test: a terminal MCP-started task is still readable after the store is closed and reopened from the same tasks.db; a task that was working at close reloads as Failed with ''daemon restarted before task completion''","Standalone construction (no injected store: adapter.go, openapi.go, stdio shim per the triage disposition) behaves exactly as today; existing mcpserver task tests pass unmodified in behaviour","PollInterval for the shared store comes from the single named settings source protoTasks.pollInterval, stated in the PR body","Gap ext-tasks-durable-before-response removed from internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go","No protocol/wire changes on either surface; no changes to internal/tasks semantics; full mcpx suite green via CI (cd pkgs/mcpx && go test ./...)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1555","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1554","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/209","triage verdict on #1555 by repo-worker-code (queue task 1609)"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 of design #1554 closes the oldest structural item in nix#209 (TASK-27/TASK-20) and makes MCP tasks durable; Phase 3 (#1557) is gated on it. Triage (task 1609) confirmed the scope is independently landable as scoped.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1555', '2026-10-28 02:40:20.705885+00', '2026-10-28 08:04:07.281603+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1643, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #666: reject hour-24 date-times in Form.isDateTime and ModelRouteLimits.parseAbsoluteTime', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/666","title":"fix(core): date-time validators accept hour 24 \u2014 ''2026-01-01T24:00:00Z'' passes Form validation and parseAbsoluteTime but denotes Jan 2","number":666,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:41:58Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Non-ISO Date.parse forms (keep the existing lenient behaviour)","ModelRouteSchedule.minutesOf (already range-checks hours > 23, #517)"],"include":["packages/core/src/form.ts isDateTime time-part validation","packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts parseAbsoluteTime time-part validation","Regression tests in packages/core/test/form.test.ts and packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/form.test.ts test/model-route-limits.test.ts (via CI, from packages/core)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''24:00'', ''hour 24'', ''date-time'' on 2026-10-28: #656/#658 covered the date part only; no issue covers the hour-24 time-part rollover in either validator.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:41:58Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"isDateTime and parseAbsoluteTime round-trip only the ISO date components; an hour of 24 rolls the parsed instant into the next day while the written date validates, so both validators accept a date-time that denotes a different day.","evidence":["Laptop probe (node, verbatim copies of isDateTime and parseAbsoluteTime from main 205db4ec10): ''2026-01-01T24:00:00Z'' -> isDateTime true, parseAbsoluteTime 2026-01-02T00:00:00.000Z; ''2026-12-31T24:00:00Z'' -> 2027-01-01; ''2026-02-28T24:00:00Z'' -> 2026-03-01; control ''2026-02-30T10:00:00Z'' correctly rejected by both","Primitive check: new Date(''2026-01-01T25:00:00Z'') and minute/second 60 are Invalid in V8; only hour exactly 24 rolls","RFC 3339 time-hour is 00-23, so hour 24 is outside the Form date-time format"],"acceptance":["Form.validateAnswer rejects ''2026-01-01T24:00:00Z'' (and +05:00 / year-boundary forms) for a date-time field","ModelRouteLimits.parseAbsoluteTime returns undefined for hour-24 ISO values; consumers (parseQuotaReset, QuotaSnapshot, MessagingTemplate.parseTime) inherit the rejection","Valid boundary times still pass: T23:59:59Z, T00:00:00Z, 2024-02-29T23:59:59Z","Regression tests added in packages/core/test/form.test.ts and packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts; CI green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/666","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/656","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/609","packages/core/src/form.ts:374-389 isDateTime","packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts:54-68 parseAbsoluteTime"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Same rollover class the fleet has been closing parser by parser (#471, #502, #609, #647, #655, #656); hour 24 is the last unguarded component and it silently shifts a form answer or a quota reset by a full day. Fix is small and mirrors the existing round-trip pattern.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:666', '2026-10-28 02:42:34.050675+00', '2026-10-28 03:49:57.479462+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1644, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: future-dated freshness — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1568","title":"aggregator: a future-dated read is ''today'' forever until its date passes \u2014 derive freshness() has no upper bound, so one skewed measuredAt pins a hub card fresh for weeks","number":1568,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:50:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["quota-current entryState freshness (#1541)","fleet-feed/orchestration generatedAt diagnosis (#1564)","saas-extract measuredAt extraction discipline (the freshness fix must hold for any future stamp, whatever its source)"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/derive.ts freshness(): future-stamp handling in both branches, with a named skew tolerance","render.ts freshnessStamp wording for future stamps if triage chooses an explicit state","Regression tests for future stamps in usage.test.ts / render freshness tests"]},"tests":["bun test test/usage.test.ts (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''freshness'', ''future-dated'', ''ageDays'': no filing covers derive.ts freshness(). Adjacent #1541 is quota-current entryState (gatherer entries, window replacement) and #1564 is feed/orchestration generatedAt \u2014 different functions and fix surfaces; neither touches derive freshness or its render callers.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:50:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"derive freshness() has no upper bound on measuredAt: future stamps clamp to age 0 and never go stale until cadenceDays after their future date.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe with the real derive.ts (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneA-freshness/probe.ts + out.log): at fixed now 2026-10-27T12:00:00Z cadence 7 \u2014 controls correct; future +1d/+30d/+365d all {stale:false, ageDays:0}; +30d stamp stale only at +38d","Code read on main db6f7d00: derive.ts:862/:867 Math.max(0,...) clamps; render.ts freshnessStamp :1651-1659 renders ageDays 0 as ''today''; saas-extract.ts:628/:651-652 freshestDate fallback can supply a future section date as measuredAt"],"acceptance":["A measuredAt in the future beyond the triage-pinned skew tolerance is never ageDays 0/''today'' with stale:false \u2014 it is stale or carries an explicit future/invalid state the render surfaces","Rule applies to both date-only and datetime branches of freshness()","Controls unchanged: yesterday = 1d/not stale at cadence 7, older-than-cadence stale, garbage/null stay {stale:true, ageDays:null}","Tests pin +1d/+30d/+365d future stamps in both forms and the tolerance boundary","freshnessStamp does not render a future stamp as ''today'' without a stale/future indication"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1568","pm-stack/aggregator/src/derive.ts:855-868","pm-stack/aggregator/src/render.ts:1651-1659","pm-stack/aggregator/src/saas-extract.ts:628","pm-stack/aggregator/test/usage.test.ts:266-270"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"freshness() is the stale-badge/age mechanism for every SaaS/PAYG hub card; a future stamp (reachable from a renewal date in a section without a Last-checked bullet, or a typo''d year) certifies an aging read as ''today'' for weeks to a year, defeating the dashboard''s dated-read honesty rule.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1568', '2026-10-28 02:42:40.279439+00', '2026-10-28 02:42:40.279439+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1646, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(quota): stop Cursor on-demand fabricating exhaustion when remaining is absent (#622)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/622","title":"fix(quota): Cursor on-demand window fabricates 100% used / $0.00 remaining when the payload omits the remaining amount","number":622,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["enterprise on_demand path via GetTeamSpend / buildEnterpriseWindows","billing_cycle / auto / api windows","VS Code quotaProviders.ts cursor path (it does not build an individual on_demand window)"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cursor.js buildWindows on_demand + plan_limit label","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cursor.test.js regression tests"]},"tests":["targeted Cursor quota tests (packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cursor.test.js) run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for ''cursor on_demand remaining'', ''spendLimitUsage'' and ''cursor remaining'' returned no covering issue; tracked Cursor issues are windowSeconds (#495/#506/#574) and percent clamping (#517/#569), different defects.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T02:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Cursor on-demand window fabricates 100% used / $0.00 remaining when the payload omits the remaining amount.","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cursor.js:270 \u2014 remaining = toNumber(individualRemaining) ?? toNumber(pooledRemaining) ?? 0","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cursor.js:222-228 \u2014 percentFromSpend returns null when remaining is null (the sibling judgement)","packages/web/server/lib/quota/providers/cursor.js:264 \u2014 plan_limit label falls back to ''$0.00'' when remaining is absent","Laptop probes this run (~/git/fleet/probe-cursor-ondemand): limit-only payload -> on_demand usedPercent 100 / ''$0.00 remaining of $20.00''; control -> 25% / $15.00; plan_limit limit-only -> usedPercent null but label ''$0.00 remaining of $20.00''","cursor.test.js contains no spendLimitUsage / individualRemaining coverage (grep empty)"],"acceptance":["on_demand with a limit but neither individualRemaining nor pooledRemaining does not report 100% used or a $0.00-remaining label (usedPercent null or window omitted)","plan_limit label makes no remaining claim when planUsage.remaining is absent; a reported remaining still labels normally","Reported remaining behaviour unchanged: 1500/2000 -> 25% and ''$15.00 remaining of $20.00''; reported 0 -> 100%; pooled fallback order preserved","cursor.test.js gains spendLimitUsage regression tests for the missing-remaining, present-remaining, and zero-remaining cases","Enterprise on_demand path (GetTeamSpend) untouched; existing Cursor quota tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/622","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/608","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/517"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Fabricated quota data on a primary Usage surface: a limit-without-remaining payload reads as fully exhausted, which can push a user to stop work or buy credit they still have. Same fabrication class as #608; normal priority.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:622', '2026-10-28 02:59:02.874525+00', '2026-10-28 04:52:08.060005+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1647, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(security): validate the login rate-limit env vars (#624)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/624","title":"fix(security): login rate-limit env vars are judged by bare Number(...) || default \u2014 a negative value locks out after one failure, 1e3 disables the limit","number":624,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:01:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["rate-limit window, lockout, and cleanup durations","the shared password/passkey attempt budget design","session TTL parsing (readSessionTtlMs, already validated)"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/ui-auth/ui-auth.js env parsing for the two RATE_LIMIT vars (+ exported helper)","packages/web/server/lib/ui-auth tests for the helper"]},"tests":["targeted ui-auth tests run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for ''ui-auth rate'', ''login rate limit'', ''OPENCHAMBER_RATE_LIMIT'' and ''rate limit env'' returned no covering issue.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:01:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Login rate-limit env vars are judged by bare Number(...) || default: negative locks out after one failure, 1e3 disables the limit, fractional values pass through.","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/ui-auth/ui-auth.js:34 \u2014 RATE_LIMIT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = Number(process.env.OPENCHAMBER_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_ATTEMPTS) || 10","packages/web/server/lib/ui-auth/ui-auth.js:37 \u2014 RATE_LIMIT_NO_IP_MAX_ATTEMPTS = Number(process.env.OPENCHAMBER_RATE_LIMIT_NO_IP_MAX_ATTEMPTS) || 3","packages/web/server/lib/ui-auth/ui-auth.js:19-24 \u2014 readSessionTtlMs in the same file validates finite + > 0 and rounds; fs/routes.js:126-146 and guests/upload.js:11-15 env readers do the same","Laptop probe this run: env=-5 -> 401 limit=-5 then 429 on attempt 2; unset -> limit 10, remaining 10/9/8; env=1e3 -> limit 1000","ui-auth.test.js / session-cookie.test.js contain no RATE_LIMIT reference (grep empty)"],"acceptance":["Both OPENCHAMBER_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_ATTEMPTS and OPENCHAMBER_RATE_LIMIT_NO_IP_MAX_ATTEMPTS are parsed by a validated positive-integer helper; negative, fractional, and non-numeric values fall back to 10 and 3","With a rejected value, login lockout happens after the default number of failures and X-RateLimit-Limit reports the default","A valid value (e.g. 5) is honoured for both vars","Tests pin valid, negative, fractional, and non-numeric inputs for the helper (exported, like readSessionTtlMs)","Unset behaviour byte-identical; no change to window, lockout, cleanup, or the shared password/passkey budget"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/624","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/604"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Operator-set env vars with safe defaults, so low priority \u2014 but the misjudged value controls the login brute-force budget / a total login lockout, and the fix is a small validated-helper swap consistent with every sibling env reader.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:624', '2026-10-28 03:02:07.69876+00', '2026-10-28 03:43:17.525967+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1648, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Routing policy alignment: produce the fleet-tier x OpenChamber-category mapping doc for #1272 (proposals only)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1272","title":"Routing policy alignment: map OpenChamber routing categories to the fleet''s Workhorse-first tiers + POOL MAP gates","number":1272,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:05:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Editing ~/.config/openchamber/routing.json or any live binding (Drew''s approval required)","Changing the POOL MAP / provider-quota-registry.md policy itself","Dispatcher (#1187) or pilot (#1191) implementation work"],"include":["Goal workspace document files/designs/code-routing-policy-alignment.md with the mapping table, per-binding pool + quota source, conflict list with proposed corrected bindings or keep-because reasons","A comment on epic #1234 linking the document","A closing comment on #1272 linking the document and summarising the proposals"]},"tests":["Every live binding in the document re-verified against the laptop routing.json at write time (cite the read timestamp)","Every pool named in the document exists in provider-quota-registry.md with a quota source, or is explicitly flagged unattributed"],"title":"Routing policy alignment: produce the fleet-tier x OpenChamber-category mapping doc for #1272 (proposals only)","dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1288 on #1272 (2026-10-28): issue open with no live follow-up task; gh issue search for routing mapping found only #1272 itself and its epic #1234; no existing mapping document in the goal workspace files/designs/.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:05:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"OpenChamber''s routing categories (live laptop routing.json, verified 2026-10-28) and the fleet POOL MAP disagree in at least three places (trivial defaults to the watched Antigravity pool; implement routes a Meta model through opencode-go, an unattributed pool; hard defaults Opus to high), and no mapping document exists that dispatch (#1187) or pilot #1191 can rely on.","evidence":["Triage task 1288 verdict on #1272 (comment 6459550737): live routing.json read fresh from the laptop 2026-10-28T03:04Z matches the issue snapshot; conflict table vs the current POOL MAP (provider-quota-registry.md, incl. the 2026-10-27 retirement of the >=85% caution zone)","POOL MAP: DeepSeek Flash high is the default workhorse; Opus high only for very complex design; the OpenCode meta provider is the only sanctioned door to the Meta pool; measurement gate requires a quota read <=60 min old per pool"],"acceptance":["Mapping table + conflict list exist in files/designs/code-routing-policy-alignment.md and are linked from epic #1234 and from #1272","Each conflict has a proposed corrected binding or an explicit keep-because with the reason recorded","The document states the current measurement gate (quota read <=60 min; pools used to 100%, closed at a known 100%) - not the retired >=85% zone quoted in the issue body","routing.json is unchanged by this task"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1272","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1234","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1272#issuecomment-6459550737"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The dispatcher (#1187) and pilot #1191 will route by one of these systems; until the mapping exists they route by accident, and one live category already draws on an unattributed pool.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1272', '2026-10-28 03:05:56.382758+00', '2026-10-28 03:05:56.382758+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1650, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Reconcile OpenChamber scheduled tasks: encode the producer-only rule in the lifecycle protocol (#1273 follow-up)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1273","title":"Reconcile OpenChamber scheduled-tasks with the fleet queue: one scheduling system of record","number":1273,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:13:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Building the producer bridge (an OpenChamber scheduled task that enqueues packets) - a separate implementation task if Drew wants it","Deleting or disabling OpenChamber''s scheduled-task feature","Changing any live scheduled task (inventory is empty; none exist to change)"],"include":["A section in files/agent-lifecycle-protocol-2026-10-25.md (goal workspace): OpenChamber scheduled tasks are producer-only; the monitor duty to inventory laptop project scheduled-task stores and treat any entries as external holders in the tracker","A closing comment on #1273 linking the protocol section; a link from epic #1234"]},"tests":["Protocol doc section names the producer-only rule, the single system of record, and the monitor''s inventory duty with the store path verified in triage","Re-read the laptop project stores at write time; if scheduledTasks is no longer empty, record the actual entries in the doc''s inventory note instead of ''none''"],"title":"Reconcile OpenChamber scheduled tasks: encode the producer-only rule in the lifecycle protocol (#1273 follow-up)","dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1289 on #1273 (2026-10-28): issue open, no live follow-up task, protocol doc has no OpenChamber scheduled-tasks section (grep verified at triage).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:13:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"OpenChamber has its own per-project scheduled tasks that can fire sessions directly, invisible to the fleet queue''s lifecycle protocol - a double-assignment surface. Triage (task 1289) verified the inventory is empty today and chose the shape: scheduled tasks are producer-only (enqueue packets, never start repo work), with the fleet monitor treating any that appear as external holders until a producer bridge exists. The decision is not yet encoded anywhere the monitor or workers read.","evidence":["Triage task 1289 verdict on #1273 (comment 6459600785): laptop project stores ~/.config/openchamber/projects/*.json for /home/user and /home/user/git/code both carry scheduledTasks: [] (read fresh 2026-10-28T03:12Z); no loop files in OpenChamber config/data dirs","Phase 3 producer framing approved by Drew 2026-10-26 (goal guide): producers enqueue repo-task/v1 packets; the queue + lifecycle protocol is the single scheduling system of record"],"acceptance":["Lifecycle protocol doc contains the #1273 section (producer-only rule + monitor external-holder duty) and #1273 links to it","Epic #1234 has a comment linking the decision","No OpenChamber configuration or scheduled task was created, edited, or deleted by this task"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1273","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1234","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1273#issuecomment-6459600785"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The double-assignment surface is latent today (empty inventory) - encoding the rule now is cheap; encoding it after someone adds a scheduled task is a cleanup.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1273', '2026-10-28 03:08:35.165095+00', '2026-10-28 03:08:35.165095+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1651, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: regenerate buffer-backup bun.lock for @types/node 26 and gate the lock-sync check (issue #998)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["lockfile-regeneration"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/998","title":"buffer-backup: bun.lock drifted again on the first Renovate bump after #781 \u2014 @types/node 26 in package-lock, 24 in bun.lock, and no CI runs the lock-sync check","number":998,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Reverting the @types/node 26 bump","Other packages'' lockfiles"],"include":["pkgs/buffer-backup/bun.lock regeneration via bun install (laptop)","Automated gate for the lock-sync check on pkgs/buffer-backup/** changes"]},"tests":["python3 pkgs/buffer-backup/check-lock-sync.py exits 0","bun x tsc -p ./ compiles in pkgs/buffer-backup after regeneration"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search ''buffer-backup lock'' / ''check-lock-sync bun.lock'' returned #781 (closed, original drift) and #997 (closed ledger for PR #980) \u2014 neither tracks the post-#980 recurrence or the missing CI gate (searched 2026-10-28)","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"bun.lock was not regenerated for the @types/node 26 Renovate bump, and the lock-sync guard runs in no automated gate.","evidence":["Merge commit 1d8dead (PR #980) changed only pkgs/buffer-backup/package.json and package-lock.json; bun.lock untouched","On main 1d8dead: python3 pkgs/buffer-backup/check-lock-sync.py exits 1 \u2014 ''@types/node: package-lock.json resolves 26.6.5, bun.lock resolves 24.19.2''","pkgs/buffer-backup/flake.nix buildPhase uses bun.lock only (bun install --frozen-lockfile); checks.lock-sync exists only in the sub-flake (flake.nix:72)","No workflow references buffer-backup: .github/workflows/ has only branch-cleanup.yml, mcpx-nixbuild.yml, opencode.yml; root flake.nix does not include the sub-flake check"],"acceptance":["python3 pkgs/buffer-backup/check-lock-sync.py exits 0; @types/node resolves to the same version in bun.lock and package-lock.json","bun install --frozen-lockfile + bun x tsc -p ./ (or the sub-flake build) still compiles on the laptop or in CI","The lock-sync check runs automatically for changes under pkgs/buffer-backup/** \u2014 a lockfile-only change that desyncs the locks fails visibly","No dependency other than @types/node (and its bun.lock knock-ons) changes in the regeneration"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/998","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/781","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/997"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Main currently fails its own lock-sync check and the shipped bun/nix build silently compiles against stale @types/node 24 while the npm path uses 26 \u2014 the exact silent divergence #781 was meant to end.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:998', '2026-10-28 03:16:25.763029+00', '2026-10-28 03:25:29.929552+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1652, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Triage: add deterministic partial-tree regression test for NoteEditor first-render fix (issue #627)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/553","title":"fix(notes): format the whole note on first render","number":553}],"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/627","title":"test(notes): PR #553''s first-render parse fix has no deterministic partial-tree regression test","number":627,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:30:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing NoteEditor production behaviour","Other editors'' live preview"],"include":["packages/ui/src/components/session/project-context/NoteEditor.test.tsx (or a unit test of the live-preview decoration plugin)"]},"tests":["New partial-tree test passes on main and fails on pre-#553 code","Existing NoteEditor tests pass"],"title":"Triage: add deterministic partial-tree regression test for NoteEditor first-render fix (issue #627)","dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for NoteEditor/ensureSyntaxTree returned only closed #534; no open issue tracks a partial-tree regression test","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:30:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"PR #553''s first-render parse fix has no deterministic regression test for the partial-syntax-tree case it fixes.","evidence":["PR #553 (head 16b49479) changed only NoteEditor.tsx (+23/-3) and DOCUMENTATION.md \u2014 no test file","Current main 763c773b (gh api contents): NoteEditor.tsx:91 ensureSyntaxTree(state, state.doc.length, PARSE_TIMEOUT_MS) ?? syntaxTree(state); PARSE_TIMEOUT_MS=200 at :66; ViewPlugin rebuilds when syntaxTree changes","NoteEditor.test.tsx on main has exactly 2 tests, both mounting BODY of 45 chars (''## Release\\n- push the **tag**\\n- check `changelog`''), which parses completely on first pass","Dedupe: gh search issues ''NoteEditor'' / ''ensureSyntaxTree'' returned only closed #534 (the original bug)"],"acceptance":["A deterministic test presents a partial initial syntax tree (near-3000-char note or stubbed/delayed parse) and asserts tail markers are hidden / bullets drawn on first render without a keystroke","The test fails against the pre-#553 buildDecorations and passes on current main","Existing NoteEditor.test.tsx tests keep passing"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/627","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/553","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/534"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Low: a test-coverage gap for an already-fixed UI race; worth pinning before a refactor silently reintroduces it.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:627', '2026-10-28 03:25:52.762566+00', '2026-10-28 04:53:03.00474+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1653, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'Triage #623: managed-servers own-server sessionCount includes isolated-space sessions', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/623","title":"Managed-servers read: own-server sessionCount includes isolated-space sessions","number":623,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Implementing the spaceId plumbing in this triage task","Unrelated managed-servers work (issue #525 / PR #619)"],"include":["Issue #623 and its direct follow-ups","packages/web/server session watcher / sessionRuntime / lifecycle.js counting path (triage read only)"]},"tests":["Per the worked issue body"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Full agent.tasks read this run (516 rows, all queues/statuses): no dedupe key names openchamber issue 623; the queue/queued label on the issue is the work order this packet satisfies.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Own-server sessionCount in GET /api/managed-servers can include isolated-space sessions: space identity (spaceId) is not retained through the watcher/session-runtime path, so getActiveSessionCount() counts space sessions against the host server.","evidence":["Issue #623 body: session watcher subscribes with { spaces: true }; packages/web/server/index.js forwards every translated payload into the same sessionRuntime without retaining spaceId; getActiveSessionCount() is used by getManagedServersSnapshot in packages/web/server/lib/opencode/lifecycle.js","Found by Codex review on PR #619 (queue task 1629, issue #525); the other three Codex P2 findings on #619 were fixed in commit 14ec09ea0, this one was split out because it needs the spaceId plumbing","Fleet monitor reconciliation 2026-10-28T03:30Z: issue carries queue/queued but a full agent.tasks read (all queues, all statuses) contains no task for openchamber issue 623 \u2014 orphaned work order"],"acceptance":["Triage confirms the counting path on current main and records the verified scope on issue #623","A follow-up implementation packet is enqueued against issue #623 (host entry counts only its own sessions, with a test covering a busy space session not inflating the host count), OR the issue is closed with evidence it is already fixed","Issue #623 labels mirror the resulting queue state"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/623","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/525","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/619"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Issue carries priority/low on GitHub; it is a correctness bug in a registry count surfaced to users, split out of an in-flight PR review \u2014 triage at the standard priority keeps it from sitting ownerless.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:623', '2026-10-28 03:27:20.858885+00', '2026-10-28 03:55:53.897339+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1654, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(encryption): welcome Reassembly has no size bound — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1577","title":"id(encryption): welcome Reassembly has no size bound \u2014 one chunk may exceed the frame payload cap, and a forged chunk stream buffers without limit","number":1577,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:27:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Signing chunks or any wire-format change","Changes to split() chunking behaviour for genuine welcomes"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/encryption/welcome.rs Reassembly::push bounds + WelcomeError variants + module doc","pkgs/id/src/encryption/tests.rs pinning tests for the new refusals"]},"tests":["cargo test for the encryption module on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search open+closed for ''welcome chunk reassembly'', ''Reassembly'', and ''chunk unbounded'': no filing covers a receive-side size bound for welcome chunks (only unrelated hit was lab-ops-hub #532).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:27:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Welcome Reassembly enforces the split side''s frame contract only as a courtesy: receive side accepts oversized chunks and unbounded totals, buffering without limit.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/encryption/welcome.rs:146-168 split() caps payload at frame_cap - CHUNK_HEADER_BYTES; CHUNK_PAYLOAD_BYTES = MAX_FRAME_BYTES - 256 (:32)","pkgs/id/src/encryption/welcome.rs:175-206 Reassembly::push checks digest/sequence/consistency only \u2014 no chunk size or total size check; payload Vec::extend_from_slice grows unbounded","Probe on laptop, verbatim welcome.rs from main dd9eb979 (original sha256 fabcbe9a0fb284c79efa01c08850c40350213f3d6b2eb7a71a7cf252055c1301): CASE1 single 1,113,856-byte chunk push -> Ok(None); CASE2 512 forged chunks x 64 KiB, total = u32::MAX, all accepted, 32 MiB buffered, no error; controls OK (log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-welcome/out.log)","The chunk check is Hash::digest of the chunk''s own bytes (welcome.rs:158, :176) \u2014 unkeyed, so a sender mints valid checks for arbitrary bytes"],"acceptance":["Reassembly::push refuses a chunk whose payload exceeds CHUNK_PAYLOAD_BYTES with a new WelcomeError variant, before buffering it","The reassembly refuses a declared total / implied reassembled size above a named maximum welcome size at the first chunk, with a distinct error","Tests: oversized single chunk refused; over-max declared total refused on chunk 0; genuine above-frame-cap welcome round-trip still reassembles; existing altered/out-of-sequence/other-welcome tests keep passing","welcome.rs module doc states the receive-side bounds alongside the split-side ones"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1577","pkgs/id/src/encryption/welcome.rs:175","pkgs/id/src/frames.rs:20"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The reassembly buffers sender-controlled bytes before the envelope is decoded or authenticated; size is the one resource a sender fully controls, and it is the only refusal the module does not make as chunks arrive. When the join flow is wired, one peer grows a joiner''s memory without limit using individually well-formed frames.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1577', '2026-10-28 03:27:53.18275+00', '2026-10-28 03:27:53.18275+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1656, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'triage(security): pin branch-cleanup actions/checkout (#628)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/581","title":"ci: add stale-branch cleanup workflow (dry-run by default)","number":581,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:29:51Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/628","title":"fix(security): branch-cleanup workflow''s actions/checkout is the only unpinned action \u2014 mutable @v4 tag in a contents:write workflow (also in code and opencode)","number":628,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:29:51Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any change to candidate rules, dry-run latch, or schedule"],"include":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml checkout pin in openchamber, code, and opencode"]},"tests":["grep verification across .github/workflows/ in each repo (no local build needed)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches in openchamber for branch-cleanup / checkout pin returned no covering issue (only unrelated #624); code and opencode searches for branch-cleanup returned no covering open issue; dezren39/nix#984 covered only the nix repo instance and is COMPLETED/closed.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:29:51Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"branch-cleanup.yml''s actions/checkout@v4 is the repo''s only mutable-tag action, in a contents:write live daily workflow; identical in code and opencode.","evidence":["PR #581 commit 933934e9 added .github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml with actions/checkout@v4 at line 33","Current main 763c773b: 34 other actions/checkout references are SHA-pinned to 3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1; branch-cleanup.yml:33 is the sole bare-tag exception (grep verified)","Workflow permissions contents:write + pull-requests:read (lines 20-22); BRANCH_CLEANUP_LIVE=true via gh variable list (set 2026-10-27T18:31:22Z); daily cron line 5","developing-today/code and developing-today/opencode current main (gh contents API): branch-cleanup.yml:33 also actions/checkout@v4"],"acceptance":["branch-cleanup.yml in openchamber uses actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1 (or a newer verified SHA), not a mutable tag","Same pin applied at branch-cleanup.yml:33 in developing-today/code and developing-today/opencode, referencing openchamber#628","grep for bare-tag actions/checkout@v across .github/workflows/ returns no hits in any of the three repos","No other workflow behavior changes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/628","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/581","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/984"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Privileged (contents:write) live daily workflow executing a mutable action tag while the whole repo convention is SHA pinning; a re-pointed tag is a supply-chain foothold. High priority, xs fix.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:628', '2026-10-28 03:31:53.16424+00', '2026-10-28 05:08:14.996321+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1657, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'triage(ci): protect open-PR bases in branch-cleanup (#629)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/581","title":"ci: add stale-branch cleanup workflow (dry-run by default)","number":581,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:29:51Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/629","title":"fix(ci): live daily branch-cleanup protects open-PR heads but not open-PR bases \u2014 deleting a stacked PR''s base would close it (also in code and opencode)","number":629,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:29:51Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any change to inactivity window, solely-behind test, deletion cap, or schedule"],"include":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml protected-set construction in openchamber, code, and opencode"]},"tests":["dry-run workflow dispatch or shell-level exercise of the protected-set logic; no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches in openchamber for branch cleanup / base / stacked returned no covering issue; code and opencode searches likewise; dezren39/nix#985 covered only the nix instance and is COMPLETED/closed.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:29:51Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Live daily branch-cleanup protects open-PR heads but not bases; a solely-behind inactive stacked-PR base would be deleted, closing that PR. Identical in code and opencode.","evidence":["PR #581 commit 933934e9: branch-cleanup.yml:75 fetches only headRefName; is_open_pr_head lines 78-88 is the only PR protection","Current main 763c773b line 75 unchanged; BRANCH_CLEANUP_LIVE=true (gh variable list, set 2026-10-27T18:31:22Z); daily cron line 5 (27 14 * * *)","All current open PRs base=main (verified via gh pr list), so the risk is latent until a PR is stacked on a non-main base","developing-today/code and developing-today/opencode current main (gh contents API): branch-cleanup.yml:75 also heads-only"],"acceptance":["branch-cleanup.yml protected set includes open-PR baseRefName as well as headRefName in openchamber","Same protection in developing-today/code and developing-today/opencode, referencing openchamber#629","Dry-run output names base-protected skips (e.g. SKIP open-pr-base)","Run still fails before any deletion when the open-PR list cannot be read; other candidate rules unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/629","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/581","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/985"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Latent: no open PR currently uses a non-main base, but the workflow is live and daily and stacked PRs are routine in this fleet; deleting a base closes the PR and loses its review/CI state. Normal priority, xs fix.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/openchamber:issue:629', '2026-10-28 03:32:00.013894+00', '2026-10-28 03:46:43.005701+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1658, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): navigation/partial cross-slot supersession — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1578","title":"id(web): a partial issued before a navigation still writes into the new page \u2014 #1462''s supersession slots never interact, so a stale search/tags refresh overwrites the navigated-to list","number":1578,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:45:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["navigate-vs-navigate and same-target partial-vs-partial semantics (already correct from #1462)","the tags WebSocket lifecycle itself (it is global by design)","server-side partial rendering"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/navigation.ts: a page-generation guard (or equivalent cross-slot invalidation) covering both issue orders","pkgs/id/web/src/navigation.test.ts: cross-case regression tests (partial-then-navigate, navigate-then-partial, reverse-order control)"]},"tests":["bunx vitest run src/navigation.test.ts (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open + closed) for ''navigation fetchPartial supersede'' and ''partial navigation stale'': only #1462 (CLOSED by PR #1550) \u2014 it covers navigate-vs-navigate and partial-vs-partial within one page; the cross-slot navigate-vs-partial interaction is untested there and unfixed on current main. #1578 is filed as its follow-up remainder, cross-linked both ways.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:45:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"navigation.ts supersession has no cross-slot rule: a fetchPartial from a previous page generation writes into the navigated-to page''s same-named target.","evidence":["Laptop Bun probe with the real navigation.ts (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneA-navcross/probe.ts + out.log): partial in flight -> navigateTo resolves and swaps #main -> stale partial resolves -> new page''s #file-list-content replaced by stale ''ab'' results, onPartialSwapped fired; both controls correct","Code read on main 74514cc7: navigation.ts:36-38 two independent token stores; fetchPartial write path :59-67 checks only its per-target token then querySelector at write time; templates.rs:176 #file-list-content on every file-list view; main.ts:860 tags-WS handler fires fetchPartial and the WS stays connected across pages"],"acceptance":["A fetchPartial issued before a navigateTo swap never writes to the DOM after that swap lands and never fires onPartialSwapped after it, regardless of target selector","A partial issued while a navigation is in flight cannot write into the page that navigation installs (or is dropped per the triage-pinned rule); the invariant is no writes from a previous page generation","Same-slot #1462 behaviour unchanged: navigation supersedes navigation, same-target partial supersedes, different-target partials on the same page generation stay independent","navigation.test.ts gains the cross cases: partial-then-navigate (stale resolves last), navigate-then-partial, and the reverse-order control","No behaviour change for the failed-current-navigation full-page fallback"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1578","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1462","pkgs/id/web/src/navigation.ts:36-38","pkgs/id/web/src/navigation.ts:51-64","pkgs/id/web/src/navigation.ts:84","pkgs/id/web/src/navigation.test.ts","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:716","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:860","pkgs/id/src/web/templates.rs:176"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Reintroduces #1462''s exact failure (content the user did not ask for last, with URL and page agreeing) across the most common interaction pair \u2014 search/tags-push then click \u2014 whenever the destination is another list view, which is the normal case for #file-list-content.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1578', '2026-10-28 03:40:47.857217+00', '2026-10-28 03:40:47.857217+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1660, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #669: drop ModelRouteOverrides entries with a present-but-malformed until', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/669","title":"fix(core): ModelRouteOverrides.parse drops a malformed until and keeps the override \u2014 an expiring instruction becomes permanent on its schedule","number":669,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:43:27Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["factor/weight handling (tracked separately in #662)","Schedule-only recurring overrides with no until field (intentional, pinned by existing tests)"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-overrides.ts parse until validation","Regression tests in packages/core/test/model-route-overrides.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-overrides.test.ts (via CI, from packages/core)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''override until malformed'' and ''until'' on 2026-10-28: #570 covered malformed schedule, #536 malformed scope lists, #662 factor/weight 0 \u2014 none covers a malformed until being dropped while the entry is kept.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:43:27Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"A present-but-malformed until is treated as absent when a schedule is present, so the override never expires; the parser''s own neighbouring rules drop the entry for malformed values in every other dimension.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe importing the real ModelRouteOverrides (temporary test in the 1643-666 worktree, removed after; model-route-overrides.ts md5 27cc94f7df44ec5a471e12979040f24b, byte-identical on both checkouts): schedule:{} + until:''tomorrow'' -> kept, until omitted; until:null -> kept, until omitted; valid until control -> preserved; no-until schedule control -> kept (intended); no-schedule + until:''tomorrow'' -> dropped","applies() at 2100-01-01 returns true for both malformed-until entries and false for the valid-until control"],"acceptance":["parse drops an entry whose until field is present but not a finite number (string, null, NaN/Infinity), with or without a schedule","Entries with a valid numeric until parse exactly as before","Schedule-only entries with no until field (intentional recurring form) parse exactly as before","Regression tests added in packages/core/test/model-route-overrides.test.ts beside the #570 malformed-schedule cases; CI green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/669","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/570","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/536","packages/core/src/model-route-overrides.ts:66-71 hasUntil / drop rule","packages/core/src/model-route-overrides.ts:92-103 entry construction"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Widening bug in the user-override parser: an expiry typo silently converts a time-limited avoid/prefer into a permanent recurring one, the same failure class #536 and #570 closed for the parser''s other dimensions. One-guard fix in one function.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:669', '2026-10-28 03:44:06.850298+00', '2026-10-28 05:10:54.439006+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1661, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(ci): protect open-PR bases in branch-cleanup in openchamber, code, and opencode (#629)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/581","title":"ci: add stale-branch cleanup workflow (dry-run by default)","number":581,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:44:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/629","title":"fix(ci): live daily branch-cleanup protects open-PR heads but not open-PR bases \u2014 deleting a stacked PR''s base would close it (also in code and opencode)","number":629,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any change to inactivity window, solely-behind test, deletion cap, or schedule"],"include":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml protected-set construction in openchamber, code, and opencode"]},"tests":["dry-run workflow dispatch or shell-level exercise of the protected-set logic in each repo; no sandbox builds","YAML validity of the edited workflows (CI on each PR)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1657, 2026-10-28: gh issue searches in openchamber/code/opencode for branch cleanup / base / stacked returned no covering issue besides #629; dezren39/nix#985 covered only the nix instance and is CLOSED; no open PR in any of the three repos touches branch-cleanup.yml protection.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Live daily branch-cleanup in three repos protects open-PR heads but not bases; a solely-behind inactive stacked-PR base would be deleted, closing that PR.","evidence":["Triage task 1657, 2026-10-28: current main of developing-today/openchamber, developing-today/code, and developing-today/opencode \u2014 .github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml in all three runs ''gh pr list --state open --limit 1000 --json headRefName'' and is_open_pr_head is the only PR protection; baseRefName never fetched (verified via gh contents API, full file read in all three)","BRANCH_CLEANUP_LIVE=true in all three repos (gh variable list, set 2026-10-27T18:31Z); daily crons 27/7/17 14 * * * respectively","All current open PRs base=main in all three repos (openchamber 8, code 32, opencode 6, gh pr list 2026-10-28T03:44Z), so the risk is latent until a PR is stacked on a non-main base","dezren39/nix#985 is CLOSED \u2014 the same heads-not-bases defect already fixed in the nix copy, usable as the implementation precedent","Fail-safe already present and must be preserved: set -euo pipefail plus the gh pr list step runs before any deletion"],"acceptance":["branch-cleanup.yml protected set includes open-PR baseRefName as well as headRefName in openchamber","Same protection in developing-today/code and developing-today/opencode, referencing openchamber#629","Dry-run output names base-protected skips (e.g. SKIP open-pr-base)","Run still fails before any deletion when the open-PR list cannot be read; other candidate rules unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/629","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/581","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/985"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Latent: no open PR currently uses a non-main base, but the workflow is live and daily in all three repos and stacked PRs are routine in this fleet; deleting a base closes the PR and loses its review/CI state. Normal priority, xs fix.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:629', '2026-10-28 03:45:21.709084+00', '2026-10-28 05:33:23.403729+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1662, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(routing): parse stats-route hours strictly (#632)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/632","title":"fix(routing): model-route stats route judges hours loosely \u2014 1e3, 0x10, 2.0 and -5 are reinterpreted instead of falling back (#604 remainder)","number":632,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:53:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["computePoolHealth and its internal numeric callers in model-route-stats.js (queryAttemptCountsPerTarget, queryActiveSessionsPerTarget)","any change to the 0.1-336 clamp range or the 24h default","pool-health route parsing (already fixed by #604)"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/routing/model-route-stats.js stats-route hours parsing","route-level regression tests in model-route-stats.test.js"]},"tests":["targeted routing tests run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --state all searches for ''route stats hours'', ''model-route-stats'' and ''stats hours loosely'' returned only #604 (pool-health route scope) and unrelated items; no issue covers the /api/model-routes/stats hours conversion.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:53:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"model-route stats route judges hours loosely: 1e3, 0x10, 2.0, padded/signed/leading-zero spellings and -5 are reinterpreted instead of falling back to the 24h default (#604 remainder).","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/routing/model-route-stats.js:211 \u2014 registerModelRouteStatsRoutes passes req.query?.hours raw to queryRouteStats","packages/web/server/lib/routing/model-route-stats.js:94 \u2014 windowHours = Math.min(336, Math.max(0.1, Number(hours) || 24))","packages/web/server/lib/routing/pool-health.js:217-225 \u2014 the canonical-decimal parser #604 added for the sibling route","Laptop probe this run (~/git/fleet/probe-stats-hours/probe.mjs): ''1e3'' -> 336, ''0x10'' -> 16, ''2.0''/'' 2 ''/''+2'' -> 2, ''01'' -> 1, ''-5'' -> 0.1, ''24'' -> 24, ''1.5'' -> 1.5, undefined -> 24, ''2junk'' -> 24 (already falls back via NaN)"],"acceptance":["?hours=1e3, 0x10, 0b101, 2.0, '' 2 '', +2, 01 and -5 all fall back to windowHours 24","Canonical values unchanged: 24 -> 24, 1.5 -> 1.5, 0.5 -> 0.5, >336 clamps to 336, <0.1 floors to 0.1, missing hours defaults to 24","Regression tests cover the stats route parsing for reinterpreted spellings and canonical cases","computePoolHealth internal numeric callers unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/632","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/604"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Same defect class and contract as #604/#554: the two sibling telemetry routes now disagree on the same parameter; a crafted or mistyped hours silently changes the stats aggregation window up to the 14-day clamp. Normal priority: the legitimate UI client sends plain decimals.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:632', '2026-10-28 03:54:29.171765+00', '2026-10-28 04:55:21.780737+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1663, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix: scope managed-servers own-server sessionCount to host sessions only (#623)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/619","title":"feat(web): add GET /api/managed-servers registry read (#525) \u2014 the snapshot consumer; land this fix on top of / after #619","number":619}],"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/623","title":"Managed-servers read: own-server sessionCount includes isolated-space sessions","number":623,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing getActiveSessionCount semantics for its existing restart-safety consumers","any other managed-servers work (issue #525 / PR #619 scope)","changing the registry on-disk format or watcher subscription"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/opencode/session-runtime.js: retain spaceId in session activity tracking (tag phase records) and expose a host-only active count (spaceId null/absent)","packages/web/server/index.js: pass the onPayload spaceId into sessionRuntime.processOpenCodeSsePayload","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/lifecycle.js (on top of PR #619): managed-servers snapshot uses the host-only count for the own-server entry","tests: session-runtime test where a busy space session does not inflate the host count but still counts in getActiveSessionCount, and a busy host session counts in both"]},"tests":["session-runtime unit test: busy payload with a spaceId leaves the host-only count at 0 while getActiveSessionCount is 1; busy payload without spaceId raises both","existing session-runtime, lifecycle, and managed-servers test suites pass"],"title":"fix: scope managed-servers own-server sessionCount to host sessions only (#623)","dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1653 verified the path on main 3e888c38; issue #623 is the tracked bug (split from PR #619 Codex review); no existing queue task implements it \u2014 task 1653 was triage-only by packet scope","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Own-server sessionCount in GET /api/managed-servers includes isolated-space sessions because spaceId is dropped between the watcher and the session runtime, so all busy sessions land in one global count.","evidence":["main 3e888c38 packages/web/server/lib/opencode/watcher.js:75 \u2014 subscribeEvent(..., { spaces: true }); emitTranslated(payload, event.spaceId ?? null): spaceId is available at the watcher","main 3e888c38 packages/web/server/index.js:1224-1227 \u2014 onPayload(payload, { spaceId }) forwards spaceId to maybeCacheSessionInfoFromEvent and maybeSendPushForTrigger but calls sessionRuntime.processOpenCodeSsePayload(payload) without it","main 3e888c38 packages/web/server/lib/opencode/session-runtime.js:449 processOpenCodeSsePayload takes no space argument; setSessionActivityPhase (~176) adjusts the single global activeSessionCount keyed only by sessionId; getActiveSessionCount (374) returns it","PR #619 branch packages/web/server/lib/opencode/lifecycle.js getManagedServersSnapshot passes getActiveSessionCount() as the own-server sessionCount","Global-count consumers that must NOT change semantics: lifecycle.js:1764 shouldSkipRestartForBusySessions and index.js:643-650 hasBusySessions \u2014 both want space sessions included for restart safety"],"acceptance":["GET /api/managed-servers own-server sessionCount counts only host (non-space) sessions","getActiveSessionCount still counts space sessions (restart-safety behavior unchanged)","a test covering a busy space session not inflating the host count passes"],"dedupe_key":"repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:623","context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/623","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/619","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/525"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Correctness bug in a user-facing registry count, split out of an in-flight PR; standard low priority matching the issue label.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:623', '2026-10-28 03:55:36.12643+00', '2026-10-28 07:19:18.061162+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1664, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): world presenter grapheme-width parity remainders (#1431 follow-up) — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1581","title":"id(web): world presenter still mis-measures \u2b1b/\u2b55, narrow-base skin tones, composed Hangul jamo and long graphemes \u2014 #1431''s folded-in classes survived its fix, and the 16-unit symbol cap has no Rust twin","number":1581,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to the Rust width semantics (unicode-width stays the source of truth)","Playwright e2e coverage (tracked by #1322)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/world-surface.ts WIDE_RANGES / graphemeWidth / symbol-length validation","pkgs/id/web/src/world-surface.test.ts parity tests","pkgs/id/src/world_presentation.rs only if triage rules the length cap should be mirrored on the Rust side"]},"tests":["vitest run for world-surface.test.ts on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search open+closed for ''2B1B'', ''2B55'', ''jamo'', ''world-surface'': only CLOSED #1431 (whose fix PR #1542 touched modifier/tag handling only) and OPEN #1322 (Playwright e2e coverage, a different item) touch the presenter; no open filing covers these classes.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T03:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"world-surface.ts grapheme width measurement and its symbol-length cap disagree with the Rust unicode-width validator for four grapheme classes, two of them remainders of a closed issue.","evidence":["pkgs/id/web/src/world-surface.ts:60-127 WIDE_RANGES has no U+2Bxx entry; :136-144 codePointWidth falls through to 1 and counts Mc marks as 0; :155-167 graphemeWidth strips emoji modifiers and measures the base alone; the cell validation in renderWorldSurface rejects symbol.length > 16 with no Rust twin","pkgs/id/src/world_presentation.rs:219 and :350 measure with UnicodeWidthStr::width (unicode-width 0.2.2, pkgs/id/Cargo.lock) and impose no symbol-length limit","TS probe on laptop, verbatim world-surface.ts sha256 3ee9823c310489668c59aa73bfcf9eaccc139db6417a7f24030e19a9ebe7f4b4 (log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-surface2/out.log): 2B1B/2B55 rendered=false at columns=2, true at 1; U+261D U+1F3FB false at 2, true at 1; jamo LV/LVT false at both; e+17xU+0301 false at 1 with the 16-renders/17-refused boundary pinned; controls x/U+1F600/#1542 sequences correct","Rust probe on laptop, unicode-width =0.2.2 + unicode-segmentation (log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-surface2/rust-out.log): 2B1B width=2, 2B55 width=2, U+261D U+1F3FB width=2 graphemes=1, jamo LV/LVT width=2 graphemes=1, U+0903 width=1, e+17 combining width=1 graphemes=1 utf16=18"],"acceptance":["renderWorldSurface agrees with UnicodeWidthStr::width (unicode-width 0.2.2) for U+2B1B, U+2B55 (2, refused at 1), U+261D U+1F3FB (2, refused at 1), composed jamo LV and LVT clusters (2), and a lone U+0903 cell (1)","The symbol-length rule is reconciled with the Rust side: TS cap removed/raised so a 1-grapheme width-1 symbol of 17+ UTF-16 units renders, or an explicit matching cap is added to world_presentation.rs with a comment naming the shared bound","Parity tests in world-surface.test.ts cover each class at its correct column count (renders) and the wrong one (refused)","Existing presenter tests still pass; the #1542 controls (U+1F44D U+1F3FD, England tag flag) still render at 2"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1581","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1431","pkgs/id/web/src/world-surface.ts:60","pkgs/id/src/world_presentation.rs:219"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The web presenter is one half of a two-presenter contract for the same validated ScreenSurface: every divergence either drops a Rust-valid screen to a raw-text dump on web or silently misaligns it. Two of the classes are ordinary emoji, and one is ordinary decomposed Korean text; two were already reported once and closed over without being fixed.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1581', '2026-10-28 03:59:45.655499+00', '2026-10-28 03:59:45.655499+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1666, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'fleet telemetry: record pool/model/effort/cost on dispatch + queue completion records (#1582)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1582","title":"fleet telemetry: record pool/model/effort/cost on dispatch + queue completion records (meta-reviewer #1340 follow-up)","number":1582,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["backfilling historical queue/dispatch records","changing routing, effort assignment, or pool policy (guidelines own that)","new pools, providers, or spend-class changes (Drew''s decisions, escalated via #1340 if ever needed)"],"include":["~/tools/repo-queue.py completion path and ~/tools/repo-task-v1.schema.json (optional pool/model/effort/cost_usd result fields)","dispatcher run-log records (same four fields per dispatch), located before editing","verification via one real completed task read back through the meta-reviewer''s data path"]},"tests":["repo-queue.py validate on a packet/result carrying the new fields and on one without (both must pass)","complete one real task and read its stored result back: new fields present and correct for the completing session"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list search (all states) for pool/model/effort/telemetry/meta-reviewer returned no existing issue before #1582 was filed by triage task 1324; #1340 names the need but is the parent design issue, not this slice.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Fleet records carry no pool/model/effort/cost fields, so model/effort grading is impossible and the meta-reviewer''s standing questions stay unanswerable.","evidence":["meta-review 2026-10-27 report: per-pool/per-effort cells mostly NOT RECORDABLE; queue payloads and events carry no pool/model/effort/cost fields; only costed samples are 3 OC sessions","meta-review 2026-10-27 report standing questions: model-up+effort-down vs model-down+effort-up = NO DATA; mechanism collecting it: none yet","reviewer-guidelines.md (files/, v1 2026-10-27): effort is recorded only from resolved session messages, never inferred from route names"],"acceptance":["A queue task completed after the change carries pool/model/effort (and cost_usd where the route exposes one) on its result record","A dispatcher run after the change logs pool/model/effort per dispatch, or #1582 records the dispatcher''s exact location and the one remaining step if it lives outside the reachable tree","New fields are optional/additive: existing packet and result consumers validate unchanged","Verification shown on the issue: one completed task''s stored result with the new fields present"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1582","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1340","goal hidden_files/meta-review/2026-10-27-report.md (NOT RECORDABLE finding, line 6 and line 23)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Unblocks the meta-reviewer''s core grading duty (#1340 acceptance criterion 3): without collection starting now, every future daily review repeats the NO DATA verdict. Normal priority per parent issue.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1582', '2026-10-28 04:05:49.533632+00', '2026-10-28 04:05:49.533632+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1669, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'docs(roadmap): add pool & routing intelligence epic rows (#1343)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1343","title":"Roadmap rows for the pool & routing intelligence epic","number":1343,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:31:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["rewriting or merging the existing Queue fleet reliability or OpenChamber dispatch rows","any non-docs change","inventing an epic issue number \u2014 take it from #1343''s epic/parent link"],"include":["planning/roadmaps/repo-and-ci.md (one new Now/Next row for the epic)","ROADMAP.md (Current focus text of the Repo-wide CI and automation row)"]},"tests":["CI treefmt/prettier checks on the PR (docs formatting)","post-merge aggregator program-view read showing the epic with children, cited on #1343"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh pr list (all states) search for 1343/roadmap-pool-routing returned no PR; origin/main grep 2026-10-28 shows no pool & routing intelligence row in repo-and-ci.md and no pool/routing mention in ROADMAP.md; no fix packet for #1343 existed (only the triage task 1328).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:31:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The pool & routing intelligence epic (steward, meta-reviewer, pool intelligence, dispatcher/babysitter) has live components but no roadmap row, so the aggregator''s program view and cross-repo roadmap omit the fleet''s oversight stack.","evidence":["origin/main planning/roadmaps/repo-and-ci.md Now table (read 2026-10-28): rows are One Jules workflow, Cache the Go build, Triage stale PRs, Queue fleet reliability, OpenChamber session dispatch + babysitter \u2014 no pool & routing intelligence epic row","origin/main ROADMAP.md (read 2026-10-28): ''Repo-wide CI and automation'' focus names ''the queue fleet program: lanes for every queue, OpenChamber session dispatch (#1233, #1234)'' \u2014 the epic is not named","Issue #1343 acceptance: PR merged; the aggregator''s program view shows the new epic with its children after its next refresh"],"acceptance":["PR merged with a merge commit on its own queue/* branch: repo-and-ci.md gains the pool & routing intelligence epic row in the existing table format, linked to the epic issue and #1340","ROADMAP.md ''Repo-wide CI and automation'' focus names the epic alongside the queue fleet program","After merge + aggregator refresh, the aggregator''s program view shows the epic with its children (verify and cite the read on #1343; if the aggregator has not refreshed by merge time, record the pending-refresh state instead of claiming it)","No other roadmap rows rewritten; diff is confined to planning/roadmaps/repo-and-ci.md and ROADMAP.md"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1343","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1340","planning/roadmaps/repo-and-ci.md Now table (Queue fleet reliability row, OpenChamber session dispatch row)","ROADMAP.md Projects table (Repo-wide CI and automation row)"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"effort/xs docs row that makes the epic visible to the aggregator''s program view \u2014 the PM structure the fleet''s own planning reads. Normal priority per the issue.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1343', '2026-10-28 04:08:59.453847+00', '2026-10-28 04:08:59.453847+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1670, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Controlled pool tests (#1342) slice 1: procedure + results template in goal workspace, #1191 results folded in', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1342","title":"Controlled pool tests: A/B real task batches before any pool change lands","number":1342,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:10:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["any pool/routing config change","executing a controlled test (that is slice 2)","re-running #1191''s trial"],"include":["files/controlled-pool-tests.md in the keep-the-four-repos-healthy goal workspace (procedure + results template + #1191 historical dataset)","a summary comment on #1342"]},"tests":["n/a \u2014 documentation slice; verify the template covers every measurement #1342 names (completion, wall-clock, tokens, stalls/nudges, 48h rework)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1327 decomposition of #1342; no existing packet names slice 1 of 1342 (checked queue claim state and goal files at triage).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:10:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Pool changes are proposed by pool-intelligence flags (first: #1409) but no controlled-test procedure or results template exists, so flags have no standing way to earn a config change.","evidence":["Triage task 1327 (2026-10-28): ls of goal files/ shows pool-intelligence-model.md but no controlled-test procedure/template; grep for controlled test in files/ hits only mentions in the model doc and findings store","Issue #1191 (routing-trial pilot) is still OPEN \u2014 its results have not been folded in anywhere","First pool-intelligence flag #1409 is open and is slice 2''s candidate"],"acceptance":["files/controlled-pool-tests.md exists with the full procedure (batch construction, arm sizes 3/6, packet-pinned routing) and a fill-in results template covering all five per-arm measurements from #1342","#1191''s trial results are recorded in the doc as the first historical dataset (or its incompleteness is stated with the partial numbers)","Summary + doc link posted on #1342"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1342","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1191","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1409"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Unblocks every pool-intelligence flag: #1409 and successors need this procedure before any controlled test (slice 2) can run.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1342', '2026-10-28 04:09:36.729015+00', '2026-10-28 04:13:08.908871+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1671, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Controlled pool tests (#1342) slice 2: first controlled test — flag #1409 (add Kimi K3.1 Pro via opencode-go to summit) vs incumbent', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1409","title":"pool flag: add Kimi K3.1 Pro via opencode-go to summit","number":1409,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:10:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing pool/routing config (verdict only; the steward lands changes)","building the procedure (slice 1)"],"include":["dispatching the two-arm batch through the normal queues with packet-pinned routes","the verdict record on #1409 and in files/pool-intelligence-model.md"]},"tests":["the controlled test itself is the test: >=3 comparable tasks per arm, same window where possible, all five measurements per arm"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1327 decomposition of #1342; slice 2 has a distinct dedupe key from slice 1 and no prior packet names it.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:10:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"No controlled test has ever been executed: pool-intelligence flag #1409 (Kimi K3.1 Pro to summit) is waiting on exactly this mechanism to earn or retire its proposed change.","evidence":["Issue #1342 acceptance: ''First controlled test executed end-to-end (two arms, real tasks, verdict recorded) \u2014 candidate chosen from the first pool-intelligence flag''","Flag #1409 is open with quantified trade (AA 55, $2.11/task, 53/57 measured probe successes)","Slice 1 supplies the procedure + template this test must follow"],"acceptance":["Gate verified at claim: slice 1''s files/controlled-pool-tests.md exists; otherwise park naming the gate","Both arms executed on real queued tasks with per-arm completion, wall-clock, tokens, stalls/nudges, and 48h rework recorded in the template","Verdict posted on #1409 and in files/pool-intelligence-model.md: pass -> PR-ready change handed to the steward; fail -> flag retired with numbers"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1342","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1409","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1191"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"First real use of the controlled-test mechanism; decides flag #1409 with evidence instead of vibes, per Drew''s 2026-10-27 directive.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1409', '2026-10-28 04:09:39.702695+00', '2026-10-28 04:19:54.967595+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1673, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(repl): quote-blind heredoc and $(...) scans in the REPL preprocessor — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1585","title":"id(repl): the preprocessor''s heredoc and $(...) scans are quote-blind \u2014 a quoted '')'' errors the line and a quoted ''<<'' drops the REPL into heredoc mode with a garbage delimiter","number":1585,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:24:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to shell_capture or the commands the REPL executes","Full shell grammar support (escapes/expansions beyond skipping quoted spans) unless triage rules it in"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/repl/input.rs heredoc check and $(...) scan quote handling + module doc comment","pkgs/id/src/repl/input.rs tests for the quoted cases","Audit of the backtick and here-string scans in the same file"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib repl on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''repl heredoc'', ''repl quote'', ''command substitution'', ''preprocess'': only CLOSED #1583 (byte-vs-char offsets in the same scan \u2014 different defect, its fix is on main) touches this preprocessor; no open filing covers quote handling.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:24:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The REPL preprocessor''s heredoc detection and $(...) paren scan ignore quoting, misparsing shell-valid lines that contain '')'' ''('' or ''<<'' inside quotes.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/repl/input.rs:215 heredoc detection is line.find(\"<<\") with delimiter = everything after it, trimmed; :267-282 the $(...) scan counts ''('' and '')'' over char_indices with no quote state","pkgs/id/src/repl/runner.rs:130-148 NeedMore consumes lines until one equals the delimiter and substitutes the content into original_line (the part before the ''<<'', i.e. the truncated line)","Laptop probe, verbatim input.rs sha256 a9138d2856f2bc7896d7e22455e6488068a86bdb28db2de96ad2a99f1a977f96 identical both sides (log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-replquote/out.log): C1-C4 controls Ready/NeedMore correct; Q1 ERR sh unterminated quote; Q2 ERR unterminated $(...); H1 NEEDMORE delimiter=\"b'')\" original=\"get $(printf ''a\"; H2 NEEDMORE delimiter=\"b\\\"\"; Q3 ERR sh unterminated quote"],"acceptance":["The heredoc check and the $(...) paren scan skip single- and double-quoted spans, so get $(echo '')'') -> ''get )'', get $(echo ''('') -> ''get ('', get $(echo \")\") -> ''get )'', get $(printf ''a<<b'') -> Ready ''get a<<b'', and get \"a<<b\" stays a plain Ready line","Regression tests in repl/input.rs cover quoted '')'' and ''('' inside $(...) in both quote kinds, ''<<'' inside a quoted argument, and ''<<'' inside a quoted string within $(...)","Existing controls unchanged: genuine heredocs, here-strings, nested $(...), backticks, |> pipe, and the #1583 multibyte tests keep passing","Backtick and here-string scans audited for the same misparse class; any case left quote-blind is named in the PR with a reason"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1585","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1583","pkgs/id/src/repl/input.rs:215","pkgs/id/src/repl/input.rs:267","pkgs/id/src/repl/runner.rs:130"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"preprocess_repl_line is the front door of every interactive id session; the heredoc failure mode looks like a hung REPL (it swallows lines waiting for an invisible delimiter) and the substitution failures blame the user''s quoting for the preprocessor''s own scan error. Ordinary quoted filenames/content with parens or ''<<'' trigger it.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1585', '2026-10-28 04:25:07.786201+00', '2026-10-28 04:25:07.786201+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1675, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): preserve YAML front matter in the markdown codec — implement dedicated front_matter node', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1369","title":"id(web): YAML front matter is destroyed on save \u2014 fences become a rule + setext heading, metadata fused into body text","number":1369,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:43:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing how the editor renders normal headings or horizontal rules","front-matter editing UI (preservation only)","TOML (+++) front matter (documented out of scope in the PR)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs front-matter handling both directions + validate_placement + codec regression tests","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts front_matter node in the rich schema (atom/leaf, non-editable block rendering)"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (in pkgs/id) \u2014 run in CI on the PR, no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Triage task 1340 for the same issue completed with the fix routed here; dedupe_key is the fix key for issue 1369, distinct from the triage key repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1369. No other open task works #1369.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:43:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The markdown codec parses front-matter fences as a thematic break plus a setext heading, so saving a front-matter doc rewrites its metadata into body structure.","evidence":["Triage re-verified on laptop main 7bd79a62: commonmark_options has no front-matter option; grep front_matter/frontmatter/FrontMatter across pkgs/id returns nothing; convert_node has no FrontMatter arm","comrak 0.56.0 crate source (laptop cargo registry): front_matter_delimiter produces NodeValue::FrontMatter(String) passed through unchanged in CommonMark output; split_off_front_matter requires file start + a closing delimiter line, so mid-document --- is never captured","Original probe on main 0cbb91b1 (issue #1369): front-matter input saves as ''-----\\n\\n## title: Hello World date: 2026-01-02 tags: \\\\[a, b\\\\]'' \u2014 silent permanent loss, a fixpoint"],"acceptance":["Front-matter doc round-trips with the YAML block verbatim (multi-key, blank-line-containing, body starting with heading or plain text), round-trip + fixpoint tests in pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs","Front matter is not presented in the editor as an editable heading/paragraph: dedicated front_matter PM node (atom/leaf) in the codec and in pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts rich schema","Control: ''Para one.\\n\\n---\\n\\nPara two.'' still round-trips with a horizontal rule; an unclosed leading --- stays a thematic break","validate_placement rejects front_matter anywhere except as the first child of doc","TOML (+++) front matter explicitly documented as out of scope in the fix PR","cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown passes in CI on the PR (pkgs/id)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1369","Triage findings + decision: comment on #1369 by queue task 1340, 2026-10-28 (agent-note handed off)","pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs commonmark_options, convert_node, prosemirror_to_markdown, validate_placement","pkgs/id/web/src/editor.ts richSchema","comrak 0.56.0: Options.extension.front_matter_delimiter / NodeValue::FrontMatter / strings::split_off_front_matter"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent, permanent metadata destruction on the first save of an extremely common markdown file shape (Obsidian/Hugo/Jekyll/Astro notes and docs). Triage is done and the design is decided; this is a bounded codec + schema change.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1369', '2026-10-28 04:37:48.048891+00', '2026-10-28 04:37:48.048891+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1676, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): split mixed task/plain lists at parse (fix #1370, per triage task 1341)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1370","title":"id(web): mixed task/plain lists cannot be saved at all \u2014 parse builds mixed lists its own placement validation rejects","number":1370,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:42:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["relaxing #1043 placement validation","editor.ts schema changes","changing pure task/plain list rendering"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs List parse arm: split mixed lists into sibling task/plain runs at parse","codec regression tests for the four mixed shapes + fixpoint"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (in pkgs/id), via CI or laptop"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Fix follow-up from triage task 1341 on #1370; fix dedupe distinct from triage dedupe; no PR addresses #1370 (checked 2026-10-27).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:42:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Parse manufactures mixed-children list docs that save-side placement validation and the editor schema both forbid, so mixed checklists are unsavable; triage decided split-at-parse.","evidence":["markdown.rs main blob 73bb6ee9: List arm line 221 picks list type from first child only; per-child conversion at ~526; placement_allowed forbids mixed children","Triage verdict comment on #1370 (task 1341): split-at-parse decision with ordered-offset and fixpoint requirements"],"acceptance":["All four mixed shapes parse to sibling task/plain lists and save without MisplacedNode","Ordered split runs render with unchanged numbering (order offsets)","PM->MD->PM fixpoint holds for mixed lists; existing web::markdown tests pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1370"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Mixed checklists are completely unsavable today (priority/high bug); fix is scoped to one parse arm.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'parked', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1370', '2026-10-28 04:40:41.01417+00', '2026-10-28 11:09:49.594946+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1677, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: julesSummary stale-note totals picked by lexicographic HHMM key — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1587","title":"aggregator: julesSummary presents a previous day''s keeper totals as the last run''s \u2014 the ''freshest note'' is picked by lexicographic HHMM key, which rolls over at midnight","number":1587,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:41:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to the keeper (jules-review) or its state-file format","mapJulesItems session mapping"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/jules.ts julesSummary note selection","pm-stack/aggregator/test/slice2.test.ts regression tests for rollover and unpadded keys"]},"tests":["bun test test/slice2.test.ts on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''jules summary totals note'' and ''julesSummary'': only CLOSED #898 (the slice that introduced the module) and #899 touch it; no open or closed filing covers the note-selection defect.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:41:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"julesSummary picks keeper totals by lexicographic HHMM key, which is not freshness: yesterday''s late note wins all day and unpadded keys mis-sort, while `at` names the actual last run.","evidence":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/jules.ts:90-94 selects bestText by string compare k > bestKey over keys matching /^jules_note_\\d+$/; :84-87 summary.at = state.last_run, independent of the chosen note","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/live.ts:1015-1019 pairs j.at with j.total/completed/failed in one ''last run totals'' sentence; scripts/collect-fleet-feed.ts:438-444,559 bakes julesSummary into the fleet feed","Laptop Bun probe, verbatim jules.ts sha256 15b46caf8b7a052a2b37fcbd6de0bca489a9e5ab9286e77a41f59ba6ccabf5f9 identical both sides (log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneA-julesnote/out.log): CONTROL 84/77/6 correct; CASE1 rollover returns 84/77/6 instead of 12/3/1; CASE2 stale-all-day returns 84/77/6 instead of 20/9/2; CASE3 unpadded returns 50/40/5 instead of 84/77/6"],"acceptance":["julesSummary reports the totals of the note written by the run last_run names (e.g. matched by HHMM), or the selection is otherwise date-aware; when no note can be tied to the last run, totals are omitted rather than taken from another run","Any remaining key comparison is numeric on a zero-padded HHMM: jules_note_905 never outranks jules_note_1458","New tests cover notes spanning midnight (2359 yesterday + 0010 today), a stale late-evening note alongside a morning note, and an unpadded key","The existing single-note ''parses keeper totals'' test keeps passing; mapJulesItems unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1587","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/jules.ts:81","pm-stack/aggregator/src/sources/live.ts:1015","pm-stack/aggregator/scripts/collect-fleet-feed.ts:438","pm-stack/aggregator/test/slice2.test.ts:215"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The Jules coverage line is how the fleet judges whether the Jules keeper is keeping up; after midnight it silently reports the previous day''s totals as the current run''s for most of every day \u2014 a wrong-but-plausible number on a health surface.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1587', '2026-10-28 04:42:13.156079+00', '2026-10-28 04:42:13.156079+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1679, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 2 of #1531 — daemon proof tests + TODO/roadmap closure (implement #1533, per triage task 1575)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1533","title":"mcpx: Phase 2 of #1531 \u2014 daemon proof: cross-directory re-point restarts on reload and the exec watch; TODO/roadmap closure","number":1533,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:50:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changes to internal/config identity semantics (Phase 1, #1532)","patching a Phase-1 defect found while testing \u2014 file it against #1532 instead"],"include":["internal/daemon reload + exec-watch tests for cross-directory re-point restart (exactly one server.restart)","pkgs/mcpx/TODO.md item 4 closure and planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md identity row closure","completion note on #1531"]},"tests":["go test ./internal/daemon/... ./internal/pool/... in pkgs/mcpx via CI or laptop"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Implementation follow-up from triage task 1575 on #1533 after the Phase-1 gate passed; fix dedupe distinct from the triage identity.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:50:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Phase 2 of #1531 (daemon proof + closure) was gated on Phase 1 merging; the gate has now passed and triage confirmed the scope as built.","evidence":["PR #1571 merged 2026-10-28T03:58:50Z (#1532 closed)","Triage task 1575 comment on #1533: files/TODO item/roadmap row verified on main, keep-vs-restart nuance named"],"acceptance":["Cross-directory re-point restarts on reload and on the exec watch, exactly one server.restart event, existing keep cases still pass","TODO item 4 and roadmap identity row closed with #1532/PR #1571 citations","Completion note posted on #1531"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1533","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1531","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1532"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Closes the #1531 design with daemon-level proof now that Phase 1 has landed.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1533', '2026-10-28 04:43:25.958592+00', '2026-10-28 08:33:33.305435+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1680, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #672: treat a blank rate-limit remaining header as unparseable, not zero', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/672","title":"fix(core): rate-limit windows read a blank remaining header as 0 \u2014 an empty value holds the target back like a spent window","number":672,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:47:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["limit parsing (a blank limit already degrades to undefined via the > 0 check)","Header collection in packages/ai (values stay as the provider wrote them by design)"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts windows() remaining parsing","Regression tests in packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-route-limits.test.ts (via CI, from packages/core)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''remaining empty'', ''holdUntil'' and ''windows'' on 2026-10-28: no issue covers blank remaining header values; #541/#549/#629 touch neighbouring rate-limit code for different defects.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:47:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"windows() uses Number(raw) for remaining: blank/whitespace strings coerce to 0 instead of NaN, so an empty rate-limit header is read as a spent window and holdUntil removes the target from rotation.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe importing the real ModelRouteLimits (probe at laptop ~/git/fleet/probe-2026-10-27-2335/probe.ts; model-route-limits.ts md5 2b01f63349b19c4a58b5ee436f9a1724, byte-identical on both checkouts): snapshot remaining {requests: \"\"} + limit 100 + reset 60s -> windows [{remaining: 0, limit: 100, resetAt: at+60000}], holdUntil = at+60000; remaining \"  \" with no reset -> windows [{remaining: 0}], holdUntil = at+60000","Existing test at model-route-limits.test.ts:86 pins the opposite treatment for a non-numeric value: remaining \"lots\" -> holdUntil 0"],"acceptance":["windows() does not report a window with remaining 0 for an empty or whitespace-only remaining value (window dropped, consistent with the NaN path)","holdUntil returns 0 for a snapshot whose only windows have blank remaining values, with or without a stated reset","A genuine \"0\" remaining still produces the spent-window hold; ordinary numeric strings parse exactly as before","Regression tests added in packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts beside the existing \"lots\" case; CI green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/672","packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts:158-172 windows / Number(raw)","packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts:143-145 MAX_WINDOW_MS / UNKNOWN_RESET_MS","packages/ai/src/route/executor.ts:42-68 rateLimitDetails copies header values verbatim","packages/core/src/model-route.ts:568 observeRateLimit consumes holdUntil","packages/core/test/model-route-limits.test.ts:86 remaining \"lots\" -> holdUntil 0 (pinned control)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A blank remaining header from a provider or gateway silently sidelines a healthy target (up to 24h with a distant reset) and masquerades as a quota wall in route history. One-guard fix in one function, with the intended treatment of unparseable values already pinned by an adjacent test.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:672', '2026-10-28 04:45:15.556873+00', '2026-10-28 05:14:04.715631+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1681, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #673: make dayReports'' provider accumulator prototype-safe', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/673","title":"fix(core): ModelUsage.dayReports loses or corrupts a provider whose id collides with Object.prototype \u2014 ''__proto__'' vanishes, ''constructor'' reports NaN","number":673,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Other Record accumulators not keyed by user-chosen IDs (route decision reasons are internal strings)","Config alias resolution (already fixed in #538)"],"include":["packages/core/src/model-usage.ts dayReports providers accumulation","Regression tests in packages/core/test/model-usage.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/model-usage.test.ts (via CI, from packages/core)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''dayReports'', ''__proto__'' and ''constructor provider'' on 2026-10-28: #538 fixed the same collision class in config alias resolution (normalize.ts) only; no issue covers the dayReports accumulator in model-usage.ts.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T04:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"dayReports accumulates per-provider shares in a plain object keyed by user-chosen provider IDs: ''__proto__'' assignments set the prototype instead of an entry, and reads for ''constructor''/''toString'' return inherited members, producing a vanished provider and NaN shares while day totals stay correct.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe importing the real ModelUsage (probe at laptop ~/git/fleet/probe-2026-10-27-2335/probe.ts; model-usage.ts md5 cf82532048c7fea28a8257223eb47878, byte-identical on both checkouts): dayReports rows anthropic(3 requests) + __proto__(7) + constructor(5) -> providers JSON {anthropic: {requests: 3, metered: 15, costUsd: 1}, constructor: {requests: null, metered: null, costUsd: null}}, own keys [anthropic, constructor] (__proto__ missing), day total requests 15 (correct)"],"acceptance":["dayReports reports a correct own entry for provider IDs __proto__, constructor and toString, summed across multiple rows with the same colliding ID","Ordinary provider IDs produce exactly the same reports as before; the providers record JSON-serialises with the colliding IDs present","Fix uses a prototype-safe construction (Map and/or Object.fromEntries), not a name blocklist","Regression tests added in packages/core/test/model-usage.test.ts beside the existing day-grouping test; CI green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/673","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/538","packages/core/src/model-usage.ts:246-255 dayReports providers accumulator","packages/core/test/model-usage.test.ts:182-195 existing day-grouping test (openai/anthropic only)"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Silent data corruption in a user-facing usage report, but only for provider IDs colliding with Object.prototype members \u2014 custom provider names are user-chosen, so reachable, yet uncommon. One-function fix with an in-repo precedent (#538).","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:673', '2026-10-28 04:46:47.675298+00', '2026-10-28 05:36:55.175204+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1682, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): per-block indent/dedent for multi-block selections (#1399 fix)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1399","title":"id(web): Tab/Shift-Tab with a selection spanning multiple blocks corrupts a paragraph and skips later code blocks","number":1399,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:00:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing single-block indent semantics or the 2-space INDENT unit","list indentation (Tab in lists is a different command path)","goto-line.ts or other #1038 optimization scope beyond resolving a merge conflict"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/indent.ts indentCommand/dedentCommand multi-block handling (per-code_block iteration)","pkgs/id/web/src/indent.test.ts multi-block regression tests"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id/web && bunx vitest run src/indent.test.ts"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Follow-up fix packet enqueued by triage task 1378 on issue #1399; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1399 is distinct from the triage identity (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1399). #714 (closed) covered wrong-line selection within one code block only; PR #1038 is a line-start lookup optimization, not this fix (coordinate, do not duplicate).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:00:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"indent/dedent commands use single-block line math for multi-block selections: later code blocks skipped, spaces inserted into a neighbouring paragraph.","evidence":["Triage task 1378 re-verified root cause on current main via gh api: indent.ts:63-65 / :100-102 derive blockStart from $from and blockEnd from $to (different nodes when spanning) and scan doc.textBetween as a single block''s text; inCode gate :42-46 checks only $from parent","Creator probes on main 452d69e6 (packet 1378 evidence): doc code_block(x\\ny)+paragraph(mid)+code_block(p\\nq), select-all, Tab -> block1 indented, paragraph ''mid  '' (spaces appended to prose), block2 unchanged","Existing tests in pkgs/id/web/src/indent.test.ts build single-block docs via rawSchema helpers; multi-block tests need richSchema docs mixing code_block and paragraph nodes"],"acceptance":["Tab with a multi-block selection indents selected lines of every overlapped code_block and modifies no non-code content","Shift-Tab under the same conditions dedents every overlapped code_block''s selected lines, prose untouched","Existing indent.test.ts suite (incl. #714 cases) passes unmodified","New tests cover code+paragraph and code+paragraph+code selections for both commands, including select-all"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1399","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1399#issuecomment-6461029108","pkgs/id/web/src/indent.ts indentCommand:38-84, dedentCommand:89-149","pkgs/id/web/src/indent.test.ts","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1038","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/714"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Select-all + Tab is a standard reindent gesture; today it silently edits prose and leaves code unindented \u2014 data corruption in a basic editor path. Fix shape decided in triage task 1378; change is local to indent.ts plus tests.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1399', '2026-10-28 04:57:13.312887+00', '2026-10-28 04:57:13.312887+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1683, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: buffer-backup cleanupCount never restores the maxFileCount limit in one pass (issue #1002)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["retention-cleanup"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1002","title":"buffer-backup: cleanupCount deletes only rolloutFileCount per pass \u2014 the maxFileCount limit is never restored when the backlog is far over it","number":1002,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:28:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["cleanupAge and cleanupSize semantics","Configuration schema/defaults in package.json"],"include":["pkgs/buffer-backup/src/extension.ts cleanupCount loop","A fixture probe/test for the over-limit count case"]},"tests":["Fixture probe: 30 files, maxFileCount=10, rolloutFileCount=5 -> <=10 remain after one cleanupCount pass","npm run compile in pkgs/buffer-backup exits 0"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue list --search ''buffer-backup'' returned only #781/#997/#998 (lockfile drift) and trackers #11/#49 \u2014 none covers cleanupCount/maxFileCount semantics (searched 2026-10-28)","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:28:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"cleanupCount deletes a fixed rolloutFileCount per pass instead of deleting down to the maxFileCount limit, so the limit is not restored when the backlog far exceeds it.","evidence":["pkgs/buffer-backup/src/extension.ts:287-303 cleanupCount: n = min(rolloutFileCount, entries.length), deletes exactly n; contrast cleanupSize :262-285 which loops until total <= maxB - rolloutB","Laptop probe (node v24, functions extracted verbatim from extension.ts at main 0270d07): count pass1 remaining 25 of 30 (max 10, rollout 5), pass2 20; size pass1 remaining 10 files / 10240B at target","activate() runs all three cleanups once at startup, so an over-limit directory stays over limit after startup cleanup too"],"acceptance":["After a single cleanupCount pass over a directory with N > maxFileCount files, at most maxFileCount files remain, oldest deleted first","When the count is at or under maxFileCount, cleanupCount deletes nothing","A fixture probe/test (staggered mtimes) demonstrates the over-limit case converging in one pass; cleanupAge and cleanupSize behavior unchanged","npm run compile (tsc -p ./) in pkgs/buffer-backup is clean"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1002","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/998"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"maxFileCount is the user''s stated hard bound on retained backups; as implemented it is only a per-interval deletion quota, so a lowered limit or a large backlog stays over the bound indefinitely under steady backup creation.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:1002', '2026-10-28 05:31:00.475592+00', '2026-10-28 05:40:09.039298+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1685, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Triage: spotlight/git-discover suites still print contradicting ok lines after failed checks (issue #1003)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1003","title":"test(scripts): #971''s ok-line fix missed spotlight and git-discover suites \u2014 failed checks still print contradicting ''ok:'' lines","number":1003,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:37:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["clean.test.sh and git-maintain-repos.test.sh (already fixed by PR #971)","Any change to the scripts under test"],"include":["spotlight-exclude-artifacts.test.sh ok-line conditionality","git-discover-repos.test.sh ok-line conditionality"]},"tests":["Run both suites on an unaffected tree: ok lines print, exit 0","Run both suites with a forced fixture/marker change: FAIL only, no ok line for the failed check, exit 1"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search ''ok line'' returned #968 only (closed, scoped to clean/git-maintain); no issue covers spotlight or git-discover ok lines (searched 2026-10-28)","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:37:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Two of the four #951-family suites still print ok lines unconditionally after failed checks, contradicting their own FAIL lines.","evidence":["spotlight-exclude-artifacts.test.sh:84-85 on current main: ''[ -z \"$(markers)\" ] || fail \"rejected runs wrote marker files: ...\"'' followed by unconditional ''echo \"ok: rejected runs wrote no markers\"''; same shape at :98-99 for the dry-run control","git-discover-repos.test.sh:123-124 on current main: snapshot ''|| fail'' followed by unconditional ok echo \u2014 the instance PR #972 added","PR #971 (head 57e54d27) applied the if/else fix only to clean.test.sh and git-maintain-repos.test.sh"],"acceptance":["spotlight-exclude-artifacts.test.sh: both ok lines print only when the corresponding marker check passes","git-discover-repos.test.sh: the :123-124 ok line and earlier group-summary ok lines print only when all checks they summarize passed","A forced fixture change still produces FAIL only (no ok), exit non-zero; passing runs still print ok lines and exit 0","No script under test changes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1003","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/968","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/964","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/971","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/972"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Log-only contradiction in regression suites; exit codes are correct, but a failed no-side-effects check reads as passing in the log \u2014 the exact defect #968 was filed for in the sibling suites.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:1003', '2026-10-28 05:38:45.777896+00', '2026-10-28 06:33:22.626254+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1686, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Triage: branch-cleanup live daily run aborts on the first failed branch deletion (issue #1004)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["branch-deletion"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1004","title":"branch-cleanup: one failed ''git push --delete'' aborts the live daily run \u2014 later candidates are never attempted","number":1004,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:37:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Candidate criteria, inactivity window, and the 50-candidate all-or-nothing cap (deliberate design in PR #961)","Open-PR head/base protection logic from PR #991"],"include":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml deletion-loop failure handling and reporting"]},"tests":["Workflow run (or extracted-script simulation) with a stubbed failing delete for a middle candidate: later candidates still attempted, failure named in summary","Dry-run output unchanged for the all-success case"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues ''branch-cleanup'' returned #984 and #985 only (both closed, different mechanisms); no issue covers deletion-failure handling (searched 2026-10-28)","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:37:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"branch-cleanup''s deletion loop has no per-branch failure handling under set -e, so a single failed delete aborts the whole live daily run.","evidence":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml:46 on current main: ''set -euo pipefail''; :154-161 deletion loop with bare ''git push origin --delete \"$branch\"'' at :155, no guard or failure collection","PR #966 body states BRANCH_CLEANUP_LIVE has been set to true and verified, and changes the schedule to daily \u2014 the loop performs live deletions every day","Minimal reproduction of the loop shape under set -euo pipefail printed only the first candidate and exited 1 when the second iteration''s command failed; the third candidate was never attempted"],"acceptance":["A failed git push --delete for one candidate does not stop the run: remaining candidates are still attempted","Each failed deletion is reported by name in the log and step summary, with deleted/failed counts in the final summary","Partial failure is visible in the run outcome, not a clean full success","Dry-run behaviour, candidate criteria, open-PR head/base protections (#985) and the 50-candidate cap unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1004","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/961","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/966","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/985"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Live daily deletion run: one undeletable branch (ruleset, concurrent delete, transient push error) blocks all later candidates indefinitely and the failure reads as a generic workflow failure.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:1004', '2026-10-28 05:38:51.345999+00', '2026-10-28 06:26:30.530246+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1687, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Triage: mcp-clients removed: report misses quoted server names in root inline tables (issue #1005)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1005","title":"mcp-clients: quoted server names in a root inline table are removed but never named in the ''removed:'' report (#958)","number":1005,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:37:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Multi-line string state in codex() \u2014 that is issue #990 / PR #996","Zed and JSON client steps","Enforcement behaviour for any mcp_servers spelling (already correct)"],"include":["mcp-clients.py _inline_table_keys quoted-key handling","mcp-clients.test.py regression case for a quoted server name in a root inline table"]},"tests":["python3 mcp-clients.test.py \u2014 full suite passes including the new quoted-name case","Direct probe: _inline_table_keys returns quoted and bare names in any order"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues ''mcp-clients quoted'', ''inline table report'', ''removed report'' returned #944/#956 only (closed, survival mechanisms); no issue covers quoted keys in _inline_table_keys (searched 2026-10-28)","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:37:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"_inline_table_keys treats a quoted key in key position as a string value, so quoted server names are never named in the removed: report.","evidence":["mcp-clients.py:197 _inline_table_keys on current main; string-skip branches at :213/:218 run before the key branch at :234","Probe on current main: _inline_table_keys with a quoted ''my.server'' key returns [''plain''] only; quoted ''myserver'' (no dot) also missed; reversed order also missed","Full codex() probe on a scratch config.toml: both foreign servers removed, output valid TOML with only mcpx, but the run reported ''removed: plain'' only"],"acceptance":["_inline_table_keys reports quoted server names (double- and single-quoted, including names with dots/spaces) alongside bare names in any position","A codex() run over a root inline table with a quoted server name prints that name in the removed: report; rewritten file behaviour unchanged (valid TOML, only mcpx, second run no-op)","mcp-clients.test.py gains a regression case with a quoted server name in a root inline table asserting removal and report; full suite still passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1005","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/958","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/956"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Reporting-only defect: the removed: line is the audit trail asserted by the #944/#956 tests, and it silently under-reports for the one TOML spelling (quoted) that names with dots or spaces require.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:1005', '2026-10-28 05:38:55.359368+00', '2026-10-28 06:11:00.091457+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1688, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #677: treat blank retry-after headers as absent in RequestExecutor', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/677","title":"fix(ai): a blank retry-after-ms header reads as 0 and discards the response''s real retry-after","number":677,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:38:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Rate-limit remaining/limit/reset parsing in packages/core/src/model-route-limits.ts (blank remaining already fixed in #672)","Web-search cooldown parsing in packages/core/src/websearch.ts (already guards blank values)"],"include":["packages/ai/src/route/executor.ts retryAfterMs blank handling","Regression tests in packages/ai/test/response-hook.test.ts or executor.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/response-hook.test.ts (via CI, from packages/ai)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''retry-after blank'', ''retryAfterMs'' and ''executor retry'' on 2026-10-28: no hits. #672 fixed the blank-Number() hole for rate-limit remaining in model-route-limits.ts only; the executor''s retry-after parser in packages/ai was outside that fix.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:38:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"retryAfterMs returns Number(blank) === 0 as a finite result, so a blank retry-after-ms overrides the same response''s valid retry-after and a whitespace-only retry-after manufactures a 0 ms wait where none was stated.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe importing the real RequestExecutor (temporary test in the route-time-windows worktree; executor.ts md5 69e35222661119713cd1db08d8d7eb93, byte-identical to main 8cd052358a; probe removed after, tree clean): {''retry-after-ms'':'''', ''retry-after'':''7''} -> {retryAfterMs: 0}; {''retry-after-ms'':''  '', ''retry-after'':''7''} -> {retryAfterMs: 0}; {''retry-after'':'' ''} -> {retryAfterMs: 0}; {''retry-after-ms'':''''} alone -> {retryAfterMs: 0}; controls {''retry-after-ms'':''250''} -> 250, {''retry-after-ms'':''0''} -> 0, {''retry-after'':''7''} -> 7000"],"acceptance":["A blank or whitespace-only retry-after-ms is treated as absent: parsing falls through to retry-after, and to undefined when that is also absent/unusable","A blank or whitespace-only retry-after is treated as absent; responseRateLimit returns undefined when nothing else is present","An authored ''0'' still yields retryAfterMs 0, and valid millisecond, seconds, and HTTP-date forms are unchanged","Regression tests added in packages/ai/test/response-hook.test.ts (or executor.test.ts) covering blank-ms-over-valid-seconds, whitespace-only retry-after, and the ''0'' control; CI green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/677","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/672","packages/ai/src/route/executor.ts:23-36 retryAfterMs","packages/ai/src/route/executor.ts:82-86 responseRateLimit (exported probe surface)","packages/ai/test/response-hook.test.ts:197-205 existing responseRateLimit tests","packages/core/src/model-route-log.ts:155 success-path consumer"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A discarded provider retry instruction causes immediate retries against a rate-limited provider and manufactures a zero-wait rate-limit snapshot on the success path; blank header values are a realistic proxy/gateway artifact, and the fix is one parse site with an in-repo precedent (#672).","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:677', '2026-10-28 05:39:28.650273+00', '2026-10-28 07:30:11.246753+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1689, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 1 of #1601 — surface ttlMs/cacheScope in mcpclient and expire the pool catalogue cache (modern era) — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1602","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1601 \u2014 surface ttlMs/cacheScope in mcpclient and expire the pool catalogue cache (modern era)","number":1602,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:39:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the hint/TTL wiring in this triage task","disk persistence and scope enforcement (Phase 2 of #1601, #1603) and register truth-up / nix#200 evidence (Phase 3, #1604)","resources/read caching, discover TTL, legacy default TTL (open questions on #1601)"],"include":["issue #1602 and design #1601 with the design doc it links","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient (client.go list types and List* methods), internal/pool/pool.go (Schemas/RefreshSchemas/SetSchemas/Invalidate), internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go (read-only references)"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./... via CI; defining tests from #1602: fake modern upstream at ttl 0/positive/absent/negative, per-page min-TTL, private-if-any, concurrent expired reads collapse to one refresh, legacy behaviour unchanged, templates page 2 surfaces)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1602 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-28) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1602 \u2014 it did not exist before this run, so its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:39:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx''s client drops upstream ttlMs/cacheScope hints and its pool catalogue cache never expires, so modern upstreams that rely on TTL alone are served stale until the daemon restarts. Design #1601 Phase 1 (#1602) surfaces the hints in mcpclient and gives the pool cache a modern-era freshness deadline.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/client.go: toolsListResult (~L183), resourcesListResult (~L204), resourceTemplatesListResult (~L209), promptsListResult (~L1117) carry no ttlMs/cacheScope fields; ListTools/ListResources/ListPrompts return bare slices; resourceTemplatesListResult.NextCursor is a plain string and ListResources fetches templates unpaged","pkgs/mcpx/internal/pool/pool.go Schemas (~L815): returns the cached lists forever once schemaAt is set; only Invalidate() (list_changed via internal/daemon/hooks.go) or manual refresh re-reads an upstream","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go:113-121: nine client caching gaps under dezren39/nix#200 \u2014 ''the client ignores ttlMs and cacheScope; the pool keeps upstream lists until list_changed or restart''","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpserver/server.go ~L690-740: the server side already emits ttlMs+cacheScope to modern peers (scope table + envelope); this phase is client/pool only","Design #1601 records the era-scoping decision: modern hints rule (absent/zero/negative = immediately stale); legacy pools keep today''s event-driven cache unchanged"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1602: scope confirmed against current main, hint-variant shape settled or explicitly left open with reasons, and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If triage finds Phase 1 as scoped is not independently landable, say exactly why on the issue and propose the rescoped Phase 1 in the design doc''s terms \u2014 do not silently shrink it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1602","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1601","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/200"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 1 is the core of design #1601 and retires five of the nine nix#200 caching gaps; Phases 2-3 are gated on it. Normal priority per the design issue.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1602', '2026-10-28 05:40:13.089266+00', '2026-10-28 05:54:41.642157+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1690, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 2 of #1601 — cacheScope at the disk boundary: private never persists, expired seeds expired, stale on refetch error — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1603","title":"mcpx: Phase 2 of #1601 \u2014 cacheScope at the disk boundary: private never persists, expired seeds expired, stale on refetch error","number":1603,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:39:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the disk/scope wiring in this triage task","client hint parsing and pool TTL (Phase 1 of #1601, #1602) and register truth-up / nix#200 evidence (Phase 3, #1604)","background revalidation (declined on #1601)"],"include":["issue #1603 and design #1601 with the design doc it links, plus Phase 1''s as-built state on #1602","pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon/registry.go (loadCache/SaveCache/cacheFile), internal/pool/pool.go (SetSchemas/Schemas/RefreshSchemas), internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go (read-only references)"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./... via CI; defining tests from #1603: private catalogue absent from saved cache file, public expired entry re-read on first Schemas, stale served on refetch failure with retry, failed first fetch unchanged)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1603 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-28) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1603 \u2014 it did not exist before this run, so its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:39:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx persists every upstream catalogue to its on-disk schema cache and re-serves it after restart with no TTL and no scope check, so a private-scoped catalogue outlives its authorization context. Design #1601 Phase 2 (#1603) makes private catalogues memory-only, gives disk entries a deadline, and defines stale-on-refetch-error.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/daemon/registry.go loadCache/SaveCache (~L249-285): every pool catalogue is persisted to the schema-cache file and re-seeded via SetSchemas(..., e.FetchedAt); no TTL is applied to FetchedAt and no scope is recorded anywhere","Register PG-10 (pkgs/mcpx/docs/compare/register/pagination-caching.md): cacheScope private = reuse only within the same authorization context, MUST NOT be shared across contexts \u2014 design #1601 records the decision: private catalogues are never persisted","pkgs/mcpx/internal/pool/pool.go RefreshSchemas: on failure the cache timestamp is deliberately left unset so a never-started server does not look empty \u2014 Phase 2 preserves this for first fetches and inverts it only for refetches of an expired entry (serve stale, stay expired)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go:121 gap caching-private-no-cross-auth (issue dezren39/nix#200): ''cacheScope is ignored, so a private upstream list is served to every downstream caller''"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1603: gate state for #1602 checked first; scope confirmed against Phase 1''s as-built plumbing, cache-file field shape settled or explicitly left open with reasons, and the implementation follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If Phase 1 has not landed, park with the gate named on the issue \u2014 do not re-triage around it","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1603","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1601","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1602","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/200"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 2 closes the scope half of design #1601 (the privacy-relevant half: private catalogues on disk); Phase 3 is gated on it. Normal priority per the design issue.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'parked', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1603', '2026-10-28 05:40:16.879886+00', '2026-10-28 10:16:46.132782+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1691, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 3 of #1601 — register truth-up, list_changed invalidation test, and nix#200 evidence — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1604","title":"mcpx: Phase 3 of #1601 \u2014 register truth-up, list_changed invalidation test, and nix#200 evidence","number":1604,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:39:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["implementing the truth-up in this triage task","any new caching behaviour (resources/read, discover TTL, legacy default TTL \u2014 open questions on #1601)","closing dezren39/nix#200 (evidence comment only)"],"include":["issue #1604 and design #1601 with the design doc it links, plus the landed state of #1602/#1603","pkgs/mcpx/docs/compare/register/pagination-caching.md, internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go, internal/daemon/hooks.go, planning/roadmaps/mcpx.md (read-only references for triage)"]},"tests":["n/a for triage \u2014 record the verification commands the follow-up must run (pkgs/mcpx: go test ./... via CI; defining test from #1604: modern list_changed empties the pool catalogue cache)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #1604 was created by the design architect in this same run (2026-10-28) with queue/queued and no packet; no prior task can name issue 1604 \u2014 it did not exist before this run, so its dedupe key has never been enqueued.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:39:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"After Phases 1-2 of design #1601 land, the pagination-caching register and conformance gaps would still describe the pre-fix state, the list_changed invalidation path would remain untested, and origin issue dezren39/nix#200 would carry no evidence. Phase 3 (#1604) is the truth-up and closure-evidence phase.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/docs/compare/register/pagination-caching.md PG-08..PG-13 still describe mcpx @ 05c78b2 (''none of the six carry them'', ''never emitted'') \u2014 the server side has since landed (internal/mcpserver/server.go ~L690-740), so the register currently understates the server and, until Phases 1-2 land, correctly states the client gap","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go:122 gap caching-notification-invalidates (issue dezren39/nix#257): ''unverified since subscriptions/listen landed upstream (#239): nothing tests that a modern list_changed empties the pool list cache'' \u2014 the wiring exists at internal/daemon/hooks.go:37-44 (OnListChanged -> Pool.Invalidate)","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go:113-121: the nine client caching gaps whose retirement (with reasons) this phase records","dezren39/nix#200 is the origin umbrella for the caching rows; design #1601''s acceptance is an evidence comment there, not closure \u2014 the umbrella tracks other registers'' rows"],"acceptance":["Triage verdict posted on #1604: gate state for #1602/#1603 checked first; scope confirmed against the landed as-built state, and the follow-up packet is enqueued (or the issue is split with linked sub-issues)","If either gate phase has not landed, park with the gate named on the issue \u2014 do not write the truth-up against unlanded behaviour","Labels left truthful after triage (queue/* mirrors the resulting task state)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1604","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1601","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1602","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1603","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/200"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Phase 3 closes design #1601: it makes the conformance register truthful and reports the landed caching slice back to origin nix#200. Normal priority per the design issue.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'parked', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1604', '2026-10-28 05:40:19.572727+00', '2026-10-28 10:16:52.718779+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1699, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #678: make ModalModels price() reject blank and negative pricing', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/678","title":"fix(core): ModalModels pricing accepts blank and negative values \u2014 a blank price erases the template cost, a negative price stores a negative cost","number":678,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Pricing/cost handling for other providers","The limit() helper (already guards range correctly)"],"include":["packages/core/src/modal/models.ts price() blank/negative handling","Regression tests in packages/core/test/modal/models.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/modal/models.test.ts (via CI, from packages/core)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''modal pricing'', ''ModalModels'' and ''negative cost price'' on 2026-10-28: no hits.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"price() accepts any finite Number() result: blank strings become 0 and erase the template cost an omitted field would have kept, and negative values become negative per-token costs.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe calling the exported ModalModels.derive (temporary test in the route-time-windows worktree; modal/models.ts md5 be297a36af07f259622f19225f5e3d7b, byte-identical to main 8cd052358a; probe removed after, tree clean): template cost {input 5, output 10, cache.read 1, cache.write 2}; pricing {prompt:'''', completion:''  '', input_cache_read:''''} -> cost {input 0, output 0, cache.read 0, cache.write 2}; pricing {prompt:''-0.000003'', completion:-0.000004} -> cost {input -3, output -4}; controls prompt ''abc'' -> 5 (fallback), ''0.000001'' -> 1"],"acceptance":["Blank or whitespace-only pricing strings fall back to the template/default cost, like an omitted or non-numeric value","Negative pricing (string or number) falls back instead of producing a negative cost","An authored 0 / ''0'' still yields a zero cost, and valid positive string/number pricing is unchanged","Regression tests added in packages/core/test/modal/models.test.ts covering blank and negative pricing against a priced template; CI green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/678","packages/core/src/modal/models.ts:85-94 price() and the sibling limit() guard","packages/core/src/modal/models.ts:25-31 pricing schema (any string admitted)","packages/core/test/modal/models.test.ts:102-126 existing omitted-pricing fallback test"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Corrupt cost data (free or negative-cost models) flows into cost accounting and displayed spend, but only when the remote Modal payload carries blank/negative pricing, so reachability is narrower than a routing bug. One-function fix mirroring the sibling limit() guard in the same file.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:678', '2026-10-28 05:41:47.12917+00', '2026-10-28 07:25:49.492993+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1702, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx(cli): exec artifact delivery overwrites same-named artifacts — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1605","title":"mcpx(cli): exec artifact delivery silently overwrites same-named artifacts \u2014 applyFrame and fetchArtifacts rename onto the bare sanitized name, unlike Store.Export''s never-overwrite rule","number":1605,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:43:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to Store.Export / uniquePath semantics (they are the correct reference behaviour)","Changes to SanitizeName''s character rules"],"include":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/exec.go applyFrame FrameArtifactEnd placement","pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/exec.go fetchArtifacts/writeNew placement","internal/cli tests mirroring TestExportNeverOverwrites for both paths"]},"tests":["go test ./internal/cli/ ./internal/artifacts/ on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''mcpx artifact overwrite'', ''artifact rename'', ''fetchArtifacts'', ''uniquePath'', ''artifacts-dir'': no filing covers CLI artifact-delivery collisions; the only artifact-overwrite guard in the repo is Store.Export''s own test. Distinct from code#1549 (id web image upload name collision \u2014 different repo area, server tag store, not mcpx).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:43:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The mcpx CLI''s two exec artifact-delivery paths write to the bare sanitized name with no collision handling, silently overwriting same-named artifacts and misreporting both Paths.","evidence":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/exec.go:313-321 FrameArtifactEnd: dest = filepath.Join(eo.ArtifactsDir, artifacts.SanitizeName(name)); os.Rename(w.Name(), dest) \u2014 rename replaces an existing destination","pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/exec.go:396-420 fetchArtifacts dest is the same bare join; writeNew''s temp file protects against partial writes but its final os.Rename clobbers a finished same-named file","pkgs/mcpx/internal/artifacts/name.go SanitizeName collapses distinct script names to one disk name: ''my shot.png''->''my-shot.png'', ''a/b.png''->''b.png'' (last component), spaces->''-'', so collisions do not require identical input names","Laptop probe (package cli test, real applyFrame/writeNew/SanitizeName/Store.Export; log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneA-mcpxart/out.log): stream two shot.png artifacts -> one file shot.png=''SECOND-BODY'', both Paths equal; writeNew twice -> dest=''SECOND-BODY''; control Export -> shot.png + shot-1.png"],"acceptance":["Both CLI delivery paths (applyFrame FrameArtifactEnd rename and fetchArtifacts/writeNew) place same-named artifacts at distinct paths using the store''s suffix convention (shot.png, shot-1.png, ...) or an equivalent never-overwrite rule shared with uniquePath","Each artifact''s Path in the result names the file that actually holds its body; a test in internal/cli mirrors TestExportNeverOverwrites for both delivery paths (two same-named artifacts -> two files, both bodies intact, suffix before the extension)","Re-running a script into a non-empty --artifacts-dir does not silently overwrite the previous run''s same-named artifact, or the overwrite is made explicit in flag help and the result","Existing artifact and CLI tests still pass; TestExportNeverOverwrites semantics unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1605","pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/exec.go:313","pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/exec.go:396","pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/exec.go:407","pkgs/mcpx/internal/artifacts/artifacts.go:551","pkgs/mcpx/internal/artifacts/name.go:81"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"mcpx run/exec --artifacts-dir is how scripts hand files back; two same-named artifacts (or a repeat run) silently destroy the first file while the result still lists both artifacts as delivered at the same Path \u2014 data loss reporting success, in the subsystem that already documented why it must never happen.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1605', '2026-10-28 05:45:02.831568+00', '2026-10-28 05:45:02.831568+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1704, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'mcpx: Phase 1 of #1601 — surface ttlMs/cacheScope in mcpclient and expire the pool catalogue cache (implement #1602)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1602","title":"mcpx: Phase 1 of #1601 \u2014 surface ttlMs/cacheScope in mcpclient and expire the pool catalogue cache (modern era)","number":1602,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:14:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["SetSchemas signature / disk persistence and scope enforcement (Phase 2 of #1601, #1603)","Register truth-up and nix#200 evidence (Phase 3, #1604)","resources/read caching, discover TTL, legacy default TTL (open questions on #1601)","Paging the standalone ListResourceTemplates method (only its shared result struct''s cursor type changes)"],"include":["pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/client.go list result types, List* methods and hint variants, templates paging in ListResources","pkgs/mcpx/internal/pool/pool.go deadline+scope beside schemaAt, Schemas() expiry fall-through, refresh collapse","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go five caching-* gap retirements"]},"tests":["go test ./... for pkgs/mcpx via CI","Defining tests: fake modern upstream at ttl 0/positive/absent/negative, per-page min-TTL, private-if-any, concurrent expired reads collapse to one refresh, legacy behaviour unchanged, templates page 2 surfaces"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Implementation follow-up enqueued by triage task 1689 on issue #1602; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1602 is distinct from the triage identity (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1602). Phase 2 (#1603) and Phase 3 (#1604) are separate issues with their own packets when their gates clear.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:14:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"mcpx''s client discards upstream ttlMs/cacheScope hints (no fields on the four list result types) and the pool''s catalogue cache never expires, so a modern upstream relying on TTL alone is served stale until list_changed or restart.","evidence":["Triage task 1689 verdict on #1602 (comment 6461796894), verified fresh on main 63ba1705: no ttlMs/cacheScope fields on toolsListResult L181 / resourcesListResult L202 / resourceTemplatesListResult L207 (NextCursor plain string) / promptsListResult L1115 in pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/client.go; ListResources fetches templates unpaged","pkgs/mcpx/internal/pool/pool.go: Schemas() L811 serves cache forever once schemaAt set; RefreshSchemas L828 uses the bare List* methods; no refresh serialisation exists (Acquire hands out concurrent leases; schemaMu guards fields only) \u2014 concurrent-refresh collapse must be added, not assumed","Five gaps at pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go:113-117 (caching-ttl-zero-stale, caching-ttl-positive-fresh, caching-ttl-absent-zero, caching-ttl-negative-zero, caching-stale-refetch), Client side, issue #200 (dezren39/nix)","Server side already emits hints: pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpserver/requirements_test.go:108-111 asserts ttlMs/cacheScope per method \u2014 Phase 1 is client-only"],"acceptance":["Fake modern upstream tests: ttl 0 / absent / negative \u2192 next Schemas() re-lists; positive ttl \u2192 served from cache until deadline, re-listed after; per-page min-TTL wins; any-page-private marks the catalogue private","Concurrent reads of an expired cache collapse into one refresh (counting test on upstream list calls), via explicit refresh serialisation added in the pool","Legacy upstream catalogue behaves exactly as before (zero deadline, no expiry)","Templates beyond page 1 appear in ListResources, with a test naming the change","Hint-variant shape per triage: CacheHints{TTLMs int64, HasTTL bool, Private bool}; ListToolsWithHints/ListResourcesWithHints/ListPromptsWithHints added; ListTools/ListResources/ListPrompts signatures unchanged as wrappers","The five named conformance gaps are retired as C(...) entries naming the new tests; go test ./... for pkgs/mcpx passes in CI"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1602","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1601","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1602#issuecomment-6461796894","pkgs/mcpx/internal/mcpclient/client.go","pkgs/mcpx/internal/pool/pool.go","pkgs/mcpx/internal/conformance/coverage_stateful.go"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A modern upstream that relies on TTL alone is served a stale catalogue indefinitely (until list_changed or daemon restart) \u2014 a correctness defect the conformance register has carried as five open gaps under nix#200. Design and triage are settled; the fix is client+pool local.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'parked', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1602', '2026-10-28 05:52:28.593972+00', '2026-10-28 10:55:44.295489+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1705, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(web): verify recorded-pid identity in the managed-servers read (#638)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/638","title":"fix(web): managed-servers read lists a recycled pid as a live OpenCode server \u2014 signal-0 liveness with no identity check, unlike the reaper","number":638,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the orphan reaper''s own behaviour in managed-process-registry.js (already identity-checked)","#623 sessionCount/spaceId plumbing","#614 phase-3 docs/conformance fixture"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/opencode/managed-servers.js liveness/identity filtering and its header comment","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/lifecycle.js getManagedServersSnapshot identity verification wiring","tests in managed-servers.test.js (and lifecycle tests if the wiring lives there)"]},"tests":["targeted managed-servers/lifecycle tests run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches for ''recycled pid managed'' and ''managed-servers pid'' returned only #612 (design) and #525 (the original registry-read issue, closed); no issue covers pid-identity verification for the managed-servers read.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"managed-servers read lists a recycled pid as a live OpenCode server: signal-0 liveness with no identity check, unlike the reaper and isOwnedOpenCodePid.","evidence":["packages/web/server/lib/opencode/managed-servers.js:84-86 \u2014 builder filters entries only by the injected isPidAlive","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/lifecycle.js:395-402 \u2014 isPidAlive is signal-0 only; :1943-1949 passes it verbatim into buildManagedServersResponse","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/managed-servers.js:9-11 \u2014 header comment claims signal-0 is ''the same check the orphan reaper uses''","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/managed-process-registry.js:119-128 + :296-300 \u2014 the reaper verifies command identity (opencode + serve + recorded port) and leaves a pid alone when identity cannot be verified","packages/web/server/lib/opencode/lifecycle.js isOwnedOpenCodePid \u2014 ''A recorded pid can be reused by an unrelated process, so it is signalled only when its command still matches''","Laptop probe this run (~/git/fleet/probe-managed-pid/probe.mjs): registry entry for a live `sleep 30` pid returned as a server {pid, port: 4096, status: ''unknown'', startedAt: ''2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z''}"],"acceptance":["A registry or draining entry whose pid is now held by a process that is not the recorded OpenCode server does not appear in GET /api/managed-servers","Where identity cannot be verified (platform without a command read), the entry is not presented as a live server on signal-0 alone; behaviour explicit in code and tests","The hosting instance''s own ready/starting/draining entry still appears with its completed fields","The managed-servers.js header comment no longer claims the read uses the reaper''s check (or is made true by the fix)","Tests cover recycled pid excluded, genuine recorded server included, dead pid excluded; existing managed-servers and lifecycle suites stay green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/638","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/525","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/612"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The read is the discovery surface external consumers (design #612) trust; a phantom entry points them at a dead server''s port indefinitely and survives restarts because the registry file is only pruned for dead pids. Normal priority: requires a pid recycle onto a long-lived process, but the codebase''s own precedent treats pid reuse as a real hazard everywhere else.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:638', '2026-10-28 05:58:53.182314+00', '2026-10-28 09:37:41.685363+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1706, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): GET /api/tags drops the value filter without a key — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1607","title":"id(web): GET /api/tags silently drops the value filter without a key \u2014 ?value= returns the whole namespace, ?subject=&value= returns all the subject''s tags","number":1607,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:58:43Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to the combinations that already honour value (subject+key+value post-filter, key+value find_by_key_value)","Changes to POST/DELETE /api/tags or the search handler"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs get_tags_handler dispatch for value-without-key shapes","Handler tests for both shapes and the controls"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib web::tags_ws (or the handler''s test module) on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''tags value filter'', ''api/tags value'': no filing covers the tags REST dispatch. Adjacent: #1547 (projector read-API limit validation \u2014 different component/parameter), #1208 (Project pool truncation in fetchProjectPool \u2014 different function).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T05:58:43Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"GET /api/tags accepts the value parameter but silently discards it in the subject-only and no-filter dispatch arms, returning unfiltered results as if the filter applied.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs:294 (Some(subject), None, _) arm calls get_tags(subject) \u2014 value discarded by the wildcard","pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs:304 (None, None, _) arm calls list_all(ns) \u2014 value discarded; ?value=rust is byte-for-byte the no-filter result","Laptop verbatim-dispatch probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneB-tagvalue/out.log): BUG1 value-only -> 4 tags incl. label=python and a value-less tag; BUG2 subject+value -> rust and python; controls key+value -> 2, subject+key+value -> 1","pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs:125 TagQuery::value doc says ''(requires key)'' \u2014 the requirement is documented but unenforced"],"acceptance":["GET /api/tags?value=... without key never returns unfiltered results: either a 400 naming the missing key, or a real value search \u2014 one behaviour, pinned by tests","GET /api/tags?subject=...&value=... without key gets the same treatment (400, or the subject''s tags filtered by value)","Handler-level tests pin both shapes plus the existing controls: key+value, subject+key+value, subject only, and no filters all keep their current results","No behaviour change for well-formed callers (the web UI''s ?subject= calls at pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:909 included)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1607","pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs:125","pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs:275","pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs:294","pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs:304","pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts:909"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"A caller passing value without key gets a superset of what it asked for with a 200 and no signal \u2014 for value-only callers, the entire namespace. Scripts and future UI acting on that response will act on tags they never asked for; the fix is a small dispatch/validation change in one handler.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1607', '2026-10-28 05:59:29.026184+00', '2026-10-28 05:59:29.026184+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1708, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: report quoted server names in mcp-clients _inline_table_keys (issue #1005)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1005","title":"mcp-clients: quoted server names in a root inline table are removed but never named in the ''removed:'' report (#958)","number":1005,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:15:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Multi-line string state in codex() \u2014 that is issue #990 / PR #996","Zed and JSON client steps","Enforcement behaviour for any mcp_servers spelling (already correct)"],"include":["mcp-clients.py _inline_table_keys quoted-key handling, on our own queue/* branch + PR","mcp-clients.test.py regression case for a quoted server name in a root inline table"]},"tests":["python3 mcp-clients.test.py \u2014 full suite passes including the new quoted-name case (run on laptop or CI, never on the sandbox)","Direct probe: _inline_table_keys returns quoted and bare names in any order"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1687 after confirming #1005; dedupe_key is the issue''s fix key, distinct from the triage key repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:1005","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:15:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"_inline_table_keys treats a quoted key in key position as a string value, so quoted server names are never named in the removed: report.","evidence":["Main 53d5ef6 mcp-clients.py _inline_table_keys: string-skip branches precede the depth==1 expecting key branch, visually confirmed from git show origin/main:mcp-clients.py lines 197-254","Laptop probe on main 53d5ef6 (triage task 1687): _inline_table_keys with quoted ''my.server'', quoted ''myserver'', reversed order, and single-quoted ''my server'' each return [''plain''] only; bare control returns [''plain'', ''other'']","Laptop codex() probe on a scratch config.toml (triage task 1687): both foreign servers removed, output parses as valid TOML with only mcpx, but the run printed ''removed: plain'' only"],"acceptance":["_inline_table_keys reports quoted server names (double- and single-quoted, including names with dots/spaces) alongside bare names in any position","A codex() run over a root inline table with a quoted server name prints that name in the removed: report; rewritten file behaviour unchanged (valid TOML, only mcpx, second run no-op)","mcp-clients.test.py gains a regression case with a quoted server name in a root inline table asserting removal and report; full suite still passes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1005","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/958","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/956","mcp-clients.py:197 _inline_table_keys; string-skip branches at :213/:218 run before the key branch at :234"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Reporting-only defect, effort/xs: the removed: line is the audit trail asserted by the #944/#956 tests, and it silently under-reports for the one TOML spelling (quoted) that names with dots or spaces require.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:1005', '2026-10-28 06:10:33.558782+00', '2026-10-28 06:16:53.665845+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1709, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(tags): parse_search_query ASCII-space-only term separation — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1609","title":"id(tags): parse_search_query only separates terms on ASCII space \u2014 tab/newline/NBSP fuse terms into one unmatchable term","number":1609,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:11:41Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to search_by_query execution semantics (AND intersection, per-term match kinds)","Changes to the CLI/REPL query construction (they already join with single spaces)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/tags.rs parse_search_query term separation (whitespace-general, quote-aware)","Parser unit tests for the new separators and the quoted-whitespace control"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib tags (parser tests) on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''search query tab whitespace parse_search'' and ''tags search separator'': no hits. Adjacent but distinct: #1607 (GET /api/tags value filter dropped in get_tags_handler dispatch \u2014 different handler/function), #1585 (REPL preprocessor quote-blind scans \u2014 different parser).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:11:41Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"parse_search_query treats only ASCII space as a term separator, so queries separated by tab/newline/CRLF/NBSP parse into a single term whose fused value matches nothing and the search silently returns empty.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1478 skip-separators loop compares bytes[i] == b'' '' only","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1492 term-end check compares bytes[i] == b'' '' && !in_quotes only","Laptop verbatim probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneA-searchws/out.log): BUG-tab-kv -> [KeyValue(name, \"foo\\tbar:baz\")]; BUG-newline/CRLF/NBSP fuse the same way; BUG tab after ''name:'' -> KeyValue(name, \"\\tpriority\"); controls incl. quoted-tab Literal all correct","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1304 search_by_query matches the fused value/word exactly, so the AND intersection is empty \u2014 silent no-matches result"],"acceptance":["Term separation in parse_search_query recognises general whitespace (at minimum tab, LF, CR, NBSP \u2014 char::is_whitespace semantics), not only ASCII space, both when skipping separators and when ending a term","Whitespace inside a quoted section remains part of that term (''\"a\\tb\"'' still parses as one Literal)","New unit tests pin tab-, newline- and CRLF-separated key:value terms, a tab-separated bare-word pair, and ''name:<TAB>priority'' matching the space form (KeyOnly + BareWord)","All pre-existing parse_search_query tests pass unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1609","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1466","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1478","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1492","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1304","pkgs/id/src/web/tags_ws.rs:434","pkgs/id/src/protocol.rs:629"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Tag search is the structured query surface for the whole namespace; a pasted multi-term query (terminals/spreadsheets routinely carry tabs and newlines) fails silently with an empty result that reads as ''tags do not exist''. The fix is a small, well-scoped parser change with strong existing test coverage to extend.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1609', '2026-10-28 06:12:34.756275+00', '2026-10-28 06:12:34.756275+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1711, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(tuple): tuple decode wraps negative ints / accepts NaN — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1610","title":"id(tuple): decode accepts negative ints that wrap to zero/positive and NaN floats \u2014 the negative branch has no range check, unlike the positive branch","number":1610,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:25:38Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Any encoder change (on-disk/document encodings must stay identical)","Changes to tags.rs key layout"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/tuple.rs decode_one negative-int, float branches and int canonicality","Unit tests in tuple.rs for the new refusals"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib tuple on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for ''tuple'' in developing-today/code returned only closed #1075 (validation audit epic); title/keyword search for ''tuple decode negative'' returned no filing. Adjacent lanes this morning covered tags REST/search (#1607/#1609), not the tuple codec.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:25:38Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"tuple::decode accepts negative-int payloads whose abs is 0 or >2^63 (wrapping to zero/positive values), NaN float payloads the encoder refuses, and non-minimal int encodings.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/tuple.rs:457 positive branch ensure i64::try_from(v).is_ok(); negative branch 464-478 has no abs check before wrapping_sub","Python replication of decode arithmetic this run: tag 0x13 payload FF -> abs 0 -> Int(0); tag 0x0C payload 00*8 -> abs u64::MAX -> Int(1); tag 0x0C payload 7F00.. -> Int(9151314442816847873)","pkgs/id/src/tuple.rs:261 encoder rejects NaN; FLOAT64 decode branch 482-499 has no is_nan check; payload 21fff8000000000000 decodes to NaN","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:585,609 decode_alpha_key/decode_omega_key trust decode() over keys read from namespace documents"],"acceptance":["Decoding a negative-int payload with abs==0 or abs>2^63 returns an error, with unit tests for abs 0, 2^63 (valid i64::MIN), 2^63+1, u64::MAX","Decoding a float payload that reverses to NaN returns an error, with a crafted-NaN unit test","Non-minimal int encodings are refused with tests, or explicitly documented as accepted \u2014 one behaviour, pinned","Existing tuple round-trip and sort-order tests still pass; no encoder change"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1610","pkgs/id/src/tuple.rs:446","pkgs/id/src/tuple.rs:464","pkgs/id/src/tuple.rs:482","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:585"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Tuple keys back the tag store''s sort-preserving index; a key decoding to a value outside its tag range silently breaks the byte-order = semantic-order invariant that tags.rs decode_alpha_key/decode_omega_key rely on. Fix is a small decoder validation change in one file.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1610', '2026-10-28 06:26:08.137886+00', '2026-10-28 06:26:08.137886+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1712, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: continue past failed deletions in branch-cleanup and report them (issue #1004)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":["branch-deletion"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1004","title":"branch-cleanup: one failed ''git push --delete'' aborts the live daily run \u2014 later candidates are never attempted","number":1004,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:27:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Candidate criteria, inactivity window, and the 50-candidate all-or-nothing cap (deliberate design in PR #961)","Open-PR head/base protection logic from PR #991"],"include":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml deletion-loop failure handling and reporting, on our own queue/* branch + PR"]},"tests":["Extracted-script simulation with a stubbed failing delete for a middle candidate: later candidates still attempted, failure named in log and summary, outcome shows partial failure","Dry-run output unchanged for the all-success case","Post-merge dry-run workflow_dispatch of branch-cleanup (dry_run=true) completes green"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1686 after confirming #1004; dedupe_key is the issue''s fix key, distinct from the triage key repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:1004","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:27:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"branch-cleanup''s deletion loop has no per-branch failure handling under set -e, so a single failed delete aborts the whole live daily run.","evidence":["Main 8e0a19f .github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml:46 ''set -euo pipefail''; deletion loop with bare ''git push origin --delete \"$branch\"'', no guard, no failure collection, DELETED echo after the push","gh variable list 2026-10-28: BRANCH_CLEANUP_LIVE=true; workflow schedule cron ''37 14 * * *'' (daily, live deletions)","Laptop reproduction of the loop shape (triage task 1686): candidates a-good/b-bad/c-later \u2014 a-good deleted, b-bad push failed, subshell exit 1 immediately, c-later never attempted, finish line never printed"],"acceptance":["A failed git push --delete for one candidate does not stop the run: remaining candidates are still attempted","Each failed deletion is reported by name in the log and step summary, with deleted/failed counts in the final summary","Partial failure is visible in the run outcome, not a clean full success","Dry-run behaviour, candidate criteria, open-PR head/base protections (#985) and the 50-candidate cap unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1004","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/961","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/966","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/985",".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml:46 set -euo pipefail; deletion loop at :154-161 with bare push at :155"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Live daily deletion run: one undeletable branch (ruleset, concurrent delete, transient push error) blocks all later candidates indefinitely and the failure reads as a generic workflow failure.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 50, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:1004', '2026-10-28 06:26:22.667562+00', '2026-10-28 06:31:31.577331+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1713, 'repo-health-nix-pilot', 'Small fix: make spotlight/git-discover ok lines conditional on passing checks (issue #1003)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"dezren39/nix","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1003","title":"test(scripts): #971''s ok-line fix missed spotlight and git-discover suites \u2014 failed checks still print contradicting ''ok:'' lines","number":1003,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:35:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["clean.test.sh and git-maintain-repos.test.sh (already fixed by PR #971)","Any change to the scripts under test"],"include":["spotlight-exclude-artifacts.test.sh ok-line conditionality","git-discover-repos.test.sh ok-line conditionality"]},"tests":["Run both suites on an unaffected tree: ok lines print, exit 0 (run on laptop or CI, never on the sandbox)","Run both suites with a forced fixture/marker change: FAIL only, no ok line for the failed check, exit 1"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1685 after confirming #1003; dedupe_key is the issue''s fix key, distinct from the triage key repo-health:v1:triage:dezren39/nix:issue:1003","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:35:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Two of the four #951-family suites still print ok lines unconditionally after failed checks, contradicting their own FAIL lines.","evidence":["Main 8e0a19f: spotlight-exclude-artifacts.test.sh:84-85 and :98-99 unconditional ok echo after ''|| fail''; git-discover-repos.test.sh group-summary ok lines and :123-124 snapshot ok unconditional","Laptop forced-failure repro (triage task 1685, patched copies in /tmp/1685-repro): spotlight planted marker -> FAIL+contradicting ok for both marker checks, exit 1; git-discover planted file after SNAP_BEFORE -> FAIL+contradicting ok for missing-value snapshot, exit 1; baseline both suites exit 0 with ok lines","PR #971 applied the if/else fix only to clean.test.sh and git-maintain-repos.test.sh"],"acceptance":["spotlight-exclude-artifacts.test.sh: both ok lines print only when the corresponding marker check passes","git-discover-repos.test.sh: the :123-124 ok line and earlier group-summary ok lines print only when all checks they summarize passed","A forced fixture change still produces FAIL only (no ok), exit non-zero; passing runs still print ok lines and exit 0","No script under test changes"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1003","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/968","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/964","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/971","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/pull/972"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Log-only contradiction in regression suites; exit codes are correct, but a failed no-side-effects check reads as passing in the log \u2014 the exact defect #968 was filed for in the sibling suites.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:dezren39/nix:issue:1003', '2026-10-28 06:31:28.995447+00', '2026-10-28 06:35:19.04174+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1715, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #681: reject unsatisfiable Form field bounds and uncompilable patterns in validateFields', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/681","title":"fix(core): Form validateFields accepts unsatisfiable field bounds and uncompilable patterns \u2014 the form can never be answered","number":681,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:42:37Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Schema-level changes in packages/schema (keep the runtime create-time check as the single gate, mirroring the when-reference checks)","Default-value validation (a separate question; not part of this packet)"],"include":["packages/core/src/form.ts validateFields bound-coherence and pattern checks","Regression tests in packages/core/test/form.test.ts"]},"tests":["bun test test/form.test.ts (via CI, from packages/core)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''validateFields'', ''unsatisfiable'', ''minLength'', ''form field'' on 2026-10-28: #601 covered when references to external fields only; no issue covers bound coherence or pattern compilability at creation.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:42:37Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Create-time form validation never checks bound coherence or pattern compilability, so malformed field definitions create forms that no answer can satisfy.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe importing the real @opencode/core/form module (route-time-windows worktree; form.ts differs from main 7001736e73 only inside isDateTime): validateFields returned undefined for all four malformed definitions; validateAnswer rejected every probed answer for each; coherent control (minLength 2, maxLength 5, answer ''abc'') passed both","packages/core/src/form.ts validateField compiles pattern via new RegExp inside try/catch at answer time and returns ''Form field has invalid pattern'' \u2014 the only place pattern validity is ever checked"],"acceptance":["validateFields rejects string minLength > maxLength, number/integer minimum > maximum, and multiselect minItems > maxItems, naming the field key","validateFields rejects a string pattern that does not compile as a RegExp at creation time","Equal bounds (minLength == maxLength etc.) and one-sided bounds still create successfully","Regression tests in packages/core/test/form.test.ts cover each inverted pair, the invalid pattern, and an equal-bounds control; CI green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/681","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/601","packages/core/src/form.ts validateFields / validateField","packages/schema/src/form.ts field schemas (bounds are independent optional numbers)"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"An unsatisfiable or bad-pattern form can never be answered, so an elicitation hangs until cancel and its errors blame the user; validateFields already exists to catch exactly this class of authoring mistake at creation (#601). Small, pure-function fix.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:681', '2026-10-28 06:43:03.890725+00', '2026-10-28 08:11:42.660006+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1716, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #682: restrict retry-after parsing to the decimal grammar in RequestExecutor', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/682","title":"fix(ai): retry-after parsing reinterprets hex and exponent spellings \u2014 ''1e3'' becomes a 1,000,000 ms wait, ''0x10'' becomes 16 s","number":682,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:43:49Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["packages/core/src/websearch.ts cooldownMillis (same Number() shape, but a separate unexported parser \u2014 note it in the fix PR if touched, do not expand this packet''s tests to it)","McpxDiagnose Number() grammar (explicit documented design, #595)"],"include":["packages/ai/src/route/executor.ts retryAfterMs grammar restriction","Regression tests in packages/ai/test (executor.test.ts / response-hook.test.ts)"]},"tests":["bun test test/executor.test.ts (via CI, from packages/ai)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''retry-after'' with ''hex'', ''exponent'', ''1e3'', ''0x10'' on 2026-10-28: #677 covers blank values only; #595 documents the Number() grammar as an explicit design choice for McpxDiagnose, a different surface. No issue covers the executor''s notation reinterpretation.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:43:49Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Bare Number() parsing of retry-after headers honours hex and exponent spellings at face value instead of treating them as unusable, inventing waits the provider never stated.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe through exported RequestExecutor.responseRateLimit on main-identical executor.ts: {''retry-after'':''1e3''} -> {retryAfterMs:1000000}; {''retry-after'':''0x10''} -> {retryAfterMs:16000}; {''retry-after-ms'':''1e3''} -> {retryAfterMs:1000}; {''retry-after-ms'':''0x10''} -> {retryAfterMs:16}; controls {''retry-after'':''10''} -> 10000, {''retry-after'':''garbage''} -> undefined"],"acceptance":["retry-after ''1e3'' and ''0x10'' yield no instruction (responseRateLimit undefined when nothing else present)","retry-after-ms ''1e3'' and ''0x10'' fall through to retry-after / undefined as blank values do after #677","Authored plain values unchanged: ''0'', ''250'' (ms), ''10'' (s), HTTP-date forms; existing executor tests still pass","Regression tests cover hex and exponent spellings for both headers; accepted grammar commented at the parse site; CI green"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/682","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/677","packages/ai/src/route/executor.ts:23-36 retryAfterMs","RFC 9110 section 10.2.3 delay-seconds grammar"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"An invented 16.7-minute wait stalls sessions and is recorded as the provider''s stated limit state; the parser already has the correct fallback for unusable values, it just never reaches it for these spellings. Remainder of the #677 fix in the same function.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:682', '2026-10-28 06:44:21.071966+00', '2026-10-28 09:39:38.709986+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1717, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(claim/doc/group): plain-text output newline forgery — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1611","title":"id(claim/doc/group): plain-text output renders names/values raw \u2014 a newline in a tag name or value forges extra rows and duplicate author=/event= fields","number":1611,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["--json output format (already correct, must stay byte-identical)","Tag claim semantics, ingest or sync validation of event content beyond the chosen output/validation contract"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/commands/group.rs tokens()/text() plain renderer (shared by claim/doc/group)","Validation in tag_claims.rs check_text and/or documents.rs media-type check, if the triage chooses refusal as part of the contract","Renderer/validation unit tests pinning the probe cases"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib commands:: (renderer tests) on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''claim list newline'', ''tokens output injection'', ''forged row'': no hits. Adjacent but distinct: #1423 (web markdown link destinations corrupted by tab/newline on save \u2014 different surface), #1457 (web UI untrusted-name rendering, cited as contrast).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"id claim/doc/group plain-text output renders unvalidated-for-whitespace names/values raw via tokens(), so a newline in a tag name or value breaks the one-line-per-row format and forges extra rows/duplicate fields; spaces and tabs make rows ambiguous.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/commands/group.rs:63-71 tokens() prints strings verbatim (''strings without quotes'', group.rs:54-60), joined with single spaces","pkgs/id/src/tag_claims.rs:145-157 check_text checks byte length + NFC only; space/tab/CR/LF are NFC-stable and pass (name max 128 at :40, value max 512 at :43)","Laptop verbatim probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneA-cliout/out.log): newline value renders 2 lines with a forged ''subject=deadbeef name=forged author=deadbeef event=deadbeef'' row; newline name renders 2 lines; space/tab cases pass and render raw","pkgs/id/src/commands/claim.rs:37-48 claim_fields prints value before author/event, giving the forged tokens first-match precedence"],"acceptance":["Plain-text rows from id claim list/search, id doc publish/events/history/frontier and id group output are always one physical line per row, whatever bytes a name, value, media type, group name/description or reason field contains","A whitespace-splitting consumer can recover every field unambiguously: values containing spaces/tabs/newlines are quoted/escaped (or refused at validation with a named error) \u2014 the chosen rule is pinned by tests and stated in the commands'' module docs","A crafted claim with a newline-bearing name/value (the filed probe cases) can no longer produce a second line or a duplicate author=/event= token in plain output","--json output is byte-for-byte unchanged, and ordinary space-free values render exactly as today (or the change is documented as intentional)","Tests pin the rule at the renderer (tokens()/print helpers) and, if refusal is chosen, at check_text/DocumentRef::check as well"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1611","pkgs/id/src/commands/group.rs:63","pkgs/id/src/commands/claim.rs:37","pkgs/id/src/commands/doc.rs:46","pkgs/id/src/tag_claims.rs:145","pkgs/id/src/documents.rs:105"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The plain key=value output is the documented listing format for claims/docs/groups and is read by scripts and operators; a peer-authored claim can plant a phantom row naming a different author/event in another node''s listing. The renderer is one shared helper, so the fix surface is small and central.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1611', '2026-10-28 06:45:47.505671+00', '2026-10-28 06:45:47.505671+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1719, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(fileops): archive tags collide within one second — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1612","title":"id(fileops): archive tags collide within one second \u2014 a second replace of the same name silently overwrites the first replace''s archive","number":1612,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:54:20Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to put''s documented overwrite-without-archive behaviour","Changes to the archive.replace/archive.rename metadata keys"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs archive_existing naming/uniqueness","pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs archive_original_tag (same fix or shared helper)","Tests for same-timestamp double replaces; delete/classify_tag enumeration compatibility"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib fileops (and web routes archive tests) on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues (open+closed) for ''archive'' in developing-today/code returned no filing covering FileOps archive naming/collision. Adjacent: #1549 (web image-upload filename collision \u2014 different namespace/mechanism), #1605 (mcpx exec artifact overwrite \u2014 different component), #809 closed (classify_tag auto- prefix, unrelated). Lane A areas this phase (cli plain-text output #1611, tags search #1609, mcpx artifacts #1605) and lane B''s own (tuple decode #1610, tags value filter #1607) deliberately avoided.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:54:20Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"FileOps (and web archive_original_tag) name archives with a second-resolution timestamp and set them unconditionally, so same-second replaces of one name overwrite each other''s archives.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs:157 archive name is format!(\"{name}.archive.{ts}\") and :158-161 sets it unconditionally \u2014 no existence check or uniquifier","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1736-1739 now_unix() returns as_secs() \u2014 one-second resolution for every archive name","Laptop verbatim probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneB-archive/out.log): BUG same-second replaces -> archive_count=1, value HASH_A, V1 archive lost; CTRL one second apart -> archive_count=2, both kept","pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs:2175 archive_original_tag builds the same {name}.archive.{timestamp} name with as_secs() and set() on the document save path","pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs:388-410 delete enumerates archives by the <name>.archive.<digits> pattern \u2014 an overwritten archive is invisible to it"],"acceptance":["Archiving a replaced file never overwrites an existing archive: a distinct archive name is chosen when <name>.archive.<ts> is taken, staying inside the enumeration shape delete/classify_tag understand \u2014 or those enumerators are updated in the same change","The same fix (or a shared helper) covers archive_original_tag in web/routes.rs","Tests: two replaces of the same destination with the same timestamp produce two distinct archives holding the two distinct hashes; returned archived_replaced/archived_original names are the names actually written","Existing rename/copy/delete archive tests still pass; single-replace behaviour and common-case naming unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1612","pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs:153","pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs:238","pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs:319","pkgs/id/src/tags.rs:1735","pkgs/id/src/web/routes.rs:2170"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The archive is the promised safety net for rename/copy replaces; scripted renames and rapid web saves routinely replace the same name twice in one second, and the loss is silent \u2014 both operations report success and return identical archive names. Fix is a small naming/uniqueness change in fileops.rs plus its routes.rs sibling.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1612', '2026-10-28 06:55:11.957791+00', '2026-10-28 06:55:11.957791+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1721, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(vscode): normalize contextLines in gitService diff functions (#640)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/640","title":"fix(vscode): gitService hands git a fractional/NaN -U \u2014 getGitDiff throws and getGitRangeDiff silently returns an empty diff (the #578 defect in the VS Code port)","number":640,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:55:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the web git service (already normalized in #578)","bridge payload schema work beyond what the service normalization needs"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts getGitDiff and getGitRangeDiff contextLines normalization","regression tests alongside the existing gitService.*.test.js suites in packages/vscode/src"]},"tests":["targeted VS Code gitService tests run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches for ''contextLines vscode'', ''gitService context'', ''VS Code git diff context'' returned nothing; ''578 vscode'' returned only #578 itself, whose scope is the web service packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js and which does not touch packages/vscode.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:55:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"VS Code gitService passes contextLines to git unnormalized: getGitDiff throws on fractional/NaN/negative/Infinity values and getGitRangeDiff silently returns an empty diff.","evidence":["packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts:2561 \u2014 getGitDiff: if (typeof contextLines === ''number'') args.push(`-U${contextLines}`)","packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts:2598 \u2014 getGitRangeDiff: `-U${Math.max(0, contextLines)}`; Math.max(0, NaN) is NaN; :2599-2600 returns stdout with no exit-code check, so a git failure reads as an empty diff","packages/vscode/src/bridge-git-runtime.ts:277-286 \u2014 api:git/diff destructures contextLines via a TypeScript `as` cast, no runtime validation","packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:39-40 \u2014 the web service''s normalizeContextLines and its #578 comment (fractional -U2.9 / -UNaN rejected with exit 129)","Laptop probe ~/git/fleet/probe-vscode-git-context/probe.test.ts on main a9bfab99e: getGitDiff threw for 2.5/NaN/-5/Infinity; getGitRangeDiff returned diffLen=0 for 2.5/NaN, 140 for -5 (rescued by Math.max), 193 for valid 3"],"acceptance":["getGitDiff and getGitRangeDiff normalize contextLines: non-negative integers (incl. 0 and 1000000) pass unchanged; fractional, negative, NaN, Infinity and non-number values fall back to 3","Regression tests (VS Code gitService bun-test style, mocked vscode, temp repo) prove each bad value yields the same diff as the default-3 call for both functions, and valid 0/3 produce their exact hunks","No behavior change for current UI callers sending contextLines 3 or 1000000"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/640","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/578"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A range diff that silently reads as empty can make a reviewer conclude there are no changes when the read actually failed \u2014 a correctness hazard on a living surface (the VS Code Diff view). Latent today because UI callers send constants, which is exactly why #578 fixed the web twin in the service layer rather than at the transport boundary. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:640', '2026-10-28 06:56:11.565241+00', '2026-10-28 07:04:30.931744+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1722, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(vscode): normalize getGitLog maxCount in gitService (#641)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/641","title":"fix(vscode): getGitLog maxCount is judged by bare || \u2014 -5 returns the entire history unbounded, 2.5/Infinity throw a raw git fatal (the #463 defect in the VS Code port)","number":641,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the web git service (already guarded, #463)","contextLines normalization (tracked separately as #640, same file, independent function)"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts getGitLog maxCount normalization","regression tests alongside the existing gitService.*.test.js suites in packages/vscode/src"]},"tests":["targeted VS Code gitService tests run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches for ''maxCount vscode'', ''getGitLog maxCount'' and ''git log vscode unbounded'' returned nothing; #463 covers only the web endpoint/service and does not touch packages/vscode.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T06:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"VS Code getGitLog passes maxCount to git --max-count unnormalized: negative values are unbounded, fractional/non-numeric values throw a raw git fatal.","evidence":["packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts:3419 \u2014 const maxCount = options?.maxCount || 50; interpolated at :3424 and :3498 as --max-count=${maxCount}","packages/vscode/src/bridge-git-runtime.ts:575-587 \u2014 api:git/log destructures maxCount via a TypeScript `as` cast, no runtime validation","packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:6365 \u2014 the web service''s positive-integer guard from the #463 line of work","Laptop probes ~/git/fleet/probe-vscode-git-context/probe2.test.ts + probe3.test.ts on main a9bfab99e: -5 on 60 commits -> total 60 (unbounded); 2.5/Infinity/''abc'' -> threw fatal not-an-integer; 0/NaN -> 50 fallback; valid 2 -> 2, valid 50 -> 50"],"acceptance":["getGitLog normalizes maxCount: positive integers pass unchanged; fractional, negative, NaN, Infinity, zero and non-number values fall back to 50","Regression tests (VS Code gitService bun-test style, mocked vscode, temp repo) prove maxCount -5 on a >50-commit repo returns exactly 50 entries, fractional/Infinity return the default page instead of throwing, and valid 2 returns exactly 2","No behavior change for callers passing a positive integer or omitting maxCount"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/641","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/463","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/640"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A negative maxCount turns a bounded history read into an unbounded one on the extension host (the exact harm #463 was filed for on the web side), and fractional values fail the log view with a raw git fatal. Latent via today''s callers, which is why the house rule puts the guard in the service. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:641', '2026-10-28 07:00:26.226698+00', '2026-10-28 07:30:39.718145+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1723, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(peers): announced-name raw TSV output forgery — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1613","title":"id(peers): a peer''s announced name is printed raw \u2014 a newline in a gossip announcement forges extra TSV rows in id peers and the REPL","number":1613,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:12:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Announcement timestamp freshness/replay (that is #1552)","Tag claim/doc/group plain-text output (that is #1611; only the escaping convention must agree)","Signing announcements (explicitly out of scope, as in #1552)"],"include":["Announcement ingest paths (serve gossip receive, PeerDiscovery::update) if the ruling sanitizes/rejects at ingest","The three peers print sites (commands/peers.rs, commands/repl.rs peers and peers_on_node) if the ruling escapes at print","Round-trip tests pinning the probe cases (newline/tab/CR names, ordinary Unicode names unchanged)"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib (discovery/commands printer + ingest tests) on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''peers name tab newline output'', ''peer announcement name'', ''in:title peers'': only #1611 (sibling \u2014 local tag data, tokens() renderer, check_text validation; distinct surface), #1552 (announcement timestamp freshness/replay \u2014 different field and mechanism), #792 (unrelated). No existing issue covers announcement name rendering.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:12:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Peer announcement names \u2014 unsigned, remotely supplied strings \u2014 are stored, served, and printed raw in tab-separated peer listings, so a newline forges extra peer rows and a tab shifts columns in id peers and both REPL peers printers.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/discovery.rs:356-368 PeerAnnouncement name is an unconstrained Option<String>; discovery.rs:430-437 update() stores announcements verbatim","pkgs/id/src/commands/serve.rs:1278-1285 gossip receive postcard-decodes any announcement into PeerDiscovery with no validation; pkgs/id/src/commands/peers.rs:434-440 the CLI''s gossip collection does the same; announcements are unsigned (see #1552)","pkgs/id/src/protocol.rs:644-651 ListPeers handler returns stored announcements unchanged","pkgs/id/src/commands/peers.rs:191-199, commands/repl.rs:1043-1052, commands/repl.rs:1091-1106: three printers interpolate name raw into ''\\t''-joined println! rows","Laptop verbatim probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneA-peersout/out.log): forged newline name renders 2 peers as 3 lines in both printers with a fully-formed forged row; tab-only name yields 5 tab-separated fields instead of 4; control renders one clean row"],"acceptance":["A peer name containing LF, CR, or TAB can no longer produce extra rows or shifted columns in any of the three print sites (commands/peers.rs, REPL peers, REPL peers_on_node); the chosen ruling (ingest sanitize/reject, print escape, or both) is stated in the PR","Stored/served announcements and printed output agree: a ListPeers consumer cannot observe a name the printers would render differently, unless that is the explicit ruling","Tests: an announcement whose name carries newline/tab/CR round-trips ingest -> ListPeers -> both printers with exactly one row per peer and four fields per row; ordinary names (spaces, Unicode) display unchanged","The fix''s escaping/sanitizing convention is consistent with the #1611 plain-text output fix (cross-linked both ways)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1613","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1611","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1552","pkgs/id/src/discovery.rs:356","pkgs/id/src/commands/peers.rs:191","pkgs/id/src/commands/repl.rs:1043","pkgs/id/src/protocol.rs:644"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"id peers output is the operator/script view of who is on the network (node IDs, names, blob counts); the name is unsigned remote input, so one hostile gossip participant forges peer rows in every other node''s listing and corrupts TSV consumers. Ingest currently validates nothing, so the pin (ingest vs print) has protocol-wide reach but a small code surface.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1613', '2026-10-28 07:13:12.167875+00', '2026-10-28 07:13:12.167875+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1725, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(find/search): match-name path traversal on download — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1614","title":"id(find/search): a remote node''s match name becomes the download path verbatim \u2014 ../ and absolute names overwrite arbitrary files","number":1614,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:20:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["cmd_show/cmd_peek output handling (caller-specified output path / temp file \u2014 not response-named)","Compile staging containment (that was #1595, closed)","Blob tag semantics beyond the download-path ruling and any rename-side validation the triage chooses to include or split out"],"include":["The four find/search write sites in pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs (:237, :268, :280, :369) and a shared name-to-path helper if the fix introduces one","export_blob/to_absolute call contract if the ruling places containment there","Unit tests pinning the probe cases (../, nested traversal, absolute, control)"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib commands::find (path helper tests) on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''find traversal name output path'', ''path traversal'', ''in:title find download'': only CLOSED #1595 (world-compile sanitize_file_name containment \u2014 different subsystem, staging path not download path) and an unrelated lab-ops-hub issue. No existing issue covers find/search download paths.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:20:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"id find/search download writes use response-supplied match names as filesystem paths with no containment, so a remote node (or a store holding a traversal name) makes the client overwrite arbitrary user-writable files with fetched blob content.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs:901-913 cmd_find_matches returns the remote node''s FindMatch list verbatim; protocol.rs:131-143 name is an unconstrained String","pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs:268/:280 output = &m.name (the name IS the path); find.rs:237 and :369 format!(\"{}/{}\", dir_path, m.name) for --all --dir in cmd_find and cmd_search","pkgs/id/src/lib.rs:357-363 to_absolute performs no normalization; lib.rs:546-563 export_blob hands the path to iroh-blobs export, which create-or-truncates the target (iroh-blobs 0.103 fs.rs:1272,1277)","pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs:141-151 validate_target accepts any non-empty rename target, so honest stores can contain traversal names","Laptop verbatim probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneA-findpath/out.log), two independent runs: ../ and absolute names overwrote pre-existing files outside the requested location in all three cases; control stayed inside"],"acceptance":["A find/search match name can never cause a write outside the location the user asked for: single/first-match writes are confined to the invocation directory tree (or refused with a named error), and --all --dir writes stay inside the given directory after normalization \u2014 covering .., nested a/../../b, and absolute names at find.rs:237, :268, :280, :369","Existing files outside the permitted location are never truncated by a find/search download; the filed probe cases are pinned as tests at the path-construction/sanitizing helper (no network needed)","The ruling for names that are not a single safe segment is stated in the PR (refuse / final component / sanitize), including what happens to legitimate slash-bearing names rename currently accepts \u2014 that consequence is addressed or filed separately","Ordinary names (plain basenames, spaces, Unicode) download exactly as today in all modes, local and remote"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1614","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1595","pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs:237","pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs:268","pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs:369","pkgs/id/src/lib.rs:357","pkgs/id/src/lib.rs:546","pkgs/id/src/fileops.rs:141"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Remote arbitrary-file overwrite with attacker-controlled content, triggered by the documented id find <NODE> query flow: the victim names no output path and may not know the match name is hostile. Priority high; the code surface (four call sites + one helper) is small, but the naming ruling has rename/store compatibility consequences, so it goes through triage rather than a creator self-solve.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 30, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1614', '2026-10-28 07:21:12.391359+00', '2026-10-28 08:12:10.912151+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1726, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'Triage: branch-cleanup live daily run aborts on first failed deletion in code/opencode/openchamber (issue #1615)', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["branch-deletion"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1615","title":"branch-cleanup: one failed ''git push origin --delete'' aborts the live daily run \u2014 same unguarded loop in code, opencode, openchamber","number":1615,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:40:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Candidate criteria, inactivity window, and the 50-candidate all-or-nothing cap (deliberate design in PR #1464)","Open-PR head/base protection logic from PR #1586 and the checkout pin from PR #1580","dezren39/nix \u2014 already fixed via nix#1004"],"include":[".github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml deletion-loop failure handling and reporting in developing-today/code","The same workflow change ported to developing-today/opencode and developing-today/openchamber as one set tracked by code#1615"]},"tests":["Workflow simulation with a stubbed failing delete for a middle candidate: later candidates still attempted, failure named in summary","Dry-run output unchanged for the all-success case"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh search issues for branch-cleanup / ''push --delete'' in developing-today/code returned #1464, #1580, #1586 and unrelated items only; no issue covers deletion-failure handling in code/opencode/openchamber (searched 2026-10-28). nix#1004 covers only the nix copy and is closed/fixed.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:40:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"branch-cleanup''s deletion loop has no per-branch failure handling under set -e, so a single failed delete aborts the whole live daily run in code, opencode, and openchamber.","evidence":["code .github/workflows/branch-cleanup.yml:46 on main b2adaf47: ''set -euo pipefail''; :150-159 deletion loop with bare ''git push origin --delete \"$branch\"'' at :155, no guard or failure collection","opencode main 9ba2221f and openchamber main 93027f59: same workflow, set -e at :46, bare push --delete at :155 (verified via gh api contents this run)","PR #1493 body states BRANCH_CLEANUP_LIVE has been set to true and verified, and changes the schedule to daily \u2014 the loop performs live deletions every day","nix main (7c9a47bb) shows the fixed shape for the same workflow: ''elif git push origin --delete \"$branch\"; then \u2026 else # One failed deletion must not abort the run (#1004)'' with deleted/failed collection"],"acceptance":["A failed git push origin --delete for one candidate does not stop the run in code, opencode, or openchamber: remaining candidates are still attempted","Each failed deletion is reported by name in the log and step summary, with deleted/failed counts in the final summary","Partial failure is visible in the run outcome, not a clean full success","Dry-run behaviour, candidate criteria, open-PR head/base protections (PR #1586), checkout pin (PR #1580) and the 50-candidate cap unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1615","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1493","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1464","https://github.com/dezren39/nix/issues/1004"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Live daily deletion run in three repos: one undeletable branch (ruleset, concurrent delete, transient push error) blocks all later candidates indefinitely and the failure reads as a generic workflow failure.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1615', '2026-10-28 07:27:45.920844+00', '2026-10-28 07:27:45.920844+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1727, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): AutoSaveManager generic-error path drops coalesced follow-up — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1616","title":"id(web): AutoSaveManager''s generic-error path drops a coalesced follow-up \u2014 an edit made during a failed save is never autosaved","number":1616,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:27:28Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to the 429 retry/backoff semantics or the debounce interval","Changes to saveNow/onNewVersion behaviour beyond what the pinned error-path semantics require","Server-side save endpoint changes"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.ts onSaveResult generic-error path (follow-up handling + followUpRequested clearing)","pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.test.ts generic-error follow-up test"]},"tests":["bun/vitest auto-save.test.ts in pkgs/id/web on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for auto-save/autosave follow-up/error returned only #1440 CLOSED (concurrent saves + stale completion + 429 serialization \u2014 its tests cover the ok and 429 follow-up shapes, no generic-error case). #1368 is the collab reconnect cap, a different module/mechanism. Lane A areas this phase (peers name #1613, cli plain-text output #1611, tags search #1609, mcpx artifacts #1605) and lane B''s own (archive #1612, tags value filter #1607) deliberately avoided \u2014 this is the freshly merged #1440 autosave code, a different area.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:27:28Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"AutoSaveManager''s generic-error result path drops a follow-up save coalesced during the failed save, stranding that edit unsaved with no save ever scheduled for it.","evidence":["pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.ts:124-128 triggerSave coalesces an in-flight save request into followUpRequested=true and returns; the requesting debounce is consumed","pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.ts:162-168 ok branch runs exactly one follow-up when followUpRequested or the generation moved; :180-191 rate-limit branch schedules a retry that the comment says also serves as the follow-up","pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.ts:192-206 generic-error branch only sets state error and a 2s reset to unsaved \u2014 no follow-up, no re-armed debounce, followUpRequested left set","Laptop probe driving the real auto-save.ts (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneB-autosave/out.log, two identical runs): CTRL-OK afterSettle=2 followUpRan=true; CTRL-429 afterSettle=2 followUpRan=true; BUG-ERROR afterSettle=1 final=1 state=unsaved followUpRan=false"],"acceptance":["Generic-error follow-up semantics pinned in a test first: an edit arriving during a save whose debounce fires before that save fails generically is not stranded \u2014 exactly one subsequent save attempt (follow-up or re-armed debounce), OR a deliberate, tested no-auto-retry pin where the follow-up request is visibly dropped and followUpRequested is cleared","If a follow-up is implemented it is bounded: one attempt, a second generic failure stops again (no retry loop on a persistent outage); followUpRequested is cleared on every onSaveResult path","New auto-save.test.ts case mirroring the ok/429 serialization tests for the generic-error shape (deferred saveFn, edit + debounce during flight, resolve {ok:false})","Existing auto-save tests (serialization, stale completion, 429 coalescing, saveNow) still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1616","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1440","pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.ts:124","pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.ts:160","pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.ts:192","pkgs/id/web/src/auto-save.test.ts"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Autosave silently stopping for an edit after one transient failure breaks the #1440 contract that requested saves are never lost; the only signal (button reverting to ''save \u2022'') is indistinguishable from a pending debounce, so a user can close the tab believing the edit was autosaved. Fix is small and local to auto-save.ts plus one test.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1616', '2026-10-28 07:29:23.187843+00', '2026-10-28 07:29:23.187843+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1729, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(find): remote find 64 KiB response cap — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1617","title":"id(find): remote find fails outright past ~1k matches \u2014 server returns all matches unbounded, both clients cap the response at 64 KiB","number":1617,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:33:25Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changes to match ranking, match_kind semantics, or local find behaviour","Changes to the Find wire format unless triage pins paging/truncation as the shape"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs cmd_find_matches response bound","pkgs/id/src/commands/repl.rs ReplContext::find response bound (or a shared helper for both)","Optionally pkgs/id/src/protocol.rs find() server-side cap/paging if that shape is pinned","Test with a synthetic Find response above 64 KiB"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib (protocol/find/repl tests) on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for remote find response size / 64 KiB / matches returned no covering filing. #1614 is the remote find download-path defect (match name as filesystem path) \u2014 same command family, different mechanism, cross-linked in the issue. #1616 (autosave) and lane A/lane B recent filings are unrelated areas.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:33:25Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Remote find/search fails outright once the unbounded server Find response exceeds the 64 KiB read cap hard-coded at both client call sites (~874-1490 matches).","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/protocol.rs:661-695 server find() collects all matches, no limit; protocol.rs:719-724 writes the whole response with no size gate","pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs:907 and pkgs/id/src/commands/repl.rs:706 both read the Find response with read_to_end(64 * 1024); local find (find.rs local branch) iterates the store with no cap","Contrast within the same protocol: List read at 1 MiB (commands/list.rs:81,147); unified MetaClient MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES = 64 MiB (meta_client.rs:28,54)","Laptop postcard probe (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneB-findcap/out.log): one match 45 bytes; >64 KiB first exceeded at 1490 / 1192 / 874 matches for 9 / 20 / 40-byte names"],"acceptance":["Remote find/search succeeds against a node returning a Find response larger than 64 KiB \u2014 read cap raised to a named bound consistent with the other meta-protocol clients (1 MiB like List, or MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES via the unified client), or the response is paged/capped server-side with truncation signalled to the client","Both call sites covered (CLI cmd_find_matches find.rs and REPL ReplContext::find repl.rs), ideally via one shared request helper/bound so they cannot drift again","Any remaining cap errors by name (find response too large / results truncated), not as a bare transport read error","Test pins the behaviour with a synthetic Find response above 64 KiB (or above the new bound); local find/search behaviour and ordering unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1617","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1614","pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs:907","pkgs/id/src/commands/repl.rs:706","pkgs/id/src/protocol.rs:661","pkgs/id/src/meta_client.rs:28"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Find/search are the remote discovery verbs; a remote namespace past ~1k matching files becomes unsearchable from both the CLI and the REPL, and the failure presents as a transport error while local search and list keep working. The bound already exists in three inconsistent sizes across the same protocol, so the fix is a small consistency change plus a test.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1617', '2026-10-28 07:34:13.002798+00', '2026-10-28 07:34:13.002798+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1730, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #686: make WebSearch cooldownMillis reject hex/exponent retry-after spellings', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/686","title":"fix(core): WebSearch retry-after cooldown reinterprets hex and exponent spellings \u2014 ''1e3'' sidelines a provider for 16 minutes instead of the 60s fallback","number":686,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:42:28Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["The RequestExecutor retry-after parser in packages/ai (tracked separately as #682)","Plain delay-seconds values, however large \u2014 those are authored instructions under RFC 9110"],"include":["packages/core/src/websearch.ts cooldownMillis grammar guard","Regression tests (packages/core/test/plugin/websearch.test.ts or a unit test of an exported parser)"]},"tests":["bun test test/plugin/websearch.test.ts (via CI, from packages/core)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''websearch cooldown'', ''retry-after websearch'' and ''cooldownMillis'' on 2026-10-28: no hits. #682 covers packages/ai executor.ts only.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:42:28Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"cooldownMillis accepts Number()''s full grammar for a retry-after header: hex and exponent spellings are honoured at face value instead of taking the 60-second fallback for unusable values.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe running the verbatim cooldownMillis body (websearch.ts md5 76bf041b0ba345521fa2fd1c49f1fbc3, byte-identical to main 771d1bd0cc; probe at laptop ~/git/fleet/probe-2026-10-28-0235/probe.ts, removed after): ''1e3'' -> 1000000 ms, ''0x10'' -> 16000 ms; controls ''7'' -> 7000, '' 12 '' -> 12000, ''-5'' -> 60000, ''garbage'' -> 60000, HTTP-date 90s ahead -> 90000, absent/'''' -> 60000"],"acceptance":["retry-after values that are not plain unsigned decimal integers and not HTTP-dates take the 60-second fallback \u2014 at minimum hex (0x10) and exponent (1e3) forms","Authored plain values unchanged: ''0'', ''7'', '' 12 '', negative-to-fallback, and HTTP-date forms behave as today","Regression tests cover 1e3 and 0x10 plus plain-value and HTTP-date controls","The accepted grammar is stated in a comment at the parse site"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/686","packages/core/src/websearch.ts:204,215-221 cooldownMillis and its 429 call site","packages/core/src/websearch.ts:160-172 randomProvider cooldown exclusion","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/682 \u2014 same grammar hole in the ai executor parser, separate code path"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"An invented 16.7-minute cooldown shrinks the random-mode web-search provider pool far beyond what the provider asked for, but only on a 429 carrying a non-standard numeric spelling, so reachability is narrow. One-function fix mirroring the grammar decision already made for the executor parser in #682.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:686', '2026-10-28 07:43:13.529564+00', '2026-10-28 09:41:19.439168+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1731, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #687: make SpeechStream.headerUsage reject blank, negative and non-plain usage headers', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/687","title":"fix(ai): SpeechStream.headerUsage manufactures usage from blank and negative headers \u2014 '''' reads as 0 characters, ''-5'' as -5 credits","number":687,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:44:17Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Sample-rate parsing in the speech protocols (regex-guarded to plain digits)","Usage accounting downstream of the finish event"],"include":["packages/ai/src/protocols/utils/speech-stream.ts headerUsage blank/negative/grammar handling","Regression tests in packages/ai/test/ speech protocol tests"]},"tests":["bun test (speech protocol tests) via CI, from packages/ai"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''headerUsage'', ''speech usage header'', ''char-count'' and ''character-cost'' on 2026-10-28: no relevant hits (char-count hits were MessagingLog/truncate issues).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:44:17Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"headerUsage accepts any finite Number() result: blank strings become a reported 0 usage, negatives become negative usage, and hex/exponent spellings are reinterpreted as counts.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe importing the exported SpeechStream.headerUsage from the real module (speech-stream.ts md5 b927177d1563b6db9199c0180508e382, byte-identical to main 771d1bd0cc; probe at laptop ~/git/fleet/probe-2026-10-28-0235/probe.ts, removed after): '''' -> {characters: 0}, ''   '' -> {characters: 0}, ''-5'' -> {characters: -5} / {credits: -5}, ''1e3'' -> {characters: 1000}, ''0x10'' -> {characters: 16}; controls ''42'' -> 42, ''0'' -> 0, ''abc'' -> undefined, undefined -> undefined"],"acceptance":["Blank or whitespace-only header values return undefined (no usage) for both characters and credits","Negative amounts return undefined; an authored ''0'' still returns a zero usage","Values outside a plain non-negative decimal grammar (at minimum 0x10 and 1e3) return undefined","Plain values unchanged: ''42'' -> 42, ''0'' -> 0","Regression tests cover blank, negative, hex and exponent inputs plus the plain controls"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/687","packages/ai/src/protocols/utils/speech-stream.ts:106-110 headerUsage and :84-103 the finish event it feeds","packages/ai/src/protocols/deepgram-speech.ts:118 dg-char-count caller","packages/ai/src/protocols/elevenlabs-speech.ts:179-180 character-cost caller (billed credits)"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Fabricated zero or negative billed usage corrupts cost/usage accounting for speech calls, but only when a provider/gateway sends a blank, negative or non-plain header, so reachability is narrow. One-function fix with an existing undefined fallback to return to.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:687', '2026-10-28 07:44:59.228827+00', '2026-10-28 09:33:04.232882+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1732, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): collab unvalidated steps poison document history — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1618","title":"id(web): collab server stores and broadcasts steps it never validates \u2014 one bad step poisons the document''s history and loops every client","number":1618,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:45:46Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Cursor/auth/name collab messages (only the Steps path and its catch-up replay)","The saved-file/autosave path (unaffected \u2014 the poison lives only in the in-memory Document history)","A full server-side ProseMirror implementation beyond what the chosen validation design needs"],"include":["Steps handling in pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs (decode, handler store/version/broadcast/Ack, catch-up replay)","Client Update failure handling in pkgs/id/web/src/collab.ts if triage chooses the terminal-error half of the fix","Tests pinning the probe cases (bogus stepType, unknown slice node, out-of-range replace, non-object step, valid control)"]},"tests":["cargo test --lib web::collab on the laptop or CI \u2014 no sandbox builds","web unit tests (vitest) if the client terminal-error path changes"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''collab steps validate'' and ''collab poison'' returned no covering issue (only the unrelated closed validation-audit #1075); backlog notes cover collab sendQueue/reconnect-cap (#1368) and cursor client_id parsing, not step validation or history poisoning.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:45:46Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"The collab server stores, versions, broadcasts and catch-up-replays ProseMirror steps it never validates, so a single unparseable or unappliable step poisons the shared history and puts every client into an endless reconnect loop.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs:164-169 Step is a flattened serde_json::Value with no validation; :536-545 decode accepts any Vec<serde_json::Value> as steps","pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs:1019-1052 handler stores all steps, bumps version by steps.len(), broadcasts Update and Acks \u2014 no parse/apply anywhere in the path","pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs:787-810 catch-up replays all stored steps to each new joiner; :694-755 anonymous clients proceed and may send Steps","pkgs/id/web/src/collab.ts:278-293 Step.fromJSON/receiveTransaction throw on invalid steps; the catch closes with 4001 and scheduleReconnect()s into the same catch-up","Laptop probes (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneA-collabsteps/out.log + out-rs.log): server decode Ok for bogus/range/non-object steps; client fromJSON throws (bogus type, unknown node), receiveTransaction throws (position 999999 out of range), control valid step applies and receives cleanly"],"acceptance":["A Steps frame containing a step that does not parse against the document''s schema, or does not apply to the document at the frame''s version, is refused (Error to the sender, no Ack): nothing is stored, the version does not advance, and nothing is broadcast","Validation is against the server''s actual document state (base doc + previously accepted steps) or an equivalent server-side model \u2014 a purely syntactic/shape check that still admits an out-of-range replace does not satisfy this","Valid multi-step frames from a client at the current version keep working exactly as today (stored, version += n, broadcast, Ack), pinned by a test alongside the refusal cases (bogus stepType, unknown node in slice, out-of-range positions, non-object step)","A client that somehow still receives an unappliable step does not loop forever on the same history: the reconnect path distinguishes a poisoned catch-up and surfaces a terminal error for that document, or the server-side guarantee is documented as the sole line of defence with a test that a poisoned history cannot be created","Validation applies before storage for authenticated and anonymous senders alike"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1618","pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs:164","pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs:536","pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs:787","pkgs/id/src/web/collab.rs:986","pkgs/id/web/src/collab.ts:278"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"One invalid step \u2014 from an anonymous, buggy or version-skewed client \u2014 permanently poisons a document session: every current client is thrown into a reconnect loop and every future joiner replays the poison in catch-up, making the document uneditable for the life of the server-side Document. Priority normal (local collab surface, no data loss \u2014 the saved file is unaffected; the live session is denied). The fix is an architecture choice (the server has no ProseMirror step model today), so it goes through triage rather than a creator self-solve.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 50, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1618', '2026-10-28 07:46:36.478351+00', '2026-10-28 07:46:36.478351+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1734, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(ci): bench-compare unit comparability — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1619","title":"id(ci): bench-compare compares medians across different units \u2014 a unit change masks a real regression as -99.8% ok (and a zero baseline prints +inf%)","number":1619,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:52:59Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Making the bench workflow blocking/gating","Changing harness units or baseline values in pkgs/id/benches","Changing the >20% default threshold semantics for same-unit comparisons"],"include":[".github/scripts/id-bench-compare.sh unit-comparability check, zero-baseline handling, threshold validation","A fixture/test for the compare script covering unit mismatch + zero baseline","Optionally pkgs/id/benches/BASELINES.md note on unit changes at re-baseline time"]},"tests":["Run the compare script against fixture baseline/current pairs (unit mismatch, zero baseline, same-unit regression, not-run, no-baseline) \u2014 shell/awk only, no heavy builds"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for bench compare / unit / id-bench returned only #1403/#1404 (harness defects in world_bench itself, different mechanism), #539/#1512/#1513 (the closed F11.8 slices that built this reporting). No covering filing for the compare script''s unit handling.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:52:59Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"id-bench-compare.sh compares medians across differing units, prints +inf% for a zero baseline, and silently disables flagging for a non-numeric threshold env var.","evidence":[".github/scripts/id-bench-compare.sh parse (lines 48-62) stores unit[name] per side; percent computation and row printing use raw medians and base_unit only \u2014 cur_unit is used only for no-baseline rows","Probe on main 2617b73a (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneB-benchunit/out.log): alpha 100 us_per_event -> 0.200 ms_per_event reported ''-99.8% ok'' (real change +100%); tiny baseline median=0.000 -> current 0.400 reported ''+inf%'' regression; BENCH_REGRESSION_THRESHOLD_PCT=abc -> no rows flagged, summary ''No benchmark regressed more than abc%''","pkgs/id/benches/world_bench.rs:249-270 units are per-benchmark literals (us_per_append/us_per_compact/us_per_event/us_per_delivery); line 76 prints median with {:.3} formatting so a fast bench rounds to 0.000"],"acceptance":["Unit-mismatched benchmark rows are reported as incomparable: both units shown, no percent change, no ok/regression verdict, and the summary explicitly calls out the unit change","A zero baseline median never yields +inf%/-inf%/nan%; it is reported as incomparable (or by a documented rule)","A non-numeric BENCH_REGRESSION_THRESHOLD_PCT is rejected with a clear message, never silently treated as flag-nothing","Same-unit comparisons, not-run and no-baseline rows behave exactly as before; script still exits 0 for missing files / no regressions (non-blocking design preserved)","A test or fixture covers the unit-mismatch and zero-baseline cases"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1619","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1513",".github/scripts/id-bench-compare.sh",".github/workflows/id-bench.yml","pkgs/id/benches/world_bench.rs:249","pkgs/id/benches/BASELINES.md"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"This report is the only regression signal for the F11.8 benchmarks and is deliberately non-blocking, so its value is entirely that its printed verdicts can be trusted. A harness unit rescale \u2014 exactly the kind of change a benchmark PR makes before re-baselining \u2014 currently produces a confident wrong verdict in both directions and mislabels the current value''s unit.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1619', '2026-10-28 07:53:46.508453+00', '2026-10-28 07:53:46.508453+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1735, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(vscode): range functions throw on bad refs in gitService (#644)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/644","title":"fix(vscode): gitService range functions report a bad ref as ''no changes'' \u2014 getGitRangeDiff/getGitRangeFiles swallow git''s exit code, unlike the web service (#640 remainder)","number":644,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:54:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the web git service (already throws, correct)","contextLines/maxCount normalization (closed as #640/#641)"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts getGitRangeDiff + getGitRangeFiles exit-code/ref handling","regression tests alongside the existing gitService.*.test.js suites in packages/vscode/src","api:git/pr-description caller error wording if needed"]},"tests":["targeted VS Code gitService tests run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches for ''range diff silently'', ''getGitRangeDiff vscode'', ''range refs resolve vscode'', ''empty diff bad ref'' and ''RangeFiles empty'' returned only #640 (contextLines scope; PR #642 touched only the two -U sites) and older web-side context-parsing issues #464/#465 \u2014 none covers the VS Code range functions'' exit-code/ref handling.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:54:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"VS Code getGitRangeDiff/getGitRangeFiles swallow git failures and missing refs, returning empty results indistinguishable from a legitimately empty range.","evidence":["packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts:2611-2612 \u2014 getGitRangeDiff returns result.stdout with no exit-code check, stderr discarded","packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts:2596-2598 \u2014 empty base/head returns {diff:''''}; :2625-2627 + :2641 \u2014 getGitRangeFiles returns [] for empty refs and for any non-zero exit","packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts:2577-2579 \u2014 sibling getGitDiff throws on non-zero exit","packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:3527-3532, :3585, :3721, :3724 \u2014 web getRangeDiff/getRangeFiles throw on missing and unresolvable refs","Laptop probe ~/git/fleet/probe-vscode-range-silent/probe.test.ts on main 78b9639f8: bad base/bad head/empty base -> {diff:''''} and [] with NO THROW, identical to the legitimate main..main empty range; good range returned the change and [file.txt]"],"acceptance":["getGitRangeDiff throws on non-zero git exit and on empty base/head; a legitimately empty range still returns {diff:''''}","getGitRangeFiles throws on non-zero git exit and on empty base/head; a legitimately empty range still returns []","The origin/<base> resolution preference in both functions is preserved","Regression tests (VS Code gitService bun-test style, mocked vscode, temp repo) prove bad base, bad head and empty base/head reject for both functions, and good/empty ranges keep their current values","api:git/pr-description keeps working and a failed range read no longer surfaces as ''No diffs available for base...head''"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/644","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/640"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"A deleted, renamed, or unfetched base branch silently reads as an empty comparison in the VS Code host, and the PR-description flow misreports it as ''No diffs available'' \u2014 a correctness hazard for reviewers, at web-parity scope. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:644', '2026-10-28 07:55:21.393043+00', '2026-10-28 09:10:26.485621+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1736, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'fix(vscode): getCommitFiles throws on a bad hash in gitService (#645)', '{"prs":[],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/645","title":"fix(vscode): getCommitFiles reports a bad hash as an empty commit \u2014 git show failure returns {files: []} instead of throwing, unlike the web service and its own sibling (#644 sibling)","number":645,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:58:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["the web git service (already validates, correct)","the range functions (tracked separately as #644, same file, independent functions)"],"include":["packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts getCommitFiles exit-code/hash handling","regression tests alongside the existing gitService.*.test.js suites in packages/vscode/src"]},"tests":["targeted VS Code gitService tests run on laptop or CI, not the sandbox"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue searches for ''getCommitFiles vscode'', ''commit files silently empty'' and ''bad hash commit files'' returned no covering issue; #644 covers only the range functions getGitRangeDiff/getGitRangeFiles.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T07:58:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"VS Code getCommitFiles swallows git show failures, returning an empty file list for bad, stale, or empty hashes \u2014 indistinguishable from a genuinely empty commit.","evidence":["packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts:3615-3620 \u2014 getCommitFiles returns {files: []} on any non-zero git show exit, stderr discarded, no hash validation","packages/vscode/src/bridge-git-runtime.ts:587-594 \u2014 api:git/commit-files checks only non-empty hash, returns success:true with the service result","packages/web/server/lib/git/service.js:6701-6703 + :6718 \u2014 web resolveCommitHash validates/verifies the hash and getCommitFiles lets failures throw","packages/vscode/src/gitService.ts:3667+ \u2014 sibling getCommitFileDiff throws ''Failed to read file content at commit <hash>'' for a bad hash","Laptop probes ~/git/fleet/probe-vscode-range-silent/probe2.test.ts + probe3.test.ts on main 78b9639f8: bad/nonsense/empty hash -> {files: []} NO THROW; good hash -> the changed file; root commit -> its added file; bad-hash file-diff -> THREW"],"acceptance":["getCommitFiles throws on non-zero git exit and on an empty/missing hash instead of returning {files: []}","Valid, root, and genuinely empty (--allow-empty) commits return exactly what they return today","Regression tests (VS Code gitService bun-test style, mocked vscode, temp repo) prove bad and empty hashes reject and the valid cases are unchanged","api:git/commit-files surfaces the throw as a failed bridge response, not success:true with an empty list"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/645","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/644"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"The commit view is a review surface: a stale or unresolvable hash currently renders as ''this commit changed nothing'' under a success response instead of an actionable error. Web-parity, small scope. Normal priority.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 70, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:645', '2026-10-28 07:59:26.953565+00', '2026-10-28 09:40:10.044369+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1737, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(outbox): parseable torn tail accepted then merged into next record — small fix #1620', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1620","title":"id(outbox): a parseable torn tail is accepted, then merged into the next record \u2014 Outbox::open only drops unterminated final lines that fail to parse","number":1620,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:08:49Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing FileJournal/ArtifactLog/Directory/GroupLog/Petnames torn-tail semantics (separate filings #1499/#1521/#1522/#1523)","Recovering or migrating already-merged two-records-on-one-line files written by the buggy path (out of scope; may be noted as a follow-up)"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/envelope_outbox.rs Outbox::open: drop + truncate any unterminated final line regardless of parseability","envelope_outbox tests: parseable-unterminated-tail regression test"]},"tests":["cargo test envelope_outbox module (via CI or laptop \u2014 no sandbox builds)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for ''outbox unterminated'', ''outbox torn'', ''envelope outbox'': only #1499, #1521, #1522, #1523, #1544, #1294, #439 \u2014 #1499/#1522 cite the Outbox as the correct sibling for unparseable tails; none covers acceptance of a parseable unterminated tail in the Outbox itself.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:08:49Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Outbox::open accepts a parseable unterminated final line instead of dropping it as torn, so the next append merges two records onto one line and the outbox fails to load thereafter.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/envelope_outbox.rs:141-157 replay loop over split_inclusive(''\\n''): parse success applies the record and kept += line.len() (:146) regardless of newline termination; torn-drop only on parse error (:148); kept == text.len() means no truncation","pkgs/id/src/envelope_outbox.rs:278-289 commit() appends record + ''\\n'' with OpenOptions::append and no leading newline, so the next record concatenates onto an unterminated line","pkgs/id/src/artifact.rs:565-583 ArtifactLog::open doc + code: a final line cut short by a crash ''was never synced, so it is dropped'' \u2014 truncation to last ''\\n'' happens before parsing, parseability irrelevant","pkgs/id/src/directory.rs:512-526 (#1521 fix): torn final fragment dropped ''parseable or not'', warned, truncated","pkgs/id/src/envelope_outbox.rs:523 existing torn-tail test covers only an unparseable fragment ({\"op\":\"queued\",\"target\"); concatenation demonstration this run: complete-JSON fragment + appended record line fails single-record JSON parse (''Extra data'')","Verified on main 1658679c this run (code read + JSON concatenation check; no sandbox build per execution-host rule)"],"acceptance":["Outbox::open drops an unterminated final line whether or not it parses, and truncates the file to the last complete (newline-terminated) line, matching ArtifactLog::open / directory replay semantics","After recovery, a subsequent commit() appends cleanly: reopening succeeds and contains exactly the pre-crash complete records plus the new one","A corrupt complete (newline-terminated) line still fails the load (existing test a_corrupt_complete_line_stops_the_load keeps passing)","New regression test: final line is a complete JSON record missing only its trailing \\n; open drops it, file truncated, following enqueue round-trips through a reopen","Existing outbox tests pass, including a_torn_last_line_is_dropped_and_not_mixed_into_the_next_record"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1620","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1521","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1499","pkgs/id/src/envelope_outbox.rs:130-165","pkgs/id/src/envelope_outbox.rs:278-289","pkgs/id/src/artifact.rs:565-583","pkgs/id/src/directory.rs:512-526"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"One unlucky crash silently accepts an unacknowledged outbox record, then permanently bricks the durable delivery queue on the next append + restart, with a corrupt-line error that hides the torn-tail cause.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1620', '2026-10-28 08:10:04.522739+00', '2026-10-28 08:10:04.522739+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1738, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(find/search): confine download writes to the match name''s final component (fix #1614)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":["security"],"level":"medium"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1614","title":"id(find/search): a remote node''s match name becomes the download path verbatim \u2014 ../ and absolute names overwrite arbitrary files","number":1614,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:36:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Store-side rename validation (filed as #1621)","cmd_show/cmd_peek output handling (already NamedTempFile-safe)","Wire protocol / FindMatch shape changes","Sanitizing names at ingestion in honest stores"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs: the four write-path sites routed through one sanitizing path helper","Unit tests for the helper covering the probe cases"]},"tests":["cargo test in pkgs/id via CI on the PR (fleet CI-first policy)","Helper unit tests: traversal names confined to final component, no-component names refused, ordinary names byte-identical"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Implementation follow-up enqueued by triage task 1725 on issue #1614; fix dedupe key distinct from the triage identity; no PR addresses #1614 (checked 2026-10-28).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:38:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"id find/search use a find match''s name verbatim as the download write path. In remote mode both the name and blob content come from the queried node, so ../ and absolute match names overwrite arbitrary local files (create-or-truncate, no containment). Verified by probe on main (issue #1614) and re-verified at triage on main a9c85406.","evidence":["pkgs/id/src/commands/find.rs: cmd_find_matches postcard-decodes MetaResponse::Find unchecked (~line 901-913); single/first-match output = &m.name (lines 268, 280); --all --dir output_path = format!(\"{}/{}\", dir, name) (cmd_find ~line 237, cmd_search ~line 369)","pkgs/id/src/protocol.rs: FindMatch.name is a plain String (lines 131-143)","pkgs/id/src/lib.rs: export_blob (546-563) -> to_absolute (357-363, cwd-prepend only, no normalization) -> iroh-blobs export, create-or-truncate with no containment check","Probe (lane A, 2026-10-28, hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneA-findpath/): --dir ../victim.txt, single-match absolute name, and single-match ../ all overwrote pre-existing files outside the target; control plain.txt stayed inside","Triage task 1725 re-verified every cited site verbatim on main a9c85406 (laptop primary clone) 2026-10-28T08:36Z","Rename-side consequence filed separately as issue #1621 (fileops validate_target accepts traversal names)"],"acceptance":["Every find/search download write (cmd_find single/first/--all --dir, cmd_search --all --dir) goes through ONE path-construction helper that derives the write path from the match name''s final path component only (Path::file_name ruling, per triage verdict on #1614); a name with no final component (.., /, trailing separator, empty) is refused with a clear error and writes nothing","Ordinary single-segment names produce byte-identical paths and behaviour in all modes (local and remote)","Unit tests at the helper pin the probe cases: ../victim.txt, ../../x, absolute /tmp/x, plain.txt control, .. refusal, trailing-slash refusal","cmd_peek/cmd_show behaviour unchanged; no change to the wire protocol or FindMatch shape","Full pkgs/id test suite green via CI on the PR (fleet CI-first policy); PR body states the final-component ruling"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1614","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1621"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"priority/high security: a queried remote node can overwrite arbitrary files on the machine running id find/search; fix is small, local, and fully specified by triage.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'done', 20, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1614', '2026-10-28 08:11:28.434404+00', '2026-10-28 10:55:23.896814+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1740, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: proposal expiry clock — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1623","title":"aggregator: proposal expiry is clocked from the delegation''s updatedAt, not the proposal''s draft time \u2014 a 72h-old proposal stays approvable, a 1h-old one reads expired","number":1623,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:35:25Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing the 48h TTL value","Changing the proposal identity triple (item id, runId, updatedAt) used for supersede checks","Publisher-side changes outside pm-stack/aggregator"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/tier-items.ts proposalExpired clock (and any doc comment that names the clock)","Regression tests in pm-stack/aggregator/test/needs-user.test.ts for both divergent-timestamp cases"]},"tests":["Bun test: pm-stack/aggregator/test/needs-user.test.ts (proposal identity + expiry describe) \u2014 light TS tests, laptop or CI"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for proposal expiry/TTL returned only mcpx #1601 (unrelated ttlMs design). #1486 is yes/no answer validation in the same file (different check); #1541/#1564/#1568 are generatedAt/measuredAt freshness gates in other modules. No covering filing for the delegation proposal TTL clock.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:35:25Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"proposalExpired clocks the #1293 proposal TTL from delegation updatedAt instead of proposal.at, so divergent timestamps make stale proposals approvable and fresh proposals expired.","evidence":["tier-items.ts:306-310 proposalExpired uses Date.parse(d.updatedAt); proposal.at is never read by the expiry path","tier-items.ts:46-47 TTL doc: ''A first-pass proposal older than this renders expired (#1293)'' \u2014 the proposal''s age; tier-items.ts:168-169 sanitizer validates and keeps proposal.at independently of updatedAt (:153-154)","Probe on main 9752a47b (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneB-proposalttl/out.log), real sanitizer + real checkActionAgainstItem: BUG-A proposal.at=72h, updatedAt=1h -> expired=false, approve returns null (accepted); BUG-B proposal.at=1h, updatedAt=72h -> expired=true, approve refused ''this proposal has expired''; controls equal-timestamp 1h/72h correct; confirmed in two independent probe runs"],"acceptance":["proposalExpired measures the proposal''s age from proposal.at (or, if triage pins updatedAt instead, the TTL comment, render text and identity docs are updated to say so explicitly and the divergence is removed or explained)","Regression tests in pm-stack/aggregator/test/needs-user.test.ts cover both divergent cases: old proposal.at + fresh updatedAt (expired; approve refused) and fresh proposal.at + old updatedAt (not expired; approve passes the expiry gate), plus the existing equal-timestamp controls","checkActionAgainstItem approve/reject behaviour matches the pinned clock in both cases","Existing aggregator test suites still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1623","pm-stack/aggregator/src/tier-items.ts:306","pm-stack/aggregator/src/tier-items.ts:46","pm-stack/aggregator/src/model.ts:532","pm-stack/aggregator/src/render.ts:1035"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The 48h TTL is the only guard stopping approval of a stale first-pass proposal, and approval is the dashboard action that applies a drafted change on the next orchestration pass. Clocking it from a state timestamp a re-publish can refresh defeats it silently, while the UI displays the true draft date beside the wrong verdict.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1623', '2026-10-28 08:36:25.347857+00', '2026-10-28 08:36:25.347857+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1741, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: gatherer snapshot dedup credential key — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1624","title":"aggregator: quota gatherer snapshot dedup ignores credentialId \u2014 two ok credentials of one provider interleave into one series and append an alternating noise point every tick","number":1624,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:39:28Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing SnapshotRecord''s shape without a documented series rule (any shape change must be the pinned triage outcome)","Changing provider fetching or credential reading in gather-quota.ts","Backfilling or cleaning existing snapshot stores"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-gather-map.ts recordsFromEntries dedup key / same-tick handling (and SnapshotRecord keying if triage pins credential-distinguished series)","Regression tests for the two-credential constant case over >=3 ticks plus single-credential controls"]},"tests":["Bun tests for recordsFromEntries in pm-stack/aggregator/test (quota-gather-map coverage) \u2014 light TS tests, laptop or CI"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for recordsFromEntries / gather-quota credential snapshot returned only feature/epic items (#1112, #1151, #1268, #1047, #1189) \u2014 no defect filing for the dedup key. #1540 is SnapshotStore append-time validation (different layer); #1560 is the registry merge (different module).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:39:28Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"recordsFromEntries dedups snapshot records by serviceId|window while the gatherer emits one entry per credential, so two ok credentials interleave into one series and append alternating noise points every tick.","evidence":["quota-gather-map.ts:254 dedup key is serviceId|window; :256 compares against the input lastAppended map only; entry.credentialId is set at :188 and never used by the dedup","gather-quota.ts runProvider maps fetchQuotaForProviderInstances results (one per credential) through entryFromResult; state merge at :339 flips the stored stamp between credentials each tick","Probe on main 9752a47b (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneB-gatherdedup/out.log), real recordsFromEntries + caller merge replicated: two ok creds constant 10/20 -> appends 2,1,1,1 over ticks 1-4 alternating; single-cred control 1,0,0 and a 10->15 move appends exactly 1; confirmed in two independent runs"],"acceptance":["With two ok credentials of one provider in a tick and unchanged values across ticks, no per-tick noise is appended: either the dedup/series key distinguishes credentials (and the record/series shape documents that), or the per-provider series rule is explicit and only one deterministic reading per serviceId+window is recorded per tick \u2014 pinned by a test","Tick 1 with two ok credentials no longer appends two contradictory points for the same series at the same timestamp (or the two points are credential-distinguishable, per the pinned rule)","Regression tests cover: two-credential constant values over >=3 ticks (no alternating appends), single-credential constant case (append once), genuine value move (append once)","Existing aggregator test suites still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1624","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-gather-map.ts:243","pm-stack/aggregator/scripts/gather-quota.ts:322","pm-stack/aggregator/src/model.ts:1256"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The snapshot store is the hub''s long-term usage series and is append-on-change by design. In the multi-credential case it gains a fabricated sawtooth (one point per 15-minute tick, ~96/day/window) that reads as usage swinging between two accounts'' readings, corrupting history/trend views and growing the store with data that never moved.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1624', '2026-10-28 08:40:21.82385+00', '2026-10-28 08:40:21.82385+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1742, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(bench): fix guest_replay benchmark — it replays zero events (restore() puts no committed Chat in replay) and its slice-2 baseline is restore-only', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1387","title":"wip(id): F11.8 slice 1 benchmark harness \u2014 four world benchmarks + just/nix runners (#539) \u2014 MERGED 2026-10-27T19:49:51Z, head ace10d6e503518cf87f0aadb2f2a54c0b6260dac","number":1387}],"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1403","title":"id(bench): PR #1387 guest_replay benchmark replays zero events \u2014 restore() never puts committed chat events in replay","number":1403,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:45:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing WorldCore::restore semantics in pkgs/id/src/world/core.rs to suit the bench","re-recording baselines for the other three benchmarks (journal_append_fsync, checkpoint_compaction, session_fanout) except where the fix PR''s CI requires it"],"include":["pkgs/id/benches/world_bench.rs","pkgs/id/benches/baseline.txt and pkgs/id/benches/BASELINES.md (guest_replay line/note only)","issue #1403, parent issue #539"]},"tests":["CI on the fix PR: bench target builds and `cargo bench --bench world_bench -- --quick --only guest_replay` (or the renamed workload) runs with the guest-count assertion in place","Deliberate-empty check: the assertion demonstrably fires when replay is empty (e.g. shown by the pre-fix code path in the PR description or a unit-style guard)"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1391 as its routed follow-up; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1403 is distinct from the triage task (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1403). Fresh gh search of open code issues for guest_replay this run returned only #1403; no live fix task owns this.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:45:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"guest_replay measures an empty guest pass: restore() never puts committed Chat events into RestoredWorld.replay, CountingProgram.seen stays 0 with no assertion, and the committed slice-2 baseline (baseline.txt guest_replay median=0.146) records restore-only time as guest-replay time for #539.","evidence":["Current main be7cf629 pkgs/id/src/world/core.rs Committed arm: WorldEventKind::Input(_) => replay.push(event.clone()); WorldEventKind::System { .. } | WorldEventKind::Chat(_) => {} \u2014 no replay.push for Chat (journal System entries push at the Journal arm above it)","Current main be7cf629 pkgs/id/benches/world_bench.rs bench_guest_replay (~line 124): journal = Created + Issued + N Committed chat_event() entries; loop `for event in &restored.replay { guest.update(event)?; }`; guest.seen is only black_box''d \u2014 no assert anywhere in the file on seen or replay length","PR #1387 state verified fresh 2026-10-28 (gh pr view): MERGED 2026-10-27T19:49:51Z \u2014 fix cannot land in that PR","Commit 7bd79a62 (#1535, #1512 baselines) added pkgs/id/benches/baseline.txt with `bench guest_replay unit=us_per_event median=0.146 min=0.142 reps=5` plus BASELINES.md \u2014 recorded from the empty-replay harness","Triage verdict with full evidence posted on #1403 by queue task 1391 (lane D, 2026-10-28)"],"acceptance":["guest_replay (or its honest successor workload) pushes exactly the N committed events through the counting guest, with an assertion on the guest-seen count that fails the bench run if replay is empty","WorldCore::restore semantics unchanged (no production-code change to pkgs/id/src/world/core.rs replay contract)","pkgs/id/benches/baseline.txt guest_replay line corrected/regenerated from the fixed harness and BASELINES.md notes the correction (old line was restore-only)","CI green on the fix PR (CI-first verification; no sandbox builds)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1403","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1387","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/539","https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/1535"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The poisoned baseline the triage warned about has already been committed (#1535): slice-3 CI diffing against a restore-only guest_replay median will misread every future change; normal priority (40).","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1403', '2026-10-28 08:40:30.736112+00', '2026-10-28 08:40:30.736112+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1743, 'repo-health-opencode-pilot', 'Small fix #690: make ElevenLabs describeOutput reject non-plain and non-positive sample rates', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/opencode","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/690","title":"fix(ai): ElevenLabs describeOutput manufactures invalid sampleRate from malformed output formats \u2014 ''pcm_abc'' yields NaN, ''pcm_-44100'' a negative rate","number":690,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:41:28Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["SpeechStream.sampleRate (already regex-guarded to plain digits)","Response-header usage parsing (tracked separately as #687)","Rejecting malformed formats at the request layer (the fix stays in describeOutput''s rate parsing)"],"include":["packages/ai/src/protocols/elevenlabs-speech.ts describeOutput rate-segment validation","Regression tests in packages/ai/test/ speech protocol tests"]},"tests":["bun test (speech protocol tests) via CI, from packages/ai"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Searched open and closed issues for ''sampleRate elevenlabs'', ''describeOutput'', ''elevenlabs format'' and ''NaN sample'' on 2026-10-28: no hits. #687 covers the response-header parser (headerUsage) in the same surface and explicitly scoped sample-rate parsing out.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:41:28Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"describeOutput accepts any finite Number() result for the format''s rate segment: non-numeric segments become NaN, negative and zero rates pass through, and hex/exponent spellings are reinterpreted as rates.","evidence":["Laptop bun probe running the verbatim describeOutput + PCM_CODECS body (elevenlabs-speech.ts md5 b2e674c85670a0b69f0948005d567351, byte-identical to main cf43cf4a4b; probe at laptop ~/git/fleet/probe-2026-10-28-0335/probe.ts, removed after): ''pcm_abc'' -> NaN, ''pcm_44.1k'' -> NaN, ''pcm_-44100'' -> -44100, ''pcm_0'' -> 0, ''wav_0x10'' -> 16, ''pcm_1e5'' -> 100000; controls ''pcm_44100'' -> 44100, ''ulaw_8000'' -> 8000, ''mp3_44100_128'' -> 44100, ''opus_48000_32'' -> 48000"],"acceptance":["A rate segment that is not a plain positive integer (at minimum abc, 44.1k, -44100, 0, 0x10, 1e5) yields sampleRate undefined in both the pcm and container results","Plain formats unchanged: pcm_44100 -> 44100, ulaw_8000 -> 8000, mp3_44100_128 -> 44100, opus_48000_32 -> 48000, bare pcm -> undefined","No NaN, negative, or zero sampleRate can reach the speech finish event''s media info from describeOutput","Regression tests cover the malformed and control formats in packages/ai/test/ speech protocol tests"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/690","packages/ai/src/protocols/elevenlabs-speech.ts:165-170 describeOutput, :18 OpenString format type, :178 finish caller","packages/ai/src/protocols/utils/speech-stream.ts:76-79 SpeechStream.sampleRate regex-guarded sibling parser","https://github.com/developing-today/opencode/issues/687 sibling headerUsage parser (response-header side; this is the request-format side)"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Fabricated NaN/negative/zero sample rates corrupt the media metadata consumers use to interpret returned speech audio, but only when a caller passes a malformed open-string output format, so reachability is narrow. One-function fix with an existing undefined fallback and a regex-guarded sibling pattern to mirror.","timebox_minutes":20}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/opencode:issue:690', '2026-10-28 08:42:29.307462+00', '2026-10-28 09:43:35.126693+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1744, 'repo-health-openchamber-pilot', 'docs(web): observability contract doc + conformance fixture for #612 phase 3 (#614)', '{"prs":[{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/620","title":"feat(web): session-activity v1 fields for external consumers (#524)","number":620,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:25:00Z"},{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/pull/619","title":"feat(web): add GET /api/managed-servers registry read (#525)","number":619,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:25:00Z"}],"set":null,"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/openchamber","risk":{"flags":["docs-only","tests-only"],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/614","title":"docs(web): external observability contract documentation + paired-client conformance fixture (design #612, phase 3)","number":614,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:25:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["production behaviour changes to either endpoint","cross-repo implementation","held/Drew-owned PRs","secrets, credentials, purchases, or Drew-only decisions"],"include":["packages/web/server/lib/opencode/DOCUMENTATION.md","new conformance fixture/test under packages/web/server/lib/opencode/"]},"tests":["new conformance fixture passes (empty-but-ready state, key sets, secret-field absence)","existing session-runtime.test.js and managed-servers.test.js still pass","bun run check:changed on laptop/CI"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Issue #614 is the single phase-3 issue under design #612; its existing queue task 1626 is the triage packet (triage dedupe family), this is the distinct implementation packet (fix dedupe family) the triage was instructed to enqueue on promotion","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:25:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Phases 1-2 of design #612 landed two external API shapes, but no external-consumer document describes the shared contract and no conformance fixture lets a paired client verify a server honours it.","evidence":["Triage task 1626 (2026-10-28): #524 and #525 both CLOSED; PR #620 merged 2026-10-28T02:58:56Z, PR #619 merged 2026-10-28T04:56:42Z - dependency in the original triage packet is satisfied","PR #620 body: session-activity returns {version:1, serverTime, watcherReady, sessions:{[sessionId]:{type,lastActivityAt,status,model,toolInFlight}}}; model is the observed {modelID,providerID}|null pair (no separate provider key); toolInFlight is null today (no in-process tool tracking)","PR #619 body: GET /api/managed-servers returns {version:1, serverTime, servers:[...]} with exactly seven entry keys pid, port, directory, version, status, startedAt, sessionCount; other instances status unknown with nulls; entry version is the server''s reported version, distinct from the top-level contract version:1","Both PRs documented their shapes in packages/web/server/lib/opencode/DOCUMENTATION.md (managed-servers.js entry and the session-activity envelope rationale section), establishing it as the doc location; targeted tests live in the same directory (session-runtime.test.js, managed-servers.test.js)","Open follow-up affecting the managed-servers description: issue #638 / PR #639 (recorded-pid identity verification) is still OPEN at triage time - the document must describe identity-verified liveness as landed on main at implementation time, not PR #619''s original signal-0-only wording"],"acceptance":["DOCUMENTATION.md (or a doc it links from the same location) names both endpoints, every landed field, and each field''s unknown representation; a reader can build the babysitter poller from the document alone","Document covers the five #612 rules, the sessions-key envelope, model as a single observed {modelID,providerID}|null pair (observed, not configured), toolInFlight null-today semantics, watcherReady empty-vs-not-ready semantics, and the two different meanings of version (contract v1 top-level vs per-entry server version)","Conformance fixture in packages/web/server/lib/opencode/ passes against a server with no active sessions (empty-but-ready state), asserts pinned key sets per entry for both reads, presence of version + serverTime, and secret-field absence by key set (no password/token/fingerprint/args keys anywhere)","Fixture asserts a stopped server is absent (or marked) within one poll cycle and runs without a real OpenCode session for the empty-state assertions","No production behaviour changes: docs + fixture/tests only"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/614","https://github.com/developing-today/openchamber/issues/612","triage task 1626 in repo-health-openchamber-pilot"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Phase 3 is the consumer-facing payoff of design #612; phases 1-2 have landed so the shapes can now be documented as fact, per issue #614 priority/low","timebox_minutes":90}', 'done', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/openchamber:issue:614', '2026-10-28 08:43:36.514133+00', '2026-10-28 11:10:35.776976+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1745, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): fix pipe inside code span splitting table cells in markdown codec', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1424","title":"id(web): a pipe inside an inline code span in a table cell splits the cell on open \u2014 code mark destroyed, phantom column, trailing fragment dropped","number":1424,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:57:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["changing GFM table semantics for rows with genuinely more cells than the header (spec-conformant drop)","plain-text \\| cell escaping (works today)","upgrading or replacing comrak"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs table parse/save handling for code spans containing pipes","round-trip fixpoint regression tests in the same file","issue #1424"]},"tests":["cd pkgs/id && cargo test --features web --lib web::markdown (table tests) \u2014 via CI on the fix PR","New fixpoint tests: pipe-in-code-span in body cell, header cell, and as a cell''s only content; 1-column-header no-drop case"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1426 as its routed follow-up; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1424 distinct from the triage task (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1424). #1424''s own filing dedupe (2026-10-27) found no other issue tracking pipe-in-code-span table splitting; fresh open-issue search this run returned only #1424.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:57:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"comrak''s table extension splits rows on pipes before inline parsing, so a pipe inside a code span in a table cell breaks the cell in the id web markdown codec: code mark destroyed, phantom column on save, trailing fragment dropped when the header is narrower.","evidence":["Filing probe (issue #1424, on main 37418e56, codec''s own functions): input row | `a|b` | c | under a 2-column header parses to THREE plain-text cells \"`a\", \"b`\", \"c\" \u2014 no code mark; save emits | \\`a | b\\` | c | (phantom column); 1-column-header variant drops the post-pipe fragment entirely","Current main be7cf629 pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs:110-114 markdown_to_prosemirror passes the raw string to comrak parse_document with commonmark_options(); commonmark_options sets extension.table = true (~line 86); no pre-processing of table rows or code spans exists in the parse path","git log 37418e56..be7cf629 for pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs: six commits (delimiter-mark edge spaces #1510, whitespace normalization #1525, HTML-atom marks #1505, Arena alias/rustfmt + image-alt markup #1417) \u2014 none touch table row parsing, so the filing probe''s behavior stands","Control from filing: plain-text escaped pipe a\\|b in a cell round-trips correctly today","Triage verdict posted on #1424 by queue task 1426 (lane D, 2026-10-28)"],"acceptance":["Code spans containing pipes survive open->save in table cells: one cell, code mark intact, column count unchanged","The 1-column-header case no longer drops cell content","New round-trip fixpoint tests cover pipe-in-code-span in a body cell, a header cell, and as a cell''s only content","Existing table tests pass unmodified (test_table, test_table_with_formatting, test_roundtrip_table, test_table_alignment_roundtrip, table-cell does-not-panic tests)","CI green on the fix PR (CI-first verification; no sandbox builds)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1424"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"Silent data corruption (restructured table, lost code formatting, possible content deletion) in a common construct \u2014 tables documenting shell pipelines, bitwise OR, or type unions routinely contain pipes inside code spans.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1424', '2026-10-28 08:43:59.028462+00', '2026-10-28 08:43:59.028462+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1746, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'aggregator: OpenCode Go reset pairing — triage', '{"kind":"triage","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1626","title":"aggregator: OpenCode Go reset dates are paired by section position, not by workspace \u2014 one missing or extra ''monthly reset'' line shifts both workspaces'' resets","number":1626,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:44:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Changing the quota view document itself or the stewardship read format","Other pools'' extractors in quota-extract.ts (except a shared paragraph-anchoring helper if triage prefers)","monthDayTime''s roll-forward policy beyond noting the BUG2 interaction"],"include":["pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-extract.ts goWorkspace reset anchoring","Regression tests for the control / missing-reset / stray-mention shapes in the aggregator test suite"]},"tests":["Bun test: pm-stack/aggregator quota-extract tests \u2014 light TS tests, laptop or CI"],"dedupe":{"basis":"gh issue search (open+closed) for quota-extract / OpenCode Go workspace reset returned #1204 (extractor health reporting), #1114, #1055, #895 \u2014 none covers reset pairing. #1541/#1564/#1568 are measuredAt/generatedAt freshness gates in other modules; #1623 is the tier-items proposal TTL clock (different file/mechanism).","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:44:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"goWorkspace pairs OpenCode Go monthly resets by section-wide match index instead of by workspace paragraph, so a missing or extra reset mention mis-dates both workspaces.","evidence":["quota-extract.ts:159-161 comment + code: resets collected section-wide via matchAll, Personal takes resets[0], Lab resets[1]; both Go POOL_SPECS entries (:276/:284) share the one ''### OpenCode Go'' section text","Probe on main be7cf629 (hidden_files/probe-2026-10-28-laneA-goreset/out.log), real extractQuotaPools, now=2026-10-28T12:00Z: CTRL Personal 2026-11-03 / Lab 2026-11-09 correct; BUG missing Personal reset -> Personal 2026-11-09 (Lab''s), Lab null; BUG2 stray Oct 5 mention -> Personal 2026-10-05 stale-past, Lab 2026-11-03 (Personal''s); confirmed in two independent probe runs","quota-extract.ts header: the quota view ''preserves dated observations'', so sections accumulate dated reset mentions over time \u2014 the pairing assumption (exactly one reset per paragraph, nothing else mentioning one) is not stable"],"acceptance":["Each Go workspace''s monthly reset is taken from its own paragraph (or an equivalently anchored match), never by section-wide index","A workspace paragraph without a reset line yields resetsAt null for that workspace and does not consume another workspace''s reset","An extra ''monthly reset'' mention elsewhere in the section does not shift either workspace''s reset","Regression tests cover the paired control, the missing-reset paragraph, and the stray-mention section (probe fixtures reusable)","Existing aggregator test suites still pass"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1626","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-extract.ts:152","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-extract.ts:160","pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-extract.ts:37"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The quota page steers fleet spend: the Go workspaces carry a burn rotation order keyed to these windows and reset dates. A shifted pairing silently renders the wrong reset for both pools (or a weeks-past date) as authoritative, and the fail-soft extractor design means nothing ever errors.","timebox_minutes":30}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:triage:developing-today/code:issue:1626', '2026-10-28 08:44:01.201172+00', '2026-10-28 08:44:01.201172+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1748, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): TS shell-contract u64 cap parity with Rust checker (fix #1441)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1441","title":"id(web): TS shell-contract checker rejects valid u64 values above 2^53-1 that the Rust checker accepts (seed, sequence, offset)","number":1441,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:47:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Rust checker changes","Contract JSON changes","Production world client wiring"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/shell-contract.ts u64 bound handling (accept non-negative integer u64 values at/above the safe range; keep exact enforcement of explicit in-range min/max)","pkgs/id/web/src/world-contract.test.ts parity regression tests"]},"tests":["bunx vitest run src/world-contract.test.ts (via CI)","existing web unit suite passes in CI"],"title":"id(web): TS shell-contract u64 cap parity with Rust checker (fix #1441)","dedupe":{"basis":"Fix follow-up for triage task 1454 on issue #1441, confirmed live on current main 2026-10-28; gh searches found no existing PR or duplicate issue for the u64 shell-contract cap, and no existing fix task for #1441 in the queue at enqueue time.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:47:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"pkgs/id/web/src/shell-contract.ts caps every u64 field at Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER (INTEGER_MAX u64 at line 64 on current main), while the Rust checker (pkgs/id/src/shell_contract.rs:445) caps u64 at u64::MAX and the contract JSON puts no max on most u64 fields. The TS checker therefore falsely rejects contract-valid frames (install_begin seed >= 2^53, view/records sequence >= 2^53). Fix per the issue''s precision note: for u64, a non-negative integer number at/above the safe range cannot be proven out of range in JS and must be accepted; explicit field min/max bounds within the safe range are still enforced exactly.","evidence":["Triage task 1454 re-verified on current main via gh api 2026-10-28: shell-contract.ts:61-64 INTEGER_MAX maps u64 to Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER; shell_contract.rs:445 FieldType::U64 => Some(u64::MAX)","Original probe on main 95cd41f0 (issue #1441): seed=2^53 rejected with ''must be in 0..=9007199254740991''; JSON-parsed u64::MAX seed and view sequence rejected identically; seed=42 and sequence=7 accepted","gh search 2026-10-28 (triage task 1454): no open/merged PR and no other issue addresses the shell-contract u64 cap"],"acceptance":["checkClientFrame accepts install_begin with seed = 2^53 and with the JSON-parsed form of u64::MAX (parity with the Rust checker)","checkServerFrame accepts view/records frames whose sequence is at or above 2^53","Negatives, non-integers, u16/u32 overflows, and explicit safe-range max violations (total_bytes > 16777216) are still rejected","u64 error messages no longer cite 9007199254740991 as a contract bound","Regression tests in world-contract.test.ts pin the parity cases; Rust checker and contract JSON unchanged","A comment at the cap explains the JS precision constraint (mirroring how the Rust side documents its bound)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1441","pkgs/id/web/src/shell-contract.ts:61","pkgs/id/src/shell_contract.rs:445"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Conformance-library parity defect (priority/low on the issue): a TS-port conformance proof currently disagrees with the contract and the Rust host; no production consumer yet, so it should be fixed before the checker gains consumers.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1441', '2026-10-28 08:45:14.574189+00', '2026-10-28 08:45:14.574189+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1752, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): sequence world records fetches so a re-request mid-pagination cannot render a stale page', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1458","title":"id(web): world records view shows a lone stale page when an input event restarts a paginated fetch \u2014 fresh pages are silently discarded","number":1458,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T09:05:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["Server-side records protocol changes (the wire format already orders answers; the defect is client state)","World surface rendering (world-surface.ts)"],"include":["pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts records fetch sequencing (generation or coalescing)","pkgs/id/web regression test with a mock WebSocket","issue #1458"]},"tests":["bunx vitest run for the pkgs/id/web world records regression test \u2014 via CI on the fix PR (no sandbox builds)","Regression sequences: control two-page fetch renders the complete set; interleave (input event between pages) renders the fresh fetch''s complete set"],"dedupe":{"basis":"Enqueued by triage task 1464 as its routed follow-up; dedupe_key repo-health:v1:fix:...:1458 distinct from the triage task (repo-health:v1:triage:...:1458). #1458 filing dedupe searched open+closed issues for records pagination terms with zero competing hits; no live fix task owns this.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T09:05:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"Overlapping paginated records fetches in pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts share one unsequenced state triple (records/recordsAfter/recordsPending), so a re-request mid-pagination lets the stale chain close the fresh fetch and renders a lone stale page while discarding fresh pages.","evidence":["Current main be7cf629 pkgs/id/web/src/world.ts:179 records handler `if (!recordsPending) return;` then merges any page and closes+renders on any next_after=null \u2014 no generation/fetch identity anywhere in the file (grep: no ''generation'')","Current main be7cf629 world.ts:212-219 requestRecords resets records={}, recordsAfter=null, recordsPending=true unconditionally and sends a first-page request; call sites :158 (snapshot), :170 (non-chat event), :268 (refresh button click)","Only world.ts commit since the filing probe (95cd41f0) is 7d043c58 (#1475 socket retire on rejoin); its diff contains no records changes, so the probed behavior stands","Filing probe (issue #1458, laptop Bun + happy-dom 21, verbatim world.ts, mock WebSocket, in-order answers; log hidden_files/probe-2026-10-27-laneB-worldrecords/out.log): control displayedRecords={a1:1,a2:2}; interleave displayedRecords={a2:2} only \u2014 a1 lost in the reset, fresh page b1 discarded","Triage verdict posted on #1458 by queue task 1464 (lane D, 2026-10-28)"],"acceptance":["In the interleave sequence (input event mid-pagination), the final rendered records are the fresh fetch''s complete set, never a single stale page","Pages/continuations from a superseded fetch cannot merge into, close, or render the live fetch (generation guard or coalescing with dirty-flag refetch)","Regression test (vitest/happy-dom, mock WebSocket, in-order answers) pins the control two-page fetch and the interleave case","Single-page fetches, snapshot-triggered fetch, and the refresh button behave as before","CI green on the fix PR (CI-first verification; no sandbox builds)"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1458","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1440"],"max_attempts":3,"priority_reason":"The records panel presents authoritative world state; in any active world (input events during a multi-page load \u2014 the common case) it silently shows a truncated stale subset as if complete, with no error or retry.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'queued', 40, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1458', '2026-10-28 08:46:05.156495+00', '2026-10-28 08:46:05.156495+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, dedupe_key=excluded.dedupe_key, updated_at=excluded.updated_at;
INSERT INTO coord_tasks (id, queue, title, payload, status, priority, dedupe_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1753, 'repo-health-code-pilot', 'id(web): saturating pagination display arithmetic in templates.rs (fix #1472)', '{"kind":"small_fix","repo":"developing-today/code","risk":{"flags":[],"level":"low"},"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1472","title":"id(web): file-list pagination display still multiplies the raw page unchecked \u2014 debug panic / wrapped inverted range for page=usize::MAX (the #931 remainder in templates.rs)","number":1472,"state_checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:52:00Z"},"scope":{"exclude":["paginate() offset arithmetic and its echo-the-requested-page behaviour in routes.rs (fixed by #931, pinned by test)","Changing the /api/files or /files response shape"],"include":["pkgs/id/src/web/templates.rs render_file_list_content display arithmetic (start, end, total_pages audit)","pkgs/id regression tests in the templates/routes test modules"]},"tests":["cargo test --features web --lib web::templates (via CI or laptop, never sandbox)","cargo test --features web --lib web::routes (via CI) \u2014 test_paginate_overflow_page unchanged and passing"],"title":"id(web): saturating pagination display arithmetic in templates.rs (fix #1472)","dedupe":{"basis":"Fix follow-up for triage task 1491 on issue #1472, confirmed live on current main 2026-10-28; #931 (closed) fixed routes.rs paginate() only and is explicitly the parent, not a duplicate; no existing fix task for #1472 at enqueue time.","checked_at":"2026-10-28T08:52:00Z"},"schema":"repo-task/v1","problem":"render_file_list_content in pkgs/id/src/web/templates.rs computes the display start as (page.page - 1) * page.per_page + 1 with unchecked arithmetic. paginate() (routes.rs, fixed by #931) deliberately echoes the requested page unclamped (pinned by test_paginate_overflow_page), so page=usize::MAX reaches the renderer: debug builds panic on multiply overflow, release builds render a wrapped inverted range (start > end, both >> total).","evidence":["Triage task 1491 re-verified on current main via gh api 2026-10-28: templates.rs total_pages at :339 and start = (page.page - 1) * page.per_page + 1 at the pagination block, end via saturating_sub only after the unchecked multiply/add","Issue #1472 probe (standalone rustc, verbatim arithmetic, paginate() outputs for ?page=18446744073709551615&per_page=50, total 300, files []): debug panic ''attempt to multiply with overflow''; release renders 18446744073709551517-18446744073709551516 of 300; per_page=200 wraps likewise; control page 2 renders 51-100 of 300 correctly","gh search 2026-10-28 (triage 1491): no PR addresses templates pagination overflow"],"acceptance":["Pagination display arithmetic in render_file_list_content cannot overflow or wrap for any FileListPage values (saturating/checked start; total_pages and end audited)","Out-of-range page renders a sane range \u2014 never start > end, never exceeding the total \u2014 while normal pages render exactly as today (51-100 of 300 for page 2, per_page 50)","Regression tests cover page=usize::MAX at per_page 50 and per_page 200 (total 300, files empty) and the existing normal paging display cases still pass","paginate()''s pinned echo-the-requested-page behaviour (routes.rs test_paginate_overflow_page) is unchanged"],"context_refs":["https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/1472","https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/931","pkgs/id/src/web/templates.rs:339"],"max_attempts":2,"priority_reason":"Crafted-query debug panic / release wrong-output on the web UI''s main listing endpoint \u2014 the exact bug class #931 was filed for, still reachable through the renderer.","timebox_minutes":45}', 'claimed', 30, 'repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:1472', '2026-10-28 08:47:52.523147+00', '2026-10-28 11:06:50.384377+00') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET queue=excluded.queue, title=excluded.title, payload=excluded.payload, status